R {5}{0}{<238>}{The auction house}{<238>. .<088>}{Bustling with great activity, the auction house is extraordinarily large and very unorganized.  High ceilings and a marble floor make the room appear even more spacious than it needs to be. Rows upon rows of wooden seats are lined in front of the auctioneer's podium, which is on a raised platform.  A small table stands next to the auctioneer's podium, holding whatever item is being bid on at the moment.  Numerous amounts of people stream in and out of the auction house, chatting, laughing loudly, and bidding.  The auctioneer screams out bids as they come in, trying to overcome the noise of the room.  Nobody seems to be sitting in the seats provided for them, however, the entire room is packed with auction items and the many people bumping into each other with their sweaty bodies.  The auction house is hot and jarringly loud. }{Pinnacle}{ahouse}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6}{0}{<278>}{North of Center (n,s,w,e)}{<278>-+-<088>}{The cobbles give way to a weird, twisting tile that makes your stomach churn uneasily.  This must be North lane. You stand at an intersection where the cobbles of Main Street, which stretches to the south, meet the stomach- wrenching oddity of an undulating tile-covered path that goes left to right.  Just to the north there is a small, unimpressive brick building with a massive iron door.  }{Pinnacle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
