R {58}{0}{<238>}{The Dragon's Breath Pub}{<238>[P]<088>}{You stand in the midst of an enormous, cavernous, room.  Tables and chairs abound, filled with all nature of hirelings and henchmen.  The floor is covered with a million shells from various nuts and other edibles.  The layer of shells is drab black, soaked in oil, beer, and other various refuse spilled from the tables or tracked in from the outside.  What little you can see of the floor puts your mind at ease that it at least exists.  Heavy cast iron chandeliers hang low from the ceiling, filled with dozens of candles in an attempt at lighting the room.  Every drip of wax that falls on the floor causes your heart to skip a beat in hopes that the room won't explode in a fiery blaze.  People duck and dodge these obstacles so as to avoid extreme injury to the skull.  Periodically a drunken idiot will stand up too quickly only to knock himself completely unconscious.  A fire burns brightly in a fireplace on the far side of the room.  There is very little refuse around the fireplace, either because it has all been burned away or because there is at least someone making an attempt at keeping the place from becoming ashes.  The actual 'bar' stretches along the entire length of the wall on the far side.  Dozens of barstools line the edge of it, all filled with large men drinking far more than could possibly be safe.  Occasionally one falls to the floor, incoherent and barely alive and is quickly dragged aside as another patron takes his place. }{Pinnacle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
