R {99}{0}{<248>}{Office of Professional Registration (e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{The sounds of clattering feet and murmuring voices completely fills this dark and rough hewen stone building.  While the interior of the structure is more visually appealing than the exterior, with its soft iridescent glow, its 20 foot vaulted ceiling, and its dark oak counters, there is still the hint of a much rougher underbelly, as evidenced by the dusty and half-worked stones underneath it all.  People mill around the area, not pausing at all for pleasantries but rather working as efficiently and quickly as possible, then exiting once their transactions are complete.  One wouldn't expect more from the Office of Professional Registration, an organization whose sole purpose is to keep track of the various professions and the people who practice it. }{Pinnacle}{profs}{}{}{1.000}{1}
