R {203}{0}{}{<-> Mars exhibit <->}{ }{You walk further along the lobby and see a large exhibit in front of you. A large circular ball representing the planet Mars, floats gently in the air and a few smaller ones rotate around it.  The large glass case that encloses the model, reflects out red laser beams that you assume is the security system of the Observatory.  There is nothing worse than when a tourist makes off with an entire solar system.  }{Carina's Observatory}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {202}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {204}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {204}{0}{}{<-> Pluto Exhibit <->}{ }{Examining the glass case, you see a small replica of the planet Pluto and its moons rotating around.  You can only assume that the models are magnetically charged, which allows them to move around silently.  Small flashes of red light emitting from the case catch your attention.  The Observatory security system must be armed.  }{Carina's Observatory}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
