R {207}{0}{}{<-> Saturn Exhibit <->}{ }{The rings of Saturn are the most known of any of the other planets in the solar system, and depicting them perfectly is the static display appropriately named.  The hustle of traffic is lessened on this part of the lobby, yet still busy with activity.  The white walls glisten under the lights of the domed ceiling above.  }{Carina's Observatory}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {206}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {208}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {208}{0}{<138>}{<-> Souvenir Stand <->}{<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>}{A small souvenir stand along the corner of the wall grabs your attention as you enter this section of the Observatory.  A whole line of products line the small shelves behind the stand.  A small sign tacked up on a solar poster lists the current items for sale.  You might as well take a look and get a little remembrance of your trip here.  }{Carina's Observatory}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {207}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {209}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {209}{0}{}{<-> The Telescopic Pad <->}{ }{The ceiling high overhead is obstructed by the long telescopic lens of the great Observatory telescope before you.  You have heard rumors that this once used to be able to transport you to the stars above, but of course that is all rumor, and the Observatory has changed. This is the pillar piece of equipment when one wants to gaze into the sky and the stars above.  Perhaps you should give it a go.  }{Carina's Observatory}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
