R {211}{0}{}{<-> Observatory lobby <->}{ }{A large bay window on the southern wall catches your attention as you enter the room.  Off to a corner in the room, you notice a few of the Observatory technicians and workers talking amongst themselves, but loud enough for you to hear portions of the conversation.  It might be wise to listen to them more closely.  Try not to make yourself too noticeable however, because they might not be happy when they find out you are listening.  }{Carina's Observatory}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {202}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {212}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {212}{0}{}{<-> Venus Exhibit <->}{ }{A medium-size planet display stands before you.  Looking inside you see a brown and orange tint colored planet floating within.  The planet Venus is often referred to as 'Earth's sister planet' because of its very similar nature.  Among all of the planets in the known solar system, Venus is the closest planet to view from the telescope and brightest in the night sky.  }{Carina's Observatory}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
