R {341}{0}{}{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy (se,ne)}{ }{The seemingly endless plane of soy changes suddenly with a very high wall rising to the west, which seems to merge with the ground in a continuous curve.  A loud, wet, burbling sound wafts in from the northeast.  Far off to the east, you see a hill, and further to the south, there seems to be some sort of large, flat vertical surface that could be some type of building. }{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {340}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {342}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {342}{0}{}{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy (nw,ne,sw,se)}{ }{A small spring of what looks like soy milk bubbles and pops loudly.  The spring issues forth a steady flow of soy milk, which burbles and makes obscene noises constantly.  From this font, a small stream flows toward the northeast.  The unremarkable landscape is different only to the southeast, where a hill of moderate size thrusts upward from the ground. }{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
