R {343}{0}{}{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy (se,ne)}{ }{The ground here is extremely warped, as though someone had picked it up and bent it.  The ground curves into a large wall, blocking off any kind of movement, save in an easterly direction.  Crumbly bits of tofu are disseminated all over the ground.  You can hear a wet, sloppy sound, much like the flowing of a viscous liquid, to the southeast. }{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {342}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {344}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {344}{0}{}{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy (ne,se,sw)}{ }{Standing atop a small hill of tofu that pops up out of the landscape, you can see nothing but a dreary land of soy, which extends as far as the eye can see.  You shiver as the cold wind whips past you, its mordant chill piercing to your very bones.  You hear a slopping, burbling sound coming from the southeast. }{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
