R {351}{0}{}{Fortress of Soy (s,e)}{ }{The passage takes a turn here: one branch heads toward the south, further into the fortress, and the other branch leads east, towards the entrance.  The walls, slick with moisture, have been cut at right angles with great precision.  Stark and unadorned, the hallway is nothing more than an empty parallelepiped volume carved out of the ensorcelled tofu of which the fortress is composed.  To the south, you see some sort of barricade made out of stacked cubes of tofu. }{The Para-Elemental Plane of Soy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
