R {396}{0}{}{The edge of a crater (se,n,sw)}{ }{Billows of steam rise from the center of the crater hiding everything but the rim.  Many blackened rocks lie around the ground near the crater's lip, and the earth around the rim is buckled up in protest against this powerful impact.  The edge of the crater is very steep and approaching it would be dangerous.  To the east, the ground slopes downwards and merges with the dry sands of a desert. }{Impact Crater}{impact_crater}{}{}{1.000}{1}
