R {397}{0}{}{The rim of a crater (s,nw)}{ }{There is a large hole in the ground here that resembles a gaping wound in the very earth itself.  Like a wounded tree leaking sap, the ground seems to be bleeding with steam and heat.  The soil is charred and blackened around the edges of the hole from the extreme heat produced from the impact.  The steep walls are cracked and broken, prohibiting travel into the center of the crater. }{Impact Crater}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {396}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {398}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {398}{0}{}{The edge of a crater (se,w)}{ }{A cloud of thick, white steam rises from the large crater and radiates heat like a fire.  The edge of the hole is sharp and the drop is precarious.  The curve of the crater indicates that it might form a hemisphere twenty metres in diameter and ten metres deep.  The steam's thickness makes it completely opaque thus obscuring the details of the crater's heart, but it dissipates quickly as it drifts towards the sky. }{Impact Crater}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {397}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {399}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {399}{0}{}{The rim of a large crater (e,sw)}{ }{An amazing amount of heat radiates from the edge of the crater and the bright sunlight does little to penetrate its dark depths.  The ground resembles something one might find in a war zone where powerful explosives have been set off.  Steam rises in a large column from the hole indicating that whatever caused the crater may have opened some sort of fissure in the earth's crust.  The yellow streaks through the steam give it a sulfurous look and the sheer amount of it makes it completely opaque. There are some loose rocks on the edge of the crater. }{Impact Crater}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {398}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {400}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
