E {19954}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {400}{0}{}{The edge of a large crater (s,ne)}{ }{The flat, barren landscape of the surrounding area is rudely broken by what seems to be a crater.  The ground is buckled around its edge and the earth looks as if something has burnt it in the moving.  Sulfurous steam clouds the center of the crater and it is difficult to determine what might have caused this wound in the ground.  The dry ground and the billowing steam indicate that the crater is an established landmark and has opened a crack that seems to go through the tectonic plate.  Small though that crack may be, the enormous pressure is pushing steam up through it at an incredible rate.  It would be very dangerous to tread near the edge of the crater. }{Impact Crater}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {399}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {401}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {401}{0}{}{The edge of a large crater (se,n)}{ }{The war that shattered the human civilization is long since over, and yet what seems be a bomb crater dominates the landscape.  It is venting hot steam from the center and it is difficult to determine what might have caused this because of the viscosity of the steam.  The ground is freshly burnt and rubble lies strewn everywhere, thrown randomly from the impact.  The heat from the steam and the sulfurous smell leads you to the conclusion that a crack must have opened down to the magma itself.  The treacherous walls of the crater prohibit deeper exploration. }{Impact Crater}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {400}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {402}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {402}{0}{}{The rim of a crater (e,nw)}{ }{Steam rises out of a large hole in the ground like so much blood pouring out of a wound in the earth itself.  The smell of sulfur fills the air and lends a yellow cast to the rising steam.  The ground is cracked, broken, and strewn with debris.  The edge of the crater has risen up to counter the displacement of the impact.  Despite the brightness of the day, it is impossible to see into the center of the crater and further investigation would be dangerous. }{Impact Crater}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {401}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {403}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {403}{0}{}{The rim of a large crater (w,ne)}{ }{The earth has been torn up by the impact of some fast-moving object, and a large crater has been formed.  Rocks and loose earth lie scattered around the sharp edge of the crater, and thick billows of steam rise from its depths.  Gusts of wind blow dust up from the dry desert surrounding the crater. }{Impact Crater}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {402}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {396}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

