R {502}{0}{<088>}{At the base of a large sand dune (sw,enter)}{<168>E<088>}{The relentless heat from the searing sun makes the air shimmer, forcing you to stop and mop the sweat off your brow. A recent sandstorm seems to have shifted one of the great sand dunes nearby revealing a tumble of twisted metal and stonework obviously the remains of one of the many ruins that lie scattered nearby. From what looks to have been the wall of an ancient building, a dark yawning hole offers respite from the hot sun and stinging sand. }{Ruined Bunker}{ruined_bunker}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {501}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {503}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {503}{0}{}{A rubble strewn room (out,e)}{ }{A few shafts of sunlight rush in through the hole high in the southern wall, warming the air in here and reminding you of the heat of the desert outside. Relieved to be out of the desert sun, you glance around to find yourself in some sort of room that extends into the gloom further to the east. Twisted girders and rubble block what was once a passage leading west.  }{Ruined Bunker}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {502}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {504}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {504}{0}{}{A rubble filled room (w)}{ }{Your eyes strain to adjust to the dim light at this end of the room. It seems that the devastation spared the western half of the room  is present here. Large steel girders from the super structure of the building have smashed through the concrete roof causing the roof to partially collapse, leaving this whole area unstable and treacherous. Almost hidden by the rubble and debris on the eastern wall are a set of heavy steel elevator doors. Who knows what lost tech might be found behind those doors. }{Ruined Bunker}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {503}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47598}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {505}{0}{<238>}{The Badlands}{<238>, `<088>}{The Badlands Dust whips through the air on harsh, burning winds.  The low rolling hills do nothing to stop the airborn grit from scouring the countryside clean of life.  Could it be your imagination, or is that the smell of burning flesh?  A foul wind whips by you as you survey this desolate landscape bringing with it dust and grit with the force of a sandblaster.  To the west you barely sense the continuation of the badlands.   }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
