R {541}{1024}{}{A turn-off from the road (nw,s)}{ }{                     Road This is a branch off of the old road running out of Houston. You can see the tops of the buildings in the distance. The pavement here is buckled and cracked in places, and is difficult to walk upon.  It's obviously not navigable by anything short of a hovercraft or a tank.  To the south lies the driveway of an abandoned gas station, and the shattered remains of the expressway lie to the north. }{Gas Station}{gas_station}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {535}{nw}{nw}{9}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {542}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {542}{0}{}{Driveway (s,n)}{ }{You stand on a small strip of only somewhat scorched grass in front of a now-defunct gas station. From the sight of things, one of the ubiquitous gangs of bikers or freaks went through the station with a large supply of incendary hand grenades.  The aluminium roof which used to cover the gasoline pumps is charred with soot, in the places where the sky doesn't shine grungily through, and the pumps themselves have been reduced to twisted lumps of metal and melted rubber tubing.  To the south stands the gas station's office, attached to which is the garage bay for the mechanics. The office and garage seem to have been spared the destruction incurred by the pump area itself. }{Gas Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {541}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {543}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {543}{0}{}{The office of a gas station (e,n)}{ }{  This is the now-shabbily decorated office for what was once a popular  roadside gas station on the road to Houston, but has since fallen prey to the wandering bands of motorcycle gangs who seem to be intent on destroying everybody along the once-bustling interstate highways.  There are several plaques on the wall proclaiming the certification of the mechanics, as well as an expired 1997 business license, and a cheap-looking picture. }{Gas Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {542}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {544}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {544}{0}{}{Garage (w)}{ }{This is the garage attached to the gas station.  Unlike the rest of the station, the garage seems to have withstood most of the destruction which rained down upon the business. The tool racks are not very disorganized, and the hydraulic lifts appear to still have pressure.  All in all, it's a completely up-to-date garage, with the latest equipment straight from the Yokohama Honda equipment consortium of 2004. }{Gas Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {543}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

