R {701}{0}{}{Top of Sinkhole}{ }{The ground takes a sudden drop, forming a sunken bowl abounding with flora.  You can't quite make out the far side of the sinkhole through all the leaves--it could be as short as a stone's throw across, or it might be farther.  The foliage tops tall trunks that originate farther below.  It's a little disconcerting to have the upper branches of the trees at eye level, and see the trunks stretching down beneath the ground. A rough trail leads down the near side into the sinkhole. }{Florida Sinkhole}{florida_sinkhole}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {700}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {702}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {702}{0}{}{Below the Rim}{ }{Underneath the tree canopy, you can see that the far edge of the sinkhole is about half a football field's length away.  Tree trunks are spread below the rim of the bowl like pillars--their bases deep down in the funnel, and their upper crown of branches just above eye level.  The sides of the hole are mostly exposed rock and boulders with years of soil built up in pockets where plants have taken root and flourished.  The sound of running water bubbles up from below. }{Florida Sinkhole}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {701}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {703}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {703}{0}{}{Waterfalls}{ }{The view is breathtaking!  The noise of rushing water fills the air as multiple waterfalls spill into the sinkhole.  The sparkling water dances its way down the funnel-shaped walls, skipping over the gaps in the boulders.  Each waterfall ends in a small rivulet of water continuing down to the bottom.  There is a small cave to the east. }{Florida Sinkhole}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {702}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {704}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {705}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {704}{0}{}{A Small Cave}{ }{This small cave has been formed by the convenient placing of several large rocks.  There is enough shelter for one person or a few medium-sized animals.  Judging from the scraps and tools lying around, it's probably occupied by a person.  It seems someone has made a permanent home here. }{Florida Sinkhole}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {703}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {705}{0}{}{Overlooking the Bottom}{ }{This level is almost like a balcony overlooking the bottom of the sinkhole.  There is a gorgeous view of the waterfalls above, cascading over the walls until they arrive at the bottom and join together to form the creek.  The vegetation on this level is low-lying plants--grasses, ferns, small palms and others.  The shade is speckled by sunlight darting through the shifting leaves of the canopy overhead. }{Florida Sinkhole}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {703}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {706}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {706}{0}{}{Bottom of Sinkhole}{ }{Tall grass and weeds make it hard to see very far in any direction but up.  The ground is very soggy and there are small standing puddles of water here and there.  The creek running across the bottom is only a short distance across.  A rusted-out vehicle of some sort is nose-down in the creek.  A few small trees are growing straight, but the medium-sized trees here are at odd angles to the floor. }{Florida Sinkhole}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {705}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

