R {814}{0}{}{Beside a lake in the swamp (nw,swim)}{ }{The swamp ends abruptly in what seems to be a small lake. Old trees and all kinds of vegetation almost cover the lake from view. You notice some crocodiles swimming around in the water and a horrible stench hits you right in your face. How can anything possibly want to live in a place like this. A strange sound can be heard from the far end of the lake. }{Swamp Lake}{swamp_lake}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {625}{nw}{nw}{9}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {815}{swim}{swim}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {815}{0}{}{A lake in the swamp (n,s)}{ }{You find yourself swimming around in a small lake in the swamp!  The only thing you can think of is that you must have gone mad or something. The swamp is north of you and you spot a small deserted house standing on a small overgrown island to your south. Whatever is out there better be good, or else you have been swimming around in this disgusting lake for nothing. }{Swamp Lake}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {814}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {816}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {816}{0}{}{A lake in the swamp (n,s)}{ }{Swimming around in the lake you start to feel the cold water bite through your skin. The horrible stench from the green water makes you want to throw up. The small overgrown island stands south of you and the old building hides in the shadows. Some small crocodiles watch you closely as you swim through the water. }{Swamp Lake}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {815}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {817}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {817}{0}{}{A small island in the swamp (swim,enter)}{E}{You have reached a small island. The vegetation here is very dense with weird flowers and a lot of grass. A small house stands here and you hear a strange moaning sound from the inside. Maybe you shouldn't enter, it might be dangerous for your health. A small door is open and an old sign says 'Welcome'. A small lake is north of here and you can see the swamp section on the other side. If you really want to get back you better start swimming. }{Swamp Lake}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {816}{swim}{swim}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {818}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {818}{0}{}{Inside an old house (out)}{ }{A very old house. Spider webs cover the ceiling and rats scurry around on the floor. A small table and some chairs stand in the middle of the room. Glass from some broken windows cover the floor and the eastern wall has almost fallen from the heavy weight of all the vegetation outside. }{Swamp Lake}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {817}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {819}{0}{<228>}{Southeastern Swamps (n,w,e)}{<228>; ;<088>}{Southeastern Swamps The canopy of the swamp vegetation blots out the sky here.  You can hear the roar of some far off motor. Who'd be way out here?  The stench of this swamp is almost unbearable. You don't think that you're going to be able to make it through this thing.  To the west and north you see the continuation of the swampland.  The blue-green waters of the gulf stretch out to the south and west. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {648}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {820}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {821}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {820}{0}{<228>}{Southeastern Swamps (n,e)}{<228>; ;<088>}{Southeastern Swamps The canopy of the swamp vegetation blots out the sky here.  You hear a loud sucking sound as you walk through the dew.  Huge trees and ferns grow in abundance here. There must be something wrong with these plants since they seem to grow so well.  To the east you vaguely detect the continuation of the swampland.  The Gulf of Mexico stretches out to the south, sparkling blue-green in the sunlight. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {819}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {649}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {821}{0}{<228>}{Southeastern Swamps (n,s,w)}{<228>; ;<088>}{Southeastern Swamps The canopy of the swamp vegetation blots out the sky here.  You hear the growls of some far off animal. You don't feel like it would be a good thing to run into anything that lives here.  You can hear the roar of some far off motor. Who'd be way out here?  To the west and north you just make out the continuation of the swampland.  The city of New Orleans rests here in the crook of the Mississippi delta, mostly submerged beneath the flood waters it desperately tried to fight for centuries. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {819}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {647}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {822}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {822}{0}{<228>}{Southeastern Swamps (n,e)}{<228>; ;<088>}{Southeastern Swamps The stench of this swamp is almost unbearable. You don't think that you're going to be able to make it through this thing.  The swamp encompasses you with its hot humid sticky filth.  There is a mist that covers the ground here. It smells of sulfur.  To the east and north you barely sense the continuation of the swampland.  The waters of the Gulf of Mexico stretch out to the west and south. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {821}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {823}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {823}{0}{<228>}{Southeastern Swamps (w)}{<228>; ;<088>}{Southeastern Swamps The swamp encompasses you with its hot humid sticky filth.  You've got to wonder how anything could survive way out here.  The stench of this swamp is almost unbearable. You don't think that you're going to be able to make it through this thing.  The waters of the Gulf of Mexico surround you on three sides. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {822}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {824}{0}{}{Murky Swamp (sw)}{ }{Ankle deep mud covers this area of the swamp. Off to one side, you see a large patch of reedy swamp grass. The sounds of crickets chirping break the stillness every so often, but it still seems like this part of the swamp is just a little too quiet. }{Jeremy's Swamp}{jeremys_swamp}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {648}{sw}{sw}{12}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {825}{follow path}{follow path}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {825}{0}{}{A Path in the Swamp Grass (d,out)}{<128>F<088>}{Large reedy swamp grass grows close on all sides here. You are standing in a shallow clearing along the path you just took. The ground looks a little more solid here than the mud in the rest of the swamp. }{Jeremy's Swamp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
