R {927}{0}{}{An Excavation Site (nw,hut,stairs)}{<238>S<088>}{You stand before a small excavation site.  Huge construction lights are focused on a gaping hole torn into the ground.  A small hut sits just off the side of the hole as machinery and workers scurry about to clear away rubble. }{Genlab}{genlab}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {879}{nw}{nw}{9}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {928}{stairs}{stairs}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {936}{hut}{hut}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {928}{0}{<278>}{A Large Construction Hole (stairs,ne)}{<278>.@.<088>}{You stand at the bottom of a large hole.  The walls stretch a full twenty feet to the ground above, with a makeshift stairs leading up to ground level. Glancing up, you're temporarily blinded by the bright construction lights focused on you from above.  Several construction workers are milling at the northeast end of this hole, where they've unearthed a heavy steel door leading into the rocky wall. }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {927}{stairs}{stairs}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {929}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {929}{0}{<238>}{An Underground Tunnel (e,sw)}{<238>] [<088>}{You stand just beyond the steel door at the entrance to the tunnel.  Faint light shines in through the opening to the southwest\; enough to see by, but if you plan on continuing east into the rock you'll need another source of light.  This tunnel seems to have been hewn from the rock in a rough manner.  Perhaps when the tunnel was built in the late 20th century they used old fashioned steel methods for excavating, instead of the laser drillers that are common these days. }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {928}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {930}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {930}{0}{<238>}{An Underground Tunnel (e,w)}{<238>] [<088>}{You're about twenty feet into the tunnel, and the darkness begins to close in around you.  You can see the outline of a door to the west, while the tunnel continues into darkness to the east. }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {929}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {931}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {931}{0}{<238>}{An Underground Tunnel (ne,w)}{<238>] [<088>}{You're about thirty feet into the tunnel, and the darkness feels tight around you.  The air is thick with moisture and you can hear a faint dripping from the side of the tunnel.  Your light reveals that the main tunnel has had a slight cave-in ahead and you'll need to head northeast around the rubble.  You look to the west and sigh\; the doorway and lights beyond it is too distant to repel the oppressive darkness. }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {930}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {932}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {42679}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {932}{0}{<238>}{An Underground Tunnel (se,sw)}{<238>] [<088>}{You're traveling a narrow path around the rubble which obstructs the main passageway to the south.  The bend in the passageway blocks out even more light from the exit to the far west ... dark shapes skitter out of the way as you bring the area into your light.  Mice, rats and bugs of varying shapes and form scuttle across the floor.  The room has a very slight movement of air, and the air feels slightly dusty.  Likely there is a small crack in the rocks that leads up towards the surface. You continue to poke your lights into the darker recesses of the tunnel and notice that you've disturbed some spiders!  Dozens of the creatures come lunging out of a small corners about the rooms, and you suddenly notice many small webs lying between rocks.  As you continue along the passageway you suddenly come to a single HUGE web!  You hope that you don't run into the giant spider that created that! }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {931}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {933}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {933}{0}{<238>}{An Underground Tunnel (e,nw)}{<238>] [<088>}{You're back to the main passageway, fallen rubble just to the west of you.  Dark shapes scurry away as you bring the light near them.  You brush past a spider web, and sneeze, stirring up some dust.  The tunnel has begun to get dry as you've moved away from the surface and the exposed water pipe.  It continues to the east, and looks that it will finally lead towards the underground Lab. }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {932}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {934}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {934}{0}{<238>}{An Underground Tunnel (e,w)}{<238>] [<088>}{You're in the main passageway, fallen rubble and the exit to the surface far to the west.  You glance to the east and see an odd reflection ahead.  You're too far to determine for sure, but if you continue east you should be able to make out the distant glint ... }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {933}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {935}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {935}{0}{<238>}{An Underground Tunnel (w)}{<238>|@|<088>}{You're finally at the object of your search, or so you hope!  To the east lies a large steel door, covered in dust so that you can barely make out the stenciled letters.  Beside it lies a small metal panel, with a faintly glowing display.  The passageway has opened up here, and the ceiling of the tunnel slants up to a height above the range of your lights. }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {934}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {42685}{enter 112524}{enter 112524}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {42685}{e}{enter 112524;e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {936}{0}{}{A Small Construction Hut (leave)}{ }{You've entered a small construction hut set just to the side of the large hole in the ground.  From outside you can hear the shouts and the chaos of workers grinding away at the rock, but in here you feel removed from the hectic work.  Looking around you notice that the small hut has a large table with several chairs scattered around it. Stacks of paper, some of them excavation plans and dig sites, others of a more scientific nature, are sorted into rough piles and lie about the room. }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {927}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {937}{0}{<238>}{The Rocky Mountains (n,s,w,e)}{<238>.^.<088>}{The Rocky Mountains The trees here are tall and sparsely foliated, the effects of radiation and pollution taking their toll.  You wonder if they will ever grow into the lush, verdant forest that once stood here.  Storm clouds hang high on the mountain peaks, dark with rain or snow.  Noble and majestic, the Rockies rise up before you. They look steep and dangerous.   }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
