R {961}{0}{}{Bamboo thicket, treeline (nw,se)}{ }{You are at the edge of a bamboo thicket that has sprouted on ground that is sloped upwards to the west. The treeline of the hillside jungle runs along a bearing of 150 degrees. Between the treeline and thicket you are hiding in is a band of dense undergrowth that seems impenetrable. To the east and north is the welcome cover of the plain of reeds. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {960}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {962}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {42755}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {962}{0}{}{Bamboo thicket, treeline (n,se)}{ }{You are at the edge of a bamboo thicket that has sprouted on ground that is gently rising into the hills. Westward lies the treeline of an upland jungle. Between the treeline and thicket you are hiding in is a band of dense undergrowth running along a bearing of 150 degrees. To the east and north are the welcome cover of the plain of reeds. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {961}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {963}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {963}{0}{}{Tall grass (se,n,s)}{ }{Tall stands of Elephant and Rapier grass fight for dominance here. There used to be a large stand of bamboo over here but a lot of it seems to have been dug out and chewed over. The husks of young bamboo shoots and the splinters of mature stems are strewn over the wet earth. Yet, new bamboo shoots are already springing forth. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {962}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {964}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {974}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {964}{0}{}{Elephant grass (s,e)}{ }{Elephant grass rules supreme here. However, the blades seem to have been cropped recently and are not as tall as they are elsewhere. A musky odour lingers in the air. Crumbling limestone cliffs preclude passage to the north and west. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {963}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {965}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {965}{0}{}{Waterfall (ne,w,s)}{ }{A waterfall leaps down from a gap high in the limestone wall to the north, crashing into a splash pool. From the pool, the water rushes south, pushing its way through a tangle of reeds. Spray from the falls mists the air and covers everything with droplets of moisture. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {964}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {966}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {979}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {966}{0}{}{Tall grass (se,sw,s)}{<128>F<088>}{You push your way through the vegetation along a narrow game path. The reeds are giving way to thick stands of Elephant and Rapier grass. The grasses are taller than you are and you can't see anything beyond the rampant growth. The stench of disturbed silt hangs in the air and starchy root fragments litter the ground. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {965}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {967}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
