R {972}{0}{}{Riverbank (ne,s,n)}{ }{The river has shrunk greatly after the end of the rains, exposing its sandbanks. The reeds have grown rapidly in the fertile mud and stop right at the water's edge. Thick clouds of insects disturbed by your presence whirr and buzz in the humid air. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {960}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {973}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {976}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {973}{0}{}{Lily pond (s,w)}{ }{A huge water-lily pond lies before you. Large piles of mud and silt have been dredged up and piled on the banks of the pond. Dense stands of Elephant grass screen this waterscape from the surrounding highlands. The yellow and red lily blooms and the succulent lily-pads attest to the skill of the unknown gardener. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {972}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {974}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {974}{0}{}{Lily pond (e,ne,nw)}{ }{Here, a section of the original path of the river has been dammed up with basalt boulders to form a lily pond. Only a few red blooms and pads are evident; a large section of the pond seems to have been systematically cleared. Reeds fringe the pond and cast long shadows on the muddy waters. }{Valley of the Tribes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
