E {1665}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1659}{0}{}{A dirt road}{ }{A road made of hard-packed earth, just to the north of Grindur runs north-south here.  The town bustles with activity to the south, with pony-drawn carts full of stone entering into it, and empty carts passing you, headed north.  The low-hanging cloud of dust reaches out towards you from the southern face of the mountain at the end of the road, where dwarves quarry stone amid the clamor of tools and song. An outspoken dwarf carrying a large satchel around his back hustles through and grunts at the locals. You watch as he often stops and has numerous exchanges with them. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1658}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1660}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1660}{0}{}{Granite Quarry of Grindur}{ }{A thick cloud fills your mouth, nose, and lungs with the acrid tang of stone dust.  Loud clangs emanate from the stone face cut into the side of the mountain, where a dozen or so dwarves are quarrying blocks of grey granite with metal spikes and wooden hammers.  Superimposed over the cacophonous percussion of the quarry workers' toil, a chorus of hearty, stentorian voices belts out lively working songs. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1659}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1661}{0}{}{A dirt road}{<160>*<088>}{A loosely-packed dirt road with a good number of cart tracks runs north-south here.  Two barracks-like buildings lie next to the road, one on either side.  The sign above the door of the eastern building reads 'Carters', and the sign above the door on the west reads 'Quarry Workers'.  There seems to be a lot of activity to the north, with many carts passing by.  The road continues to the south. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1657}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1662}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
