R {1663}{0}{<238>}{The Southern Face Tavern}{<238>[P]<088>}{The inside of the tavern smells of freshly cut wood, spilled ale, and pungent meats.  Several dwarves are seated at the three long, thick wooden tables with matching benches which stand in the middle of the room.  The entire tavern is made from thick beams and planks of the same solid wood as the tables and benches, joined together with great skill.  There is a bar in the back of the room, where it looks like you can order drinks and food. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1656}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1656}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1664}{0}{}{Stonemasons' Guild Hall}{ }{The interior of the Stonemasons' Guild is spartan, yet suggestive of power.  Large banners of the Stonemasons' Guild hang from the sturdy wooden beams in the ceiling, giving a column-like effect, making the ceiling seem loftier than it really is.  There is a large wooden table in the middle of the hall, completely covered in charts, maps, and other documents.  The walls to the sides of the door are lined with bunk beds. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1657}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1657}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1665}{0}{}{Boggor's Dry Goods Emporium}{ }{The small store is cluttered with wares and goods to the point where it hinders movement about the store.  Large sacks of various grains and flours are piled up against one wall, while long coils of various types of rope hang over them.  Axes, picks, hammers, and other implements of toil hang from leather straps from the beams in the ceiling.  A series of steel spikes, buckets, pots, pans, and other sundry items occupy the remaining shelves in the store, and any other available surface. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1658}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1658}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1666}{0}{}{Carters' Quarters}{ }{Spartan yet homey, the quarters for the carters gives them a place to call home.  There are some bunks built into the walls, with some chests on the floor near them.  There is a large rack of equipment in the center of the room, where the accoutrements of the cart drivers' profession are stored.  There is a door to the south, which leads to the stables, and the open door to the west, which leads out onto the main road of town. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1661}{road}{road}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1669}{stables}{stables}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
