R {1667}{0}{}{Quarry Workers' Quarters}{ }{The thing that strikes you most about the Quarry Workers' Quarters is that everything has a light covering of grey stone dust.  Small, neat bunks line the walls of the wooden building, giving the quarry workers a place to sleep and rest after a long day's work.  At the foot of each set of bunks is a large wooden chest, which must hold the belongings of the workers.  In the center of the room is a large table with piles of equipment heaped on top of it. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1661}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1661}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1668}{0}{}{Quarry Workers' Quarters}{ }{The Quarry Workers' Quarters looks as though it has been abandoned for a long time, given the amount of dust in the room, but you soon realize that it has been brought in by the quarry workers.  Neat bunks line the walls, giving the quarry workers a place to sleep after their daily toil.  Large wooden chests, which probably contain the belongings of the workers, lie at the foot of each bunk.  A table in the center of the room is covered in dust and piles of equipment. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1662}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1662}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1669}{0}{}{Stables of Grindur}{ }{The sweet smell of hay, lightly mixed with manure invades your nostrils.  The interior of the stables is partitioned into two halves, one of several stalls occupied by ponies, and the other of a storage area, where the carts are kept.  There is a large, open door to the west, leading out to the road.  To the north, a door connects the stables to the Carters' quarters. }{Grindur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
