R {1736}{0}{<278>}{Balcony}{<278>[ ]<088>}{Stepping out onto a balcony, you look out over the forest, and can see nothing but trees for miles around.  It has a nice calming effect on your mind allowing you to forget about the day's battles and wounds.  The balcony itself is surrounded by a solid black iron railing with ghost-white vines painted on it.  The floor is made from four large walnut logs, cut in half to give a flat surface for walking on.  In each corner of the balcony sits a chair and matching table for anyone to use day or night. }{Guiles Mansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1735}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {1737}{0}{<268>}{Hallway}{<268>[ ]<088>}{As the hallway continues east and west, you notice north of you is a room that appears to be some kind of common sitting room.  It might be worth investigating further or you might just continue onward and forget that room altogether.  With nothing more to do here in the hallway, you should move on one way or the other. }{Guiles Mansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
