R {2084}{0}{}{An old, dusty lobby}{<168>O<088>}{   Your lungs wheeze as piles of dust wrack and strain them, your eyes watering and clenched from the stale and rancid air. The walls around you are dark and peeling, half-covered with an ancient wallpaper that was once gaudy and bright, but now is chipped and bleeding its pigment onto the warped wooden floor below.  This is a dark lobby of a near-condemned hotel that is apparently under current rent.  A broken chandelier,  dimmed and yellowed, sprinkles small diamonds of hollow light onto the bleak room.  Couches, red velour loungers that reek from years of mold and mildew are centered around a dark wood- en table that was probably just as dingy new as it is now.  An abandoned and boarded-up desk is nestled into the northwestern wall, and hallways lead all directions except south, where a large double door leads out to the Manhattan streets. }{Whorehouse}{whorehouse}{}{}{1.000}{1}
