R {2136}{0}{}{The end of the hall}{<168>E<088>}{   Before you to the north lie a set of double doors covered in leather and chrome studs.  From beyond these doors the sounds of loud, merciless dance music causes periodic rattling in the hinges.  You get the deep feeling that something very... unfamilylike...is beyond.  In your wonderment at what must lie beyond those doors you almost neglect to notice a set of doors to the east that are almost the exact polar opposite of the leather gateway...these east doors are almost pure white, decorated with gold-leaf wreaths that surround the number 310. The choice is now at hand...at this, the end of the hall, do  you dare to enter and infiltrate the unholiness to the north, or recline in luxury and elegance to the east?  The hall does lead back to the south for those undecided at heart. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
