R {3958}{1024}{}{At the gates of the Bard Guild (w,e)}{ }{The entrance gates to the renowned Bard Guild stand open in front of you.  Beyond them you see a courtyard leading to a large stone tower, where brightly colored flags flap briskly on the ramparts.  Loud shouts of laughter and strains of music drift down through the open air.  On the left outer wall next to the gate pillars, a proclamation has been tacked up which you may wish to read.  To the right of the gates, a wooden message board has been staked into the grass allowing visitors from Wayhaven to leave missives for bard friends. }{Bard}{bards}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3957}{e}{e}{2}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3959}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3959}{0}{}{Center Courtyard (n,s,w,e)}{ }{Sunshine beats down on your head as you stroll through the giant flagstone courtyard.  The centerpiece of the courtyard is a marble sculptured fountain carved in the shape of a harp.  Surrounding the fountain, darker flagstones radiate outward in a cross, creating paths that lead west to the tower proper, or north and south to arched openings in the courtyard wall.  On the lighter flagstones around the path, occasional benches and planters blooming with flowers allow visitors to sit back and enjoy the outdoors.  The entrance gates to the east lead out to the Garden District of Wayhaven. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3958}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3960}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3974}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22091}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3960}{0}{}{Southern Garden Entrance (sw,n)}{ }{You stand on the threshold of an arch that separates the Garden of the Poets from the courtyard of the guild tower.  A wide flowerbed abutting the tower is filled with pruned well-kept rose bushes of various sizes and colors.  The wild colors extend out of sight around the curve of the tower wall.  Running alongside the garden is a quaint cobblestone path.  It separates the roses from a wide green lawn that stretches right up to the outer tower wall.  The trimmed grass creates a park-like open expanse under the bright blue sky.  In the center of it a massive oak tree bends its long thick branches down in graceful curves.  It is easy to imagine someone spreading a picnic blanket beneath its protective canopy.  Near you beside the path, a large stone statue presides silently over the surroundings. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3959}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3961}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3961}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (sw,ne)}{ }{Further down the cobblestone path, you come to a large gold plaque mounted on an angled stone block set in the neatly manicured lawn.  A flowering slender olive tree nearby sways gently in the wind, its shadow playing over the surface of the plaque.  The breeze sets loose small petals that curl and dip lazily about before coming to rest on the surrounding grass.  A quick glance at the plaque shows a list of names, perhaps a memorial of some kind.  Against the tower wall, the flower garden displays a wide array of dahlias of impressive size with the rich glowing colors that only dahlias can achieve. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3960}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3962}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3962}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (w,ne)}{ }{The walkway continues around the tower grounds, and as you round the corner you find a pleasant array of berried plants.  Saint John's wort lines the front with light green delicate speckled leaves and red and black berries.  For groundcover you recognize thin tendrils of blackberries native to the more northern regions.  Further back, attractive salmonberry bushes add a splash of melon color, but also make it apparent that not everything beautiful here is edible.  On the lawn side of the garden a holly bush sprouts thick waxy healthy-looking leaves and bright red berry clusters. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3961}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3963}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3963}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (w,e)}{ }{On the lawn side of the garden, a smaller path leads off of the main path to the south and loops around a man-made reflective pond.  A nice diversionary stroll, the pond almost perfectly captures the blue sky and fleecy clouds above, save for the occasional ripple that spreads across the surface when a breeze gusts through.  There is a slight bubbling at one end of pool that suggests it is fed by an underground water source that keeps the water fresh and clear.  In the center it is graced by the figure of a woman on a pedestal.  On the far edge of the pond, a weeping willow dips its long thin branches down to the water. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3962}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3964}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3964}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (nw,e)}{ }{With a loud crunch your boot heel crushes a round nut underfoot.  The walkway is littered with fallen hazelnuts from a tree bordering the path.  The rest of the area, however, is spotless.  The lawn has closely-cropped grass, and the flowerbeds are perfectly pruned.  Their intermingled abundant fragrant scents waft gently over to you.  How odd to have such a carefully tended garden yet such an atrociously messy path. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3963}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3965}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3965}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (nw,se)}{ }{The colors in the garden are very cool and refreshing.  The deep purple of violets mingle with the lighter blues of irises.  Bluebells wave delicately in the breeze, and tall white carnations sway in time with them like the gentle swell of white-capped oceans.  They form a perfect complement to the pale blue sky and its wispy tufts of white clouds.  On the wide green lawn on the other side of the path, a laurel tree spreads its leafy branches. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3964}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3966}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3966}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (n,se)}{ }{In contrast to the wild creative patterns of the rest of the garden this section is noticeably structured in comparison.  Perfectly squared bushes and carefully pruned plants form convoluted geometric shapes.  There are wild foxgloves and other tall leafy fronds in the centerpiece, and around that are rows forming alternating concentric circles and squares, with a large triangle overlaying the entire design.  It is all completely constructed out of plants and gravel beds without the aid of dividers or supports.  On the other side of the path, a pine tree grows on the lawn.  Its long shadow falls across the grass and barely brushes against the statue of a tall man in scholarly robes. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3965}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3967}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3967}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (n,s)}{ }{There is a fresh minty smell in the air.  In the garden, various fragrant bushes are growing in abundance.  A bumblebee dips and hovers around the flowering tips of a large mint plant.  Next to it is a thick rosemary bush with spiky branches, and a smaller thyme bush with little round yellow-tipped leaves.  There are also smaller herbs like a light green sage plant, and thin stalks of chives with round purple blossoms on top.  A eucalyptus tree spreads its tall smooth branches up to the sky on the other side of the path. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3966}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3968}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3968}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (ne,s)}{ }{The gardenbed along this side of the tower is a field of golden colors.  Along the back row, tall sunflowers graciously dip their heavy heads.  Closer up front, chrysanthemums, marigolds, and other flowers create a field of yellows and oranges.  The sunlight reflecting off their bright surfaces makes the entire garden glow.  In contrast, the lawn across the path is a cool uniform green.   Although, in the branches of a maple tree nearby you spot the darting yellow form of a goldfinch. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3967}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3969}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3969}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (ne,sw)}{ }{Following the path around the tower, you come to a giant elm tree with an elegant spread of branches.  Shadows of dancing leaves sway daintily back and forth on the surface of the path and you can hear the leaves rustling and sighing in the tree overhead.  The cool shade under the tree encourages you to linger for a while.  You could lie under the branches and look skyward at the bits of blue peeking through the leaves, or you might sit with your back against the tree and take in the blooming gardens next to the guild tower. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3968}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3970}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3970}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (e,sw)}{ }{This area of the garden has been recently cultivated.  A young apple tree growing next to the path has a few ripe red delicious apples dangling temptingly over the pathway.  Likewise, the flowerbeds along the tower wall have young seedlings, many of the shoots still too tender to be able to determine their species.  You can see from their arrangement that when they bloom they will form the shape of a harp.  It is apparent from this new project that the garden is in a constant state of evolution and change. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3969}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3971}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3971}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (e,w)}{ }{As you curve around the north side of the tower, a pleasant gurgling reaches your ears.  Here, a little brook burbling up from an underground source cuts across the lawn for some distance.  It is spanned by a wooden bridge that lets you cross from the cobblestone path to the lawn on the other side of the creek.  Just beyond the bridge, two figures are preserved in stone in a loving embrace in the shade of a cherry tree.  On the guild side of the bridge, the flowerbeds next to the tower wall sport rows of bright red roses of varying hues.  A cool breeze rises off the water and fans your cheek. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3970}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3972}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3972}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (se,w)}{ }{The wind rustles lazily through an old yew tree alongside the path.  This section of the garden is comprised of various flowering bushes, which create a predominant swath of green punctuated by occasional bits of bright color against the tower wall.  Small azalea bushes, medium-sized hibiscuses, and larger rhododendrons are some of the more recognizable species.  Other generic leafy topiaries are sculpted into miniature lawn creatures that run underfoot. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3971}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3973}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3973}{0}{}{Garden of the Poets (se,nw)}{ }{As you wander along the path, you come to a large silver plaque mounted on an angled stone block set in the neatly manicured lawn.  It rests in the protective shadow of a giant sycamore that reaches its wide-leafed branches up to the blue sky above.  A quick glance shows a list of names, perhaps a memorial of some kind.  Against the tower wall, a flower garden blooms with fresh smells that tickle your nose.  The lush green lawn on your other side invites you to take off your shoes and wiggle your toes in the cool dank grass. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3972}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3974}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3974}{0}{}{Northern Garden Entrance (nw,s)}{ }{The sky is a pale blue expanse that covers the world overhead, dotted with faint smeared tufts of white clouds left like dust trails after a jalopy on a dusty road.  You stand just outside an arch that separates the Garden of the Poets from the courtyard of the guild tower.  In a wide ring encircling the base of the tower is a neatly pruned flowerbed filled with various species of colorful flowers.  A cobblestone path runs alongside it for visitors to stroll on and admire the surroundings.  The path divides the flowers from an immaculate spacious green lawn that runs right up to the edge of the outer tower wall.  On the lawn, a stone bench provides a shady spot to rest under an ash tree.  It faces an imposing white stone statue beside the path. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3973}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3959}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3975}{0}{<278>}{-= Garden Way =- (n,s,enter)}{<238> E <088>}{You are on Gardenway road, which leads north towards Everlynd Park, and  south towards Arcadia Boulevard. This section of town is remarkably clean, and the buildings you see tell you very few paupers live in this area.  To the west you see a tall wrought-iron fence, with an open pair of heavy oaken gates to allow carriages to access the estate property. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3957}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3976}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3977}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3976}{0}{<278>}{-= Garden Way =- (s,w,e)}{<278>-+-<088>}{You travel along Gardenway road, which leads south towards Arcadia Boulevard.  This section of town is remarkably clean, and the buildings you see tell you that very few paupers live in this area of Wayhaven.  The pleasant-looking Roseway road leads west into the Garden District and Park Avenue extends east from here.  The white marble wall of Everlynd Park runs along the north of the road. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3975}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3979}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {4065}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3977}{0}{}{-= Hackaway Estate =- (s,leave)}{ }{Standing just inside the wrought-iron fence, you look south to see a mansion and gape like a tourist at the evident wealth of its owner.  A full city block deep, the curved carriage way is lined by oaks and to the south the tudor mansion sits in a cultured field of small wild flowers.  While it is unclear who the owners of this elegant manse are, the name 'Hackaway Estate' in combination with the apparent lack of concern for security suggests to you that the owner assumes his reputation for swift and sharp conflict is sufficient to keep snoops like you away. }{Houses of the Rich}{houses_of_the_rich}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3975}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3978}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3978}{0}{}{-= Hackaway Estate =- (n)}{ }{In the courtyard before the stately mansion you look to the north and admire the field of so-called wildflowers.  You worry about the pit bulls you saw mentioned on the fence though. }{Houses of the Rich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3977}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3979}{0}{<278>}{-= Roseway Road =- (n,w,e)}{<278>-+-<088>}{Roseway Road leads east and west here through the Garden District of the City of Wayhaven. This section of town seems to be populated by the richer citizens, as the streets are free of trash and the buildings are all clean. The road intersects Gardenway Boulevard to the east, and to the north lies the beautiful marble entrance to Everlynd Park. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3976}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3980}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
