R {3983}{0}{<238>}{Wayhaven Theatre (out,enter)}{<238>[<138>E<238>]<088>}{This is the infamous Wayhaven Theatre.  The finest plays and operas are performed here nightly.  Only Wayhaven's most prestigious citizens can attend these performances.  The building was painstakingly constructed of the most expensive stone.  Exquisite marble columns, embedded with golden swirls, stand on either side of the heavy wood doors.  A sign announcing tonight's performance hangs over the entrance. }{Bell Tower}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3981}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3989}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3984}{0}{}{-= Taxmore Estate =- (leave,s)}{ }{Standing just inside the moon archway, you look south to the mansion and you are in awe at the flagrant display of wealth. A full city block deep, the stately carriage way is lined with ancient horn-beams and to the south the mansion sits in a perfect lawn.  While it is unclear who the owners of the place are, the name 'Taxmore Estate' suggests that perhaps some of your own hard-earned coin went into building this place. }{Houses of the Rich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3980}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3985}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3985}{0}{}{-= Taxmore Estates =- (n)}{ }{At the front door of the mansion you look north at the grounds and you marvel at their beauty.  The way the stately horn-beams line the long lane, the perfect lawns ... Everything is just breathtakingly beautiful.  The building before you is no slouch either. }{Houses of the Rich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3984}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3986}{0}{}{-= Stolenaway Estate =- (leave,e)}{ }{Standing just inside the archway, you look south across the property and you are struck dumb by the size of this estate. Whoever owns this place invented the word 'flaunt'.  A full city block deep, the circular carriage way extends off to the east, and through the carefully copsed hardwoods you catch a glimpse of what can only be described as a mansion.  It is not clear who owns this estate but from the name 'Stolenaway Estate' you can only guess that it might belong to someone high up the criminal hierarchy. }{Houses of the Rich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3982}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3987}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3987}{0}{}{-= Stolenaway Estate =- (leave,w,s)}{ }{Standing just inside the archway, you look south across the property and you are in awe that this much money could even exist.  A full city block deep, the circular carriage way extends off to the west, and is lined with carefully pruned hardwoods.  To the south the mansion rises out of a perfect lawn, and looks big enough to house an army.  It is not clear who owns this estate but from the name 'Stolenaway Estate' you can only guess that it might belong to someone high up the criminal hierarchy (or for that matter a bureaucrat). }{Houses of the Rich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3986}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3988}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3981}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3988}{513}{<088>}{-= Stolenaway Estate =- (n)}{ }{You are on the carriage way just in front of the mansion. As you look north you can see the perimeter walls of the estate through the hardwoods. }{Houses of the Rich}{}{}{}{1000.000}{1}
E {3987}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15803}{enter mirror}{enter mirror}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {3989}{0}{}{Inside a Theatre (out)}{ }{You marvel at the beauty of this building.  Red velvet covered chairs span the width of the theatre.  A polished wood stage lies in front of you.  Heavy wool curtains hang effortlessly from the ceiling rafters.  Backstage, you catch a glimpse of some the exquisite costumes used in the different productions.  Large crystal chandeliers dangle in the air. }{Bell Tower}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3981}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

