R {4344}{0}{<238>}{A disused forest path (se,w)}{<238>. .<088>}{The branches of the rotting gnarled trees have matted and tangled together overhead forming an impenetrable canopy, of rotting mildew ridden branches. Rotting leaves cover this portion of the path deadening the sound of your footsteps. The forest is deathly quiet here, almost as if it were holding its breath, waiting for something to happen. Just a little further to the west you can see some kind of clearing. }{Abbey}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4343}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {4345}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {4345}{0}{}{A forest clearing (n,w,e)}{<030>G<088>}{Here in the center of this clearing 3 tracks meet forming a small crossroads. From the east you can barely make out a faint golden light shining out the darkness of the forest. Whilst openings in the forest to the North and West mark the entrance points of the forest tracks. Resting at a crooked angle is an ancient and weatherbeaten signpost. Resting just behind it, is an ancient oak tree, now quite dead its branches devoid of leaves. Hanging from the lower branches is an iron wrought gibbet that creaks slowly in the wind that occasionally gusts through this deserted clearing. }{Abbey}{gareth}{}{}{1.000}{1}
