R {4402}{0}{}{Exhibit Room (ne,w)}{ }{This room contains many wonders. Displays hold mounted skeletons and fossils of extinct creatures, fluorescent rocks and chemicals rest on shelves housing insects pinned to boards, strange creatures preserved by the arcane art of taxidermy, and electrical devices of uncertain function and origin - all covered by a thick layer of dust. Glass jars hold samples of human and animal organs preserved in alcohol - hearts, livers, kidneys, and even brains. Some of the jars are attached to devices that send a spark through the liquid, making their contents twitch and convulse. Some other jars are cracked, their preservatives have oozed away, and their contents putrefied in a rotten heap on the floor. The room reeks of pure decay. }{Mordenheim's Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45152}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45154}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {4403}{0}{}{Grand Balcony (w,sw)}{ }{This walkway connects the sitting room with the exibit room, and offers a breathtaking view of the Sea of Sorrows. The railing of the balcony appears to be rotted. This is the eastern end of the balcony, the rest is to the west, and you can enter the house to the southwest. }{Mordenheim's Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
