R {4583}{0}{<238>}{Blood Of the Vine Inn (s,e)}{<238>[P]<088>}{The Blood of the Vine Inn This is the restaurant of Barovia.  The room is strangely silent, but does have an upbeat feel to it.  There are only a few other people here eating.  They don't seem to notice you, but you can sense their fear. There is a light coming from the east and you hear people talking. }{Barovia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4582}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {4584}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {4584}{0}{<238>}{The Blood of the Vine Tavern (w)}{<238>[P]<088>}{You are in the Blood of the Vine Tavern. There is a blazing fire in the hearth giving warmth to an otherwise cold and empty town.  There are only a handful of customers enjoying the pub.  The rest are who-knows-where.  The proprieter of the place is Arik.  He is a kind soul who has seen much in life, too much. The menu is posted behind the bar:  _*________________________*___**______ (*_*________________________*_*__*_____) *|  *                        *    *  *| *|   *THE BLOOD OF THE VINE TAVERN * *|  |  *                               * |  | *        spring water : 400 coins *|  |*       Arik's special : 70 coins  *|  * Barovian firebreather : 210 coins  |  * elixir of restoration : 3000 coins |  |*___________________________________| (__*___________________________________) }{Barovia}{}{}{pub}{1.000}{1}
E {4583}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {4585}{0}{<278>}{street (n,s,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{You continue along the cobblestone street.  Your footfalls echo in the empty street.  Along side of the road are two houses, one to the north and one to the south.  From the northern house you can hear a horse neighing faintly, it must be a stable.  The sky  is still black as night and you shiver from the chill wind blowing. To the east is more of the town and to the west you can see a large house and what looks like a church in the distance. }{Barovia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4582}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
