R {4600}{0}{<278>}{road (sw,n)}{<278>- -<088>}{The road continues on through the forest.  On either side of you, you can see the woods loom out of the darkness.  The towering tops of the trees are lost in a heavy gray mist.  The muddy roadway is damp to the touch and you see many wagon ruts dug into it.  The ruts look rather old and you can tell that this road has not been used in a long time.  You can see some animal tracks on the side of the road and wonder what made them. The road continues on its course as far as the eye can see. }{Ravenloft}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4599}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45539}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {4601}{0}{<268>}{church courtyard (n,e)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{You are standing in a small courtyard south of a church.  The ground is very moist here and you can see dew forming on the plants here in the garden.  The church itself is a small place with many holy symbols painted on the doors and windows.  The door to the church is wide open, as it always is and you see light on the inside.  You feel somewhat safe here and wish to go into the church to see what's happening. }{Barovia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4599}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {4602}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {4602}{0}{<268>}{church (s,w)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{The inside of the church is about 50' wide by 120' long.  Around you, there are pews for the congregation.  Many of them are smashed and clawed.  Looking up, you see small holes in the roof.  The old rafters strain feebly to keep the whole place from crashing inward. At the altar, praying, you see a tall man in a white robe.  He looks at you with a warm smile.  Off to the west you see a small entryway. }{Barovia}{ravenloft_donavich}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4601}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {4603}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30002}{kneel}{kneel}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30002}{n}{kneel}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {4603}{0}{<248>}{cemetery (nw,e)}{<248>. <178>+<088>}{This is the cemetery of Barovia, though it has not been used for decades.  Barovians no longer bury their dead for fear of them becoming something worse than death.  Cremation is now practiced. You feel a numbing cold here as if it were winter.  You know the chill is coming from beyond the grave.  In the ground are old crosses and tombstones marking the graves of Barovian ancestors.  The moon shines down on the graveyard and you think you see something moving. As you look west, you see a castle, dark and forboding high on a cliff. }{Barovia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4602}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {4604}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {4604}{0}{<228>}{Forest clearing (se)}{<228>, `<088>}{You stand in a small clearing far northwest from the graveyard. There is a small campfire here, barely holding back the gloom that emanates from the dark trees.  You sense that you are not alone. }{Barovia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4603}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

