R {5795}{0}{}{holodeck (n,turbolift)}{ }{The main holodeck on board the starship Enterprise. The holodecks have been rather barren lately due to the restrictions placed on their use by captain Picard.  It seems that too many members of the crew have been abusing the battle simulation program by wagering on it.  This has limited its use by the crew considerably.  However, you are not part of the crew, so you are not restricted by such an order. }{USS Enterprise (TNG)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5796}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1568}{turbolift}{turbolift}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1567}{place hand on plate}{place hand on plate}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5796}{0}{}{holodeck controls (holodeck2,s,holodeck1)}{ }{U.S.S. Enterprise holodeck controls. The holodeck is a miracle of technology as it can simulate any event you want as though it was real.  Right now, the program compiled in the holodeck subprocessors is a simulated starship battle between the U.S.S. Enterprise and the Romulan warship, the Kuhl Manar.  Officers use this program to help prepare them in the event of an attack.  Lately, however, the more 'liberal' of them have taken to wagering on the outcome, turning it more into a game.  If you would like to try your luck against another player, read the panel and follow the instructions. }{Starship Battle (sim)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5795}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5797}{holodeck2}{holodeck2}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5798}{holodeck1}{holodeck1}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5797}{0}{}{main bridge (out)}{ }{This is the main bridge of the Kuhl Manar. Lights and touchpads surround you as you assume full command of the ship with an able-body crew to command. The vessel is a galaxy-class starship capable of long voyages into outer space.  The ship has a heavy arsenal at its disposal and is designed to be warship. Above all that though, the starship is designed to be a pinnacle of engineering technology, a flagship in the Romulan armada.  There is a panel next to the captain's chair with a list of commands. }{Starship Battle (sim)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5796}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5798}{0}{}{main bridge (out)}{ }{This is the main bridge of the U.S.S Enterprise. Lights and touchpads surround you as you assume full command of the ship with an able-body crew to command. The vessel is a galaxy-class starship capable of long voyages into outer space.  The ship has a heavy arsenal at its disposal and is designed to be warship. Above all that though, the starship is designed to be a pinnacle of engineering technology, a flagship in the Starfleet armada.  There is a panel next to the captain's chair with a list of commands. }{Starship Battle (sim)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5796}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5799}{0}{}{Turbolift (out)}{ }{This is the main turbolift on board the USS Enterprise.  The capsule-like compartment is more or less a futuristic type of elevator.  No hands are needed for the turbolift as it works by simply alerting the computer to your request by saying the destination.  The destination can be any area of the ship accessible by your present clearance (bridge, holodeck, and most any others you can think of).  You may also ask the computer to halt the turbolift, or resume course, at any time. }{USS Enterprise (TNG)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
