R {5845}{0}{<268>}{Standing in a church narthex (out,n)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{Standing just next to the sturdy oak door, you look out over one of the most beautiful decorated narthex you've ever seen. The floor is made out of white, almost crystal clear marble and it continues all the way through the nave of the church. Looking northward you see that the floor changes colour to a richer sandy-yellow tone by the chancel. Several handmade candle holders stand next to the doors and the smell of freshly lit candles lies heavily in the air. The church is currently empty but apparently it is always open for worshippers.  }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{westersea_church}{}{}{1.000}{1}
