R {5846}{0}{<268>}{Standing in a church nave (e,w,n,s)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{You're standing in the middle of the nave. Several rows of wooden benches occupy this area and they are as beautifully carved as every other piece of furniture in here. Several large colourful windows have been mounted in both the eastern and western wall causing a radiant display of colours to sparkle over the pale marble. High above you is the vaulted ceiling and you spot several adorned roof beams. Two rows of lit candles are directly to the east and west of the benches, forming a very beautiful wall which separates the centre area from the rest of the church. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
