R {5850}{0}{<248>}{Standing in a church chancel (s)}{<248>.<118>@<248>.<088>}{You've reached what might very well be the most beautifully decorated chancel you've ever seen. Standing just three steps above the centre nave you have an extremely good view over the entire church hall. The floor is made out of the finest sandy coloured marble and its clear surface causes the daylight to reflect into a cascade of glowing light. Along the northern wall are several smaller benches and standing in the northeastern corner is a small desk. A small wooden podium has been mounted up front, allowing the minister to be clearly visible during service. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{westersea_alister}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5846}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
