R {5852}{0}{}{On a small church walkway (d,e)}{ }{The second floor consists mainly of a small walkway in an eastern to western direction. There are not nearly as many decorations here but it still looks quite pleasant. The floor is made from wooden boards which have been sanded down to perfection. A ladder leads down through a small opening in the southwestern corner of the room. Looking through it you realize that it must lead to the lower level of the church. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5851}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5853}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5853}{0}{}{On a small church walkway (e,w)}{ }{The small walkway continues in a eastern to western direction. Not a single person is in sight and you'd guess few ever come up here. The lighting up here is dim but you can still see fairly clearly. Not detecting any light source you can't help but wonder how this is possible. As you turn eastward a whiff of fresh air hits your face from somewhere close. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5852}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5854}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5854}{0}{}{On a small church walkway (u,w)}{ }{You're at the eastern corner of the small walkway. A slim ladder leads up through a hatch in the ceiling and you feel a very clear draft coming from above. The walls and floor remain the same as the rest of the walkway. There are a few decorations here and there but nothing as elaborate as what you saw in the centre nave. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5853}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5855}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5855}{0}{}{In the middle of a church tower (u,d)}{ }{The small ladder leads onward in an upward and downward direction. You feel fresh air coming from all around and glancing up, you see daylight. The ladder itself is made from fine iron and shows few signs of rust or other types of decay. Looking around, you notice that the walls are made from wooden boards, and look from the inside very different than the rest of the church. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5854}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5856}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5856}{0}{}{In a belfry (d)}{ }{You're standing in the belfry. It's constructed out of a wooden platform with a small wooden railing attached to it. A dome shaped ceiling stretches high above you and as you look up you see several beautifully carved wooden beams. The bell itself hangs down on an extremely thick and sturdy looking rope. It's connected by a pulley system which is mounted high beyond your reach. There is a large cord that hangs down next to the actual bell. As you look around you marvel at the incredible view you have up here over the entire city. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5855}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5857}{0}{<278>}{On a metal stairway (d,u)}{<278>.@.<088>}{The stairway winds its way down into the deeper part of the church. Colourful daylight trickles in from the opening above and looking up you can see parts of the inner chancel. Looking down, the only thing you see is darkness and an occasional lantern mounted to the stone wall. The stairway itself is made out of the finest steel and appears rather sturdy. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5850}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5858}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5858}{0}{<278>}{On a metal stairway (d,u)}{<278>.@.<088>}{The metallic steps gleam in the yellow lantern light. You've climbed a fair amount of them and are somewhere between the bottom and the top level of the church. Dark stone walls surround you on all sides. As you reach out and run your hand along one of them you can't help but marvel how extremely finely polished they are. You can't detect a single crevice or protruding piece of stone anywhere. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5857}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5859}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5859}{0}{<278>}{On a metal stairway (u,d)}{<278>.@.<088>}{You are standing on the lower part of the staircase. Below you, you can see stone floor and a passageway that continues off in a northern direction. Glancing up, you see nothing but darkness and an occasional lit lantern. Running your hand along the fine steel railing you continue on your way. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5858}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5860}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5860}{0}{<278>}{In a dark catacomb (n,u)}{<278>.@.<088>}{The catacomb tunnel is fairly narrow. You can move around in it without any problem but that's about it. The tunnel itself seems to have been cut directly from the rocky ground, however it's been polished down to an almost completely smooth surface. Several lanterns have been mounted to the stone walls providing ample light for anyone who is down here. As you look around, you notice that the tunnel slopes downward in a northern direction. There is also a staircase here leading upwards back to the surface.   }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5859}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5861}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5861}{0}{<238>}{In a dark catacomb (n,s)}{<238>] [<088>}{The stone tunnel continues onward into the darkness. There are some lanterns mounted on the rocky walls but their light isn't strong enough for you to see what lies ahead in either direction. In each wall are several oblong compartments and you notice that there are small golden plaques hanging next to them. The tunnel continues to slope downward in a direct northern direction. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5860}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5862}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5862}{0}{<238>}{In a dark catacomb (n,s)}{<238>] [<088>}{Even though you are several meters underground you are not cold or even chilly by any means. Something keeps you warm but there are no obvious signs of what. The stone tunnel keeps on going in a straight northern to southern direction and shows no hints of changing. More compartments, all the same size dot each wall and golden signs hang next to each.  }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5861}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5863}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5863}{0}{<238>}{In a dark catacomb (n,s)}{<238>] [<088>}{The flickering lights coming from the many lanterns are starting to play tricks on your eyes. Shadows dart and dance against the dark stone walls. You think you catch a movement behind you but as you turn around you see nothing. Small square compartments have been cut into each wall and you see small labels next to each one. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5862}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5864}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {5864}{0}{<108>}{At a dark tunnel fork (w,e,n,s)}{<108>[ ]<088>}{This is the first fork in the stony tunnel that you've encountered down here. Small pitch-black tunnels lead off in an eastern to western direction, while the larger main tunnel continues northward. There are no lanterns or any other sources of light here; however with the smooth tunnel floor you're not that worried about tripping and falling. }{The City of Westersea (Church)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5863}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
