R {5897}{0}{<238>}{Under a stone bridge (u,nw)}{<238>===<088>}{You're swimming in the southeastern corner of the canal. The water is filtered through a large metal grate mounted on the southern wall and probably leads off to be recycled somewhere. The narrow stone walls surround you to the east, west and to the south. Directly above is the bottom of an elevated stone bridge. There are small handles mounted directly on the eastern wall, allowing you to climb out should you want to. The canal continues off in a northwestern direction. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
