R {6218}{0}{}{The Hall of Orders (se,sw,ne,nw,u,d)}{ }{You are in a new room in the castle that has been constructed for the members of the guild's nine orders.  The walls of this room have been carved from the bedrock and now are decorated with tapestries representing the orders.  In each of the five prime directions there lies a room dedicated to a specific order within the guild.  To the northeast lies the Order of the Lance, the Order of the Shield is to the southwest, to the northwest lies the Order of the Argent Sword, to the southeast lies the Order of the Knights errant, and the Order of the Crown Knights is down from here.  A stone staircase spirals up and leads to the rest of the castle. }{Knights}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1988}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6219}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6219}{0}{}{The Order of the Lance (sw)}{ }{Fortress of the Knights of the Lance- You are standing just inside the Stronghold of the Knights of the Lance. The area around the large, brass-bound double doors serves as an antechamber. Numerous large plants sit in the glow of magically-provided sunlight, suffusing the area with their soothing scent and gentle light. Along the wall to your right are a number of wooden man-sized frames. Several esquires wait here, ready to help assist you out of your armour. As the room opens up, you realize this is actually a vast complex, supported throughout by enormous pillars, carved in the shapes of lances. Directly opposite the doors, two rows of tall candelabras provide a long corridor reaching to the far wall. There sits a display case of crystal and gold, wherein rests a curious artifact: a broken lance. Looming behind the display is a tremendous statue, the last of Stardust's great works. Between the candelabras nearest the case starts a progression of giant pennons. Only a few now are present, leaving one to speculate that there is plenty of room for more. Along the east wall you detect tables and chairs sitting before a long counter with a glass case. Movement can be seen in the area as various attendants wait to perform their duty. To the west lay areas for relaxation and talk. Covering the western wall are strategic maps of the Kingdoms, of both lands known and legendary. The shadowy corners hide recesses containing further facilities. }{Knights}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6218}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6220}{0}{}{Entrance Building to Pinnacle (jump)}{ }{		Login Room You are standing in an enormous enclosed chamber.  A single iron door sits in the floor of this structure surrounded by a granite doorframe. The ceiling is a dome completely covering the building.  People seem to appear here from nowhere, perhaps from another dimension, some call it 'reality'. }{Pinnacle}{login}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1}{jump}{jump}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6221}{0}{}{The Beginning of Infinity (u,d)}{ }{You are standing above a long, swirling hallway of great promise.  Unexplainable barriers block your passage in most directions though you stand at the precipice of greatness. }{Pinnacle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
