R {6396}{0}{<228>}{Neutral Dragon Realms (s,w,e)}{<228>, `<088>}{You stop in your tracks and stare in wonder at the cavern you have stumbled into. In the center sits a huge pool of lava, and it is surrounded by dozens of large dragons. The dragons are apparently basking in the heat. The lava is bubbling and spurting molten rock high into the air. The ceiling of the cavern is hundreds of feet in the air and opens out to blue sky at the very top. The steam and heat distortion obscures anything that might be across the pool to the north-east. It looks to be a solid wall however. The dragons seem  to have little interest in each other. You are still in the shadows and haven't attracted any attention yet. You might still be able to avoid detection if you retreat back the way you came. There is also a small passage to the west that offers a quick retreat. }{Neutral Dragon Realms}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6395}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6397}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
