R {6574}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (n,s)}{ }{You are now in a narrow hallway that leads to the north and the main part of the castle.  The walls are crumbling with age, and the floor is covered in rubble. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6558}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6575}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6575}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (e,w,s)}{ }{You are now near the heart of the castle.  Perhaps once a dining room, this room is now in shambles.  There is a large table at the center of the room with a shattered chandelier lying on top of it.  The walls are crumbling and a light cloud of dust floats in the air. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6574}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6576}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6577}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6576}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (w)}{ }{This room most likely acted as a kitchen for the castle.  The food preparation area for the complex is a very long room with a variety of details.  At the southwest corner of the room are two cooking pits, each large enough to cook an animal as large as a deer.  Long tables line each wall, and there are scattered containers on them, some upturned.  There are spoiled pieces of food all around, and the smell in the room is very uninviting. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6575}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6577}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (e,n)}{ }{This room appears as if it was used at one point for before and after-dinner activity.  Drinking was probably the most popular pasttime here, for there are several broken earthenware tankard mugs smashed on the ground below a row of hooks on the wall. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6575}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6578}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6578}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (s,nw)}{ }{At the center of this room is a large carved statue, full-size, of a nude human female, beckoning with arms out front in a very alluring pose.  The walls of this room, like the others you have been in, are crumbling. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6577}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6579}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6579}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (se,e,n)}{K}{Although the walls of this room are the same as elsewhere, the floor of this room is covered with ceramic tiles arranged in mosaic fashion.  Arrayed throughout the room are fourteen different pools. }{Zelligar's Castle}{zellkey}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6578}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6580}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6583}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6580}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (e,w,n)}{ }{The stronghold's trophy room consists of an assortment of various curiosities accumulated over the years.  Unfortunately most of the collectibles have long since been destroyed. At the west end of the room is a basilisk frozen in stone.  On the east wall is a dwarven skeleton, suspended from a pair of irons near the ceiling giving the entire chamber a macabre presence.  Elsewhere on the walls are a variety of mementos. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6579}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6581}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6584}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6581}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (w,s)}{ }{The hallway comes to an end here with a large open doorway to the south.  Through the doorway you can make out several bunks and beds lining the walls. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6580}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6582}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6582}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (n)}{ }{This large, open room was once the dwelling place for the guards and men-at-arms of the stronghold.  Scattered throughout the room are about forty common beds, and about half that number of chairs and stools.  There are several large wooden tables along various walls, and at the south wall is a large wooden chest of drawers. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6581}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6583}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (s,e)}{ }{The floor of the room is covered with dust, but beneath is a beautiful and shiny surface of polished red granite.  The stone is inlaid in large blocks and extends uniformly to within a foot of each of the walls.  In the very center of the room within the floor surface are blocks of white granite within the red stone.  There are three large oaken tables within the room, one in each of the west, north and east wings of the room.  There are several wooden chairs scattered about.  Wall sconces designed to hold torches for illumination are mounted on the walls all around the room.  The library is rather modestly supplied with books, volumes, and tomes of various sizes. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6579}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6584}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6584}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (e,w,s,n)}{ }{Once the showplace of the entire castle, the garden has, over the passage of time become a botanical nightmare.  With no one to tend the gardens, the molds and fungi have grown out of control. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6583}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6585}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6580}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6621}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6585}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (e,w,n)}{ }{You are now standing at the very center of Zelligar's Castle.  It seems the ravages of time (and perhaps other contributors) have been particularly devastating to this section of the castle, as the entire ceiling has caved in leaving large piles of rubble on the ground and exposing the castle to the natural elements.  The floor here is particularly damp, perhaps from a recent drizzle. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6584}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6586}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
