R {6650}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (w,e)}{ }{This seems to be one of the only places in the castle that is well kept.  You stand in a small study, perhaps where Zelligar does most of his reading and research.  There is a small wooden desk in the corner with several books on it, and the south and north walls both have large book shelves.  There is a soft satin chair in the southeast corner of the room with a small light beside it. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6649}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6651}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6651}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (w,n)}{ }{This is a small hallway that connects Zelligar's study and his bedroom.  To the north you can see perhaps the most luxurious room in the castle.  Back to the west is Zelligar's study. }{Zelligar's Castle}{zelldoor}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6650}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6652}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6652}{0}{}{Zelligar's Castle (s)}{Z}{This is the master bedroom of the Castle.  The room is quite large and extravagant, with an elevated semi-circle at the back of the room on which the king-sized bed rests.  Long purple drapes cover the two large windows on the sides of the room.  There is a small dresser on the wall with a full length mirror beside it.  There are a few books that look as if they have been discarded, tossed in disgust to the side of the room. }{Zelligar's Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6651}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

