R {6677}{0}{}{Interview Room (s)}{ }{Untainted by personal touches or frivolous decoration, this is a room designed purely for business. Centered in the middle is a long boardroom style table, which is encircled by evenly spaced chairs. The walls are washed with a calming blue and are unadorned by distracting ornamentation. }{Pinnacle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6676}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6678}{0}{}{Interguild Discussion Room (n)}{ }{This is the discussion room for the Interguild community. Players selected as qualified administrative representatives for their respective guilds may discuss issues here as well as on the InterGuild chatline.  A soft glow emanates from behind slightly-raised, subtle paintings that are scattered liberally around the walls, illuminating the large, central table surrounded by plush chairs. }{Pinnacle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6676}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6679}{0}{}{Central Council Chamber (u,d,n,s,w,e)}{ }{		Central Council Chamber This is the room where many decisions are made concerning Three Kingdom's future.  Here, players can read and write on the various boards, giving their opinions about upcoming changes and new ideas. Nearly all of Three Kingdoms most prestigious citizens can be seen here at one time or another.  If you're lucky, you might even get to see one of the high wizards aimlessly roaming the halls (probably looking for the bathroom).  Also, this is where you learn about the different guilds available to the players here at 3 Kingdoms.  A large glass case in the center of the room contains each of the prospective guild objects.  There is a large sign here with arrows pointing in various directions. }{Pinnacle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6673}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
