R {6860}{0}{}{Approach to the Blue Stronghold (nw,se)}{ }{  The path here widens to about twenty feet across, and the forest in this area has been cut back an additional twelve feet from the sides of the trail.  To the southeast, a large stronghold rises above the woods, thrusting twin towers over one hundred feet high.  The stone of the stronghold seems to be some sort of glorious blue marble, which glistens in the brilliance of the sun. }{Portal of Life}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6859}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6861}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6861}{0}{}{Blue Stronghold (n,nw)}{ }{Directly to the north stands a magnificent stronghold.  The stones of its construction appear to be hard blue marble, and the lowered drawbridge is made of solid oak.  The way into the keep seems to be clear since the portcullis is  raised. Twin towers thrust high into the sky, and a large flag is flying from one of the towers. }{Portal of Life}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6860}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {6863}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {6862}{0}{}{Entrance Hall (w,e,s,n)}{ }{This is the main entrance hall for the stronghold. Large tapestries hang from the ceilings and passages lead off in each of the cardinal directions.  The floor is made of sturdy granite, and the ceiling appears to be made of some beautiful sparkling stone which you've not seen before. }{Portal of Life}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
