R {7377}{0}{<248>}{A huge chamber (s)}{<248>. <178>+<088>}{The huge chamber you have entered is the tomb of lord Koth himself. The room is enshrouded in darkness, preventing you from seeing the ceiling. An immense black sarcophagus has been placed in the center of the room. On its sides stand two tall braziers. Three tapestries hang on the walls, once magnificent, now decayed with age. The floor is covered with a thick layer of dust that swirls up into the air as you walk towards the center of the chamber. The sarcophagus itself seems to be made of some kind of black stone and radiates pure evil. You get an uneasy feeling as you sense an alien mind touching your own. }{Elven Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7376}{s}{move left brazier;s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7378}{0}{<248>}{A large chamber (e)}{<248>. <178>+<088>}{You step into a large chamber engulfed in darkness. This chamber is the tomb of Kael, son of Lord Koth. In the middle of the room a small sarcophagus has been placed. A thick layer of dust blankets the room. As you move around it swirls in the air making you gasp for breath. The walls are decorated with rotting tapestries that are trying to defy the decay of time. }{Elven Graveyard}{}{}{"speak lava"}{1.000}{1}
E {7376}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7379}{0}{<248>}{A chamber of the dead (w)}{<248>. <178>+<088>}{You step into a large chamber engulfed in darkness. You see a black stone sarcophagus in the center of the room. The walls are decorated with rotting tapestries that once may have been extremely beautiful. The floor lies solid beneath your feet, covered with a thick layer of dust. A small moaning echoes in the chamber as you walk towards the sarcophagus. }{Elven Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7376}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7380}{0}{<108>}{Dark tunnel (u,w)}{<108>[ ]<088>}{As you climb down the hole beneath the pedestal you can feel an intense heat coming from below. As you reach the ground you find yourself standing in a huge cavernous tunnel. The floor and walls are roughly cut from the gray stone. To the west the tunnel stretches onwards into the darkness, and from that direction a low humming can be heard. The air smells of sulfur and excrement and seems to vibrate slightly from the heat. }{Elven Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7376}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
