R {7669}{0}{}{A wind torn mountainside (e)}{ }{You grab hold of a rocky outcropping to prevent being torn from the  mountainside by the gale which ravages it.  A small trail threads  it's way along the mountainside, skirting sheer drops and immense  boulders.  Ice and snow reach down from their perch high above on  the mountain's peak, threatening to crash down and bury you at any  moment. }{Necromancers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7668}{gate}{gate}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7670}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7670}{0}{}{A wind torn mountainside (w,enter)}{E}{You stand at the base of a small tower clinging precariously to  the side of a wind swept peak.  Ice and snow cover the jagged rocks  above you nearer the peak of the mountain, some patches falling to  cover the thread of a trail which winds along the mountainside away  from the tower.  The silvery light of the moon glimmers off the  ice, shining eerily in the night. }{Necromancers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7669}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7671}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7671}{0}{}{The tower's library (s,w)}{ }{You marvel at the numerous shelves of books and scrolls which  occupy the tower.  As you scan the shelves you find tomes on  subjects you've never dreamed of.  All about the tower, seated at  small reading desks, are fellow liches and followers of Joica,  pouring through tomes and scrolls in their search for arcane  knowledge.  You may join them in their efforts or to further your  own power, the collected knowledge of liches for ages will be your  guide.  Simply type 'study <power>'to begin.  <Power> should be the  name of the power you wish to memorize.  Remember though that you  only have a finite number of empty memory globes in which to hold  your powers.  Once filled, you must wait for your phylactery to refresh  its powers before you may memorize more.  You may also add a  number to the end of the study command to make it easier to study  many powers at once.  An example of this would be 'study alarm 5'.  Remember also that your reagents are used to prepare a power when  it's studied, so you must have them now. }{Necromancers}{talia}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7670}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7672}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7672}{0}{}{A chill trophy room (n)}{ }{You've found your way into a small side room in the tower.   You can hear the howling wind tear at the stone walls outside,  a gentle reminder of the icey mountains you've had to cross to  reach this solitary refuge.  Soft lighting spreads over the  room from small glowing orbs hung from the walls, illuminating  the enormous trophy case which wraps around the room. }{Necromancers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7671}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

