R {7852}{0}{<148>}{Riverside (u,w)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{Steps carved from stone rise to the east and into the darkness. The cavern floor is level except for a rather deep puddle that fills a natural depression in the rock. Just to the west this cavern opens to a larger one and a bridge of solid stone spans a small but swiftly flowing underground river. Though difficult to make out in the darkness, it appears that the bridge leads from this opening to a shelf of rock that follows alongside the river on the other side of the cavern. }{Tunnels of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
