R {7856}{0}{<238>}{Shelf (n,w)}{<238>^ ^<088>}{This shelf of rock, several paces in width, acts as a walkway along the west side of the river. Here the cavern's southerly passage ends, but a tunnel has been bored through the rock to the west. To the east the river flows into a passage only large enough to carry the water and disappears from sight. A crumpled mass, once a large water wheel, is wedged into the hole, though the water is flowing through it smoothly. }{Tunnels of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
