R {7858}{0}{<238>}{Tunnel (s,w,e)}{<238>] [<088>}{The tunnel begins a steepening downward slope to the west, descending into stagnant water, which appears to end further along as the passage slopes upward once again. Near the edge of the water, a metal rod is firmly planted into the stone floor, and from it a taut rope extends to the west above the water. Along the southern wall lies an opening to yet another tunnel, though it appears to be markedly different from this one. The most notable differences being the sharp edges of the entrance, and the step up you would have to take to enter, as the opening appears to be misaligned with this passage for some reason. The walls also appear to have dark blemishes, possibly scorch marks, near the opening. }{Tunnels of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
