R {7863}{0}{<238>}{Intersection (n,w,e)}{<238>. .<088>}{Two passages form a tee here. Light filters in from a well-lit area through the passage to the north, and in that direction are what appear to be massive stone gates. Carvings adorn the walls to the east and west, though there is a break here and the southern wall is bare. The east tunnel fades into darkness but you think you can make out a dead end to the west. You notice that the floor is very worn, creating an almost imperceptible depression. }{Tunnels of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
