R {7872}{0}{<178>}{Garden (e)}{<168>*<158>*<138>*<088>}{You have entered an unusual interpretation of a formal garden.  At first glance the garden seems to comprise a multitude of species, but upon closer inspection all of the plants seem to be varieties of self-supporting vines.  The vines twist into shapes that resemble bushes, topiaries, hedges and trees.  Some are even in bloom, with disparate varieties of blossoms throughout the garden.  The brilliant hues jump out from the gray surroundings to beautiful effect. }{Grand Hall of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7871}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7873}{0}{<248>}{Throne (s,w,e)}{<248>.<118>@<248>.<088>}{Before you, at the head of the Grand Hall and upon a dais, lies the throne of the King.  To its right sits a lesser throne in size but of equal craftsmanship.  To its left sits a more diminutive seat, which in another setting might pass for a throne of its own.  Two large torchiers rise just behind and off to the sides of the arrangement, casting a brilliant glow about the area.  The wall behind the throne is covered in royal banners and ornate tapestries.  High above you, the northern pair of pillars cross on their way to the lofty ceiling. }{Grand Hall of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7871}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7874}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7877}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7895}{n}{bribe danar;y;press leaf;n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7874}{0}{<268>}{Hall (n,s,w,e)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The expansive Grand Hall of Rohm Giddor extends around you almost as far as the eye can see.  Six enormous square pillars extend diagonally from the east and west sides of the hall, the three pairs crossing each other before they reach the ceiling far above.  Brilliant orbs of light line the tops and bottoms of the pillars, providing most of the light for the Hall.  You are positioned about dead-center in the Grand Hall.  Though lacking enough clarity to comprehend, voices of distant dwarves echo with unusual volume to this location.  High above you, the center two pillars cross on their way to the lofty ceiling.  To the north is a raised area of the Hall, accessible by a wide stone staircase of about a dozen steps. }{Grand Hall of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7873}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7870}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
