R {7901}{0}{<238>}{Chamber (w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{Impressive neither in size nor grandeur, the chamber of the king is striking in a much more visceral way.  The furniture is built like the king himself, with trunk-like legs holding up the wide and heavy masses. Aside from the necessities, which are primarily made of wood, there is a desk with many drawers that appears to be carved out of stone.  The only amenity is a wrought metal washbasin, above which a steady stream of water keeps it continuously filled. }{Grand Hall of the Rohm Giddor}{temper3}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7900}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7902}{0}{<238>}{Chamber (s)}{<238>] [<088>}{Within the bed chamber of the dwarven queen, wall-mounted torches provide a warm glow while shedding no discernible smoke.  A wide bed, large wardrobe, and two chairs comprise the furniture of the chamber.  While the room is sparsely furnished, each piece is finely crafted and elegant. }{Grand Hall of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7900}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

