E {7989}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7927}{0}{}{The mouth of a tunnel. (se,u)}{ }{You are standing in the mouth of a tunnel which slopes gently into the ground in a southeasterly direction.  There is plenty of activity going on around you, with people carrying logs down into the tunnel and returning with piles of dirt.  The tunnel must still be expanding. The mouth is quite wide, with several piles of logs waiting to be carried down and large mounds of dirt waiting to be carried off. }{Excavation Site}{excavation_site}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7926}{u}{u}{16}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7928}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7928}{0}{}{Inside a tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{Here, not far into the tunnel, you can still see the glow of light from the northwest but already it is beginning to get much dimmer.  You can hear muffled sounds drifting up from further down the tunnel, but find it impossible to judge distance in the confined space. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7927}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7929}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7929}{0}{}{Inside a tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{Continuing your way into the tunnel, you find it still sloping downwards in a southeasterly direction.  Torches now appear intermittently along the walls, lighting your way, although you can still make out the entrance up to the northwest.  The smell of the earth around you is strong now, filling your senses with its musty, dank scent. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7928}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7930}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7930}{0}{}{Inside a tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The tunnel continues to slope southeasterly into the earth, making your impression of the operation grow considerably with each step.  The amount of work expended on just this much of the tunnel must have been enormous, and you have no idea how much further the tunnel extends.  You try to listen to the sounds emanating from the southeast, but the way things echo in here, you can't tell if the end is a hundred feet or two miles off. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7929}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7931}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7931}{0}{}{Inside a tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{Looking back towards the entrance of the tunnel, you can see a line of torches heading upwards towards a faint white glow which might be the tunnel opening, but you really can't be sure.  The torches continue southeast, but after a short distance disappear altogether.  It could be that you are nearing the end of the tunnel, or that something more sinister is afoot. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7930}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7932}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7932}{0}{}{A bend in the tunnel. (ne,nw)}{ }{The tunnel bends here, turning down to the northeast.  This must be the reason you couldn't make out any more torches in this direction.  Down the slope to the northeast, you can hear the same vague sounds you have been hearing all along, with no difference in how close they appear.  To support the corner here, the logs have been made into a more complicated structure, but equally solid-looking. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7931}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7933}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7933}{0}{}{A quiet stretch of tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{Having turned the corner, you feel a sense of foreboding hanging over you, as if losing sight of the entrance means there is no way back.  The tunnel here seems quiet in comparison to the first stretch, though there are still a number of people carrying their loads up and down.  The slope is unchanged, still heading downwards at a steady rate. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7932}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7934}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7934}{0}{}{Another quiet stretch of tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel continues downward relentlessly.  Whatever lies at the bottom must be something particularly important, as already you guess that you are over fifty feet down.  This stretch of tunnel is quiet, though the faint noises from below still echo their way up to your ears. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7933}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7935}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7935}{0}{}{Inside a tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The walls of the tunnel here are particularly rocky, with the earth filled with stones of all shapes and sizes.  Perhaps this was once an old river bed.  It must have made hard going for whoever is doing the digging, but obviously they got through, as the tunnel continues northeast. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7934}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7936}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7936}{0}{}{Inside a tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{An old river bed continues here, leaving the walls strewn with rocks and stones.  The torchlight bounces off them much more readily than off the more earthen walls, leaving this section of tunnel more brightly lit. Occasionally, there is a rock with a streak of quartz or schist which sparkles like a jewel, making the area quite beautiful. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7935}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7937}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7937}{0}{}{a bend in tunnel. (nw,sw)}{ }{The tunnel takes another bend here, turning down towards the northwest.  The slope continues unabated however, as do the faint, unidentifiable noises echoing up from below.  You take heart in reaching a corner, at least it signifies some kind of progress in your descent.  The walls here continue to look like an ancient river bed, though you can tell that towards the northwest the amount of stones lessens. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7936}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7938}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7938}{0}{}{An echoing stretch of tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The noise within this piece of tunnel echoes a lot more than previous sections, as if there were a large open area ahead.  From here though, you can't make out anything other than more tunnel.  You seem to have left the buried river bed behind you, as the walls here are almost entirely earth once more. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7937}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7939}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7939}{0}{}{An underground cavern. (nw,se)}{S}{The tunnel here has broken through into a huge underground cavern!  It is truly a sight to behold, as the ceiling located about forty feet above you is absolutely covered in giant glowing lights.  The lights shine in all colors of the rainbow and reflect off the walls, highlighting a thousand dancing sparkles.  You appear to be standing at almost the top of the cavern, as the ground extends at a vicious slope off to the west, and the tunnel diggers have carved a path northwards, following what you assume was the planned course of the tunnel. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7938}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7940}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7957}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7940}{0}{}{The middle of a great cavern. (nw,se)}{ }{You judge yourself to be roughly half way across the huge cavern, walking along the path carved into the steeply sloping floor.  Above you the lights continue to glow in their rainbow colors, making this section of your journey astoundingly beautiful.  The path here is a little narrower than the tunnel, and occasionally you are bumped and jostled by the people toting their loads up and down the path. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7939}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7941}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7941}{0}{}{The edge of a large cavern. (nw,se)}{ }{You are near the northwestern edge of the cavern, and can see the path disappear into the cavern wall ahead, becoming a tunnel once more.  Torchlight flickers from within, not looking nearly as enticing or beautiful as the glowing lights from the ceiling within the cavern.  The path widens once more as it nears the cavern wall, making it easier to walk without getting knocked around by those trying to pass you carrying their loads. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7940}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7942}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7942}{0}{}{Back inside a tunnel. (sw,se)}{ }{With the large cavern just behind you to the southeast the tunnel takes an immediate turn to the southwest.  The walls here are once more supported by the logs you have seen people carrying down the tunnel.  You guess the tunnel must still have a way to go as people continue to carry logs past you.  The glowing lights of the cavern behind you give the entrance to the tunnel a multi-colored glow, making the torchlight around you look pale in comparison. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7941}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7943}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7943}{0}{}{Another section of tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{This section of tunnel is thoroughly unremarkable.  Its walls look particularly uninteresting, lined with logs and torches as they are.  Even the other people around you seem to hurry through this stretch of tunnel, as if they will find something more interesting elsewhere.  The smell of earth is very strong here too, as the tunnel walls are almost entirely comprised of dirt once more, needing more support from the logs. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7942}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7944}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7944}{0}{}{A steep section of tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel here is much more steeply sloped than other sections.  In the worst bit, there are actually a couple of stairs carved into the tunnel floor to make the going easier.  The people carrying logs and dirt find it hard to shift their heavy loads up and down this section. Briefly looking around, you don't see any reason for the steep slope, perhaps it is because you are nearing the end of the tunnel? }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7943}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7945}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7945}{0}{}{A steeply sloping tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel continues sloping steeply here, with a few more stairs making traveling easier.  Though the steep slope is somewhat inconvenient for walking, you are sure it will enable the tunnel to reach its intended destination with more speed than if it had remained at the fairly gentle slope it originally had.  The walls here are beginning to become a little tainted with clay, giving them a more muddy-brown tinge, rather than the rich dark brown of the more pure earth. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7944}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7946}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7946}{0}{}{A bend in the tunnel. (ne,s)}{ }{The tunnel walls begin to turn again here, though the turn is not as sharp as the previous ones you have encountered.  It appears to be turning towards the southeast, but only very slowly so that here you can follow it southward.  The slope has evened out once more, regaining its steady downward heading, making it easy to travel once more.  The people passing you certainly seem to be having an easier time of it. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7945}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7947}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7947}{0}{}{A curving piece of tunnel. (se,n)}{ }{The long curve of the tunnel continues here, though it looks as if the tunnel straightens out to the southeast, once more heading downwards in a straight line.  To the north, the tunnel curves away out of sight, though you know eventually it reaches the surface.  The walls here are mostly clay, reassuring you with their strength but offending your nose. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7946}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7948}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7948}{0}{}{More tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The tunnel here continues sloping downwards to the southeast, and upwards to the northwest.  From further down the tunnel you can still hear muffled sounds which could easily be from either battle or digging.  People are still carrying dirt up the tunnel, so you guess that it is more likely to be from digging, but you never can tell. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7947}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7949}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7949}{0}{}{Inside a tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The walls of the tunnel here are beginning to become a mixture of clay and soil once more, giving your eyes and nose some relief from the starkness of the plain clay walls to the northwest.  You find yourself still traveling through the tunnel, with no end in sight in either direction.  You try not to think about the immense amount of soil above your head should the tunnel collapse. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7948}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7950}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7950}{0}{}{A narrow stretch of tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The tunnel narrows here, becoming only about 4 feet wide.  The walls bulge inward, and seem to be a different material than earth or clay.  You can sense that as the tunnel continues in both directions, it widens once more, allowing much easier traveling than here.  You are getting jostled quite a lot by people carrying their loads up and down the tunnel, it might be best if you continue on your way. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7949}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7951}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7951}{0}{}{A bend in the tunnel. (ne,nw)}{ }{The tunnel takes another bend here, turning downwards towards the northeast.  Looking up the tunnel towards the northwest, you can see that it narrows in that direction, and there is a bit of congestion as people make their way through carrying their loads.  A misshapen pile of rubble rests in the corner, against the wall.  You can still hear muffled, vague noises coming from further down the tunnel, indicating that you may yet have some way to travel to discover its final destination. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7950}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7952}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47314}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7952}{0}{}{A damp stretch of tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel here feels damp, though you can see no water, and the walls and earth are dry.  There is a certain moistness to the air which you cannot put your finger on, lending an intriguing feel to this place.  The tunnel continues downwards to the northeast, where you might find the source of the moisture, or perhaps it comes from back up the tunnel to the southwest. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7951}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7953}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7953}{0}{}{A dripping tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel here is slick with moisture, and you can now see the cause of it.  Emerging from half way up the eastern wall, and flowing right across the path is an underground stream!  The diggers must have intersected its path, cutting right through where it normally flowed.  It is quite a substantial flow, and you wonder if it was always an underground river, or if it once flowed on the surface and has slowly become encased in the earth like so many hapless creatures.  The water looks clear where it emerges from the wall, but picks up silt and dirt as it flows through the tunnel, so is a muddy brown by the time it disappears into the western wall. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7952}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7954}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7954}{0}{}{A damp tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel here feels damp, as if the air were somehow filled with moisture.  Lit by the torches on the walls, you can see that the tunnel continues to head downwards to the northeast, and upwards to the southwest.  One of these directions probably holds the cause of the moisture in the air, and it is up to you to decide which way you are going to head. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7953}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7955}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7955}{0}{}{A bend in the tunnel. (nw,sw)}{ }{The tunnel takes another bend here, heading once more down to the northwest.  The usual noises coming up the tunnel sound different from here, as if they are echoing slightly more.  Listening more closely doesn't help though, you still can't make out any substance to the noises.  The tunnel itself seems dry once more, and the bend to the northwest continues to lead down into the earth, with what destination you can only guess. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7954}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7956}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7956}{0}{}{An echoing tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The noises drifting up from further down the tunnel definitely echo more here, indicating there may be another cavern to the northwest.  The walls of the tunnel here are partly comprised of rock once more, giving further indication that you may be near an open space, as well as adding to the echo effect. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7955}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7957}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7957}{0}{}{Halfway down a huge cavern. (nw,se)}{ }{Looking around in awe, you find yourself walking along a path carved into the steeply sloping floor of a huge underground cavern.  The floor slopes sharply upwards to the east, and drops off almost vertically to the west.  Looking up the slope, you can see a mass of rainbow coloured lights far above, on what must be the ceiling.  This is the same cavern you passed through earlier!  Looking up the slope for confirmation, you can just make out small figures making their way along the path near the top of the cavern.  Having spiraled its way downward into the earth, the tunnel has returned to pass through the cavern much further down! }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7956}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7958}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7971}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7939}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7958}{0}{}{A path across a cavern. (nw,se)}{ }{The cavern comes to an end just ahead to the northwest, and the path once more becomes a tunnel as it disappears into the cavern wall.  Far above you, the multi-colored lights glow on the ceiling and provide light for the cavern, negating the need for torches along this stretch of path.  The floor of the cavern rears upwards to the east, and falls away dizzyingly to the west, with no chance of climbing in either direction. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7957}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7959}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7959}{0}{}{A turn in the tunnel. (sw,se)}{ }{The path, upon entering the wall of the cavern and becoming a tunnel once more, immediately takes a turn towards the southwest.  Just to the southeast is the huge cavern, and all the noises still echo here, this close to its open space.  The slope of the tunnel continues unabated, carving its way further and further down into the earth. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7958}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7960}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7960}{0}{}{A sloping tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel here continues to slope down as it heads southwest, and upwards as it heads in the opposite direction.  The walls are a mixture of rock and earth here, giving them an interesting texture and appearance.  The light from the torches lining the walls flickers off the rock, creating dancing shadows whenever one of the people heading up or down the tunnel passes by. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7959}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7961}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7961}{0}{}{A sloping piece of tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel continues to slope down to the southwest, and up to the northeast, giving you two choices of direction in which to head.  The walls here are mainly earth, with the supporting logs spaced more closely together once more in order to lend their strength to the walls and stop them from collapsing.  Noises echo up from further down the tunnel, but they are so muted and distorted that you find it impossible to make out anything clearly, or even tell how far away the source is. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7960}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7962}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7962}{0}{}{A slowly curving tunnel. (ne,s)}{ }{The tunnel takes a slow curve here, heading northeast and south.  Southwards the tunnel continues to slope downwards, and it appears that the curve continues in that direction, though how far you cannot tell.  The walls straighten as they head up to the northeast, and continue to slope in that direction for as far as you can make out. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7961}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7963}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7963}{0}{}{A long curve in the tunnel. (se,n)}{ }{The tunnel curves slowly off to the north from here as it heads upwards towards the surface.  The curve ends to the southeast, as the tunnel heads downwards in a more direct line in that direction.  Your way is lit by occasional torches lining the walls, which flicker every now and then when a slight breeze moves through the tunnel.  People continue to pass you by, carrying their loads of dirt and logs towards their destinations. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7962}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7964}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35432}{hidden}{hidden}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7964}{0}{}{A plain section of tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{This area of tunnel appears quite plain and simple.  The walls are completely made of earth, making the construction of this section very basic.  Towards the southeast the tunnel continues downwards, and towards the northwest you could head back up towards the surface. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7963}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7965}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7965}{0}{}{A plain section of tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The tunnel slopes down to the southeast here, and disappears into the distance upwards to the northwest.  You must be a long way underground by now, but don't have any reliable way of judging just how far.  Whatever the destination of the tunnel is, it must have been buried for a long time to be so deep.  The walls in this section have a few scattered stones through their otherwise earthy surface. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7964}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7966}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7966}{0}{}{A corner in the tunnel. (ne,nw)}{ }{As the tunnel continues to slope downwards, it curves around to the northeast, creating a corner here.  The straight sections of the tunnel seem to be getting shorter as it moves downward, creating a spiral effect.  The logs supporting the walls here are structured carefully to continue to lend their strength as the tunnel curves. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7965}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7967}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7967}{0}{}{In a tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel continues in both upwards and downwards directions here.  Down lies to the northeast, and up to the southwest, giving you two choices of which way to head.  It appears that the tunnel curves just to the southwest, but continues straight for some distance to the northeast, though you cannot tell how far.  Running between this section of tunnel and the next to the southeast is an underground stream, now flowing right across the tunnel floor.  You will have to step over it to continue that direction, but it is not wide, so should not be a problem. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7966}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7968}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7968}{0}{}{An ordinary stretch of tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{Apart from the underground stream separating this section of tunnel from the portion upwards to the southwest, the tunnel here is quite ordinary.  Towards the northeast, the tunnel slopes downwards, continuing the journey into the earth, the way lit by flickering torches lining the walls. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7967}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7969}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7969}{0}{}{A corner in a tunnel. (nw,sw)}{ }{The tunnel continues here, but curves around a corner, and now slopes downwards to the northwest.  The way back up to the surface lies to the southwest, though the surface is quite a distance off.  Perhaps it would be easier to head down and see what might be at the end of the tunnel.  The smell of earth fills the tunnel, emanating from the walls. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7968}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7970}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7970}{0}{}{A straight section of tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The tunnel straightens here as it heads northwest, but up to the southeast you can see that it curves once more and disappears from sight.  Echoes from below seem to come more frequently here, as if there were some commotion or excitement, but they are no less garbled and you are just as unable to make them out.  The walls of the tunnel are pure earth, illuminated by the torches spaced along them. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7969}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7971}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7971}{0}{}{The bottom of a huge cavern. (nw,se)}{ }{You have emerged into a huge cavern!  You are standing right at the very bottom, with the floor rising steeply upwards to the east.  Far far above, you can see the glimmering of lights upon the ceiling, looking like a blanket of color.  The path travels across the cavern, without even having to be carved into the floor, as it follows the same slope intended by the tunnel. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7970}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7972}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7980}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7957}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7972}{0}{}{A curving tunnel. (sw,se)}{ }{The tunnel curves here, heading down to the southwest, and up into the huge cavern to the southeast.  The glowing light from the cavern is visible at the entrance, though because of the height of the ceiling, the glow is very faint.  To the southwest, torches light the tunnel as it continues downwards, disappearing further into the earth. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7971}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7973}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7973}{0}{}{A short section of tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel here is straight, but you can see that in both directions the tunnel soon curves out of sight.  The spiral that has slowly been working its way inwards is getting to be very tight, possibly as it heads towards the destination of the tunnel.  The walls are a mixture of rock and earth here. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7972}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7974}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7974}{0}{}{A slowly curving tunnel. (ne,s)}{ }{The tunnel curves slowly here as it slopes downward, turning from heading southwest to head south.  Back up to the northeast, the tunnel eventually would lead you to the surface, though it is a long way off. The walls are still a mixture of rock and earth here, and the support logs are well spaced out. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7973}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7975}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7975}{0}{}{A slowly curving tunnel. (se,n)}{ }{The tunnel curves away upwards to the north, and straightens out down to the southeast.  The echoes coming from further down the tunnel sound much louder now, though they are still so distorted that you cannot make them out.  People continue to bustle past in both directions, carrying logs down and excavated soil up. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7974}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7976}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7976}{0}{}{In a tunnel. (nw,se)}{ }{The tunnel continues to slope downwards as it heads southeast.  Is it your imagination, or is the slope flattening off slightly?   To the northwest, the tunnel heads upwards and eventually leads to the frozen icelands.  The walls of the tunnel seem to be becoming more rocky and less earthy the further down the tunnel you head. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7975}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7977}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7977}{0}{}{A tunnel corner. (ne,nw)}{ }{The tunnel curves again here, leading you closer to the centre of the spiral.  You must be fairly close to the destination by now, given how far the tunnel has spiraled in on itself already.  Strange sounds continue to echo up from further down the tunnel, though they are garbled from the distance.  The walls are almost completely rock now, with only a few scattered patches of earth. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7976}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7978}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7978}{0}{}{A tunnel. (ne,sw)}{ }{The tunnel here is carved through solid rock, making any sound echo between the walls.  The rock itself glistens in the torchlight thrown out by the occasional torch that is attached to the wall.  With all the rock here, this section of tunnel must have taken quite some time for the diggers to excavate. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7977}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7979}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7979}{0}{}{A bend in a tunnel. (nw,sw)}{ }{The tunnel sweeps around another curve here, and now slopes down to the northwest.  The slope definitely seems to be slightly less steep in that direction, though you only notice it because you are so familiar with the tunnel by now.  Off to the southwest, the tunnel slopes upwards and outwards as it spirals towards the surface.  }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7978}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7980}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7980}{0}{<248>}{A short stretch of tunnel. (nw,se)}{<248>% %<088>}{The tunnel continues to slope downwards, though not so steeply as earlier sections.  Off to the southeast, the tunnel leads back upwards, and people carry their loads of rock in that direction.  From down the tunnel to the northwest, you can make out muffled sounds, but they echo off the rock walls in such a fashion that you cannot make out anything about them.  The feeling that you are close to the end of the tunnel is strong here, urging you onwards. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7979}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7981}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7971}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7981}{0}{<248>}{Another bend in the tunnel. (sw,se)}{<248>% %<088>}{The tunnel bends once more here, curving around to the southwest where it looks like the tunnel may finally flatten out, but it might just be wishful thinking on your part.  The walls are completely rock here, surrounding you with their hard, unyielding darkness.  Thankfully, there are torches spaced along the wall, lighting your way. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7980}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7982}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7982}{0}{}{A change in the tunnel. (ne,s)}{ }{The tunnel changes drastically here, this is where the downward slope of the tunnel finishes, and it flattens out.  To the south the tunnel continues at this level, suggesting the end may lie quite nearby in that direction, and to the northeast the tunnel starts its long upward spiral back to the surface. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7981}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7983}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7983}{0}{}{A turn in the tunnel. (se,n)}{C}{The tunnel almost looks as if it were supposed to end here, but a solid wall of ore-like substance to the east looks to have foiled that plan.  The tunnel therefore continues off to the southeast, probably in an attempt to find a way around the impenetrable barrier. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7982}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7984}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7984}{0}{}{A curving tunnel of rock. (ne,nw)}{ }{The tunnel curves around quite tightly here, obviously close to its final destination.  The wall on the northern side is more of the ore-like substance, making it impenetrable.  The tunnel no longer slopes downward, reinforcing the feeling that the end may be near, but listening to the sounds echoing from the northeast, you are still unable to discern anything about them. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7983}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7985}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7985}{0}{}{A tunnel of rock. (nw,sw)}{ }{The tunnel here continues to travel in a circular motion, and is still traveling horizontally.  On the western side of the tunnel is a wall of the impenetrable ore-like substance which the tunnel has been following around.  It is possible that the destination of the tunnel lies on the other side of that wall.  The rest of the tunnel is solid rock, making it extremely difficult to tunnel through, but the diggers don't seem to have had any trouble. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7984}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7986}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7986}{0}{}{The end of the tunnel (grisly). (s,se)}{ }{You have finally come to the end of the tunnel, but as you look around you might almost wish you hadn't.  The floor here is strewn with pieces of flesh, splatters of blood, and broken splinters of bone, all of which seem to have been flung from the cavern-like room to the south.  Whatever the destination of the tunnel was supposed to be, it is doubtful any of the people involved were expecting this.  Whatever lies to the south has caused this destruction, and should give you pause before entering. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7985}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {7987}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7987}{0}{}{A terrible scene of carnage and destruction. (n)}{ }{You find yourself in a huge dome-shaped cavern, strewn with dismembered and crushed remains.  Torn pieces of flesh and splintered shards of bone litter the floor, and trails of blood splatter the walls.  This is truly a scene from the darkest nightmares, the places of dread we hope never to see in reality.  In the center of the chamber lies an enormous skeleton of a dragon, amazingly intact amidst all the destruction around it.  The only exit from the room is back the way you came, a portal of hope in this room of despair. }{Excavation Site}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7986}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7988}{0}{<168>}{Icelands (n,s,w,e)}{<168>^ ~<088>}{Icelands The snow crunches underfoot.  This is a cold, icy region of the north.  The wind moans like a dying soul.  Further to the east you see that the land of ice continues.   }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
