R {7997}{0}{}{The Catacomb's Necessities Shop (ne)}{ }{This fair sized room has been cleaned up and furnished with crates of all shapes and sizes.  What's in the crates you can't be sure, but whatever it is, it's for sale here.  This small pocket business sure could use a better location, but I guess you take what you can get right? }{Catacombs}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7996}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7998}{0}{}{The Tavern, Razed (nw)}{ }{You've found your way into the catacomb's tavern.  It's not much to  look at as far as pubs go, but then again when you build in the  ruins of an ancient citadel you can't expect pristine conditions.   A few stools are snugged tight against the long counter, but no  tables have been set up.  Apparantly these folks don't have many  people stay around for long.  A small sign over the counter has a  list of drinks. }{Catacombs}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7996}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {7999}{0}{}{One of the citadel's crumbling halls (n,s)}{ }{You pick your way through the rubble littering the floor of the  corridor, listening for the telltale signs of danger lurking in the  darkness.  Your footsteps kick up small puffs of dust which swirl  about your ankles to cling to your boots and leggings.  Here and  there along the corridor you can find the remains of ancient  dwarven carvings which once brightened the citadel with their  craftsmanship. }{Catacombs}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7996}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8000}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8000}{0}{}{A rubble strewn hall (n,s,w,e)}{ }{The dark and dusty corridors are littered with crumbling stone  fallen from the walls and ceiling over the ages.  The strong  dwarven constructed foundation is all that remains of the once  great citadel which presided over the trade routes.  As you wander  down the dark subterranean corridors you marvel at the power  brought to bear which could destroy such magnificent construction. }{Catacombs}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
