E {8289}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8287}{0}{}{Springfield Retirement Castle - Bea Simmon's room (w)}{ }{    This room is slightly more colourful than most of the private rooms in the home.  Bright curtains have been hung over the window, and the drab brown sheets on the bed have been replaced with a quilt done in blues and greens.  A bedside table with several photo frames completes the rooms furnishings. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8286}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8288}{0}{}{Springfield Retirement Castle - An empty room (e)}{ }{    It is a sad fact of life in the Retirement Castle that sometimes the residents pass on.  This room is empty of any personal belongings, containing only a small bed and a standard-issue bedside table.  A thin layer of dust has been allowed to settle over the room. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8286}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8289}{0}{}{Springfield Retirement Castle - Abraham Simpson's room (n)}{ }{    It is to this room the Simpson family has condemned its grandpa.  It is a drab room, with very little in the way of decoration.  A single bed with brown sheets sits in one corner next to the window.  There is a comfy chair, and a small wooden bedside table.  A single picture frame sits on the table, facing the bed. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8286}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8290}{0}{}{The Simpson's Front Yard (s,e,enter)}{<168>E<088>}{   The rolling green pastures of the front lawn and the idyllic facade of the house before you seem to hide a latent disturbance,  faint but perceptible.  Within the pastel walls of the Simpson home resides a veritable ocean of Chaos.  The smooth black asphalt welcomes you back to the comforting embrace of Evergreen Terrace, to the south.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8227}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8291}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8297}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8297}{n}{enter}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8291}{0}{}{The Simpsons' Driveway (n,w)}{ }{   This driveway leading north into an open garage is stained with skid marks and leaking oil trails.  Within the dank hollow car cavern you can barely make out a lot of...garbage...  If garbage isn't worth investigation, I don't know what is.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8290}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8292}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8292}{0}{}{The Simpsons' Garage (n,s)}{ }{   This grungy old garage is so encrusted with smut and soot, it actually looks like a dark stone cave!  You fear that each step might land you on a mousetrap or bottomless pit or 5 month old tuna sandwich.  A doorway that leads into the house lies to the north while the huge (and broken) garage door is eternally in the open position.  There is an almost unbelievable amount of garbage strewn about the place.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8291}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8293}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8293}{0}{}{A Dark Corner of the House (w,s)}{ }{   A door leads south to the garage from this dirty, stinky corner.  Roaches and waterbugs of various sizes scutter across the floor, accumulating the food that will help them live through those tough winter months.  Procreation is the only thing that matters for roaches. Behind the walls, you can sense hundreds and thousands of roaches overtaking the house.  *SHUDDER*  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8292}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8294}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8294}{0}{}{The Simpson Kitchen (s,w,e,out)}{<168>O<088>}{   Dirty dishes abound, not just in the sink either.  Waffles are stuck to the ceiling.  The presence of household appliances does little to alleviate the inherent repulsiveness of this room.  You wonder how Marge can stand to operate in such filth!  A dirty corridor to the east leads towards the garage, and a screen door leads out back to the spacious backyard.  The dining room to the west is just a football field's length away.  I mean, short length away.  Blah, same thing.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{marge}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8293}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8295}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8297}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24627}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24627}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8295}{0}{}{The Simpson Dining Room (s,e)}{ }{   This room's centerpiece is a long table for those special occasions when the Simpsons have guests.  This table has consequently fallen into disuse.  The walls are encrusted with splattered peas and other such consumables that have been laid to waste, martyrs of the innumerable food wars that have played out at this site.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8294}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8296}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8296}{0}{}{The Simpson Living Room (n,e)}{ }{   This is where it all happens...the living room.  The place where families come together and live out their lives in harmony. There is always an entertaining family show on the television, there are couches and chairs for stimulating family discussion, and there is a waffle on the ceiling.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{grampa}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8295}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8297}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8297}{0}{}{Main Hall of Da Simpsons House (n,w,out,stairs)}{<168>O<088>}{   This is the hub of the house.  You can see a kitchen to the north, the living room to the west, and a staircase leading up to the second floor.  The door to the normal outside world is right behind you, should you decide to forsake the madness that lies within this home.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
