R {8405}{0}{<248>}{Homer's Workroom (e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{   True to the irony of George Jetson's predicament... that of a capable man whose job is to merely push one button repeatedly all day...Homer Simpson's console resembles the cockpit of a 747.  Yet Homer's capabilities lie barely in brushing his teeth, let alone controlling deadly nuclear reactions and atomic radiation. A broken-down stool is the only furniture in the entire room. }{Simpsons}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8404}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {8406}{0}{<268>}{North Hallway of the Nuclear Power Plant (w,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{   Various functions and jobs are carried out within the rooms which line this hallway, none of which concern you in even the slightest. The massive, imposing lobby is ever-present to the south, while the hall takes an extremely sharp turn west here.  You get the impression that maybe the hallway to the west was not intended for visitors such as yourself. }{Simpsons}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
