R {14079}{0}{<278>}{Cape Road (n,se,e,nw)}{<278>- -<088>}{The cape hooks abruptly to the east at this point, as steep cliffs lie to both the south and west.  To the south the open ocean extends for as far as the eye can see, and to the west lies Zahar Bay.  The sound of gulls cuts through the roaring wind, as they circle the cape.  An old road runs northwest and east along the cape.  Just to the east and northeast, the high cliffs rapidly give way to lower headland and beach. To the northeast, you can see the immense Dragonspire Bay.  To the southeast you can clamber down to a rocky spur, which stretches out into the ocean, and then circles back westward under the cliffs. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
