R {14235}{0}{}{Conning Tower (leave,d)}{ }{Quite a bit of rust has accumulated around the conning tower. A large pole has been extended from a covered opening in the deck. A panel sits on top of the pole. Various instruments are mounted on the fore side of the tower. The hatch that leads below has been cut open and set aside. }{The Lost Submarine}{lost_submarine}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14237}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14234}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14236}{0}{}{Crew Quarters (aft,fore)}{ }{Bunks, stacked three high, line each side of the compartment. Near the command deck is a small protected space which appears to be the captain's cabin. Several metal boxes are stacked underneath each of the bunks. On the opposite side from the captain's cabin is a large cabinet. The space here is very cramped, but very well utilized. }{The Lost Submarine}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
