R {14401}{0}{}{Church steps (nw,s)}{ }{You stand on the steps of one of the most marvelous pieces of architecture that you have ever set eyes upon.  It is a spectacular gothic church made completely from stone and obviously very old indeed.  Two stone gargoyles guard the entrance to the church, sitting watchfully over the church doors. }{Mortimer's Church}{mortimers_church}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14352}{nw}{nw}{9}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14402}{s}{open door;s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14402}{0}{}{Church entrance (n,sw,se)}{ }{You stand inside the entrance hall to this church. The notice board on the left wall catches your immediate attention, as it has several notes on it, some of which are quite colorful.  The walls themselves are made of ancient looking stonework, implying that this church was built many years into the past.  A glorious red carpet lines the floor and leads onward into the church itself. }{Mortimer's Church}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14401}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14403}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14404}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14403}{0}{}{Church aisle (s,e,ne)}{ }{This is the right aisle of the church; rows of oak benches are to the west and east.  In front of the benches are desks that seem to contain hymn sheets and copies of the Holy Bible.  On the right wall are hung many tapestries containing scenes that most likely come from the Bible.  As you gaze around you marvel at the huge stone pillars that provide what must be a strong foundation for this marvelous piece of ancient architecture.  You note that the carpet stops at the beginning of the aisle and that the floor is now made up of cold stone slabs. }{Mortimer's Church}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14402}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14405}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14408}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14404}{0}{}{Church aisle (s,w,nw)}{ }{This is the left aisle of the church; rows of benches are to your left and right.  The benches are wooden and probably made of oak, in front of the benches are desks that seem to contain hymn sheets and copies of the Holy Bible. A vast stained glass window that seems to depict some event from the Bible itself, dominates the left wall of the church.  On either side of the window are statues of angels splendidly carved from some ancient stone.  You note that the carpet stopped at the beginning of the aisle and that the floor is now made up of cold stone slabs. }{Mortimer's Church}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14402}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14406}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14408}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14405}{0}{}{Church aisle (n,e,se)}{ }{Standing just before the altar you notice that the corner of this area holds what seems to be a small library.  Bookcases line the walls and each one is full of ancient tomes and books, though most seem to be covered in dust.  Slightly off to the left, just before the altar, is a beautiful organ, probably made from mahogany; you guess that many a tune was skillfully played on this, with the congregation singing loudly in accompaniment. }{Mortimer's Church}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14403}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14410}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14409}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14406}{0}{}{Church aisle (n,w,sw)}{ }{Moving further down the aisle you come to the end of the rows of benches and desks and step into an area of mainly open space just before the altar.  In the left corner of this space is a beautiful font, which is brilliantly decorated with what seem to be rubies and various other baubles.  On the walls here, hang crosses of gold and many other equally valuable items. You come to the conclusion that the building must have at one time had someone with great wealth to help finance it. }{Mortimer's Church}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
