R {14575}{0}{<238>}{Acid Eaten Forests (n,s,w,e)}{<238>( *<088>}{Acid Eaten Forests You can only imagine how beautiful these forests must have once been, before man and his progress shattered everything.  The ground is sodden and bare, the life-giving minerals leeched out of it by punishing acidic rains.  Soft, dark earth gives way beneath your feet as you travel through the sickly forests of the northeast.  Since the late twentieth century there have been warnings about the effects of acid rain, but now with the mass increase in industrialization and the radiation, the deforestation is at an all time high.   }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
