R {14586}{0}{<238>}{Acid Eaten Forests (n,w,e)}{<238>( *<088>}{Acid Eaten Forests Soft, dark earth gives way beneath your feet as you travel through the sickly forests of the northeast.  Since the late twentieth century there have been warnings about the effects of acid rain, but now with the mass increase in industrialization and the radiation, the deforestation is at an all time high.  Drops of water fall from the leaves above and stain your clothes a dark sickly color, a sure sign of the pollution they carry.  The ground is sodden and bare, the life-giving minerals leeched out of it by punishing acidic rains.  To the west and north you almost miss the continuation of the wasteland.  The remains of the city of brotherly love can be seen strewn across the horizon. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
