R {14820}{0}{<238>}{Desolate plains (s,w,e,enter)}{<238>,<228>E<238>`<088>}{Desolate plains You've got to wonder how anything could survive way out here.  You catch the smell of something rancid burning. You probably don't want to find out what it could be that could be burning.  A foul wind whips by you as you survey this desolate landscape.  To the south you detect the continuation of the plains.  The sprawling city of Chicago curves around the southern end of Lake Michigan, braving the harsh winds and acid rain to provide homes for millions.  The entrance to that city's airport lies just ahead. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
