R {14844}{0}{}{Syderman's Light Shop (ne)}{ }{This small room is so well lit, that you are almost blinded by the sheer brilliance. There are lights hanging everywhere, and you can see shelves full of items and equipment used to construct the lights. What you can see of the walls from looking around all the stuff piled on them, is that they look like shiny smooth rock. There is a sign over a small counter here that directs you to 'list' to see what is available. You can also type: buy <#> <item>. }{HTC Northern Expansion Terminal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14843}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14845}{0}{}{Syderman's Merckentile and Trade (nw)}{<128>$<088>}{This square room has shelves all over the place. It looks as if this small store is frequented rather often from all of the wear and tear on the place. The walls, ceiling and floor all look to be made out of a strange glasslike looking stone, and there is a large table in one corner. }{HTC Northern Expansion Terminal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14843}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14846}{0}{}{Syderman's Ammo Dump (se)}{ }{This long rectangular room looks like it's been carved right out of the surrounding rock and stone. The walls are lined with shelves of items stored away in blast proof containers. There is a small desk in one corner with a small sign attached to it which read 'list' or type 'buy <#> <item>'. This whole rooms reeks of gunpowder. }{HTC Northern Expansion Terminal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14843}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38868}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14847}{0}{}{Syderman's Drink Shop (sw)}{ }{This long oblong room seems to have be cut directly from the surrounding rock. You can see that the walls are as smooth as glass. On the far end of the room is a small counter with a sign hanging below it directing you to 'list' or type: buy <#> <item>. }{HTC Northern Expansion Terminal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14843}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14848}{0}{}{Under the Terminal (n,u)}{ }{A smooth square well lit tunnel stretches out before you. The light shines off of the rock from further down the tunnel. You can hear the sounds of the Bullet Train terminal coming from above as the trains come and go. There are many large beams and metal poles coming down through the ceiling. There is also a large black metal stairway leading back up to the surface. }{HTC Northern Expansion Terminal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14843}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14600}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14849}{0}{}{Under the Terminal (w,u)}{ }{You stand in a large tunnel that stretches out underneath the Houston Transportation Center's Northern Expansion Terminal. It seems like the tunnel was made by just melting away the rock, because the walls look like a stone form of melted butter. There is a lot of light coming from further down the tunnel, and there is a metal stairway leading back to the surface. }{HTC Northern Expansion Terminal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
