R {14876}{0}{<238>}{Desolate plains (n,s,w)}{<238>, `<088>}{Desolate plains Before you stretches a vast expanse of destruction and desolation.  You've got to wonder how anything could survive way out here.  The ground under your feet cracks and snaps as you walk. The dirt is jet black, with soot, ash, and pieces of bone strewn throughout.  The waters of Lake Michigan lap at the shoreline, blown by icy northern winds. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14821}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15188}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14875}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14877}{0}{}{Curbside Dropoff (n,leave)}{<168>L<088>}{Narrowly escaping death by taxi, you find yourself in front of a newly refurbished building.  Overhead, the words "O'Hare International Airport" are etched into a massive sign.  Directly in front of you are a pair of large doors leading into the terminal.  Beyond them you can see a throng of people waiting in a line.  Looking to your left and right, you see a swarm of cars and buses letting off other passengers, all hoping to gain passage out of this cesspool called Chicago.  To the left of the doors is a smaller sign with what looks like directions. }{O'Hare International Airport}{ohare_international_airport}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14878}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14820}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14878}{0}{}{Check in (w,s)}{ }{The sudden blast of cold air hits you in the face like a hammer.  Looking about, you take in the fact that this cavernous room is packed with people, all waiting in one line or another.  Directly in front of you is the beginning of the longest line.  To your left you can see flashes of an airline uniform through the crowd.  Over the heads of the people in line you spot a row of monitors filled with words. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14877}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14879}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14879}{0}{}{Stuck in Line (w,e)}{ }{Stepping into the line, you feel like time has stopped.  You've been waiting here for well over 10 minutes, and the line doesn't seem to have moved an inch.  Even if it was moving, the massive amount of baggage the person in front of you has would keep you standing in place anyway.  From behind you, you can just barely hear a soft grumbling... }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14878}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14880}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14880}{0}{}{Still waiting... (n,e)}{ }{Somehow, you moved a whole 10 feet closer to the end of the line, but don't seem to have gotten anywhere.  From here you can see nothing but the people pressing in around you from all sides.  In front of you is that mountain of baggage, all of it belonging to one person. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14879}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14881}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14881}{0}{}{Not there yet... (e,s)}{ }{You can see outside of the line from here.  If anything, more people seem to have crammed into the line behind you.  To the north, monitors packed with flight information can be seen over the heads of those in front of you.  The air conditioning is beginning to be overwhelmed by the sheer number of people in the room.  Those around you are starting to sweat, but if it's from the heat or the risk of missing their flights, you're not sure.  Ahead of you is yet another person with way too much baggage. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14880}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14882}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14882}{0}{}{Almost there... (e,w)}{ }{Against all odds, you've made it to the front of the line.  The idiot with too much baggage is screaming at an airline official off to your left about the cost of each extra bag.  Only a short pole with a sign stands between you and your ticket.  From here, you can clearly read the monitors overhead.  Directly in front of you stretches a long counter covered with United Airlines logos. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14881}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14883}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14883}{0}{}{I have to what now? (e,w)}{ }{In front of you is a long counter with gaps every few feet.  Behind it, you can see agents walking back and forth.  None of them seem to be in any great hurry to help the travelers on your side of the counter.  There seems to be a conveyer belt of some type behind the counter as well, presumably to move baggage to the sorting area.  On the wall behind the counter there is a small LED sign strip. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14882}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14884}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14884}{0}{}{Not again... (e,w)}{ }{Shuffling forward, you reach the end of yet another line of people all waiting to get on a plane.  Stretching down a hallway and around a corner, the line is kept organized by two sets of guide ropes, one on either side.  If it weren't for someone in front of you quoting how late they were going to be every three minutes, you'd swear time was standing still.  Over the heads of those in front of you, a flashing red light can be seen. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14883}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14885}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14885}{0}{}{Didn't we just leave this party? (w,n)}{ }{Another line, another wait.  Ahead of you, several dozen people are standing around waiting, just like you.  From this vantage point you can see around the corner slightly.  Mainly you just see more people waiting in line.  The flashing red light seems to be coming from farther up ahead.  No one is moving forward from this point, so if want to keep going, you'll have to force your way through the crowd. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14884}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14886}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14887}{s w}{s w}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14886}{0}{}{What the...? (s,w)}{ }{As you round the corner, you are confronted with the presence of armed guards stationed throughout the rest of the checkpoint.  The mood of the crowds has noticeably changed from one of irritation, to one with an undercurrent of fear.  The people are staying well back from the ropes separating them from the area the guards are patrolling.  That flashing red light is almost directly ahead of you. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14885}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14888}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14887}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {14888}{0}{}{Does it ever end? (e,w)}{ }{The added security has gotten heavier as you get closer to the terminal itself.  Guards move around in the background, looking through people's bags and triple checking their identification.  A flashing red strobe light keeps the crowd noticeably subdued as you near the end of the line.  The people around you cautiously move past the guards stationed closest to the line, their faces giving evidence of their anxiety. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14886}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14889}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {14889}{0}{}{Thank you, can I go now? (e)}{ }{This is the end of the line, literally.  Ahead of you is the TSA security checkpoint.  Dozens of x-ray machines, personnel, and lines are meant to keep passengers moving, but things are currently at a stand-still.  Dozens of people are milling around in front of the machines, all waiting for their chance to pass through once the current situation is resolved.  Beyond the machines are closed barriers, preventing anyone from going into the terminal itself.  A red strobe light attached to the ceiling gives silent warning that going beyond the barrier is a bad idea right now. }{O'Hare International Airport}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14888}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

