R {15113}{0}{<238>}{Acid Eaten Forests (s,w)}{<238>( *<088>}{Acid Eaten Forests You can only imagine how beautiful these forests must have once been, before man and his progress shattered everything.  Dark clouds blanket the sky, blotting out the sun and only making this desolate forest that much more depressing.  The trees around you almost seem to cry out in agony as their limbs weaken under the relentless assault of industry's by-products.  To the south and west you barely sense the continuation of the wasteland.  Lake Michigan stretches out to the west while to the north Lake Huron blocks you from the north peninsula. }{Science}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15112}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15115}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

