R {15457}{0}{}{Audience Chamber of Castle Peeron (n,s,w,e)}{<158>M<088>}{		Audience Chamber of Castle Peeron As you attempt to assess the vastness of this chamber, you experience a slight degree of vertigo.  The soft blue carpet extends into this room from the south where it splits at the exact center as if reacting to a polygonal prism.  The primary colors red, yellow, and green refract at ninety-degree angles from the central focus, drawing your eyes to the exits in the north, west, and east ends of the  room. The colors blend in between, forming a beatific color wheel; it is quite breathtaking.  A beautiful young lady with long silky, jet-black hair sits serenely at the desk of purest white marble at the chamber's center.  Taking in the entirety of the scene, it becomes apparent that the desk acts as the central light source for the artistic carpetry. One wall is adorned with extensive writing while another boasts the Top Marble Finders List. }{Marble Castle}{marble}{}{}{1.000}{1}
