R {15480}{0}{<238>}{** The Mountains of Ao ** (se,e)}{<238>.^.<088>}{You're walking along a precarious path that leads through the mountains of Ao. The black stones of the mountains absorb the heat of the harsh afternoon sun, making your hike almost unbearable as your body wears down and the exertion takes its toll. Very little grows amongst the sharp inclines and steep precipices of the mountains. A few patches of scrub grass and some stunted palms survive, but little else. Down below you to the east you can see the tops of the palm trees that make up the jungle canopy. To the west is a vertigo inducing drop onto the rocky shore of the island. The drop must be at least 200 feet. Falling from this vantage would spell certain death. The mountain range continues to the southeast. }{Isle of Ao}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
