R {15494}{0}{<238>}{^;^ Entrance to the Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (nw,enter)}{<238>|@|<088>}{The sounds of the jungle echo all around you as you make your way through the dense foliage. Palm fronds slap against your face, their wet edges stinging your skin. Before you, half-hidden by the wilderness, is a tall stone monument. The stone is slick with condensation and solid black in color. Etched into the stone are intricate patterns and symbols. The monument towers into the tops of the trees, the symbols disappearing into the green canopy overhead. Set in the middle of the monument is an archway that leads into the darkened interior chamber. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{dragon_labyrinth}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15470}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15497}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15497}{ne}{enter}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15495}{0}{<248>}{** A Cave Within the Mountains of Ao ** (back,forward)}{<248>% %<088>}{It's very dark in this series of caves. The rock walls are solid black as are the ceiling and ground. What little light you are able to shine in here seems to be absorbed directly into the stone. The air is very warm and excessively dry. Scuff marks can be seen on the ground, as if a struggle might have occurred recently. Dried blood is splattered on the walls as well. The cave leads deeper underground up ahead or you could choose discretion over valor and head back to the cave entrance behind you. }{Isle of Ao}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15496}{forward}{forward}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15493}{back}{back}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
