R {15499}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (nw,s)}{<248># #<088>}{The tunnel slopes downward toward the northwest while also expanding outward, creating more room to maneuver. Large fissures mar the surface of the rocky ground, creating very dangerous footing for anyone without an adequate light source and a careful eye for detail. Tectonic movement deep beneath these tunnels has broken the rock in many places. One day these tunnels are likely to collapse altogether. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15498}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15503}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15500}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (w,e)}{<248># #<088>}{The interior of this structure is even more dilapidated than what you saw outside in the main tunnel. Now that you're inside, you realize that this was once a church. Although you have no idea what race might have held mass here in this underground tabernacle, the rows of stone pews leave little doubt as to this building's original purpose. The ruins of the church stretch off to the east while the archway leading back out is to your west. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15498}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15501}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15501}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (e,w)}{<248># #<088>}{You're standing amidst the ruins of an ancient underground church. Crumbling pews are lined up and down the broad expanse of the building's interior. The stone walls are cracked and decayed, flaking bits of debris onto the broken floor beneath your feet. A draft blows through the room, the air apparently coming from somewhere behind the cracked walls. The pews continue off to the west while a tall stone altar stands in the distance to the east. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15500}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15502}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15502}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (w)}{<248>.<118>@<248>.<088>}{A tall altar of stone rises before you, dwarfing you in the darkness of this crumbling tabernacle. Unlike the broken walls and pews of this underground church, the altar looks well preserved, its surface smooth despite its apparent age. The stone of the altar is the same black hue seen throughout the Labyrinth however in contrast to the rest of the church, the altar's surface shines with a dark luminescence that suggests some magic may be at work in preserving its sanctity. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{scroll_of_shadows}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15501}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15503}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (se,n)}{<248># #<088>}{This portion of the Labyrinth is little more than a shallow shelf of rock. Just beyond where you stand is a deep chasm caused by the constant seismic activity within these tunnels. Higher and more stable ground can be found to the southeast. Miraculously, a narrow bridge of stone still stands to the north. The bridge appears to span the chasm although the far end of the bridge is too dark to make out clearly. How this bridge has managed to avoid falling into the chasm as a result of rock upheavals is truly beyond comprehension. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15499}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15504}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15504}{0}{<238>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (s,e)}{<238>===<088>}{You're standing in the middle of an L-shaped bridge of stone that spans a deep chasm within the Labyrinth. The bridge is around 20 feet in width and twice that in length. Regular quakes shake the bridge, sending pebbles plummeting off its edges and into the inky depths below. It's no small wonder that this bridge still stands given the violent seismic activity present in these tunnels. Whatever ancient race built this structure must have been highly skilled. The bridge reaches either side of the chasm to the south and the east. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{aon_marble}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15503}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15505}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15505}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (se,ne,w)}{<248># #<088>}{This oval-shaped chamber serves as a hub for several passages that branch off in various directions. A few of the passages are blocked by rubble, but pathways leading northeast and southeast remain open. The chamber comes to an abrupt end to the west, ending in a sheer drop into a chasm. A stone bridge spans the chasm, allowing travel to the other side for those brave enough to cross. Stalactites hang from the ceiling, results of mineral deposits collecting over the course of the centuries. The stalactites look like teeth, waiting to chomp down on unsuspecting visitors like you. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15504}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15506}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15507}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15506}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (nw,e)}{<248># #<088>}{This tunnel slopes steeply downward to the east, forming a natural ramp toward a large open chamber below. Standing at the far end of that chamber is the crumbling remnant of an underground castle. The castle's stark walls of stone rise into the darkened heights of the chamber, becoming lost overhead in the blackness. In the middle of the ancient structure is a vast entry, an opening into the subterranean stronghold. An eerie light emanates from this opening, a red glare that hurts your eyes after becoming accustomed to the darkness throughout this Labyrinth. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15505}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15508}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15507}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (sw,e)}{<248># #<088>}{This passage is so cluttered with rock and debris from recent tremors that you can barely make your way through it. Dust hangs in the air, coating your lungs and making it difficult to see your surroundings even with your light burning its way into the darkness of these underground tunnels. Footing in this tunnel is extremely treacherous and the broken walls bruise your body with every turn. The passage appears to widen further to the southwest. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15505}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15515}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15508}{0}{<248>}{^;^ Dragon Labyrinth ^;^ (n,s,w)}{<248># #<088>}{This echoing chamber serves as the entry hall to a vast underground castle. Created over a thousand years ago, the castle's original inhabitants are long dead and forgotten. The black stone walls of the hall are cracked and broken, but they still stand as testament to a once imposing structure. The ceiling is high overhead and shadows play across its surface from a red glare that emanates from both the north and south passages stemming from this hall. Not a hint of furnishings can be found, just a bare stone floor silently beckoning your exploration. }{Dragon Labyrinth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15506}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15509}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
