R {15646}{0}{<268>}{Temple of Kourlyn (n)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{You are in front of the Storm shrine, where many come to worship the Goddess. The whole room is illuminated by floating candles floating in troughs carved out of the wall of the temple. The shrine itself is a small altar piled with various offerings to the Kourlyn herself as well as to Elektra, the lightning and to Ventrys, the wind. People pray here for safe journeys both for themselves and for their loved ones. A statue of Kourlyn flanked by her attendants sits majestically on the altar. }{Kourlyn Temple}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15626}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15647}{0}{<268>}{Temple of Kourlyn (n)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{You are in front of the Sea shrine, where many come to worship the Goddess. The whole room is illuminated by floating candles floating in troughs carved out of the wall of the temple. The shrine itself is a small altar piled with various offerings to the Kourlyn herself as well as to Aquatys, the sea and to Poiselis, ruler of fish. People pray here for a good harvest from the ocean which is their livelihood. A statue of Kourlyn flanked by her attendants sits majestically on the altar. }{Kourlyn Temple}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
