R {15810}{0}{}{Outside a shed (ne)}{ }{You step through the chest-high grass and face a small run-down shed. The only window is caked with grime from the inside, impossible to see through, and the wood appears warped and ready to fall apart.  This must have been used to store field-tending equipment at some point in time, but it barely looks safe enough to stand right now. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15809}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35654}{knock door}{knock door}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15811}{0}{}{Grassy Field (sw,se,nw,n,s,e,w)}{ }{You are standing in a grassy field, just west of a small dirt path.  In the distance you see a pair of crows, exploring the field with a certain gusto, probably for food.  Their incessant cawing rises above the whispers of the wind through the grass, and you can hear the sounds of other creatures in the far distance. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
