R {15826}{0}{}{A quiet bedchamber (ne)}{ }{A small crescent shaped room which the lightkeeper must use as his bedroom.  The inner wall follows the curve of the tower, and the outer wall mirrors it, giving a strange shape and leaving few flat walls for furnishings.  A bed of sturdy oak planks and a goose down mattress rest against the farthest wall of the chamber. A chest is nestled up against the foot of the bed, and a small table sits in the curve of the outer wall, holding writing tools and a flickering oil lamp. }{Tower of Fire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15825}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15827}{0}{}{A turning in the stairs (d,climb)}{ }{       The stone stairs upon which you travel cling to the interior wall of the lighthouse by what appears to be sheer will.  No railing stands between you and the floor far below, and in spite of what your brain tells you, these steps seem very narrow all of a sudden.  Above you a hatch stands open, leading out onto the roof of the tower.  The floor far below  appears as just a mass of clutter from this height.  Hope you don't fall over the edge by accident. }{Tower of Fire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36129}{climb}{climb}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
