R {15860}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The street is full of throngs of people, merchants garbed in bright-colored fabrics, brave explorers, mysterious conjurors, and scruffy-looking vagabonds of every persuasion. Thatch-roofed shops and wooden carts are along the way, stuffed with merchandise eagerly offered for sale or trade. Smoke drifts through the air, coming from some food vendor not far away. The smell of roasting meat is tantalizing, making your mouth water. The black flagstones underfoot are hot, burning from the scorching desert sun high overhead while the sunlight reflecting off the city's glittering walls dazzles your eyes. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15859}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15896}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15861}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{Merchants walk down the street, peddling their wares. The sun overhead blazes down on streaming banners of black and gold that hang on wooden poles set along the street at regular intervals. Makeshift shops consisting of brown fabric canopies draped over frames of sago palm wood and thatched fronds grace the sides of the street. The canopies create a bit of shade, but it remains stifling hot. Waves of heat rise off the flagstones and waver before your eyes. The street continues both to the west and the east. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15859}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15862}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15862}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (sw,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{A canopy of golden silk completely covers the street, stretched from one side of the street to the other. It hangs about fifteen feet above your head, suspended by hooks and rings set into the sides of the buildings. The bright desert sun can still be seen past the eastern and western edges of the silk, but beneath it, the air is much cooler from the canopy's welcome shade. The buildings appear to be the homes of some of Xaxis's more wealthy merchants. A thinner avenue just beyond the canopy leads off toward the southwest. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15861}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15863}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15864}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15863}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (sw,ne)}{<278>- -<088>}{This quiet avenue seems vastly different from the busy city street to the northeast. On either side of the avenue grows a thick hedge that prevents anyone from wandering off the intended path. The stones of this avenue are the same black flagstones found throughout the main streets of the city, but the edges between each stone are painted in gold. Southwest of you stands the destination of this quiet boulevard, the most dominating structure in Xaxis, the Auruetian Tower. Made of solid gold and reaching into the heavens, this magical edifice is a testament to beauty and power. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15862}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15898}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15864}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{Bright red conical buildings rise from both sides of the street into the desert sky. These strange houses are the homes of the local priests and clerics, worshippers of the Sun God, Helvareq. There are fewer merchants wandering through this section of the city, likely a sign of respect for the worshippers' beliefs and power. Arcane symbols grace the walls of the buildings, painted in gold, often scrolling from one end of the building all the way to the other. Indecipherable to you, these symbols are the language of worshippers so ancient, their very existence is all but forgotten outside Xaxis's city walls. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15862}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15865}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15865}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (s,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{This is the northeastern corner of the streets of Xaxis. The streets continue to the west and south. Tall palm trees block the eastern end of the street, their fronds waving gently overhead in the hot desert breeze. The trees are planted in dark circles of soil that apparently fill deep hollows dug from the surface of the floating city. Beside each tree is a golden cistern holding water for the local gardeners that maintain this beautiful flora. A decorative path of red stones leads through the trees into a small guard house set up for the city's local Xill warriors. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15864}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15866}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15867}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15866}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{This street runs north and south through some of Xaxis's shops and inns. People bustle back and forth in route to whatever commerce they might be engaged in, paying little attention to your gawking. Strangers are common in these streets and generally go unnoticed. Occasionally a shopkeeper will poke his head out from his door or window to shout something to the vendors passing by or one of the city's children will skip past on their way to some mischief or another. This hub of activity is often busy day or night, providing adventurers untold possibilities. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15865}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15868}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15867}{0}{}{<< Guardhouse of Xaxis >> (w)}{💂}{This dim lit room is cramped, lacking all but the most basic of comforts. The stone walls and ceiling are jet black, absorbing virtually all the light given off by the torches that sit in their sconces along the walls. An open doorway leads back outside to the streets of Xaxis and opposite that doorway is a low sitting bench made of the same black stone as the rest of the room. These rather austere quarters serve as a guard house for the Xill warriors that protect the city from invasion. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15865}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15868}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,s,w)}{<278>- -<088>}{A side street leads off to the west while the main thoroughfare continues both north and south. Shops lie in every direction, commerce bustling with the comings and goings of countless people in need of supplies for their journeys. The desert heat bakes the flagstones of the street, heat waves rising before your eyes and clouding your vision. The sounds of the city echo around you, merchants shouting for your attention and more importantly, your coins. A smart traveler could find the proper provisions in a city like Xaxis, but a fool and his money are soon parted. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15866}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15869}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15870}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15869}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{Running both north and south, this street is lined with the shops and houses of local residents. The houses are made of stone and clay with roofs of thatched straw and palm fronds. The shops look similar to the houses, but feature signs in their glass windows that advertise the goods sold inside. Alongside some of the shops are wooden vending carts stuffed with merchandise for busy travelers and citizens alike. Occasionally one of the merchants selling these goods looks your way and hollers, attempting to gain your business. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15868}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15872}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15870}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The hustle and bustle of Xaxis's commerce seems especially prevalent on this busy avenue that leads towards the city's main streets to the east and towards its most popular store, Everything Under the Sun, to the west. People wander in and out of doorways, packages under their arms from the purchases just made within the surrounding shops. There is no limit to the variety of goods and services to be found in Xaxis. Regardless of your personal tastes, you might find something useful if you cared to enter the store ahead. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15868}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15871}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15871}{0}{<138>}{<< Everything Under the Sun >> (e)}{<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>}{This cluttered store is the most popular in Xaxis. Merchandise sits piled on shelves along almost every inch of wall space and you can barely make your way through the piles stacked up all over the floor. Known for being a waystation for travelers making their way through the desert, Xaxis sees its share of commerce and this store is as good a place as any to find a bargain or two. Feel free to shop around and find an item to purchase for yourself. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15870}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15872}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{This is the southeastern corner of the streets of Xaxis. Streets lead further off to the west and north. To the east stands a cluster of palm trees that blocks the end of the street and camouflages a building set off behind the trees and down a path of flat red stones set into the ground. The gently waving fronds of the palms create a bit of shade in the otherwise stifling heat. The trees are planted in dark circles of soil that seem to fill deep hollows dug from the surface of the floating city. Beside each tree is a golden cistern holding water for the local gardeners that maintain this flora. The all-but-hidden building is a small guard house set up for the city's local Xill warriors. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15869}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15873}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15874}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15873}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (s,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The street continues both to the east and west. Directly to the south lies a shipping dock for some of the strange airships that fly to and from Xaxis. Just to the north is a source of brilliant spiraling light that is so bright it nearly blinds you. The fragmented colors of the light are streaming forth from a giant spinning globe sitting atop a golden building. The globe spins so fast that it creates a constant breeze filled with a charge of energy that tingles on your skin. The building at the base of the globe looks impregnable. No doors or windows can be seen. You can only guess that it houses the power source of the globe. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15872}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15875}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15876}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15874}{0}{}{<< Guardhouse of Xaxis >> (w)}{💂}{The interior of the guard house is very basic. Dimly lit by a pair of torches on the walls, the room features nothing more than the walls made of smoothly chiseled black stone, a matching ceiling, a sandy floor, and a low stone bench sitting opposite the doorway. The quarters are meant to act as a buffer from the sunlight for the city's Xill warriors who are assigned to guard Xaxis. Other than giving them a bit of shade, the building serves no other purpose. The open doorway beckons you back to the streets directly to your west. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15872}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15875}{0}{}{<< The Docks of Xaxis >> (n)}{ 🛩<088>}{The activity along this dock is nearly overwhelming. Everywhere people move about, loading supplies, repairing hulls, making deals, all while airships float in and out of the steel gates suspended in the sky over the desert. The ships are breathtaking, large colorful balloons with beautiful artwork painted on their sides, wooden hulls attached beneath them that hold their passengers and cargo for their journeys through the skies. The girders that support the gates are decorated in silk streamers that flutter in the hot breeze and a variety of birds float about, screeching at the people below. These docks are one of the key components of Xaxis's success. Traders and adventurers of all sorts are able to use these docks to house their airships and stop off for necessary supplies. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15873}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15912}{board ship}{board ship}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15876}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The street divides just in front of you, leaving a circular area in between the flagstones before rejoining on either side and continuing both east and west. In this divide is a pool of swirling black fluid. The liquid bubbles and steams as it moves around swiftly in this underground reservoir. The smell of the steaming fluid is strong, leaving a burnt tinge to the air. It looks very dangerous, but a guardrail has been built around it to prevent clumsy passersby from falling in. On either side of the divided street stand several statues of gold and onyx. The eyes of the statues all stare forward, seemingly keeping watch over the pool below. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15873}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15877}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15877}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The barracks which house off-duty Xill warriors lies just north of this virtually empty section of the street. The building is stark-looking, solid black stone with little decoration or architectural flair. The black flag representing the Xill flies from a pole set into the eastern side of the barracks. The flag's black background with six red serpents, each wound together to form a star, hangs limp, only occasionally fluttering in the slight desert breeze. The entrance to the barracks is still further off to the west. South of the flagstoned street stands a pair of exotic trees, such as travelers rarely if ever see on the Fantasy mainland. They're about twenty feet high and seem to be made of living mirrors. The sunlight reflects off their shining boughs, creating a sparkling image of yourself and the building behind you that is simply boggling. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15876}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15878}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15878}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The street continues both to the east and west, the flagstones baking beneath the desert sun. To the north lies a stone staircase leading down into the open doorway of the Xill barracks. It looks cooler within that doorway as it is sheltered from the heat, but it also looks dangerous. The Xill are known to be fierce warriors and these barracks are their private quarters. South of the street stands a glass fountain that is about ten feet high. The fountain is tall and slender, cylindrical in shape. It sits in a small pool of water that gathers the liquid dripping down the sides of the glass, feeding it back into the fountain itself to flow back through yet again. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15877}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15879}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15880}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15879}{0}{<278>}{<< Xill Barracks >> (s,w,e)}{💂}{It is quite dark within the interior of the barracks. Although the bright sunlight is just a few feet away outside the entrance to the south, it does not filter within these stone walls. It's difficult to make out without better light, but the walls appear to be decorated with drawings of spiders. Hundreds of them stare back at you from the flat stone, their multiple eyes and spindly legs crudely drawn but unmistakably arachnid in design. The ceiling overhead is similarly decorated, not with spiders but with moons. These are drawn in a brighter chalk, but somehow no less eerie. It would probably be wise to leave this place immediately before you risk being caught by its inhabitants. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15878}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15881}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15882}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15880}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The street is less crowded this close to the Xill barracks which lie just to the north. The black flag of the Xill with its six red serpents wound into a star flies high on the pole set into the western side of the building. The entrance to the barracks is still further off to the east. On the southern side of the flagstoned street stands a pair of beautiful trees, the likes of which cannot be seen anywhere else on the Fantasy mainland. They aren't more than twenty feet high, but seem to be made of living crystal. The sunlight gleams off their transparent boughs, creating a sparkling phenomenon that is simply breathtaking. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15878}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15883}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15881}{0}{}{<< Xill Barracks >> (e)}{A💂}{The darkness within the interior of the barracks makes it difficult to make out a lot of the detail of your surroundings. The room feels a bit cramped, as if the dark stone of the walls was closing in around you. An acrid odor hangs in the air, no doubt a result of the yellowish cloud of gas that floats along the floor. It curls around your feet and almost seems to slither. A small ledge leads around the room against the walls. It is probably deep enough to sit on, but given the oppressive nature of this place and the awful smell of the gas, you might be wiser to leave as quickly as you can. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15879}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15882}{0}{}{<< Xill Barracks >> (w)}{💂}{This appears to be a room designed as a sparring arena for the Xill. It is so dark that you can barely make out your surroundings, but what you can see is vaguely disturbing. The floor is plain enough, simple black stone, but the walls are covered in sharp spikes that look very dangerous. Getting slammed into these spikes in the heat of battle may only serve as a painful lesson to a Xill, but it would likely kill a member of a thinner-skinned race, like you. Hanging from the ceiling are dozens of razor-edged weapons of steel. No obvious means of reaching these weapons is apparent to the naked eye. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15879}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15883}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The street continues both to the east and west, however right before you, the street divides in a circular path before becoming whole again. In the center of this divide is a pool of swirling black fluid that bubbles and steams as it moves round and round in its underground reservoir. The smell of the steaming fluid is strong, but not entirely unpleasant. It looks very dangerous and a guardrail has been built around it to assist in keeping clumsy passersby from falling in. Alongside the street on either side of the divide stand several statues of gold and onyx. The eyes of the statues all stare forward, seemingly keeping watch over the pool below. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15880}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15884}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15884}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (s,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{Kaleidoscopic light dazzles your eyes. Combined with the bright sunlight overhead, you can scarcely see at all. The brilliantly fragmented colors are streaming forth from a giant spinning globe sitting atop a golden building on the northern side of the street. A hot breeze blows past you, created by the globe's rotation. There doesn't appear to be any way inside the building at the base of the globe. You can only guess that it houses some type of power source. To the south lies a shipping dock for Xaxis's famed airships and the main thoroughfare continues both east and west. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15883}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15885}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15886}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15885}{0}{}{<< The Docks of Xaxis >> (n)}{ 🛩<088>}{The scene before you is amazing. People bustle about in every direction. Some carry loads of goods to and fro while others work on the machinery that hums as it powers the gates and pulley systems of the docks. Many are preparing for departure on their voyages in the ships that hover in midair just beyond the walkway on which you stand. Colored streamers of silk flutter from the steel girders of the gates and birds of all varieties float about as they watch the activities unfold around them. These docks are one of the key components of Xaxis's success. Traders and adventurers of all sorts are able to use these docks to house their airships and stop off for the necessary supplies for their journeys. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15884}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15886}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{This is the southwestern corner of the streets of Xaxis. The streets continue to the east and north. Just west of here stands a group of palm trees, whose trunks rise into the heat of the desert sky towards their leafy fronds. These fronds offer shade over the circles of rich black soil that surround the base of each tree. The soil fills deep hollows dug from the surface of the floating city into its hidden depths below. Beside each tree is a golden cistern holding water which is used by the local gardeners charged with the upkeep of the city's flora. An almost hidden path of red stone leads past the trees into a guard house that these trees are meant to decorate and camouflage. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15884}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15887}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15888}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15887}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{A large amount of desert flora grows alongside the flagstoned street underfoot. Cacti of several types stand between the shops, their needles sharp amidst the pink flowers growing from their thick green skins. Palm trees offer a modicum of shade where they stand tall between the golden walls of the city and the street where you now stand. The shops that do business within this portion of the street look relatively busy, but don't seem to offer much of interest to a traveler such as yourself. Perhaps more intriguing commerce can be found to the north or south where the street continues. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15886}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15889}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15888}{0}{}{<< Guardhouse of Xaxis >> (e)}{💂}{In stark contrast to the bright sunlight outside on the streets, the light within this small enclosed room is very dim. The walls of this building are made of jet black stone. The structure houses the guards that keep Xaxis safe from invasion. Along the walls are sconces holding torches and a long stone bench occupies the wall opposite the open doorway leading back out into the city. The room is intentionally sparse, meant to keep the guards' focus on their duty rather than any unnecessary stimuli. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15886}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15889}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,s,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The squat stone buildings containing the shops of Xaxis are sparse here. In their place are gardens of cacti. The tall spiny plants line the western side of the street, blocking your view of most of the city's wall. To the east lies a side street that leads deeper into the heart of the city while the main thoroughfare continues to the north and south. Sand blows gently along the ground at your feet, disturbed by the slight desert breeze that stirs the day's heat but does nothing to cool the scorching temperature. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15887}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15890}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15891}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15890}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (n,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{Interspersed between low buildings of stone and clay on either side of the street are tents of various shades of red and gold. The buildings contain some of the local shops while the tents provide housing for some of the city's tradesmen and workers. Occasionally the desert wind blows down the street, ruffling the fabric of the tents and sending sand skittering down the hot flagstones underfoot. Voices carry on the wind, as the locals go about their business, paying you little attention. The street continues to the north and south. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15889}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15893}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15891}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{This avenue is even livelier than the busy street to the west. People come in and out of the inns and pubs that line the street, stumbling about on the hot flagstones as they attempt to gather their senses in the bright sunshine after having just left the much cooler and darker confines of such establishments as The Flying Oasis which lies a bit further to the east. For any adventurer seeking rest and refreshment from the scorching desert heat, this portion of the city seems ripe with opportunity. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15889}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15892}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15892}{0}{<238>}{<< The Flying Oasis >> (w)}{<238>[P]<088>}{This dimly lit pub is much cooler than the desert heat outside. Fans hang from the ceiling, blowing air across the room. The floor is a bit gritty, no doubt from sand tracked in by the pub's many patrons. Tables and chairs are set up throughout the interior, providing plenty of seating for the pub's thirsty clientele. A menu hangs over a long stone counter that graces the wall farthest from the door. Behind the counter stands a smiling bartender awaiting your order. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15891}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15893}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (s,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{This is the northwestern corner of the streets of Xaxis. The streets continue to the east and south. To the west stands a cluster of palm trees, their trunks rising up into the sky towards their healthy green fronds. Circles of rich black soil surround the base of each tree, the soil apparently filling deep hollows dug from the surface of the floating city. Beside each tree is a golden cistern holding water for the local gardeners charged with the upkeep of this beautiful flora. A small path of red stone leads past the trees into the half-hidden guard house that these trees are meant to decorate and camouflage. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15890}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15894}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15895}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15894}{0}{}{<< Guardhouse of Xaxis >> (e)}{💂}{The light is dim within this small enclosed room. Made of jet black stone, this building houses the guards that keep Xaxis safe from invasion. Torches sit in sconces along the walls and a long bench occupies the wall opposite the open doorway that leads back out onto the streets. There is very little to see here as the room is intended to keep the guards' focus on their duty rather than any unnecessary stimuli. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15893}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15895}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{Cone-shaped buildings standing well over forty feet high line the street on either side. These bright red structures serve as housing to some of the city's clerics and priests. High overhead, the desert sun burns down upon you, brightening the day to a near blinding state. The warm flagstones of the street underfoot send waves of heat undulating across your vision, further impairing your ability to accurately discern what lies ahead. The outer walls of the city, seen now and again from between the conical houses, glitter in their golden splendor, a testament to Xaxis's wealth and power. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15893}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15896}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15896}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (se,w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{The multitude of merchants is a bit thinner on this portion of the streets in comparison to the city's entrance which lies further off to the east. In place of the hundreds of vending carts are cone-shaped domiciles, strange buildings painted a garish red that rise into the bright sunshine above the flagstoned streets. The buildings stand in clusters just inside the city walls and appear to be the homes of some of Xaxis's population. The vendors that peddle this portion of the city seem a bit more sedate, almost as if they deemed this area and its inhabitants as more worthy of respect than those closer to the city's gates. The street continues both east and west. A thinner avenue leads off toward the southeast. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15895}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15897}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15860}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15897}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (se,nw)}{<278>- -<088>}{This avenue is much quieter than the busy street to the northwest. Thick hedges of thorn-filled bushes grow on either side of the flagstones, preventing anyone from wandering off the intended path. The avenue itself is also slightly different from the main streets of the city. The edges between each well-fitted stone are painted in gold. Further to the southeast stands the destination of this quiet boulevard, the most dominating structure in Xaxis, the Auruetian Tower. Its golden walls shine in the bright sunshine and emanate a magical power. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15896}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15898}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15898}{0}{<278>}{<< The Streets of Xaxis >> (enter,nw,ne)}{🗼}{This is the location of the true heart of Xaxis,  the Auruetian Tower. It stands at the tip of this street, a monument to the power of the sun. Its glistening walls of gold tower into the sky, reaching for the heavens, and tempting those that believe they have the strength to enter its magical boundaries and learn its profound secrets. The hedge surrounding the tower borders the street, allowing passage only into the tower or back towards the main city streets to the northeast and northwest. Do not doubt that the mysteries within this tower are far more dangerous than anything you'll meet on the relative safety of the streets around you. Enter at your own peril. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15863}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15899}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15897}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15899}{0}{}{<< The Auruetian Tower >> (exit,sw,se)}{ }{You stand inside the entrance to the Auruetian Tower. The doorway leading back outside remains open while large archways lead deeper into the tower both to the southeast and southwest. The room is very large, the ceiling easily twenty five feet overhead. The archways are probably thirty paces beyond the doorway. The floor is quite interesting, almost mesmerizing. Light seems to sizzle across it, shooting from one end of the room to the other in lightning quick bolts. A light hum vibrates along the floor and echoes off the walls which appear to be solid gold. The only decoration in the room is on the ceiling. Painted overhead is a giant sun, blazing gold and white like a giant glowing eye staring down upon you. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15901}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15902}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15898}{exit}{exit}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15900}{4104}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {15902}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15901}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15901}{0}{}{<< The Auruetian Tower >> (e,ne)}{ }{The strangest of sights stands before you. Sand seems to seep from the center of this room's ceiling, inching its way along the ceiling until it reaches the walls. From there, it slides down the golden surfaces before falling to the floor where it sifts back and forth with the electric charged bolts of light that sizzle from one end of the room to the other. The whole effect is amazing. Perhaps even more mystifying, amongst all of this sand, a marble dining table and chairs stand in the center of the room, spotless. Not a speck of sand mars the table's surface or dusts the matching chairs. There is no doubt, a very strong magic resides in this tower. Perhaps you should leave before you come across its source. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15899}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15900}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15902}{0}{}{<< The Auruetian Tower >> (u,nw,w)}{ }{Without visible cause, sand seeps from the center of this room's ceiling, clinging to its surface as it moves to the edges of room where the ceiling meets the golden walls. From there, it slides down the walls before drifting to the floor where it sifts back and forth with the electric charged bolts of light that sizzle from one end of the room to the other. This magic spectacle continues unending, the sand apparently stemming from a limitless source. Untouched by the sand are several couches that sit in this room as if for guests to await the tower's master. It seems a bit absurd given the tower's menacing air, but they sit here nonetheless. On the eastern end of the room is a wide staircase that ascends to the second floor of the tower. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15899}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15903}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15900}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15903}{0}{}{<< The Auruetian Tower >> (d,nw,w)}{ }{This rather bare room only holds a couple of plain stone tables in its center. They look like laboratory tables, thick, cold, and sterile. Much more interesting than the room's sparse furnishings are its walls. They're covered with drawers, literally hundreds of them lining the walls from floor to ceiling. Each is made of matching gray stone set into the golden walls. Each is decorated solely by its plain black handle. These drawers probably hold instruments and ingredients for the master of this tower's magic spells. Arched doorways lead to other parts of the tower both to the west and northwest while an onyx staircase leads back down to the floor below. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15902}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15904}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15906}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15904}{0}{}{<< The Auruetian Tower >> (se,sw)}{ }{This appears to be some sort of sauna. Like the other rooms on this floor, the walls are gleaming gold while the floor and ceiling and made of gray stone. However, in the middle of the floor is a large pool of what appears to be liquid gold, shiny enough to match the walls. From this pool billow clouds of golden-hued steam that waft throughout the room, making clear vision difficult. Hanging from the walls are several onyx reliefs of various symbols. A few are recognizable, a diamond, a cross, a dragon, a ring, while others are completely foreign to your understanding. Spaced between the reliefs are torches, their light diffused by the steam, but still enough to see by. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15903}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15905}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15905}{0}{}{<< The Auruetian Tower >> (u,ne,e)}{ }{You've stepped inside one of the Auruetian Tower's many libraries. Books cover shelves that line every wall floor to ceiling. Several reading tables sit in the room, many of which are also covered in books. Comfortable leather-bound chairs sit beside the tables although none of them are occupied at present. The room has a bit of a musty smell, likely from the age of some of the books, several being quite ancient. The walls match those throughout the tower, solid gold that gleams slightly in the torchlight, while the ceiling and floor are made of simple gray stone. A white marble staircase ascends from the western corner of this room up to the next floor of the tower. }{Xaxis}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15906}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15904}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15907}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

