R {15991}{0}{}{Aracel's Tower (exit,u)}{ }{Aracel's Tower Standing within the entrance to Aracel's tower, your attention is immediately drawn to the walls of the structure.  Made of a translucent material, they are tinged green due to the sunlight and vast amount of foliage outside.  All along the walls are rivulets of liquid silver that stream from the ceiling to the floor before collecting into a hidden pump and starting the cycle over again.  These shiny rivulets look like a sort of magical rain that nourishes the trees that crowd the inner portion of the room.  The trees are so plentiful, you'd think you were still outside if it weren't for the walls and the spiraling silver staircase that stands in the middle of the room, beckoning you to explore the tower's heights. }{Isle of Equinity}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15993}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15986}{exit}{exit}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15992}{0}{<278>}{Medlar Approach (e,w)}{<278>- -<088>}{The cliffs fall away from you here, and are not so sheer up above you. You can now see that the sky is overcast and there is a cold breeze beginning to blow. The path you are following looks very heavily used, but it seems to be much larger than it really needs to be. To the east the path becomes a narrow passage between the cliffs, and to the west the land starts to widen out a bit more. }{Medlar Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1769}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15994}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15993}{0}{}{Aracel's Tower (d)}{ }{Aracel's Tower The top end of the winding silver staircase leads to a mass of vines and plants, their green tendrils snaking along the floor and twisting around the upper rungs of the stairs.  Through the wild foliage lies an open circular area with a large design painted on the floor.  The design features several concentric rings surrounding a single golden tree.  Over and around the entire room is a huge glass dome, acting as walls and ceiling for this solarium.  On the far side of the room sits a five foot high cauldron centered on a round platform that glows red with heat. }{Isle of Equinity}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15991}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15994}{0}{<278>}{Approach to Medlar (nw,e)}{<278>-+-<088>}{A hill rises up in front of you, it looks very rocky and hard to climb. The cliffs flank the hill on both sides. It looks like the only way up is to the northwest. The vegetation is very  sparse, and the wind is picking up. It is getting cold. }{Medlar Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15992}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15995}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15995}{0}{<278>}{Approach to Medlar (n,se)}{<278>- -<088>}{As you top the hill you are blasted by a frigid wind and pelted by small hail stones. It is very hard to make out anything that is more than twenty paces away. What you can see is that the hill slopes down and away from you here to the north and west, and there is some kind of large path leading down the hill to the north. }{Medlar Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15994}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15996}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {15996}{0}{<278>}{Approach to Medlar (w,s,n)}{<278>- -<088>}{The large path continues both up and down this incline. The wind is now cutting through your clothing, and you are getting covered in fresh snow. You can see a very large footprint in the snow on the path, heading down hill. Off to the north and west you can  just make out a big shadow of some kind of structure looming off in the distance.}{Medlar Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15995}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15997}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
