R {16007}{0}{}{Approach to Medlar (e)}{b}{The wall of the castle rises up to the north. To the west and south there is a very dense grove of evergreen trees. It looks very dark in among their trunks. There is a bit more wind here and the snow is swirling about, making it very difficult to see much of anything. }{Medlar Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {16004}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16008}{0}{<278>}{Courtyard (e,n,w,s)}{<278>( )<088>}{The snow falls quietly around you here. The hard packed ground is covered over with newly fallen snow, although you can see many large footprints in it. To the north you can see the castle proper with an immense door in the front. To the south are the castle gates, and the courtyard continues on around you both east and west. }{Medlar Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
