R {16515}{0}{}{Beside the light ocean (n,s,se,e)}{ }{Though night is well advanced, light seems to softly glow from nothing, or everything; perhaps both at once.  Tall and straight, trees rise like skyscrapers from the land to touch the sky.  Ocean far and ocean wide, pulsing, living with the tide.  Like a beacon in the endless ocean, an island swathed in light lies far to the northwest.  Often glimpsed, but never to be touched, the moon is awash with nothing but luminescence.  A piercing call, sending a ray of light dancing in the night, echoes from nearby. }{Night of Colour}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
