R {16710}{0}{<248>}{A dark cave (leave)}{<248>% %<088>}{You stand at the bottom of a hole, which ascends upwards into darkness.  The cave is somewhat larger down here than that above, the scratch-like gouges even deeper than seen previously.  The stench is abominably bad down here, which seems to be emanating from the north passage. }{Rimalkins Cave 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1617}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16711}{512}{}{Rocky Tundra (leave,proceed)}{ }{You are standing not far off from the base of Trophea's Peak.  Rocks of varying shapes and sizes surround you, all of which seem to have shaken loose (or been thrown from) the peak of the volcano itself.  Legend tells of how the Dragon Queen Trophea birthed her only son, Nussicon, upon this very peak.  When the immortals came down to praise the dragon-child, the denizens of the 9 hells seized the opportunity to engage them in an epic battle for the 7 heavens.  Trophea fled with her newborn child while the good and evil immortals battled on, nearly tearing the mountain down.  It is not clear how the battle ended but there are rumors that the elder gods, of both realms, were not in favor of this conflict and snapped the astral links of all participants.  This sudden shattering of the link between mortal and immortal realms left a permanent rift between the two realities.  It is said that if you ascend the mountain to Trophea's Peak that you, too, could become immortal... }{The Ascended Guild}{}{}{}{1000.000}{1}
E {404}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {16712}{proceed}{proceed}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16712}{0}{}{Trophea's Peak (leave)}{ }{The desolate rocky base of Trophea's Peak thrusts itself out of the surrounding plainlands.  Little grows at the base of the mountain but further up magnificent trees can be seen proudly offering their blossoms up in honor of the gods.  There is an eerie quiet as if even the birds and insects have taken an oath of silence or perhaps have been dumbstruck.  Occasionally the entire mountain quakes and trembles as the inhabitants atop go about their godly business.  The sun hangs low in comparison to Trophea's Peak as the very summit transcends even the clouds.  A treacherous path up the mountain exists but seems at times to disappear, forcing any would-be climber to scale the mountain with hands and feet alone.  Those who wish to attempt the climb may 'ascend'.  There are also 4 statues here that can be examined for more information on the immortal forms. }{The Ascended Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {16711}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {16713}{proceed}{proceed}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16713}{0}{}{Trophea's Forge (e,w)}{ }{Named for the Dragoness who gave this mountain its name as well as the fine shop that has been established by Aggalaggia, this is not only the forge at which the immortal races are able have their gear modified, but also the central corridor of the immense mountain home.  Tapestries the size of the mortal buildings hang from the walls, unable to reach the floor far below.  The dome-like apex in the ceiling opens to the sky above\; the sunlight reflects blindingly off of several of the smithing implements that Aggalaggia has gathered for his work.  You can 'modify' your armors and weapons to be large enough to fit your form or grip.  Similarly you can 'unmodify' them to reduce them back to mortal sizes.  A large cave opening can be seen off to the west. }{The Ascended Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {16712}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {16714}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16714}{0}{}{Stonesplinter's Stock (e,n,s)}{ }{The arsenal of the Ascended beings holds all those items that other immortals have found beneficial to their cause.  Stonesplinter stands guard over the collection and seems a bit new at his post.  The cavernous storehouse goes on for miles to make room for the massive hauls of treasure the Ascendeds are known for collecting.  There are torches on the walls but they are little needed with the amount of direct sunlight streaming in through window-like openings.  Stonesplinter looks at you, ready to assist. }{The Ascended Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {16713}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {16715}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {16716}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16715}{0}{}{Legends Cavern (s)}{ }{This absolutely enormous cavern is home to hundreds of thousands, if not millions, of tapestries.  Walls are honeycombed throughout the cavern to provide space to hang them.  Upon these tapestries can be found the history of this world from the perspective of dragonkind.  They chronicle the dawn of the age of man, and the rise and fall of empires.  They display graphics of the rise of mountains, the slow roll of the oceans, and the hue changes of the sky over the millenia.  Unfortunately the tapestries are not in any order that makes sense to anyone but the dragons that placed them here.  It's clear that, at first, the tapestries were merely hung around the room clockwise-ish, and when they ran out of room they hung some higher, then lower, then added some interior walls of granite to hang some more.  This has gone on for so long that the ensuing order of tapestries is essentially random.  Additionally, the great bulk of them are completely uninteresting.  For instance there are probably 5000 of them dedicated completely to how quiet things were before humanoids were introduced.  There is a tiny sign up near the entrance that you can read. }{The Ascended Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {16714}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16716}{0}{}{a quiet alcove (n)}{ }{You are in an enormous open cavern.  From a dragon's perspective, this is considered an alcove.  But, it has been furnished with a variety of chairs, tables, desks, and bookcases large enough to fit an Ascended comfortably.  The other remarkable aspect of this alcove is how quiet it is.  Even the tiniest of muffled whispers would be heard throughout the cavern if it weren't for the apparent magical dampening in this place. }{The Ascended Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {16714}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16717}{0}{}{Time twist (s)}{<158>M<088>}{As you enter this room you notice a strange instability in time.  The sun flickers back and forth crazily in the sky.  You consider the shuddering of the scenery to the south, and wonder if it's safe to go that way. Who knows where... or indeed WHEN you could end up? There is a strange purple looking mist here. }{Land of the Dinosaurs}{land_of_the_dinosaurs}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {16718}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3113}{enter mist}{enter mist}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {16718}{0}{}{Arid environment (sw,n,s,e,climb)}{<238>C<088>}{You find yourself in an arid environment\; the ground is hard and rocky and the air above it shimmers in the heat.  The shimmering to the north seems slightly different, though.  You can hardly see through it at all... The hot, dry land continues to the east, but to the south and southwest you see greenery.  In all directions, except back to the north, you notice large creatures moving about. }{Land of the Dinosaurs}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
