R {17444}{0}{}{Oak Street (n,s)}{ }{   Oak street runs north/south, through some of the more seedy parts of town.  The Springfield Police Station is nearby however, and is ready to strike into full effect should anything 'go down', as it were.  Such rhetoric is unknown in this cartoon world however.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {50824}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {50825}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17445}{0}{}{Springfield Avenue (n,s,w,enter)}{<168>E<088>}{   Oak Street banks west and turns into Springfield Avenue at this junction.  The main building flanking the cul-de-sac is the Springfield Police Station, where the finest minds in the city come together to solve crime and drink a little coffee, eat a little danish, you know, just a nosh.  Springfield Avenue begins here and leads west, straight to the Power Plant.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {50824}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51126}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17447}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17448}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17448}{e}{enter}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17446}{0}{}{The gates of Burns Manor (n,w)}{ }{    A massive iron gate blocks the road here, through which you can see the sprawling grounds of Burns Manor.  The Manor house sits high on the hill, lights twinkling from its many windows. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51126}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17449}{w}{open gates;w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17447}{0}{}{Springfield Avenue (w,e)}{ }{   Springfield Avenue leads directly to the Springfield Nuclear Power Plant.  In the real world, and even more esoterically, the entire town leads to the plant.  The prosperity and wealth of its people depends on the plant.  If the reactor goes down, the people of Springfield go down with it.  Figuratively of course.  This is all figurative you realize. Good.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17445}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17452}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17448}{0}{}{The Springfield Police Station (s,w)}{ }{Police officers scuttle back and forth in the distance, fetching their coffee as the subtle sounds of Muzak gently ease your brain into submission.  This is the Springfield Police Station, where crimes are solved over long periods of time and coffee is spilled over important documents.  There is a set of chairs here for waiting to report the crime done unto you, and a desk in front of you is where all the serious work gets ignored.  A revolving door leads outside to the west, and a doorway with a sign that reads 'Authorized personnel only' leads south.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17445}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17450}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17449}{0}{}{The grounds of Burns Manor (s,e)}{ }{    The grounds of Burns Manor are very well tended.  Perfect green grass, neatly trimmed trees, immaculate paths and gleaming fountains complement each other.  The massive bulk of Burns Manor is to the south, and the gates to the east. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17446}{e}{open gates;e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17470}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17450}{0}{}{Chief Wiggum's Office (enter,n)}{<168>E<088>}{This office is the workplace of one Police Chief Wiggum, the pride of all Springfield.  It is at this desk that some of Springfield's most unsolvable crimes remain unsolved.  Papers are everywhere, most of which have coffee stains all over them.  There is a temporary holding cell to the south where criminals may meet with their lawyers under Wiggum's supervision of course.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17448}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17451}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17451}{s}{enter}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17451}{0}{}{A Holding Cell (out)}{<168>O<088>}{This cell is extremely dirty and scummy, from hundreds of dirty scummy people residing here for extended periods of time.  The metal bars prevent the inmates from strangling anyone outside the cell, although those inside are fair game.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17450}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17450}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17452}{0}{}{The Springfield Nuclear Power Plant Parking Lot (e,enter)}{<168>E<088>}{The Springfield Nuclear Power Plant casts an immense shadow over both you and the entire parking lot you stand in.  The  absolutely momumental twin reactor housings tower above the rest of the world like gigantic bombs, waiting to annihilate the universe. Directly in front of you, the grey monolith of the control building invites both workers and visitors alike to tour its halls in naivete, unknowing and oblivious to the vast crime on the environment and on humanity that this entire compound commits.  Very few windows allow the sacriligious solar energy to infiltrate their synthetic world of radioactivity, but a revolving door allows you the opportunity to observe the power for yourself.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17447}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17453}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17453}{w}{enter}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17453}{0}{}{The Springfield Nuclear Power Plant (n,s,w,out)}{ }{Even in this age of technology, the concurrence of nuclear power and worldwide corruption is conspicuous.  Towering metal walls, sterile and clean in their arcs above you, confine this main lobby area hugely.  There is one main hallway which leads off north and south from this point, and a workroom directly to the west of where you stand.  Banners and various other pieces of propaganda attempt to quell the notion that atomic power is at all...dangerous.  One very prominent in-house advertisement hanging above your head states 'Nuclear Energy and you: Perfect Together'.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17454}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17455}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17456}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17452}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17452}{e}{out}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17454}{0}{}{North Hallway of the Nuclear Power Plant (s,w)}{ }{   Various functions and jobs are carried out within the rooms which line this hallway, none of which concern you in even the slightest. The massive, imposing lobby is ever-present to the south, while the hall takes an extremely sharp turn west here.  You get the impression that maybe the hallway to the west was not intended for visitors such as yourself.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17453}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17458}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17455}{0}{}{South Hallway of the Nuclear Power Plant (w,n)}{ }{   The carefully-engineered sounds of MUZAK waft sweetly across the idle walls in this spartan hall.  The massive lobby is visible to the north, from where you can hear the echoing footsteps of a human being in the process of walking.  There is a workroom to the west that appears to be emitting lots of beeps and whirrs.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17453}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17457}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17456}{0}{}{Carl and Lenny's Workroom (e)}{ }{   The console is full of all sorts of buttons and lights and whatnot! It is all sparkly and pretty and bright, and the neato nifty keen buttons and levers and dials and switches... really makes you want to instigate a nuclear disaster.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17453}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17457}{0}{}{Homer's Workroom (e)}{ }{   True to the irony of George Jetson's predicament... that of a capable man whose job is to merely push one button repeatedly all day...Homer Simpson's console resembles the cockpit of a 747.  Yet Homer's capabilities lie barely in brushing his teeth, let alone controlling deadly nuclear reactions and atomic radiation. A broken-down stool is the only furniture in the entire room.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17455}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17458}{0}{}{A Narrow Hallway (w,e)}{ }{   As you walk through this hallway, you get the feeling that this part of the reactor isn't exactly meant for casual touring. It does not seem as frequented as the other areas, and there is a sign on the wall which says 'This Area Not For Casual Touring' which heightens this intuition somewhat.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17454}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17459}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17459}{0}{}{A Restricted Area (s,e)}{ }{   Now you realize that this is a place in which you TRULY do not belong...red and white striped bands line the room in obvious warning, and a sign attached to the wall beside you demands attention.  Notice that the sign shows up even if you are lazy and are exploring in brief mode.  I am TOO nice.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17458}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17460}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17460}{0}{}{**A Restricted Area** (n,s)}{ }{   This room is tiny...the steel walls seem rough, as if they have been dented, scraped and marred and then been made to look as if they had endured no such weathering.  You can even discern a faint patch of blood on the floor which could not be totally cleaned.  A square metal tunnel leads through the south wall, and the dire stench of death seems less upon you to the north.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17459}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17461}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17461}{0}{}{**A Restricted Area** (u,n)}{ }{   Spikes jut out from the wall, preventing you from leaning up against them for any reason.  The floor is a slick blue metal alloy, creating a bind...if you slip you had better not fall into the wall.  In general, the appearance of this room reinforces the idea of 'restricted'.  A metal lattice stairway leads up to another area which you might guess is quite restricted as well.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17460}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17462}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17462}{0}{}{**A VERY Restricted Area** (d,n)}{ }{   Torn bits of human flesh are scattered about the floor here, making this room resemble a slaughterhouse.  Caked innards lend much ambience to the walls and ceiling, and slimy brown marrow and busted bone parts crackle underfoot.  A metal lattice staircase leads down to the first level, and a hand-shaped archway is set into the north flesh-colored wall.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17461}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17463}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17463}{0}{}{**A VERY Restricted AREA** (n,s)}{ }{   Ghostly gray tapestries line the interior of this square chamber.  A sickly chill numbs your knees as the howling of distant spirits bewitches you utterly.  A mistlike curtain to the north conceals what lies beyond, and a hand-shaped archway leads south.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17462}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17464}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17464}{0}{}{**A VERY Restricted Monkey Area** (s,vine)}{<228>V<088>}{   This room -- decorated strangely and completely with leaves, vines and other such junglish accoutrements -- smells like monkey poo.  Sounds from the wild kingdom echo far in the distance as you step in a pile of chimp chechre.  A thick vine leads up into a hole in the ceiling, while a mistlike curtain provides an exit south.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17463}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17465}{vine}{vine}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17465}{0}{}{**An UNBELIEVABLY Restricted Area** (d,s)}{ }{   The walls are covered in sweet, SWEEEET honey!  It drips from the ceiling, slips and slides down the walls...your salivary glands swell at the sight and aroma of all this sweet, natural sugar.  You wonder where all this honey came from!  A hole in the floor leads down to a vine, and a veritable waterfall of honey piques your curiosity as to what lies beyond it.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17464}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17466}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17466}{0}{}{**An UNBELIEVABLY Restricted Area** (n,s)}{ }{   This room is painted completely red!  On top of the red facade has been painted numerous yellow lightning bolts... is this just a motif representing the energy generated by the reactor core of the power plant?  Or does it signify something else... something more...fictional?  A lightning bolt-shaped doorway leads to the south. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17465}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17467}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17467}{0}{}{**A MONUMENTALLY Restricted Area** (u,n)}{ }{   This room, in stark raving contrast with its predecessors, is elegant and Victorian.  Finely crafted furniture with plush surfaces and polished burgundy woods rest atop a marvelous parquet floor.  A suit of armour provides period decoration, whilst a chandelier beset with heart-faceted Austrian crystals and Brazilian sapphire dust illuminates the room with posh brilliance.  A very stately hand-carved circular staircase leads up to somewhere special.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17466}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17468}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17468}{0}{}{The Private Office of Mr. Burns (d)}{ }{   The evil in the air is monumental here.  You feel the goodness of every man, woman and child who has ever walked this earth, and you feel it evaporate within these walls.  The ceiling, a full 30 feet above your head, is painted a dark red hue, and the walls, lined with extremely valuable birch panels, surrounds a room the size of football field.  You can feel your heartbeat echo endlessly through the expanses of this monumental office, at the head of which is but a simple desk, behind which rests a simple leather chair. A giant stuffed polar bear looks over the proceedings, its claws outstretched and its jaw open, fangs bared, ready to feast upon the dead. A huge picture window overlooks the power plant, and the dark pall of black smoke which wafts from the reactor housing's heights enforces its stranglehold on the defenseless community of Springfield as you stand with awe at this occasion.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17467}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17469}{push button}{push button}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17469}{0}{}{Within the Reactor Core Housing}{ }{   The temperature is unbearable as you are bathed with the green fumes of radioactive decay.  You stand within an immense cement tower set eerily aglow from the green sparks that leap about before you. You stand on a metal grate that shakes slightly beneath your feet, both from the tremors coming from the machinery and from the fear you hold that this is the most dangerous situation you have ever had nightmare enough in which to be caught.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17452}{move grate}{move grate}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17470}{0}{}{The door to Burns Manor (n,w)}{ }{    A set of wide marble steps lead up to the doorway to Burns' Manor. The white doors are massive, each made from thick wood and set with an impressive bronze handle.  There are two dog kennels set just to the side of the doors. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17449}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17471}{w}{open door;w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17471}{0}{}{Inside Burns Manor (u,n,s,e)}{ }{    The entrance hall of Burns Manor is a massive room, lit by a large chandelier that hangs from the ceiling.  Two large statues flank either side of a wide staircase that leads up to the second floor.  A large persian rug has been placed in the center of the marble floors.  Archways lead off from here to other parts of the mansion. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17470}{e}{open door;e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17472}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
