R {17473}{0}{}{Dining room (s)}{ }{    A massive wooden table stretches over thirty feet across the dining room.  Two chairs, one positioned at each end, demonstrate that Mr. Burns is not one for visitors.  Several animal trophies have been hung on the walls, and there is a large fire dancing in the fireplace. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17471}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17477}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17474}{0}{}{Living room (n)}{ }{    This is Mr. Burns' living room, a massive space filled with all the comforts he could ask for.  Soft lounges, comfortable reading chairs, a massive TV and shelves of books are all scattered around the room.  There is a large fireplace next to one of the chairs, complete with a roaring fire.  A large set of armour stands in one corner. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17471}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17475}{0}{}{Mr. Burns' room (e)}{ }{    Mr. Burns' private bedroom is mostly occupied by his massive four poster bed.  The rest of the room contains a bedside table, a mirror and a large window overlooking the grounds.  There is also a massive wardrobe standing open, in which you can see a variety of strange garments.  There is a laundry chute tactfully concealed in one corner of the room. }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
