R {17485}{0}{}{-=\x7D Jugglers' Ring \x7B=- (s,nw)}{ }{The second ring is cluttered with chainsaws, plates, fiery torches, and clubs.  This must be where the jugglers perform their amazing feats.  You also see two unicycles for the truly daring juggler.  One is short and the other is about six feet tall.  You've tried to juggle balls before but to no avail, and have always found juggling one of life's great mysteries. }{Billy Bob's Big Top Circus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17483}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17487}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17486}{0}{}{-=\x7D Prancing Horses Ring \x7B=- (w)}{ }{One of the fanciest rings you've ever seen.  Small spotlights with colorful gels in them sit on the ground lighting up the ring.  Sequined saddles lie in a row.  Bits of chewed apples are scattered around.  A small horse crop lies next to the saddles.  It is only used as a noise maker, never to hit the horses. }{Billy Bob's Big Top Circus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17483}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17487}{0}{}{-=\x7D Clown's Ring \x7B=- (sw,se)}{ }{-=\x7D Clown's Ring \x7B=- This ring is jammed packed with funny horns, seltzer bottles, big red shoes, and tiny cars.  Yeah, the clown ring.  You love clowns.  They make you laugh, cry, giggle, and sigh.  On the left side of the ring is a long table with a bunch of cream pies.  You always wanted to get hit with one of those. }{Billy Bob's Big Top Circus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17485}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17488}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17488}{0}{}{-=\x7D Trapeze Ring \x7B=- (se,sw,ne)}{ }{-=\x7D Trapeze Ring \x7B=- This is the high flying trapeze ring.  Two tall poles with small platforms attached to them stand inside the ring.  Single bar swings dangle from a thick cable in the top of the tent.  A safety net hangs from ropes tied to the poles.  This is one of the more death defying circus acts. }{Billy Bob's Big Top Circus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
