R {17507}{0}{}{~o~ Along the bank of the River Isis ~o~ (nw,se)}{ }{Along the bank of the River Isis The sun is shining in the crystalline English winter twilight\; only a few wispy grey clouds can be seen.  The rolling countryside is coated in soft white snow, with the occasional tree and hedge poking out of the blanket.  The river is to the southwest and bends gently here.  Its surface is frosty and frozen. A footpath heads along the bank of the river towards the southeast.  Towards the northwest is a strange icy fog.  As though normalcy is completely dissolving, it's difficult to focus properly on anything, and it's almost as though this space is overlapping with some other place that happens to be filled with curious bush shapes. }{Looking-Glass Land}{looking_glass_land}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17500}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17508}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17508}{0}{}{~o~ Along the bank of the River Isis ~o~ (sw,e,nw,ne)}{ }{Along the bank of the River Isis This bit of the river bank is broad and flat, a vast expense of white snow.  A few travelers can be seen trudging through the snowy paths, going to and fro.  Icicle-coated trees line the river bank. The widest path leads up a gentle slope to the northeast, where one can see the stone snow-capped tops of the buildings in Oxford.  The foot path follows the river around to the northwest and east.  A wooden bridge crosses the river to the southwest. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17507}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17509}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17510}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17511}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17509}{0}{}{~o~ Outside the Liddells' cottage ~o~ (s,sw,ne)}{ }{Outside the Liddells' cottage Nestled in the gently rolling hills to the southwest of the River Isis is the Liddells' cottage.  The two story house is one of many modest homes in the area.  Warm light shines through the windows, and dark smoke curls from the chimney. Snow has been shoveled on either side of a cobblestone path leading to the front porch of the house south of here.  A walkway leads around the house to the yard in the southwest.  The track back to the river leads off to the northeast. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17508}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17513}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17514}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17510}{0}{}{~o~ In the bushes near the River Isis ~o~ (w)}{ }{In the bushes near the River Isis Everything here takes on a cool bluish glow from the bright sunshine reflecting up from the snow.  The shade from the foliage makes this area rather secluded. Even though the river continues towards the east, the path seems to end here due to the cramped bushes and trees.  Snow covers the ground and there's little evidence of anything passing recently.  A largish hedge seems to stick out for some reason. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17508}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17511}{0}{}{~o~ Christ Church, Oxford ~o~ (e,sw)}{ }{Christ Church bears the distinction of not only being a cathedral, but also a major college of the University of Oxford.  The buildings are truly stunning, bearing the somber and serious air of the combination of religion and study.  Students rush between doorways, most of them seem to be rather late given the pace they're going.  The quad is covered in bright snow. Through the gates is a snow-covered track leading towards the River Isis to the southwest.  The mathematics classrooms are in a nearby building just to the east. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17508}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17512}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17512}{0}{}{~o~ Logic Classroom, Christ Church, Oxford ~o~ (out)}{ }{Logic Classroom This is a classroom in the mathematics hall in Christ Church.  Daylight streams through the windows, illuminating dust motes in the air, giving the entire space an almost unearthly shimmering brilliance.  It's full of wooden desks for students. The room is a bit more cluttered than many of the others nearby - the bookshelves are full of not only math books, but also poetry and stories.  In one corner is a collection of complicated looking photographic equipment.  There are three slate blackboards at one end of the room.  The teacher's desk at the other end is covered with a hodge podge of papers. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17511}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17511}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17513}{0}{}{~o~ The Liddell drawing room ~o~ (u,n)}{ }{The Liddell drawing room The drawing room of this cozy house is lit by oil sconces.  There's a gorgeous wooden table between two green sofas.  Some dark coats are hung up on the wooden coat rack, and there are a number of bookshelves filled with leatherbound books.  A china cabinet is in one corner, filled with bright teacups and a silver tea service.  The winter landscape can be seen through the tall bay windows. The door out is to the north, and there's a staircase that goes upstairs. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17509}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17515}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17514}{0}{}{~o~ Beside the Liddells' cottage ~o~ (w,ne)}{ }{Beside the Liddells' cottage The snow-lined cobblestone path leading beside the Liddells' cottage is dimly lit in the winter dusk.  The path winds to the front of the house towards the northeast, and then into a secluded garden to the west.  Trees line the western side of the path, and little drifts of snow are everywhere. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17509}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17516}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17515}{0}{}{~o~ Upstairs in the Liddells' cottage ~o~ (d)}{ }{}{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17513}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17517}{crawl through glass}{push chair;crawl through glass}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17516}{0}{}{~o~ The Liddells' garden ~o~ (e)}{ }{The Liddells' garden A small snow-covered garden lies just to the west of the Liddells' cottage.  A cobblestone path winds from the side of the house to the east and makes a loop around a thick tree in the center of the garden.  The branches of gracefully curving trees make the garden still and secluded.  A few stalks from dead flowers can be seen poking up through the snow.  There's a glass gazing ball on a short pedestal in one corner. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17514}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17517}{0}{}{~o~ Upstairs in the Liddells' cottage ~o~ (d)}{ }{The Looking-Glass House - upstairs How curious!  Everything within view of the looking-glass appears exactly as it did in the Liddells' family room, but things start to get rather strange about the edges.  The most immediately noticeable example of this is the clock - the shape looks the same, but the face, facing away from the mirror, is SMILING at you!  There's still a circle of comfy looking armchairs, with one of them leaned up against the hearth.  There seems to be some kind of commotion over by the chessboard, or at least some wiggling. There aren't any doors in this room, and the only way out appears to be the staircase downwards. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17518}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17515}{crawl through glass}{crawl through glass}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17518}{0}{}{~o~ Downstairs in the Looking-Glass House ~o~ (u,n)}{ }{The Looking-Glass House - downstairs The drawing room of this cozy house is lit by brightly burning oil sconces.  The angles in this room all seem a little off - the broad staircase bends oddly, and none of the corners seem entirely square.  Tall bay windows circling the room look out across the verdant landscape.  A gorgeous claw-footed table is between two red sofas, and a wooden coat rack stands next to the front door to the north. The door out is to the north, and the staircase winds upwards. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17517}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17519}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17519}{0}{}{~o~ outside the Looking-Glass House ~o~ (se,s)}{ }{Outside the Looking-Glass House Nestled in the gently rolling hills is a haphazardly angled white house, poking out in contrast to the colorful landscape.  The sun is bright, high up above in the azure summer sky, radiating warmth down on the lush grasses and tall swaying trees. A gravel walkway between the house and a neatly trimmed hedge goes to the southeast, and the front door of the house is to the south. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17518}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17520}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17520}{0}{}{~o~ entrance to the Garden of Live Flowers ~o~ (e,nw)}{ }{Garden entrance A perfect circle of gravel marks the entrance to the Garden of Live Flowers, with one walkway stretching back around the house to the northwest, and another plunging east into the garden itself.  The trees here arc gracefully overhead, shading the path.  There's a curious stillness here, as if something is waiting for you to make your next move. }{Looking-Glass Land}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
