R {17578}{0}{}{A small, dark crevice (exit)}{ }{There is barely enough room to breathe in this tiny crevice, let alone move around or look at things properly.  It is very dark, and there could well be something alive in here with you and you might never know.  With so little room to move around, you might find it hard to get back out into the freezer.  Then again, you might just pop out like a greased sausage. }{The Sausage Dimensions}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17577}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17577}{exit}{exit}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17577}{w}{exit}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17579}{0}{}{Fire escape on the third floor (s,w,sup)}{ }{   The hotel room through the window to the west seems awfully inviting compared to the frigid gusts of wind that whip about in this sick Manhattan island.  A set of stairs leads south and up to the fourth floor and you could curve around the stairs to the south to continue down the side of the building. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17580}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17582}{sup}{sup}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {2138}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17582}{e}{sup}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17580}{0}{}{Fire escape outside the third floor (n,w,ndown)}{ }{   This rusty brown fire escape makes you pray that no fires actually erupt during your stay here.  A set of stairs leads north and down to the second floor, and the stairs that lead up another floor could only be reached by going north first. You could climb through a window to the west. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17579}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {2137}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17581}{ndown}{ndown}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17581}{0}{}{A fire escape (u,s,w)}{ }{   A set of steps leads up to the next floor to the south, and you could curve around the stairs to access what looks like a ladder that drops down into an alley.  The cooing of pigeons is irritating and the bitter New York air is sending rashes up and down your arms.  You could climb through the window to the west to get out of this wretched atmosphere if you wanted to. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17591}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {2113}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17580}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17582}{0}{}{A fire escape (ndown,n)}{ }{   The window to the west has been bricked up with blocks of white cinder.  You wonder why the fourth floor is restricted so. A set of stairs, brown and rusted, leads north and down to the third floor, and the other end of the fire escape landing is to the north. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17583}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17579}{ndown}{ndown}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17579}{w}{ndown}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17583}{0}{}{Fourth floor fire escape (u,s)}{ }{   A rickety ladder leads up the side of the building onto the roof.  You might want to watch your step.  To the south is the other end of the landing, where you could access a set of stairs that lead down to the third floor. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17582}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17584}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17584}{0}{}{On the roof of the hotel (d,s,w)}{ }{   You gaze up at the smog-hazed sky from this rooftop, your feet treading upon all sorts of schmutz.  Strange large architectural elements prevent you from going in any direction except for west and south.  A ladder leads down the side of the building to the fire escape. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17583}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17585}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17586}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17585}{0}{}{A dead end on the roof of the hotel (n)}{ }{   You are cornered by the protrusions from the roof here... the tar is blotchy and covered with bird poop here...LOTS of bird poop.  You get the feeling that this deserted corner is very popular among the wild pigeons of Manhattan for some reason.  The only way you could go from here is north. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17584}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17586}{0}{}{On the rooftop (s,e)}{ }{  You are surrounded by large, tar-covered cubes that compensate for some architectural elements on the floor below.  The only directions you could travel are east, or south through two large masses.  The view of the city is actually not at all bad...you could enjoy being up here if you really wanted to. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17584}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17587}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17587}{0}{}{The rooftop (w,n)}{ }{   You stand squeezed between two giant black walls which rise above you like giant black monoliths coated with pasty tar.  Pigeon poop covers the ground almost completely, and your only escape from these chechre'd expanses are to the north and west. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17586}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17588}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17588}{0}{}{Outside a small shed (enter,e)}{ }{   You stand at the edge of the roof, overlooking death. There is a small shed here, old and rickety.  Its door hangs from at most, one of its original hinges.  The only other way away from the edge is to the east. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17587}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17589}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17589}{s}{enter}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17589}{0}{}{Inside the shed (out)}{ }{   The stench of mold is hideous in this small metal shed.   Webs of all sorts soften all corners, and a solitary lightbulb  hanging from one wire lights the place.  The floor is  littered with junk...papers, boxes, stuff that would be more appropriate in a garbage can.  The shed doesn't apparently lead to anywhere, leaving the only exit as back out through the door. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {50809}{move junk}{move junk}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {50809}{d}{move junk}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17588}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17588}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17590}{0}{}{In the middle of a hideous alley (n,s)}{ }{   Gaunt winds blow the stench of human decay past your face as you stand uncomfortably in this dark alleyway.  Boxes that serve as homes for some poor people seem on the brink of collapse as blankets and rags are piled on top of them, in an effort to better-insulate and perhaps decorate them.  The end of the alley is near to the north, and the other end to the south seems to have a ladder within reach leading up to a fire escape. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17592}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17593}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17591}{0}{}{A fire escape (d,n,w)}{ }{   This is a rusted brown fire escape running alongside the east wall of the hotel.  From here, a ladder leads down to a very dangerous-looking alley.  There is a stairwell leading up to the next floor but you would have to go to the north first because of the way the fire escape is built.  You could also climb back through the window to the west. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17581}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17592}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {2112}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17592}{0}{}{A vile, filthy alleyway (u,n)}{ }{   You are standing in a dank, skinny alley between two tall, dark buildings.  Shreds of slimy newspapers cover the excrement that fouls the turf here, and cardboard boxes, salvaged and  rearranged to form small shelters line the vandalized brick walls in haphazard rows.  A brown metal fire escape ladder is within reach jutting down from the side of the west building. }{Whorehouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17591}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17590}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

