R {17682}{0}{}{Snack Bar (nw)}{ }{This is the Bowling City snack bar.  It seems to serve all kinds of delicacies, ranging from french fries to onion rings.  Behind a counter, serving the generally fat and scruffy-looking customers, are two whiny ladies wearing official snack bar shirts.  The floor has probably never been cleaned since this place was built, evident by the amount of grease and assorted condiments that are smeared on it now. }{Bowling City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17680}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17683}{0}{}{Arcade (n)}{ }{You've ended up in the pretty pitiful arcade of Bowling City.  All around, games that look like they came straight from the eighties are here.  It's a pretty dingy, small room that probably has not been cleaned for many ages. While you are obviously enthralled with these amazingly crappy games, maybe you should just move on before you get your ass whooped in Street Fighter by some arcade freak. }{Bowling City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17680}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17684}{0}{}{The bathroom (w)}{ }{Well this must be the fabled men's bathroom of Bowling City!  Fabled only because no one has actually survived long enough to get back out and relate the tale.  The floor is slick with who knows what substance and the walls are visibly dirty, covered with a strange greasy slick. More horrible than the sight, is the stench of this infernal place.  It is apparently the inner circle of the lord of stench.  Caustic fumes rise from drains producing such a foul odor you begin to feel light-headed.  Behind one of the two stalls you can hear agonized groaning and grunting.  Perhaps you should leave here soon. }{Bowling City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17680}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17685}{0}{<238>}{Lanes 1-50 (e,s)}{<238>|||<088>}{You gaze out upon the seemingly infinite amount of bowling lanes that are present here.  Each one carefully polished so that you slip at the exact time at which you want to throw the ball, ending up flat on your face. Each lane has its own deadly ball return.  OOOO and look an electronic score keeper! }{Bowling City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17678}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {17679}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17686}{0}{}{Backroom (n)}{ }{Somehow you have managed to get into the back room behind the desk. This is an employees-only area so you probably shouldn't stay here too long. In the corner of the room you see a few Chinese sweatshop workers sewing together some really ugly-looking bowling shoes.  Next to the workers sits an extremely large pile of various colored bowling shoes. }{Bowling City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17679}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17687}{0}{<248>}{Billiards room (e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{This poorly-lighted section of the Bowling center is devoted to billiards. Apparently these particular tables are relics from the ancient Greek pool sharks, because the felt is so worn down it is shiny. There are multiple sticky spots on the table which must be the result of another drink someone carelessly poured on this miserable excuse for a pool table.  The warped rails add a new dimension to the game, and you think even the best hustlers would have trouble making a decent bank shot here.  In each corner of this dingy room squats a brown garbage can, although most garbage seems to be left on the table tops.  Cue sticks line one wall, and despite there being approximately nine hundred thousand, not a single one is straight. Another wall is covered by lockers containing bowling implements of all kinds. }{Bowling City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17679}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {17688}{0}{}{lego Pathway (n,s,w)}{ }{North of here stands a brightly colored lego archway. At your feet a brown path curves westward.  The region around you is landscaped with pretty cone-shaped plastic trees lined up along the path and tiny plastic flowers protruding from the ground. }{New Legoland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17597}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
