R {19404}{0}{}{Fear (reality)}{ }{You have been sucked into some sort of metaplane of emotions.  You begin to theorize about the nature of this strange place when a feeling of terror begins working into the pit of your stomach.  You see no boundaries here, or directions.  You simply float in a sea of shadows. }{Chaos Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19403}{reality}{reality}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19405}{0}{}{Death (reality)}{ }{You have been gated to the top of a pile of bones that rises up over the surrounding landscape.  With each step old brittle bones break and shift underneath you.  This area is highly unstable. }{Chaos Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19403}{reality}{reality}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19406}{0}{}{The Black Lodge (reality)}{ }{You've been taken to yet another place that mortals were not meant to enter.  This time you are standing in a room with red curtains instead of walls.  In the exact center of this strange place is a black leather chair. }{Chaos Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19403}{reality}{reality}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19407}{0}{}{A Grey Walled Prison Cell (reality)}{ }{This is a damp and dank prison cell used by some dreaded being to hold prisoners.  There is one sturdy door leading out of here, as well as the rift in reality that brought you here. }{Chaos Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19403}{reality}{reality}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19408}{0}{}{A small square room (d,u)}{ }{   You find yourself in a small square room.  There is nothing here other than the ladder you just climbed down from and another one leading down. The walls are all empty and painted white, as is the floor. }{Laboratory Maze}{laboratory_maze}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19200}{u}{u}{16}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {44315}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19409}{0}{}{The Streets of London (n,s)}{ }{You are standing in a half-lit street, surrounded in a thick pea-soup fog that makes seeing anything difficult.  The only source of light to be seen is an occasional gas-lamp.  It is almost painfully cold and the air seems to suck the warmth from your bones.  Your footsteps echo in a strange muffled tone on the cobblestones beneath your feet, and your senses are assailed by a truly awful stench that seems to come from all around you.  A signpost stands here, giving you a chance to orient yourself in this new setting.  }{Old London}{old_london}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19200}{s}{s}{4}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19410}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19410}{0}{}{The Streets of London (s,e)}{ }{You've arrived at a sharp right hand turn in the road.  The surrounding buildings loom darkly out of the fog, and you can hear the occasional sound of movement off somewhere in the distance, or perhaps right by you.  The fog is distorting your sense of distance, and it is nearly impossible to judge what might lie just near you, let alone some distance away.  An old signpost sits on the corner, the only indication of where you might be.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19409}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19411}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19411}{0}{}{The Streets of London (w,n,e)}{ }{You stand at the junction of two roads, one sprawling out to the north, the other running from the east to the west.  Somewhere in the distance you hear someone scream, but in the miasmic fog you cannot tell from which direction it has come from.  The lighting here is making the fog an eerie and sickly yellow, and it smells terrible.  A weathered signpost stands here to guide you. }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19410}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19412}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19413}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19412}{0}{}{The Streets of London (n,s,e)}{ }{The street continues through the murk of the London fog, weird sounds echo about adding further to your sense of disorientation.  There is an almost tangible feeling of panic within these streets, as the fear of the Ripper takes hold on the city.  The strange yellow lights of the gas-lamps hold no comfort here, only the single signpost guiding the way seems to give off any sense of normality.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19411}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19414}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19415}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19413}{0}{}{The Streets of London (w,e)}{ }{You are standing in a half-lit street, surrounded in a thick pea-soup fog that inhibits your vision.  The only source of light around are the occasional gas lamps lining the road.  It is almost painfully cold and the air seems to suck the warmth from your bones.  Your footsteps echo in a strange muffled tone on the cobblestones beneath your feet, and your senses are assailed by a truly awful stench that seems to come from all around you.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19411}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19425}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19414}{0}{}{The Streets of London (s,gate,e)}{ }{The road you are walking along swings from the south to east here.  It seems somewhat darker here than normal, although the lamp posts still continue on at regular intervals.  The fog swirls about you, almost concealing a wooden fence on the west side of the corner that holds a rickety iron gate within it.  You can't make out what lies on the other side of it, but there are no buildings that you can see in that direction.  A signpost just next to the gate points out your options.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19412}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19416}{gate}{gate}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19417}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19416}{n}{gate}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19415}{0}{}{Mitre Square (e,w)}{B}{You have entered into a small clear space, known to the locals as Mitre Square.  The fog is not quite as thick here as it is elsewhere, and you can see the surrounding buildings a little more clearly than you have been able to elsewhere.  Improved visibility does not really make the place seem any more attractive however, as broken cobbles underfoot, and a weak and tottering looking brick fence seem to give the square the impression of decay.  Mounds of garbage give the area a very foul odour, and you're not surprised at the complete absence of anyone else here.  At least it would seem there is no one else here.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19412}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19423}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19416}{0}{}{Dutfield's Yard (gate)}{A}{You're in a tiny yard that runs off the side of the roadway.  There is not a lot to see here.  A small stable sits just to the left, while the ground is comprised of the same types of cobblestone pieces as the lane.  Even with a light source it is amazingly dark in here, with deep shadows everywhere.  The swirling fog makes the shadows seem to writhe about as the light reflects off it, and you get the creeping sensation that there are things moving about in them.  With the Ripper on the loose this doesn't strike you as the safest place to be.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19414}{gate}{gate}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19414}{s}{gate}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19417}{0}{}{The Streets of London (e,w)}{ }{The street you are on runs from east to west through what can only be described as an extremely run-down part of the city.  Dark and dreary, even the fog seems ragged and worn along here, being swirled about by a slight breeze that seems to waft through the cold night air.  The smell is as bad as ever, reeking of coal and rubbish, and it is truly a wonder anyone would tolerate this kind of environment.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19414}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19418}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19418}{0}{}{The Streets of London (e,w)}{ }{The street you are wandering down runs from east to west through the blinding fog.  The fog is so thick in this area that you have trouble even making out the ground beneath your feet.  The air seems colder here as well, and the sound of your footsteps is so muffled as to sound far away, causing it to sound like someone or something is following.  That's ridiculous of course, why would anyone be following you? }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19417}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19419}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19419}{0}{}{Spitalfield Square (n,s,w,e)}{ }{You've entered a large open square.  There is a slight breeze through here, and the fog has thinned as a result, swirling and eddying through the pale yellow lights of the lamp posts that have been placed about the square.  A series of closed market stalls fill most of the area, creating a warren of dark nooks and passageways throughout.  The surrounding buildings are dark and lifeless, and you feel quite exposed here.  A large signpost dominates the center of the square, pointing off in all four cardinal destinations to the various exits.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19418}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19420}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19421}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19422}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19420}{0}{}{The Streets of London (s,e)}{ }{The lane you have been following turns sharply here, heading off to both the east and south.  It is quieter than normal around here, and your breath echoes in your ears.  The fog is somewhat thicker as well, and you can only just make out the signpost that marks the corner, giving you some sense of direction.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19419}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19428}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19421}{0}{}{The Streets of London (w,n,s)}{c}{This section of the streets seems to be darker than the rest for some reason.  The lighting is more a muddy brown than the usual off yellow of the lamps.  Strangely you can't even work out why this is the case, as the lamps around here seem normal enough.  Perhaps the fog itself is polluted here.  A signpost stands here, allowing you a moment to orient yourself.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19419}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19423}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19424}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19422}{0}{}{The Streets of London (e,w)}{D}{You're heading along a street that runs from east to west.  The fog is sparser here somewhat, but it is still incredibly hard to see clearly. The buildings on either side of the street are dark and lifeless, and it is difficult to tell if they are even used anymore.  There is a strange smell in the air, as if something has gone off.  It's sickly sweet and it is difficult to breathe properly, so strong is the scent. It seems to be emanating from a bundle of rags over by the side of the road.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19419}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19435}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19423}{0}{}{The Streets of London (e,w)}{ }{The street here is almost deathly silent.  Compared to other parts of the fog-enshrouded city, the silence here seems somewhat sinister.  The shadows on the edge of your vision seem to twitch and move.  All you can hear through the thick air is the sound of your harsh breath.  If anything were to happen to you here, no-one would ever know it until it was far too late. }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19421}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19415}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19424}{0}{}{The Streets of London (n,w,door)}{ }{You stand before a large tavern that is out of character with the rest of the street.  Bright and full of light and noise, it looms out of the fog like a safe-haven.  A large sign dangles by its open door, and you hear sounds of singing and merriment from within.  The street outside it however has lost none of its sinister edge, and it swings northward, a single signpost marking the end of one street and the beginning of another.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19421}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19425}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
