R {19427}{0}{<238>}{The Frying Pan Public House (out)}{<238>[P]<088>}{The Tavern is bustling with activity.  Large crowds cluster about the bar, all clamouring for more ale or whatever they're drinking.  Serving maids struggle with glasses and overly friendly patrons as they cross amongst the large number of tables scattered about the room.  Despite the chill of the night it is quite pleasantly warm in here, and the rich aroma of food fills the air.  }{Old London}{}{}{pub}{1.000}{1}
E {19424}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19424}{w}{out}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19428}{0}{}{The Streets of London (e,w)}{ }{Running from east to west, the street you have been following is dark and menacing.  Fog clouds your vision, eddying wildly about in front of you, distorting things in strange ways.  What sounds you can make out are muffled, giving the road an ethereal and unreal quality.  Shadows loom dark and deep all about you, making it hard to discern if anyone, or anything is hidden amongst them.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19420}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19429}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19429}{0}{}{The Streets of London (n,w,e)}{ }{You have arrived at a tiny junction between two roads.  To the north a small alleyway runs between the buildings, allowing you to head in that direction if you desire.  The larger road continues to both the east and west through the thick fog that engulfs everything.  Black shadows make it hard to see anything clearly beyond your immediate surroundings, so it is difficult to tell which is the better path to take.  A signpost stands just nearby, and may help guide you.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19428}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19430}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19431}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19430}{0}{}{Miller's Court (s,e)}{ }{You've entered a tiny courtyard surrounded by bleak and dark buildings on all sides.  Two dark alleyways run out of here to the east and south, not that it is much brighter in the courtyard itself.  The only illumination seems to be coming from a window up on the second floor of one of the buildings.  Even with your own source of light combined with it, it's difficult to make out your surroundings.  As with everywhere else the fog is thick and makes it hard to see.  Shadows line the walls of the buildings, where almost anything could be concealed.  }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19429}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19433}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {40866}{n}{search shadows;enter}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19431}{0}{}{The Streets of London (gates,n,w,s)}{ }{You're at the meeting point of two roads that form a t-junction here.  The junction itself is overshadowed totally by the huge set of gates that sit just east of here.  Some kind of huge manor house can be seen beyond them, rising above everything around it by a good three stories.  A signpost sits to one side, almost unnoticeable next to the grandeur of the house. }{Old London}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19429}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19432}{gates}{gates}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
