R {19703}{0}{}{Academy Masters Office (n)}{ }{This room looks more like a throne room than an office, but you didn't think an Academy would have a throne room. In the centre of the room on a raised dais stands a... well, a throne. Made in the shape of an easter egg, with a part cut out for the head Easter Bunny to sit in, it takes up most of the room. }{Easter Bunny Academy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19702}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19704}{0}{}{Academy Quartermasters. (e)}{ }{The quartermasters' is where all the bunnies get their eggs before going off on their deliveries. There is a door at the back of the room which has what looks to be like a combination lock on it. These eggs must be something really special to be under such guard. There is a desk right in front of you. }{Easter Bunny Academy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19702}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19705}{0}{}{In a Tree (d)}{ }{You are up inside the hippie children's tree house.  It is really well made, you can tell Birch constructed it himself.  A small set of chairs surround a table, and a fake wooden hookah with four hoses stemming from it sits in the middle.  Bright yellow curtains flap in the breeze coming from the little windows on all four walls.  All in all, it is very cozy, and you wish you had one when you were young. }{Hippie Commune}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1172}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19706}{0}{}{Entrance to an apartment (s,w,out)}{<168>O<088>}{A white marble floor covers the entrance of the apartment. It gives way to a gray carpet after about three feet. White pillars frame the west exit which seems to lead to an eating area, and a long hallway can be seen to the south. Various items are lying about the apartment, and a strong mildew odor gives you the feeling that whoever lives here might have other things on their mind rather than cleanliness. }{Gamer's House}{gamers_house}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6526}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19707}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19708}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19707}{0}{<268>}{A Hallway (n,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The hallway stretches before you leading south to the den, and north to the entry. The baseboards in this room are darkened with dust and dirt, and are dented as if the occupant bashed something heavy into them. There is a thermostat on the wall and the vent for the air conditioner protrudes from the ceiling. Beside the vent is a light with a burnt out bulb. }{Gamer's House}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19706}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19709}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19708}{0}{}{Dining Room (s,w,e)}{ }{The dining room is furnished with a bashed-up old wooden table and a rickety-looking chair. A gaming magazine is lying on the table, whose job in life is to hold dishes until somebody gets around to washing them. Water stains cover the surface of the table  and bits of food, spilled while they were being eaten, are scattered across the surface. This room and the living room to the south are actually one large room. }{Gamer's House}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19706}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19710}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19711}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19709}{0}{}{A Den (n)}{<128>C<088>}{A long desk with several computers on it occupies the east wall of the computer room and a half-full bookshelf lies on the west wall. Various posters from computer games are pinned to the wall, and hand-made maps from old games are lovingly displayed as well. Chairs are set up along the length of the desk for easy access to the computers that lie on it. On the far side of the room is a printer. }{Gamer's House}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19707}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
