R {19942}{0}{<278>}{An Overgrown Path (s,e)}{<278> +-<088>}{Turning somewhat brown, the grass here is very tall, almost waist high. The ground under your feet seems sturdy, and looking down, you notice an old cobblestone pathway almost covered by the dirt and grass. The remains of an old wooden fence stand unsteadily, supported by the bushes and grass that has grown through the slats over the years. }{Abandoned Garden}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19934}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19949}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19943}{0}{<228>}{A path through a dense forest (e,w)}{<228>( *<088>}{Following the path through the trees, you find yourself trudging through a very tightly packed area of forest.  The green of the leaves and bushes assaults your senses, and the closeness of the tree trunks to the path makes you start feeling a little claustrophobic. }{Hacketoff's Bridge}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19934}{e}{e}{2}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19944}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19944}{0}{<238>}{Eastern side of a bridge (w,e)}{<238>===<088>}{Emerging from the forest, as if growing straight out of the earth itself, is a stone bridge.  It arches up westward over a deep sinkhole which drops dizzyingly into the ground.  You can make out the western edge of the bridge as it disappears into the forest on the far side of the sinkhole. }{Hacketoff's Bridge}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19943}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19945}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19945}{0}{<238>}{The middle of a bridge (w,e)}{<238>===<088>}{You stand on the middle of the great stone bridge which arcs over the sinkhole.  Forest swarms right up to both sides of the bridge, with only small gaps where the path is quickly swallowed up.  It's nice to have a little space here.  Far below, you can hear the gurgle of the river as it passes underneath.  There appears to be a small business here, with a sign advertising its purpose. }{Hacketoff's Bridge}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19944}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19946}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19948}{'interested}{'interested}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19946}{0}{<228>}{The edge of a bridge (w,e)}{<228>( *<088>}{Before you, a deep sinkhole creates a huge open expanse as it drops vertically down into the ground.  The trees grow right up to the edge, hiding it from view to anyone stumbling through the undergrowth.  Good thing you were following the path, or you might be seeing it from the bottom instead of the top. Stretching out eastwards over the hole is a great stone bridge, and you think you can see something in the middle of it. }{Hacketoff's Bridge}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19945}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19947}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19947}{0}{<228>}{Dense forest (path,e)}{<228>(<238>P<228>*<088>}{The path you are on is pushed in on all sides by some of the densest forest you have ever seen.  Trees grow only a few feet apart, and between them grows a mass of undergrowth.  There's no chance of wandering off the path here, even if you wanted to. }{Hacketoff's Bridge}{hacketoffs_bridge}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19946}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19929}{path}{path}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19948}{0}{}{You are flying!}{ }{Whoah!  After having been thrown from the bridge, you now find yourself on the end of a stretchy vine, soaring up and down above the river at the bottom of the sinkhole!}{Hacketoff's Bridge}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19945}{flap arms}{flap arms}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19949}{0}{<278>}{A Small Pathway (w,n,e)}{<278>-+-<088>}{Weeds and thistles grow high in this deserted garden, the bright bloom of flowers past two old gateposts catches your eye, and the crumbled remains of the gate have almost been buried in the tall greyish green grass. You can almost see a cobbled pathway underneath the dirt and grass beneath your feet. Something sparkles in the sunlight to the east. }{Abandoned Garden}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19942}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19950}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19951}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19950}{0}{<178>}{A Small Well Tended Garden (s)}{<168>*<158>*<138>*<088>}{Brightly coloured flowers dance in the gentle breeze. Tiny violets, bold tall sunflowers reaching towards the sky, graceful roses climbing up the fence posts, many different flowers bloom on the bushes of the garden. A basket of small cards stands on an old bench beside one of the gateposts. }{Abandoned Garden}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19949}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19951}{0}{<278>}{A Deserted Pathway (w)}{<278>-+ <088>}{Old gnarled fruit trees twist their branches together forming a canopy just above your head. You can hear tiny twinkling giggles coming from somewhere just out of eyesight. An old wrought iron garden seat stands under one of the trees, grass slowly covering the legs of the seat, yet still not covering it totally. What used to be a small clump of rosemary has slowly taken over the whole southern part of the garden. }{Abandoned Garden}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19949}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19952}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19952}{0}{<238>}{A Cosy Hidden Bower (n)}{<238># #<088>}{Well hidden by the huge rosemary bush surrounding you, tiny pieces of blue material and little blue gems mark this as the nest of a bower bird. The stalks scratch against your face and hands, and although it hurts the friction against your skin releases the soft but insistent scent of the rosemary. The dirt under your feet is covered in trampled grass and old leaves from the bush around you. }{Abandoned Garden}{}{}{marble}{1.000}{1}
E {19951}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19953}{0}{}{Hidden Stairwell (d,s)}{ }{This is a hidden stairwell that leads down into some sort of hallway. You can hear noises of people walking and talking from below. }{Mage Tower}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1546}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {21166}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19954}{0}{}{The middle of a crater (nw)}{ }{You are standing in the middle of a huge crater.  The walls of it extend at least ten meters above your head and it is roughly twenty meters in diameter.  All around you are small cracks from which an incredible amount of steam is billowing.  Luckily you have managed to find a safe spot to stand, so you are not being burned directly, but the heat down here is incredible.  The concave shape of the crater is amazingly precise,  almost as if someone has scooped out a section of the earth with a large spoon.  The ground beneath you is very hot and you are thankful that this hole doesn't go any deeper.  It is quite a bit darker down here, and that, combined with the overpowering smell of sulfur and other gases leads you to not want to spend too much time searching.  At the center of the crater lies a small depression that you can't quite see into from this angle.  }{Impact Crater}{}{}{marble}{1.000}{1}
E {396}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19955}{0}{}{An electron (u,n,s,cave)}{<108>C<088>}{A strong glow is playing havoc with your sense of sight here, and there is constant motion whirring around you.   A humming sound comes to you from everywhere, and is really annoying you beyond what you feel you can handle.  The air vibrates with energy, and the hairs on your body fire off in all directions. }{Electric Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {18881}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19956}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19957}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19958}{cave}{cave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19956}{0}{}{An electron (se,s)}{ }{This room is dead...no energy at all.  There are tiny charged dust particles in the air which light your way......but the life of this room has been sucked out of it......nothing left but a heavy grey mist.  The room contains active electric dust but the awesome glow has left it..... }{Electric Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19955}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19957}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19957}{0}{}{An electron (nw,n)}{ }{A blinding glow prevents you from seeing anything.  There is constant  motion around you.  A slight hum penetrates your soul and shakes it.  SNAP!  A bolt of electricity snaps by your ear and charges the room. }{Electric Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19955}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19956}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19958}{0}{}{A cave (s,enter)}{<108>E<088>}{This is a single room cave about 50 feet high and 40 feet deep.  The  entrance is large enough to shed some light into the room.  In the  corner you see a fresh campfire.  Against the back wall is a strange electric blue glow, it looks like some sort of entrance to something. You see strange LARGE footprints on the ground, something very big has been living here.  You are in somebody's house. Unfortunately for the resident of this cave, it seems that recently the dwelling has become the home of a small stream, which flows through the cave from behind some stalagmites. }{Electric Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {18582}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19955}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19959}{squeeze between stalagmites}{squeeze between stalagmites}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19959}{0}{}{}{ }{}{Otyugh Cave}{otyugh_cave}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19960}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19960}{0}{}{tunnel (ne,s)}{ }{A non-descript tunnel winding its way through the otherwise solid rock.  The stream has gotten a little higher, and your feet splash through a few  inches of water as you walk. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19959}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19961}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19961}{0}{}{tunnel (nw,sw)}{ }{A nondescript tunnel winding its way through the otherwise solid rock.  The stream is starting to speed up a little here, and you are forced to take precautions not to lose your footing.  There is a little engraving on the eastern wall, but it's in an unfamiliar language. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19960}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19962}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19962}{0}{}{tunnel (se,n)}{ }{A nondescript tunnel winding its way through the otherwise solid rock.  The stream is a good four or five inches deep now.  You think you feel slimy things running against your legs. There is a scribble on the eastern wall which looks readable. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19961}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19963}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19963}{0}{}{Dam it! (s,ne)}{<138>J<088>}{You watch your step in the now half-foot-deep waters as you come to a  slightly cleared out portion of the tunnel, a bit larger than the previous  few areas were. This is mainly due to the fact that there is no wall on the  west edge, just a dam which stands about four feet high and which reeks of  something you think you recognize. Maybe you should take a closer look at it? }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19962}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19964}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19965}{jump dam}{jump dam}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19964}{0}{}{Small waterfall (sw)}{<158>E<088>}{The muddy ground drops away here like a swimming pool, and all of a sudden you are up to your boobies in the dark water of this cavern. You feel all sorts of gross things sliding around under the water, and  you thank your gods that all of your equipment is somehow waterproof. The pool feeds into the stream which you have been travelling through, to the southwest. The pool is in turn fed by a man-sized hole on the opposite side of the cavern, roughly fifteen feet off the ground. Water pours out from the hole and splashes noisily into the murky pool that surrounds you. There is a trickle of light escaping from the hole as well. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19963}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19967}{enter hole}{enter hole}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19965}{0}{}{Otyugh lair (sw,e,nw)}{ }{You find yourself in a dark, abhorrently fetid abode, if this place can actually be refered to as such. Feces and scum cover the ground, walls, and everything else in sight, and the smell of putrid waste and decay threatens to disrupt your digestive process in a BIG way. Bones lay scattered about, and there is a pool of blood at the far end of this 'home sweet home'. A  tiny trickle of water passes through the dam on the eastern side of the room, but it's well contained by the packed dung. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19966}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19968}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19963}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19966}{0}{}{Otyugh lair (n,sw,w,ne)}{ }{You find yourself in the nightmarish quarters of what must be absolutely vile creatures. There are small piles of dung scattered about, and some  random small animal bones have been thrown about, leaving not an inch of  the place uncovered by filth. You think you smell vomit, but you can't really distinguish any scents anymore, it all smells like your grandma's beanfarts. You are forced to ask yourself, 'What the HELL could live in  this place?!?' }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19965}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19975}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19976}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19969}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19967}{0}{}{tunnel (n)}{ }{You are crawling though a long tunnel in which a smooth current flows over your body, and you have to strain your neck to keep your head above the waterline. The water is extremely cold, and as it splashes into your mouth you notice that it is salt water. You see light coming from an opening up ahead to the north. You have no choice but to head towards it, since you don't think you could wiggle your way backwards through the tunnel. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19978}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19968}{0}{}{Otyugh lair (s,w,se,nw)}{ }{You find yourself in the nightmarish quarters of what must be absolutely vile creatures. There are small piles of dung scattered about, and some  random small animal bones have been thrown about, leaving not an inch of  the place uncovered by filth. You think you smell vomit, but you can't really distinguish any scents anymore, it all smells like decayed nose- hairs. You are forced to ask yourself, 'What the HELL could live in  this place?!?' }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19965}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19969}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19970}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19971}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19969}{0}{}{Otyugh lair (w,n,s)}{ }{You didn't think these rooms could get any worse, but this one takes the cake. It seems the otyugh leader is a cannibal, as you see hunks of otyugh meat strewn about, covered in a greyish mixture of blood and  dung. There seems to be a recently killed humanoid body in the corner, and a pool of warm urine sits stagnantly by the southern wall. Of course, this room is not without heaps of dung and scattered, half-eaten bones. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19968}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
