R {19977}{0}{}{Otyugh Dungheap (e)}{ }{This room is just one enormous pile of excrement. The otyughs come here to get their delicious meals, when they can't find any fresh droppings in the caves and tunnels leading to their lair. Everywhere you walk your feet sink into the feces, and you think 'Gee, if mom could see me now...'. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19969}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19978}{0}{}{Pod chamber (s,n)}{<158>P<088>}{The first thing you notice about this room is that it is lit. You cannot tell where the light comes from\; there are no torches, fires, lamps, or any other conventional light source- not even a nuclear reactor. The light fills the room with a wonderful white aura, a blessed change from the areas you just passed through. As you look around, you see that the walls are lined  with eight metal pods, each with a small, closed entrance door. There is a long cord hanging from the ceiling in the center of the room. The stream here is getting rather strong, and you have to pay attention to staying on  your feet. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19967}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19979}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19980}{pod 5}{pod 5}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19981}{pod 3}{pod 3}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19958}{pull cord}{pull cord}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19979}{0}{}{Oceans Edge (s)}{ }{You force yourself into the room, pushing against the heavy current, and are immediately dumbfounded by what you see here. You are in a wide corridor which ends about thirty feet up ahead at a dead end. The incredible part is that the dead end is not rock- it's a sheet of water! You must be underneath an ocean! You are shocked when you realize that part of this vertical waterwall has broken, and the water pouring  through the seams of this wall has become the stream which you've been following for some time now. }{Otyugh Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19978}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19980}{0}{}{Entrance to the Linux promotion (s,n,w)}{ }{This room is filled with bright fluorescent lights.  It has plain, grey carpeting on the floor, and seems to be filled with posters, display cases, and soft background muzak.  It seems to be a large promotion for something called Linux.  The room continues on to the north, where you think you see camera flashes.  To the west there is a doorway to what looks like a shop.  The way out of this strange place is to the south. }{Linux Fair}{linux_fair}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19982}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19983}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19978}{s}{s}{4}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19981}{0}{<248>}{R'lyeh (s,e)}{<248>~ ~<088>}{You are just inside the great city of R'lyeh.  You see signs of a lot of activity here recently.  Apparently, the ancient creatures that inhabit this place are once again active.  Better watch your step. What's even stranger, is that you notice some obvious signs that other humans have been here.  Most likely, environmentalists.  You're not sure which is worse, them or the slimy inhabitants of this island. }{R'lyeh}{rlyeh}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19984}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19985}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19982}{0}{}{Photo opportunity with Bogo (s)}{ }{This room looks like it's decked out for photo opportunities.  There is a large chair here, and a polaroid camera on a tripod facing the chair. On the walls a few T-shirts are displayed featuring pictures of nerds hugging a large penguin.  In the corner you see a small pile of blank T-shirts and a tray of chemicals -- which you assume must be used in affixing the photos to the T-shirt material. }{Linux Fair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19980}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19983}{0}{}{The Linux Cafe (e)}{ }{This is a brightly lit shop, filled with posters, CDs, books, stickpins, and even inflatable penguin dolls.  There's also a small bar where food and drink is being sold.  A few tables are spotted about, and on the wall there is a list of things for sale. }{Linux Fair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19980}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19984}{0}{<248>}{R'lyeh (s,n,e)}{<248>~ ~<088>}{There is a lot of slime here.  Better watch your step or you might slip and fall.  You smell a lot of dead fish around here, but all you see is bones.  Something around here has been eating them.  Hope you don't find out what. }{R'lyeh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19981}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19987}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {19989}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {19985}{0}{<248>}{R'lyeh (se,w,s)}{<248>~ ~<088>}{There is no telling what might lurk beneath the muck.  It will be hard to leave, but it shouldn't be impossible.  You notice that other sea creatures are also swimming in the muck.  Well, at least it's not toxic. }{R'lyeh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19981}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
