R {20065}{0}{}{Guard Post (door,e)}{<238>D<088>}{Guard Post -  A large wooden door with metal braces leads into the guard tower of the fort.  The dirt is well packed and depressions in the dirt show you that there is often a guard posted here.  The distinctive smell of horse manure comes from the east.  It would probably be best to turn around and head back into the main area of the fort. }{Fort in the woods}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20064}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20067}{door}{door}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20066}{0}{}{Fort Stables (w)}{ }{Fort Stables -  The smell of hay and horse manure dominates the building.  A large pile of hay is partially baled in the back corner.  The building is made out of wood, and doesn't contain any formal structure of stalls, but lets the horses walk about free within an enclosed pen.  A couple of benches containing horse blankets, saddles and other horse equipment are near the entrance gate. }{Fort in the woods}{}{}{marble}{1.000}{1}
E {20064}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20067}{0}{}{Fort Stairway (stairs,door)}{<238>D<088>}{Stairway -  The inner guard tower is small with a spiral staircase leading up. Several torches line the wall giving light to the area.  The stairs are dusty and contain the footprints of leather boots.  The floor is made of wood planks. }{Fort in the woods}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20065}{door}{door}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20068}{stairs}{stairs}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
