R {20079}{0}{}{Outpost watchtower (d)}{ }{You are in the watchtower of this fort, a sparsely decorated room with slits in the walls through which the defenders can shoot at the attackers.  A stairwell leads back down into the fort. }{Military Bunker}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20077}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20080}{0}{}{Outpost's supply room (e)}{ }{You are in the supply room of the outpost.  Shelves and shelves of dusty and useless stuff cover the walls.  In the middle of the room is a large desk where Sergeant Nachschub sits and terrorizes the poor enlisted men wanting their supplies. }{Military Bunker}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20078}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20081}{0}{}{Outpost's main office (w)}{ }{This, as indicated by the sign on the massive oak desk filling up most of the room, is the office of General Krieger.  Looking around, the first thing you notice is that the room is very, very clean, clean to point of being empty, aside from the massive oak desk and chair. My god, one has got to wonder about this man Krieger. }{Military Bunker}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20078}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20082}{0}{}{Underground corridor (u,n)}{ }{You are walking along a bare underground corridor.  Your footsteps echo back at you on the concrete walls, unadorned aside from plain electrical lights.  Steps lead up to ground level here. }{Military Bunker}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
