R {20116}{0}{}{Anteroom (d)}{ }{The spiral stairway ends in a plainly furnished room.  An iron- bound door made of wood leads somewhere, probably farther up into this tower. }{Zith-el}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20115}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20133}{u}{unlock door;open door;u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20117}{0}{}{Rahshaiya's quarters (n)}{ }{This room is lit by a glowing flower hanging from the center of the ceiling.  It is decorated in greens and browns.  The chairs, bed, and desk are made of a smooth, brown wood, possibly idani, instead of the rare ebonwood that appears elsewhere in this edifice.  The floor is a deep green marble, several shades darker than the walls.  The room smells like a windswept meadow. }{Zith-el}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20113}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20118}{0}{}{Koh's quarters (e)}{ }{This dark room smells of myrrh and furnished in primitive elegance. The four-poster ebonwood bed is lacking any carvings and the chairs are plain and have no cushions\; an unassuming desk rests against one wall.  A green patchwork quilt lying on the bed is the only ornate object in the room. The floor is black marble with veins of green running through it that match the dark green walls.  A picture of a cloaked man hangs from the wall opposite the archway you entered.  The room is spotless, with no traces of dust or spider webs. }{Zith-el}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20113}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20119}{4104}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
