R {20161}{0}{<238>}{Spring of Kierlanai (s,nw)}{<238>.^.<088>}{The old man says: "The first time that I came to the Spring of     Kierlanai, I can remember stopping here, surveying the view.    Legends held great weight on my soul, and I was a spiritual     man... this spring bore both in excess. I stood mere feet away     from the kneeling statue, studying her smooth silhouette, not    breathing, for fear of realizing I wasn't truly there." }{Spring}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20164}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20165}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20162}{0}{}{Spring of Kierlanai (out,bridge,ne)}{<168>O<088>}{The old man says: "When you reached the top of the mountain, the    path forked into two directions, circling around the summit edge,    meeting to the north. Through the middle flowed the water from the    spring, above which were two statues, two guardians. All around you    was nature's glory, as you could see far off into all directions    but north." }{Spring}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
