R {20329}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* The Street of Sorrows *\x7D=- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{This street defines the southeast border of the city.  On the east side of the street, the ruins of largely intact larger dwellings hold back the forests, while on the west side similar dwellings block access to an overgrown parkland.  Stepping quietly on the uneven cobblestones of this street you listen for signs of life and hardly surprisingly, you detect none at all.  Any living thing with any common sense avoids this place.  By the street, grander buildings in disrepair amongst the rubble hide both treasures beyond the imagination and unimaginable death.  It is difficult to see approaching danger, as taller grasses obscure the approaches to the lower buildings. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
