R {20387}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* The Street of the Evening Star *\x7D=- (nw,e)}{<278> +-<088>}{A huge hotel sits to the southeast, while to the northeast you see the walls of a castle in the distance.  Stepping quietly on the smooth bricks of this street you listen for signs of life and hardly surprisingly, you detect none at all.  Any living thing with any common sense avoids this place.  On either side of the street, multi-story buildings and offices with some holes in their roofs wait quietly for you to explore.  It is very quiet.  Small weeds poke through the steps, stairs and ornamentation of the ruined buildings. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20385}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20651}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20388}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* The Street of the Evening Star *\x7D=- (se,w)}{<278>-+ <088>}{You watch the high towers in the distance for signs of predators as you proceed cautiously down this street made of pavers.  It is hard to detect advancing foes, as low shrubs dot the landscape and choke the openings.  Just off to the sides of the street, homes and shops with some holes in their roofs pay silent testimony to the dreadful devastation that took place here.  To the south is a huge building, while to the northeast is another huge building.   }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20385}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20389}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20389}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* The Street of the Evening Star *\x7D=- (nw,e)}{<278> +-<088>}{By the street, leveled buildings and foundations hide both treasures beyond the imagination and unimaginable death.  It is impossible to see hidden foes, as low shrubs blanket the rubble.  Enormous buildings tower out of the rubble.   }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20388}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20390}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

