R {20555}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Halidom Street *\x7D=- (sw,n)}{<278>- -<088>}{Through the trees to the southeast you see the shadow of the long-abandoned Hall of Guild Faunists.  It is unnerving, as small creeping vines and grasses run over the buildings.  Just off to the sides of the street, multi-story buildings and offices with some holes in their roofs pay silent testimony to the dreadful devastation that took place here.  A small movement in some shrubs in the distance catches your eye.  You pause in the middle of the street and wish you could just disappear into the small rocks and hide.  If you wait out here in the open much longer your wish may come true. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20340}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20556}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20556}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Halidom Street *\x7D=- (sw,ne)}{<278>- -<088>}{By the street, larger edifices and shops that are mostly intact hide both treasures beyond the imagination and unimaginable death.  It is frighteningly silent.  There are not even any birds in the small trees that have taken root in and around the foundations of the buildings.   }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20555}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20557}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20557}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Halidom Street *\x7D=- (ne,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{On either side of the street, large houses and buildings in serious disrepair wait quietly for you to explore.  It is mostly clear of vegetation.  The street, made of pot-holed cobblestones, was first constructed by the elves and their human companions over 1000 years ago, and was destroyed over 600 years ago.  To the southeast you see a large building with numerous shattered towers, while to the west you see the largely intact remnants of a large building.   }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20556}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20545}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20558}{0}{<238>}{II_iII The Six Tyryl Towers II_iII (w,e)}{<238>] [<088>}{This once vast building was largely destroyed in the downfall of Murus Faralain, when the apprentice wizards who dwelt here fought against the army of evil and met a brutal end.  The two western-most towers still stand but are separated from the eastern towers by devastation\; the centre of the building was blown apart in the final battle of the city.  At the time of the battle, the Six Tyryl Towers was a newly-established school of wizardry. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20545}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20559}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20559}{0}{<238>}{II_iII The Six Tyryl Towers II_iII (w)}{<238>] [<088>}{This once vast building was largely destroyed in the downfall of Murus Faralain, when the apprentice wizards who dwelt here fought against the army of evil and met a brutal end.  The two western-most towers still stand but are separated from the eastern towers by devastation\; the centre of the building was blown apart in the final battle of the city.  At the time of the battle, the Six Tyryl Towers was a newly-established school of wizardry. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20558}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20560}{0}{<238>}{=[]= House Audark =[]= (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{Past home to one of the wealthiest human citizens of Murus Faralain, this building has had one of its wings reduced to rubble.  The roof has been blown off, presumably by excessive magical force used by the extended members of the Audark family during the overrun of the city. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20542}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20561}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Blazen Street *\x7D=- (sw,n)}{<278>- -<088>}{It is impossible to check the houses at a distance, as thick shrubs obscure the entrances, windows and holes of buildings.  To the sides of the narrow street, multi-story buildings and offices with some holes in their roofs pay silent testimony to the dreadful devastation that took place here.  Once home to the more affluent of mages and merchants, this street proceeds in a north-south direction through overgrown parkland with largely intact buildings on either side of the street.  As you make your way down this narrow street you notice that the pot-holed cobblestones shows no signs of recent traffic. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20537}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20562}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20562}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Blazen Street *\x7D=- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{Once home to the more affluent of mages and merchants, this street proceeds in a north-south direction through overgrown parkland with largely intact buildings on either side of the street.  A small movement in some shrubs in the distance catches your eye.  You pause in the middle of the narrow street and wish you could just disappear into the broken cobblestones and hide.  If you wait out here in the open much longer your wish may come true.  On either side of the narrow street, large houses and buildings in serious disrepair wait quietly for you to explore.  It is deadly silent and not a living thing can be seen. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20561}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20563}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20563}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Blazen Street *\x7D=- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{You watch the high towers in the distance for signs of predators as you proceed cautiously down this narrow street made of round field stones.  Once home to the more affluent of mages and merchants, this street proceeds in a north-south direction through overgrown parkland with largely intact buildings on either side of the street.  It is unsettling, as huge vines and leafy shrubs seem to crawl out of and obscure the openings in the buildings.  To the sides of the narrow street, large houses and buildings in serious disrepair pay silent testimony to the dreadful devastation that took place here. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20562}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20564}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20564}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Blazen Street *\x7D=- (s)}{<228>,<278>|<228>`<088>}{Once home to the more affluent of mages and merchants, this street proceeds to the south through overgrown parkland with largely intact buildings on either side of the street.  Further to the north you see buildings holding back a wall of forest.  Just off the narrow street, large houses and buildings in serious disrepair wait patiently for the original inhabitants to return and repair the devastated mess.  It is unnerving, as small creeping vines and grasses run over the buildings. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20563}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20565}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* A lane *\x7D=- (ne,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{On either side of the lane, multi-story buildings and offices with some holes in their roofs wait quietly for you to explore.  It is deadly silent and not a living thing can be seen.  Following the course of a stream to the west, this small lane leads off into parkland dotted with smaller white stone buildings.   }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20512}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20566}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20566}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* A lane *\x7D=- (sw)}{<278>- -<088>}{Stepping quietly on the cracked bricks of this lane you listen for signs of life and hardly surprisingly, you detect none at all.  Any living thing with any common sense avoids this place.  Following the course of a stream to the west, this small lane leads off to the south into parkland dotted with smaller white stone buildings.  Far across the parkland to the north and through the trees, you can make out other buildings and the wall of forest beyond them.   }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20565}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20567}{0}{<148>}{A stream (ne,s)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{The gravel bar you are standing on is dry and slopes gradually up to unclimbable banks to either side of the creek.  The stream widens here at the mouth of an ornamental lake just to the south.  To the northeast, you see water rushing over the top of a dam.   }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20514}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20582}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20568}{0}{<148>}{A stream (ne,s)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{Despite the ruined cityscape visible from up and over the bank, the stream is relatively clear of any signs of the holocaust.  The dark water runs over the gravel as it makes its way roughly northward.  The banks rise steeply up from the creek to the city above.  Tangled brush obscures your view of what's overhead in the city.  The stream passes through parkland, while further north you see it pass beneath a bridge.  To the south you see some sort of structure.   }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20514}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
