R {20571}{0}{<148>}{A stream (sw,n)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{The stream curves to the west here as it approaches a bridge further south.  On the banks overhead you see the ruins of Murus Faralain.  The dark stream waters wash over the white stones of the gravel bed.  Long ago this creek probably washed a significant river of blood and gore out of the heart of Murus Faralain.  Steep banks join with a narrow gravel bed beside the creek.  The banks are covered with thick vines and shrubs. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20570}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20572}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20572}{0}{<148>}{A stream (n,s)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{The stream continues its travel through the city.  Further south you see the ruins of buildings high up on the banks.  The deep water pools darkly here, and small currents form dimpled patterns on the smooth black water of the stream.  The banks rise steeply up from the creek to the city above.  Tangled brush obscures your view of what's overhead in the city. }{Murus Faralain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
