R {20690}{0}{<268>}{Hall of Kings (n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{Hall of Kings The dim confines of the southern chamber house the sarcophagi of two of the realm's lesser known monarchs, Queen Riselia and King Frarod.  While these rulers are forever encased in the eastern and western walls of this room, the southern wall is decorated with a large vermilion marble tablet dedicated to their memory.  Torches are ensconced in the walls and provide just enough light to make out the details of the room.  Fluted columns rise from the stone floor to the darkened ceiling and small silver plaques are attached to the front of each sarcophagus, naming the ruler within. }{Hall of Kings}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20684}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20691}{0}{<268>}{Hall of Kings (e)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{Hall of Kings The western chamber is dimly lit by recessed torches that create shadows on the fluted columns that rise up into the darkness of the vaulted ceiling overhead.  Both the southern and northern walls of this chamber feature elaborate sarcophagi set into the polished stone. Across the expanse of the inlaid floor is a large tablet of gray marlstone hanging on the western wall that is engraved with details of the royalty entombed within this room.  Small silver plaques decorate each of the sarcophagi, offering the names of those that lie within as well. }{Hall of Kings}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20684}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20692}{0}{<268>}{Hall of Kings (w)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{Hall of Kings The eastern chamber of the Hall of Kings has a particularly somber air.  It is here that the last rulers of the realm lie entombed for all eternity.  Elegant columns line the chamber from end to end, rising from the patterned stone of the floor up into the upper reaches of the vaulted ceiling overhead.  Wan torchlight flickers on the golden sarcophagi set within both the northern and southern walls.  Each is decorated with a silver plaque listing the names of those buried within.  A large tablet of white onyx hangs on the eastern wall providing more details concerning these last members of the monarchy. }{Hall of Kings}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20684}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20693}{0}{<148>}{In a beautifully carved gazebo (out)}{<118>|<138>|<148>|<088>}{This structure is built by very strong looking wood. You detect no nails or other means of holding the pieces together. It's almost as if it was carved from the same block of wood. There is a small bench standing along the eastern part of the gazebo and next to it is a finely built writing desk. Also, standing on the other side of the desk is a fairly tall wooden pole with a small metal cup at the end. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5909}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5909}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20694}{0}{<248>}{In a foyer of a large mansion (s,out)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{You're standing in the foyer of a very large mansion. Dark wooden boards, sanded down to an almost perfectly smooth surface, have been laid as floor. The walls are made from stone but a wooden panel has been put up to cover the bottom half. It matches the floor flawlessly. There is a red carpet laid on the middle of the hallway and it leads off further into the mansion. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
