R {20731}{0}{<248>}{Dining hall (s,e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{At one point in time this room must have been the epitome of extravagance, but now after years of neglect the dining room has fallen into disrepair.  The huge table that nearly fills the room is covered with a half inch of dust.  Deep gouges that look as if they might have been made by swords cover the oaken table.  At the head of the table is a huge chair with intricate carvings running along the arms and back, but the upholstery is ripped apart and the deep red color has faded to a pale, flesh colored pink.  The rest of the chairs around the table are in even worse condition, many of them broken apart.  Shards of wood cover the floor.  The dusty, crystal chandelier hanging over the table is tilted wildly and looks as if it is only being held up by the numerous cobwebs draped from it to the ceiling.  The walls are covered with faded and rotten tapestries, splashed with highlights of dried blood. }{Der'Thalas}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20730}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20744}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20732}{0}{<238>}{Library (n,w)}{<238>"""<088>}{You stand in the massive library of Der'Thalas Keep.  Ancient books and tomes of every sort line the massive bookshelves.  Sadly, most of the books are burned and torn apart.  A thick layer of dust blankets everything in the room as it seems to have been left undisturbed for some length of time.  Along the far side of the room are a pair of hardwood desks.  Both lie splintered and broken as if crushed by some great force.  The thick, musty smell of decay lingers here, most likely from the slowly rotting leather and vellum of the books. }{Der'Thalas}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20730}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20734}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

