R {20735}{0}{<248>}{Armoury (n,w)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{You stand in a broken room.  This place was once the armoury of the elven keep, but it has long been forgotten by time.  Rotted elven skeletons and broken skulls lay randomly about the room, indicating a great battle took place here long ago.  Scattered amongst the vile remains are bits of broken weaponry and armour.  Glancing around, you notice spots of dried blood on the walls, symbolizing a bitter hatred now past.  On the far side of the room, propped on its side against the wall is a large wooden table.  The table must have once held many fine pieces of elven armour and weapons, but all it displays now is the hanging skeleton of some forgotten elven warrior, crucified to the wood by two rusted swords run through its decaying ribcage. }{Der'Thalas}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20734}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24336}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20736}{0}{<248>}{Captain's chambers (e)}{L}{This room lies in hushed silence.  Along one wall is a broken bed while a crushed bookcase lies against another.  Burned in half, a large desk lies in ruin against the far wall.  The air here is thick with dust and cinders and smells of old death.  There is a powerful presence here though, as you can feel it in your soul. }{Der'Thalas}{lyriac}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20734}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20737}{0}{<238>}{Guards' quarters (s,w,stairs)}{<238>] [<088>}{As you enter this room you are immediately assaulted by the pale stench of old death.  Not so much an odor as it is a horrid feeling of sorrowful oppression and dread.  Beds and chests litter the area, mostly broken and utterly useless.  This was clearly a guards' quarters, as the toppled bunks and various accoutrements indicate.  Your light barely holds back the everpresent darkness and casts shades of brownish amber upon everything.   It is clear that nothing has been here for years, yet faint wails of mourning can be heard from somewhere close ... or nowhere at all.  The stone floor is lightly covered with a thick coating of dust, as your new footprints indicate. Broken bits of armour and weapons also litter the room, along with the remains of several guards, long since dead.  A heavy, iron gate blocks the path halfway down a dark stairwell leading into the bowels of the keep.  A strange, chilling wind seems to bellow forth from the dark hole.  It is as if the keep itself is somehow alive. }{Der'Thalas}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20733}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
