E {20737}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20740}{0}{<248>}{Guest chambers (e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{You stand in a large but desolate room.  It looks as though the chamber has been stripped of everything.  Only deep, crimson streaks are splashed upon the walls here.  The scent of death and decay is extremely strong here, as some horrible, vile massacre must have taken place in this cursed room. }{Der'Thalas}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20738}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20741}{0}{<248>}{Master bedroom (s)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{The personal chambers of the king himself.  Broken bits of furniture line the walls, charred and burned like the rest of the keep.  The scent of charcoal is heavy in this room.  A large, burned bed rests in the northeast corner, ashes now replacing the elaborate sheets, while an oaken wardrobe rests in another. }{Der'Thalas}{}{}{marble}{1.000}{1}
E {20739}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20742}{0}{<268>}{Forgotten chapel (e)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{You stand within an old chapel, located deep within the keep.  The walls of this place stand strangely untouched, as if immune to the dark curse that has befallen the land.  Large pillars of pure marble spiral upward toward the mosaic glass ceiling.  The moonlight filters through the colored panes in gentle waves of peace, softly filling the room with a feeling of serenity.  Near the western edge of the room, an ivory altar resides.  The holy dais seems to glow with a faint blue light.  Near the southern wall, a small wooden box lies open to the moonlight.  Small bells line the ceiling border.  Though they look as though their music would provide you with some respite from the evil of the haunted keep, they lie silent now. }{Der'Thalas}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20739}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20743}{0}{<278>}{Dungeon (e,w,n,stairs,s)}{<278>.@.<088>}{            You stand in the center of a dark shrine to death and pain.  Before The Fall, the dungeon cells of Der'Thalas Keep were only places to keep prisoners of war, or thieves and such.  Now, however, the dark cells are infested with vermin and dank with rot.  The moisture is thick here, coating the walls and iron cell bars with a slick layer of dank slime.  The putrid moss has overgrown much of the room, leaving only the cells and broken bits of furniture visible above the vile green carpet.  Boiling every now and then with a bubble of gas, the vomitous mass emits a highly disgusting odor, almost making you retch. A dark iron gate stands partway up the misty stairway, sealing shut the dungeons from the keep.  There are four dungeon cells here, one in each of the cardinal directions. }{Der'Thalas}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51343}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51344}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
