R {20977}{0}{<248>}{A darkened chamber (nw)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{A darkened room which seems to have been a storage room at some  time in the past.  Shattered casks and crumbling crates litter the  floor, yet strangely seem to have been swept away from the center  of the room.  A portion of the floor has been charred as if by  recent and frequent fires.  Someone has camped here, and not so  very long ago. }{Catacombs 2}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20976}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20978}{0}{<268>}{A rubble strewn hall (n,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The dark and dusty corridors are littered with crumbling stone  fallen from the walls and ceiling over the ages.  The strong  dwarven constructed foundation is all that remains of the once  great citadel which presided over the trade routes.  As you wander  down the dark subterranean corridors you marvel at the power  brought to bear which could destroy such magnificent construction. }{Catacombs 2}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20976}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {20979}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {20979}{0}{<268>}{One of the citadel's crumbling halls (n,s,w,e)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{You pick your way through the rubble littering the floor of the  corridor, listening for the telltale signs of danger lurking in the  darkness.  Your footsteps kick up small puffs of dust which swirl  about your ankles to cling to your boots and leggings.  Here and  there along the corridor you can find the remains of ancient  dwarven carvings which once brightened the citadel with their  craftsmanship. }{Catacombs 2}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20978}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
