R {22038}{0}{}{The end of the rainbow bar (s)}{ }{You have come to the actual bar, in the End of the Rainbow bar. The  mecca to any self respecting Leprechaun. As if touched by god, golden shafts of light stream into the room and rest on the bottles of spirits kept behind the bar.  It's almost as if this place has a feeling of reverance about it and if you didn't know better...was that a heavenly choir singing 'hallelujah' in the background...Tacked to the bar is a  sign you might want to read. }{Leprechaun Village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22036}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22039}{0}{}{Before an impressive house (enter,nw)}{<138>E<088>}{You stand before the doorway of an impressive mushroom house. Over the doorway lintel is the skull of a stag, complete with antlers. Obviously some kind of chieftain lives here.  Perhaps you should go in and find out exactly who lives in here.  }{Leprechaun Village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22033}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22040}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22040}{0}{}{In the king's house (out)}{ }{You have entered a large room, immaculately tidy, with a plush red carpet leading to a small golden throne.  Bright shafts of sunlight stream through the windows of this room leaving the air warm and  filling you with that comfortable warm contented feeling that makes  you want to yawn.  All manner of smells assault your nose from the  smell of tanned leather to the ardent smell of wood polish.  Obviously  whomever lives here is held in high respect by their people.  As with  the smaller houses a set of stairs lead to the house's upstairs quarters. }{Leprechaun Village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22039}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22041}{0}{}{A damp and dismal cave (w)}{ }{You find yourself in a small cave deep in the bowels of the hill.  Bones litter the floor and the air in this cave is stale and filled with the smell of corruption and death.  This must be the lair of some foul creature.  You had best beware, lest you become another set of bones. However this isn't what catches your eye, for chained to the far wall is a young leprechaun who looks at you with hopeful tear filled eyes. }{Leprechaun Village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22037}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

