R {22274}{0}{<248>}{Ms. Haagen's Room (e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{You walk into a flurry of activity.  The Call, WLC's student-run newspaper, is in its final stage of production, layout.  Everybody's patience is at an end.  Every two minutes someone screams.  The tension in here is so thick you could cut it, nevermind...  }{Walled Lake Central High School}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22271}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22275}{0}{<248>}{Ms. Kirk's Room (w)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{Man!  Your nose is assaulted by the smell of formeldehyde! This place reeks of old people!  The walls are decorated with tacky portraits, and cut flowers in vases are everywhere.  The only thing missing is the lace doilies.  That would make this place an exact replica of an old folks home...  }{Walled Lake Central High School}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22273}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22276}{0}{<248>}{Ms. Walters' Room (e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{You enter the teen health room, a large room with lots of skeletons in it.  It would appear that you interrupted a SADD meeting.  'Welcome!' the members say.  They beckon you towards them and point out a desk for you to sit at.  'Initiation is about to begin...'  }{Walled Lake Central High School}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
