R {22317}{0}{}{The front of a greenhouse (e,s,n,w)}{ }{This is the front end of the greenhouse.  Plants and flowers of a variety of types grow from the ceiling, patches of soil, and in an assortment of pots.  A slight mist is sprayed upon the plants periodically keeping them moist.  The mist is spread about by a slight breeze from vents in the ceiling, adding to the heavy humidity of the room.  Sets of automatic sliding glass doors lead to the west, north, and south.  Many more plants are growing in the open area to the east. }{Greenhouse}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
