R {22483}{0}{}{The Master Bedroom (n)}{ }{It is surpisingly underfurnished. There is a simple queen sized bed on one wall, with a dresser opposite the foot of the bed. On the dresser is an older tv. Two nightstands flank the bed. It doesn't look like they really get to spend much time in here. }{Toddler House}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22482}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22484}{0}{}{Silas' Nursery (s)}{ }{A medium sized bedroom, its walls are painted a light shade of blue, common to nurseries for little boys. Large painted wooden letters adorn the walls spelling "SILAS" just above the crib. There is a changing table opposite the window. Next to the changing table is a diaper pail. Toys are strewn about the room as if a tornado had been through here. }{Toddler House}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22482}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22485}{0}{}{Stuck in the mud}{ }{You are deep within a mud puddle.  The mud around you sucks and pulls at your limbs, oozing into your every orifice.  The mud is warm, almost comforting.  Your senses must be somewhat distorted from a lack of oxygen because you seem to be able to see microscopic critters swimming around you in the mud.  It is hard to tell which way is up. }{Mud Puddle}{mud_puddle}{}{}{1.000}{1}
