R {22512}{0}{}{Country (leave,s)}{<138>L<088>}{The sun is beating down on the beautiful country setting. The trees are lush with deep, rich green leaves and all the flowers are in full bloom. The smell of fresh cut hay lingers in the air. Birds gather bits of straw and twigs to aid in their nest building. The sounds of farm animals echo through the warm summer breeze. In the distance you can see a pleasant country farmhouse that has a long, gravel lane-way. }{Rampage of the Piggies}{rampage_of_the_piggies}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {197}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22513}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22513}{0}{}{Lane-way (s,n)}{ }{This long gravel lane-way looks well used and welcoming. Just ahead you can make out the farmhouse and its white picket fence. The ground beneath your feet is uneven and filled with potholes. Straw pieces litter the ground almost everywhere you look. Bits of grass can be found growing up through the rocks and stones. Just beyond the house you notice their yard is well cared for and healthy green in color.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22512}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22514}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22514}{0}{}{Farm House (e,s,w,n)}{ }{The white picket fence seems to surround the whole house with a gate opening up to the farmhouse just ahead. The house appears to be very quiet and empty. The gate is open for all to venture forward. There is a walkway made from patio stones here that go all the way to the steps of the house. The soft humming sound of a young girl can be heard ever so faintly.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22513}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22515}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22516}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22517}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22515}{0}{}{Yard (w)}{ }{You have made your way into the yard of the Owles family farm. Here you can see the yard is scattered with items that must belong to a pleasant young lady. A toy horse and a stuffed piglet seem to be her best friends at what appears to be an afternoon tea party. The grass is well trimmed and a rich green tone shows years of good landscaping. }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22514}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22516}{0}{}{Barn (climb,n)}{<238>C<088>}{This barn is well taken care of with very high ceilings. Bits of straw drop occasionally from the cracks in the loft floor above. The smell of manure is very strong in here. A large bin full of feed is against the far wall. Glancing around you see a hayloft not far away, with the only access being up that wooden rickety ladder against the wall.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22514}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22518}{climb}{climb}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22517}{0}{}{Garden (w,e)}{ }{The garden you are standing at the edge of grows Hickson county's largest assortment of blue ribbon vegetables. Carrots, tomatoes, onions, potatoes, pumpkins, squash, turnip, and corn appear to be just some of the vegetables you can see growing nicely here. Just over to your left you can see a shed that appears to be broken down. Fertilizer bags litter the ground here as well as a few garden tools. Wooden stakes with seed packets are lined up in rows marking the vegetable types. Dark rich soil is packed down quite nicely here and makes for a perfect growing environment.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22514}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22519}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22518}{0}{}{Hayloft (d,jump)}{ }{Bales of hay are stacked everywhere up here. Each bale seems to be tied nice and tight with binder twine and stacked perfectly. There are no signs of a light switch or any electrical fixture that could cast some light up here. Sunlight streams through the cracks in the barn boards casting a little light. Upon further inspection you notice that many birds have made nests in the rafters above. The only way out of here other than back down the way you came is through the loft window. Just in the near distance you can see a beautiful pasture.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22516}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22520}{jump}{jump}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22519}{0}{}{Shed (e)}{ }{Standing before you appears to be a partially broken down shed. The door hangs lopsided but appears to be unlocked. The windowpane is cracked and covered with some sort of brown paper from the inside. You can just peek in the window through a rip in the paper. It seems this shed is filled quite to its capacity, with no room for even the smallest garden tool. You can see that it is full of accessories to help aid in the continued production of prize-winning veggies. The ground here is soft but lush with green foliage.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22517}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22520}{0}{}{Pasture (e)}{ }{The sun shines brightly in the cloudless sky. The birds and bees fly lazily through the air with such grace and ease. Stretching as far as the eye can see is beautiful grazing pastureland. Very pleasant to walk through if you are careful. Tiny pieces of straw are scattered through the grass and flowers. Trees can be seen far off in the distance. Just ahead you can see where the pasture ends and the wooded area of this land begins.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22521}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22521}{0}{}{Woods (w)}{ }{Large trees of various kinds with lush green foliage are growing plentifully here. The trees provide a gentle breeze and protection from the rays of the afternoon sun. Many different varieties of leaves and nuts can be seen on the ground. Your way is blocked here, if you had intended your nature walk to continue. There must be another way into this forest.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22520}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22522}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22522}{0}{}{Trail (sw,n)}{ }{The smell lingering in the air here is not quite the smell of animal but of sawdust and oil. Now how could that be? The large leaves on the trees prevent the sun from brightening up the path. Twigs, leaves, and bits of composting material enrich the soil beneath your feet. The path continues just ahead through the darkness and cover of the thick bush.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22521}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22523}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22523}{0}{}{Sawmill (w,ne)}{ }{Emerging from the trees you have stumbled upon an old abandoned sawmill. Sawdust is on the ground everywhere you step. Bits of wood chips and tree bark cover the ground. The footprints are not man-made, but of an animal, suggesting the sawmill is not quite as abandoned as it would appear. Grunting sounds of pigs can be heard in the distance. The sawmill looks quite old and broken down. The roof has red shingles on it, with a small chimney that appears to have smoke coming out of it. From here you can see the docking area of the sawmill.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22522}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22524}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22524}{0}{}{Docking bay (e,s)}{ }{This docking bay is where the big trucks back up to pick up the finished wood. A skid of wood stands here waiting to be removed. The ramp is crumbling apart from lack of repair and damage taken from the elements. Tiny bits of cement crunch under your feet. Just ahead you see a doorway with the door itself completely missing.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22523}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22525}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22525}{0}{}{Office (e,n)}{ }{You have stumbled upon the office of the head ringmaster of this operation. A large pine desk is littered with papers that appear to be plans of some sort. There appears to be another exit just behind that box.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22524}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22526}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22526}{0}{}{Mud pit (s,w)}{ }{You seem to be in a mud pit. Rather soft and wet this mud provides a soft landing nonetheless. This must be where the pigs come to cool off. The center of the pit is very wet and squishy but the outer edge appears to be a bit drier and more stable.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22525}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22527}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22527}{0}{}{Log pile (e,n)}{ }{After crawling out of the mud and finally being back on dry ground you notice a huge pile of logs before you. These must have been long forgotten when the mill was abandoned. Perhaps a more thorough investigation of this pile of lumber is in order.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22526}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22528}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22528}{0}{}{Abandoned truck (w,ne)}{ }{Sitting here with two wheels buried deep in the mud is an old abandoned truck. The outside is covered in rust and the tires appear to be very flat. Garbage litters the box of the truck making it quite the eyesore. The driver's side door is open showing the inside is also pretty torn up. The glove box is open showing the contents have been removed long ago. Dust covers the dash, and the windshield is layered in cobwebs. The seat is in the same disrepair as the entire truck.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22527}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22529}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22529}{0}{}{Tool shed (se,sw)}{ }{Hardly looking like a tool shed any longer, this broken down structure must have served its purpose well when it was new. The window is covered half way over with a board nailed on diagonally, with the door missing completely. Bits of sawdust litter the ground making it a lot easier to walk on and less muddy.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22528}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22530}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22530}{0}{}{Garbage dump (nw,e)}{ }{A huge garbage dump stands like a mountain before you. It seems the pigs have their own built in food supply right on the site. Food and garbage of every imaginable kind are piled here. Cans, jars, bags, lids, and plastic eating utensils are just a few of the items seen here.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22529}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22531}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22531}{0}{}{Compost pile (w)}{<138>J<088>}{With the sun to assist the breaking down process, this huge decomposing pile seems to be rotting away nicely. It would seem that what did not decompose yet will soon be consumed by the new tenants to this area. Banana peels, eggshells, sandwich halves, cobs of corn, and old rotting pizza make up a tiny portion of this heap. Some of this food cannot even be identified anymore.  }{Rampage of the Piggies}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22530}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {197}{jump}{jump}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22532}{0}{}{Inside the Budweiser racing boat}{ }{You are sitting inside the Budweiser racing boat.  A few control panels are on the dash, and the two gas turbine engines lie directly behind you.  Let's just hope for your sake you know how to drive something with so much power. }{Brewery Swamp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {17621}{push button}{push button}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {22533}{0}{}{On Stage With Pat (w,e)}{ }{This is where the game begins.  You think that you can get up closer to the board if only Pat were out of here.  You see a big wheel in front of you, with brightly coloured wedges. Everything seems sparkly and bright, the glamour of the stage almost overwhelms you! The place where the contestants are supposed to stand is to the west. Perhaps you should head that way if you want to play. }{Game Show}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {16705}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {22534}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

