R {23164}{0}{}{Foothills of the eastern peak (nw,s,w)}{ }{An occasional bit of dirt and debris fall from the peak above as the wind blows away loose sections of the mountain.  The forest ends into a small foothill section before the eastern peak of Mount Perplexus.  The peak rises high above you.  The foothills are made of dust and dirt with the occasional boulder that has fallen from the eastern peak of Perplexus.  To the west you sort of detect an opening to a forest.   }{Around the town of Angelo}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
