R {23295}{0}{<228>}{A clearing (w)}{<228>, .<088>}{The clearing to the south of the rocky hill seems desolate, although the grass is as green and the wildflowers as vibrant as anywhere else. The forest to the south and east presses in forbiddingly, and no breeze stirs the blades of grass. A ceaseless tune drifts across the grass, lonely and sad. To the north, a rocky slope juts up from the greenery to the hill above. }{Alagon's Hill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23293}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23296}{0}{<228>}{A clearing by a hill (e,se,s)}{<228>, `<088>}{To the north and west, the forest presses in on the clearing. Trees cluster together along the grassy border, growing around and into one another. A somewhat steep but passable slope leads up a hill in the southeast. It's almost uncomfortably warm here. The ever-present melody drifting from the east hangs flat in the still air. Wildflowers grow in abundance here, layering petals atop the grass.}{Alagon's Hill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
