R {23310}{0}{<278>}{On the Road to Harfain (n,w)}{<278>-+ <088>}{Lazy sunlight beats down from above as you trudge on the roughly cobbled road to Harfain.  Deeply worn paths in the stones at your feet tell the tale of a bustling trade coming and going from the  town.  The road continues west and north.  Thick trees stand back  from the heavily traveled roads.  The forest is dark, likely the haven to some of the more unsavory individuals of the town. To the southeast you notice the ground rises abruptly toward a rocky mountain. }{Harfain}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
