R {23426}{0}{}{Ending of a natural tunnel (w)}{ }{The tunnel ends in a myriad of stalagmites, stalactites, and columns to the east, these would be impossible to cross. A river flows from the west, in between these with a splashing sound. Towards the northern wall there is an elevated plateau on which you see some rags lying in a small pile that could resemble a bed. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23425}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23427}{0}{}{Bright hallway (s,n)}{ }{Green stones form the walls, fading from blue towards the north and yellow to the south. The stones in this section of the hallway are rectangular, 2" wide and 4" tall, resembling the scales of a fish. The hallway continues to your north and south. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23414}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23428}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23428}{0}{}{Bright hallway (s,n)}{ }{The hallway is dominated by the mosaic of a great yellow sun, formed from small pieces of bright yellow stones. The sun spans from the east wall, across the ceiling, and half way down the western wall, where it is partially covered by a bright green curtain, making it look like the sun is rising up over a grassy field in the springtime. The hallway continues to your north where it fades to green south. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23427}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23429}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {37359}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23429}{0}{}{Great hallway (s,n)}{ }{The long hallway ends in a big ebony door with an ivory crest embossed on it. The same crest can be seen on the east and west walls, only here it is made of thin interwoven gold threads on a background of lapis lazuli stones that have been carefully cut into squares and placed on the walls. The brightest of these semiprecious stones lies towards the north, and the darkest is closest to the black ebony door to your south. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23428}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23430}{s}{open door;s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23430}{0}{}{A study room (w,n)}{ }{This room appear to be a study, the walls are lined with bookshelves and an oak desk dominates the centre of the room. The desk is flooded with books and scrolls in no apparent order. There is an ebony door to the north, and to your west you see something that looks like a bedroom. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23429}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23431}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23431}{0}{}{The master bedroom (e)}{ }{The walls of the master bedroom are covered in tapestries and a high white carpet covers the floor. The ceiling has been painted black with small gold dots on it. A king size bed covered with silk stands against the west wall with bed tables on either side of it. A big white closet stands in the southeastern corner of the room. A large mirror hangs in the middle of the north wall. A small table vith various perfumes and makeup has been placed in front of it, with a pillowed chair placed under the table. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23430}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23432}{0}{<238>}{Forest Road (nw,n,w)}{<238>. .<088>}{Forest Road Dead leaves rustle beneath your feet as you walk. The forest has a sweet smell about it, and the fine day puts a spring in your step.  You are standing on an old road winding through a forested valley.  Lofty peaks form natural barriers in most directions.  To the north, you can make out that the mountain forest clears.  You notice a narrow path cut through the forest to the northwest. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8046}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23433}{nw}{nw}{9}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23434}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23433}{0}{}{A Mountain Path (se,w)}{ }{You are on a path running from the southeast, and surrounded by a dense forest.  To the west, it leads down into a small ravine.  The path is very narrow, and the trees are extremely thick, which leaves only enough room for one person to pass at a time.  There are birds chirping in the trees, and the mountain air is cool and refreshing. }{Explorer's Tomb}{explorers_tomb}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23432}{se}{se}{6}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23436}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23434}{0}{<278>}{On a Road (s,d)}{<278>- -<088>}{On a Road The sun is shining and it's a nice day to be out.  The road winds its way through the hills and you could easily leave the road.  This road bears the evidence of many years of frequent travel.  To the west and east exploration is blocked by impassable mountain ranges.  To the north, a deep ravine with a river at the bottom.  Across the ravine, you think you make out a ruined town.  Just at the edge, you can make out a bridge.  From here, the road leads south into a forest or down to the edge of the ravine where the bridge lies. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23432}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23435}{d}{d}{32}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23435}{0}{<238>}{Bridge across Balooga River (u,n)}{<238>===<088>}{You stand at the edge of a deep abyss. A long wooden bridge, suspended by ropes, crosses the abyss to the other cliff side. Below, you see the Balooga River raging towards the east. The wind is very strong. A sign is posted to the left here. To the south, a road leads up into the hills. }{Balooga Falls}{balooga_falls}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23434}{u}{u}{16}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23445}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23436}{0}{}{An Archeological Dig (e)}{ }{The ravine is small, about the size of a cottage, and is accessible only from one side.  The hard clay floor is divided into equally sized squares by wooden pegs pressed into the clay and connected by pieces of string.  Some of the squares have been excavated and partially uncovered bits of pottery and bone are visible in the shallow pits.  One of the pits near the ravine wall is quite deep, and a ladder peeks over its mouth.  The ravine is lined by thickly packed trees pierced only by a narrow trail leading east. }{Explorer's Tomb}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23433}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23437}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23437}{0}{}{The Entrance to a Tomb (w,u)}{ }{The clay has been scraped away from the wall of the ravine to reveal a carved stone doorway about the right size for a very tall dwarf.  The clinging clay has been cleaned from the top of the door frame, revealing some ancient runes.  The door itself, which is open a crack, is intricately carved in bas-relief.  A rickety ladder leads up the sticky clay walls of the hole to the ravine floor above. }{Explorer's Tomb}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23436}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23438}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23438}{0}{}{An Unspoiled Tomb (e,n,s)}{A}{A large pillar stands in the center of this dusty room, blocking your view of the far wall.  A serpentine dragon, carved from stone, coils around the pillar.  Its jaws open wide as if in a roar.  Stone arches form the chamber's low ceiling.  The tomb is lost in darkness to the north and south.  A scattering of footprints disturb the thick layer of dust on the floor here, filling the air with motes of dust that dance in the light. }{Explorer's Tomb}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23437}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23439}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23440}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23439}{0}{}{An Unspoiled Tomb (w,s)}{ }{This corner of the tomb is covered in deep shadows.  In the dim light the strange carvings that cover the walls look mysterious and arcane.  The ceiling is made of thick stone arches about five foot high.  The floor is covered in inches of dust, mostly undisturbed save for a few recent looking footprints.   The air is filled with sparkling motes of disturbed dust.  A large pillar carved with a serpentine dragon stands in the center of the chamber to the southwest. }{Explorer's Tomb}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23438}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {37485}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23440}{0}{}{An Unspoiled Tomb (w,n)}{ }{This corner of the chamber is covered in thick shadows that hide the walls and slide menacingly up the ceiling. The broad arches of the ceiling are high enough for a tall dwarf and are made of dark stone that eats the light and makes the shadows seem darker.  The walls are covered with glyphs and pictographs that seem to move in the half-light.  A large pillar encircled by a raised carving of a serpentine dragon stands in the center of the chamber to the northwest. }{Explorer's Tomb}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23438}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {37483}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23441}{0}{}{An Unspoiled Tomb (e,n)}{C}{The walls of this corner of the chamber are smooth and unadorned except for a large stone button in the center of the south wall.  The great arches of the ceiling are made of dark stone and seem to eat the light, making the chamber dark and full of shadows.  To the northeast, a large pillar stands in the center of the chamber encircled by a raised carving of a serpentine dragon. }{Explorer's Tomb}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37483}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23442}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23442}{0}{}{An Unspoiled Tomb (w,n,s)}{D}{The room is dominated by a large pillar entwined with a carving of a serpentine dragon that stands in the center of the room to the east.  A large stone door stands in the center of the western wall, adorned with carvings of a lifesized gnome who seems to be staring at you. }{Explorer's Tomb}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23441}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23443}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
