R {23740}{0}{<238>}{Lotharon's Library (s)}{<238>"""<088>}{This is the King's library. Giant walnut bookshelves cover the walls, reaching from the flagstone floor to the vaulted stone ceiling above. Thousands of books grace these shelves. Books on virtually every subject imaginable in the kingdom. Four leather chairs sit in the room, making a vague reading circle should the King or Prince wish to discuss literature with their guests. A ladder is attached to the shelves that can be moved about the room for anyone wishing to reach a book on one of the upper shelves. A large wooden chandelier hangs from a chain attached to the apex of the ceiling that provides light for the room. South is the archway leading back out into the entrance of the castle. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23733}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23741}{0}{<238>}{Lotharon's Great Hall (e,s,n,w)}{<238>] [<088>}{Wow. You're standing in the middle of the Castle in what is known as the Great Hall. The ceiling towers overhead. The ceiling is painted with a beautiful scene of the Florin countryside. The floor is covered in a plush red velvet carpet and the stone walls are covered in banners and paintings that hang between the sconces that light the room. Overhead to the west just past the giant painting is a balcony overlooking this hall. Smaller corridors lead off in several directions and to the immediate west is a set of large golden doors standing open. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23739}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23742}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
