R {23747}{0}{<238>}{Lotharon's Billiard Room (e,nw,s)}{<238>] [<088>}{The billiard room is where the King and his guests come to relax after a hard day of running the realm. The stone walls are hung with dark fabrics that dampen the light from the sconces into a soft glow. Along the northern wall is a wooden rack full of pool sticks and several plush chairs sit along the edges of the room for guests to sit in. In the center of the room is a huge pool table, carved from solid mahogany with a perfectly smooth red velvet top. The balls for the game shine brightly from their slot in the side of the table, awaiting the King to come play with them. To the northwest is a large wooden door. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23744}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
