E {45224}{w}{push knot}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23753}{0}{}{Lotharon's Southern Tower (d,u)}{ }{Steep brown stone stairs lead both up to the top of the tower and back down into the castle hall. The stairs are wide and deep, made to accommodate troops of several men across in times of trouble. Along the plain stone walls are metal sconces, lit to provide a soft glow to light your way. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23746}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23761}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23754}{0}{}{Lotharon's Bedroom (e)}{ }{These are the sleeping quarters of King Lotharon and his beloved Queen Bella. The walls are hung with black and gold fabrics while a large window looks out onto the gardens and forest that lie west of the castle. The stone floor is covered by a large bearskin rug and candelabra stand in each corner to illuminate the room. The southern wall features a large fireplace with a small fire burning inside. A beautiful canopied bed sits between the window and the door while a tall mahogany chest stands against the northern wall. The fireplace keeps the room quite warm and the candles suffuse the bedroom with a soft glow. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23746}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23755}{0}{}{Lotharon's Castle Balcony (s,w,n)}{ }{This is the balcony overlooking the ground floor of the castle. Down below you can see the great hall and above that, the beautiful painted ceiling depicting a scene of the Florin countryside. The balcony continues to the north and south while a door stands to the west. Along the walls are sconces that light your way. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23746}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23756}{w}{open door;w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23757}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23756}{0}{}{Lotharon's Council Chambers (e)}{ }{This is the War Room of King Lotharon. Rarely used these days by the King himself, it is much more often frequented by the King's son, Prince Humperdinck. The room is dominated by a large round table that sits in the center of the room. High-backed chairs are placed around the table, twelve in all. Along the walls are symbols of war and state: flags, banners, shields, pikes, swords and the like. On the western wall there is also a large fireplace to keep the room warm during the bitter cold of winter. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23755}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23757}{0}{}{Lotharon's Castle Balcony (u,s,w)}{ }{This is the northern end of the castle balcony.  On the northeast it opens up to a wonderful view of Florin City. Down below in that direction you can the goings-on of the townspeople. To the north climb a set of stairs up into the northern tower while a door stands to your west. The hall continues back to the south, lined with sconces on the walls and red carpet to pad your footing. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23755}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23758}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
