R {23822}{0}{}{G.R.O.S.S. Headquarters (d)}{ }{The treehouse seems to have been assembled quite well, no doubt Calvin's father, and not the boy himself put the hours into this place.  This is where the best laid plans of the neighborhood's most devious mind come to fruition -- G.R.O.S.S Headquarters. }{Calvin and Hobbes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23812}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23823}{0}{}{Riding the Bus}{ }{The bus is a long tube of steel sheet filled with green vinyl benches big enough for two.  With each turn and gust of wind, the frame groans and creaks.  The windows are either stuck closed or open, and the floor is very sticky. }{Calvin and Hobbes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}

R {23824}{0}{}{Leaving the School (walkway)}{ }{A walkway leads from this parking lot into the school.  This is where the buses line up to take weary children home after a day of school.  There is no snow on the paved walkways, for safety reasons.  A walkway leads east into the school and there is a sign here. }{Calvin and Hobbes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
