R {23989}{0}{<168>}{Dead End (w)}{<168>[ ]<088>}{The continuously flowing water drips slowly onto the floor. It's accumulating into shallow divots on the floor. The icy walls are pulsing with an eerie sense of cold. Large scratches have been dug into the darkened corners. A large icicle has formed all of the way to the floor, reaching down from the darkness above. The ice formations seem to be natural, and yet completely undisturbed for what must be ages. }{Jaffa's Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23988}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23990}{0}{<168>}{A Dark Icy Cavern (n,e)}{<168>[ ]<088>}{An overwhelming silence fills this barren area, blocking out the numerous sounds from the lands above. A quick scan of the cavern seems to reveal nothing out of the ordinary. However, the walls are reflecting the light in an odd manner, as it travels through the crystal-like chamber. The ground is unquestionably damp, gathering the icy waters that continuously drip from the ceiling high above. A single damp, extinguished lantern hangs from a lone, darkened crevice on the wall's otherwise smooth, icy, cold surface. }{Jaffa's Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23988}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23993}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23991}{0}{<168>}{A Dark Icy Cavern (s,w)}{<168>[ ]<088>}{This is a wide empty corridor in the icy cavern, where little can be seen from the surrounding area, or heard from the land above. The water, from the now visible ceiling, is dripping to the floor and landing in the various puddles below. Huge gaps run along the bottom of the walls. Ice shavings, and some larger chunks of ice, have frozen to the ground in no obvious pattern. The ceiling has some enormous spikes of ice hanging down dripping water into the room. }{Jaffa's Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23988}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23994}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23992}{0}{<168>}{Dead End (e)}{<168>[ ]<088>}{The area's sloping floor is slowly filling up with water, running down toward a pool of water in the center. The dark and cloudy water is covered with a thin layer of ice making the ground below very difficult to make out. One wrong step may perhaps whisk one under a deep river of icy water. The walls are smooth and send a faint flickering reflection of the light. A single, ancient looking lantern protrudes out of the far darkened corner. }{Jaffa's Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23988}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {23993}{0}{<168>}{Dead End (w)}{<168>[ ]<088>}{This is a frigidly cold section of the cavern. The chilling walls are barren, except for the many cracks indicative of someone or something scraping at the walls. The corridor sharply narrows here to a dead-end. The extreme slope of the walls and ceiling enhance the claustrophobic feeling of an already narrow chamber, not to mention the long, slender, icy columns hanging from the gradually declining ceiling. }{Jaffa's Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
