R {24004}{0}{}{Harpy's Lair (s)}{ }{You have entered into the Haglar Harpy's Lair.  Dung and other refuse lie    heaped upon the floor.  You are instantly repulsed by the living    conditions and foulness of the lair. }{Catapult}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24003}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24005}{0}{}{Base of the Tower of Pak-Tor (u,n,out)}{<228>O<088>}{You have just entered the legendary magical Tower of Pak-Tor, renowned for its unsurpassed beauty, inestimable wealth, and tireless strength. However, after a brief look you can tell that this legend has come to an end.  What you see laying about you, if once was the Tower of Pak-Tor, is no longer the mighty citadel it used to be.  Cobwebs cover the ceilings and walls masking any glimmer of beauty that this tower once had.  A set of spiral stairs, old and rotting, lead up into the darkness.  Light pours in dimly from an open, broken window on the south side of the tower.  Crumbled pieces of the odd material that Pak-Tor was made of lay in ruins at your feet.  There is a door in the northern side of the Tower, and the exit to the tower is to your south. }{Tower of Pak-Tor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8495}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24006}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
