R {24030}{0}{}{Eating Chamber (n,s)}{ }{You have entered the main eating hall for the giants. A large, wooden table sits in the center of the room. Wooden chairs of various sizes, shapes, and colors are arranged around the table. Resting atop the table is a large, half-cooked piece of some kind of meat that is best left alone. Bowls, goblets and platters are scattered about the top of the table. Arranged around the room, in no particular order, are several torches that provide light. }{Fire Giant Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24029}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24031}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24031}{0}{}{Nursery (s)}{ }{This part of the caverns ends in what appears to be the nursery for the fire giant cubs. You notice all the normal things that would belong in a nursery. A few small beds line the back wall and several toys are scattered around the room. What looks like a human skull lies in one corner while several long bones clutter another. Several torches line the walls providing light. }{Fire Giant Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24030}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24032}{0}{<238>}{Guard Room (n,s)}{<238>] [<088>}{This section of the cavern appears to be some sort of guard room. Very little adorns this room except a small table and a few chairs. A few torches allow you to notice deep scars in the rock walls of this room. }{Fire Giant Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24026}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
