E {24073}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24075}{0}{}{Campfire (sw,e)}{ }{Before you is a large roaring campfire.  Stones are lined around the fire to help prevent it from spreading beyond where it's wanted to burn.  There are benches set on all four sides of the fire, placed roughly six hands away from it.  Any grasses or plants unfortunate enough to try and grow near the fire just get burnt up and die.  This would be the perfect place to sit around and tell war stories to your friends while enjoying the warmth of a fire on those chilly nights when there is nothing left to do but wait for morning to arrive. }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24073}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24076}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24076}{0}{<278>}{Woodlot (ne,s,w)}{<278>. .<088>}{You have entered what the villagers use as their woodlot.  They have logs piled as high as they could safely pile them here.  Every kind of wood they could find are in the piles.  These piles are stacked according to length, shorter cuts of wood for fires and cook stoves alongside longer poles used to build cabins and other buildings. }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24075}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24077}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24078}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24077}{0}{<278>}{Canteen (e,ne,n)}{<278>[ ]<088>}{You're standing in the center of the village's canteen.  There are a few tree stump benches placed around the area and a cook stove on the south side of the path.  With the fast-paced comings and goings of the troll hunters, no one has really had the time to build a dining hall, so they make do with this outdoor eatery.  }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24076}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24079}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24080}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24078}{0}{}{Bunkhouse (e)}{ }{This bunkhouse was built in case new people arrive to help out the team on their troll hunting.  If it wasn't here, where would the new arrivals sleep?  There are four rows of bunk beds lining this cabin and a small potbellied wood stove smack dab in the middle of the room, providing warmth on those chilly nights.  }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24076}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24079}{0}{<278>}{Amphitheater (w,e)}{<278>[ ]<088>}{You have entered the camp's small amphitheater where they put on plays and recite poetry to entertain each other on those rainy and boring nights.  The stage is just big enough to hold three actors and a couple of chairs.  There is enough bench seating to hold the whole camp plus a few guests that happen by.  The main attraction is of course the bard's songs of heroic battles won by such great warriors that have come and gone through the camp.  }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24077}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24081}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24080}{0}{<278>}{Outhouse (sw)}{<278>[ ]<088>}{This small outhouse was built so the residents of the village had somewhere private to attend to their business.  The shack is barely big enough to turn around in and has a flat board seat, with a hole cut in the center of it that leads into a dark pit.  The door leading into this building has a half moon cut out at the top of it to allow for lighting and there is no need for locks since, well, who would even be tempted to bother someone using this place?  It's not as if it's a local teen hang out. }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24077}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24081}{0}{<228>}{Dirt path (w,se)}{<228>, `<088>}{This section of the path leads from the forge to the canteen.  The dirt has been trampled so much that it is as hard as rock and a dead giveaway that someone travels along here way too much.  The only notable thing along this section of the path is the beginnings of another building to the south of the path.  Its base looks large enough to be some kind of store or bar.  That's just speculation though, we will have to wait and see what they create.  }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24079}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24082}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24082}{0}{<278>}{Forge (nw,ne)}{<278>[ ]<088>}{Set off to the south of the path, a brick forge was created so the villagers can repair any damage their weapons or armor happen to take during battle with the trolls.  There is a pile of coal off to the left side of the furnace and a bellows to the right side to help stoke the fire when in use.  There are four barrels of water for cooling the heated metal and an anvil right next to them to shape the metal on.  A rack of tools hangs just off to the right of the anvil, within easy reach so the smith doesn't have to waste time looking for the right tool while the metal quickly cools on him.  }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24081}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24083}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24083}{0}{}{Playground (sw,n,se)}{A}{Following the path you have come to a makeshift playground with monkey bars that look as if they could keep the most spoilt kid smiling.  A sandbox filled with interesting dirt-moving toys is on one side and a small tree house is on the other.  The path continues in two directions, north to a fish cleaning station and southwest deeper into the village. }{Troll Hunter's village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24082}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24084}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
