E {24138}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24138}{0}{}{A small tent (n,ne)}{ }{This must be the leader's tent, everything here is of a much better quality than what you'd expect to see from a normal desert nomad. The ground is covered entirely by vibrant rugs, with the exception of a small open spot surrounding the fire pit. Upon these rugs lie a good quality bedroll and the small chest. }{Nomad Camp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14111}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24137}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24139}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (e,s)}{ }{Scorpion Caves You wander deeper in these caves and find more reddish sand.  It looks like some of this sand has been moved around for creatures to live within these caves.  The walls are still fine red sandstone apparently carved by a fine pick, claws or pinchers. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24150}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24153}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24140}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (e,nw)}{ }{Scorpion Caves Exploring further into the caves, you notice these walls need a little more work on being carved.  They are made out of a brightly colored sandstone.  There is a small trickle of water that runs down the wall adding a little moisture to the air. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14046}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24141}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24141}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (e,s,w)}{ }{Scorpion Caves Deeper still you venture in this sandstone cavern, lost in red sand that seems to be drier and darker as you travel further from the entrance, light, and moisture.  These walls are looking more worn as if creatures pass by and rub next to this stone more frequently, wearing away more of the sand to mix with the sand of the floor. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24140}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
