R {24144}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (sw)}{ }{Scorpion Caves This is the scorpions' throne room.  This is where the queen scorpion lives.  The walls are carved out of a reddish sandstone.  The walls are bare and rough to the touch. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24142}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24145}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (w)}{ }{Scorpion Caves You are nearing the heart of the cavern.  The sand reveals many different tracks as if this was the passing room.  The wall shows signs of new digging.  The tunnel continues to go further into the deep caves. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24143}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24146}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (w,nw)}{ }{Scorpion Caves The reddish sandstone here gives off a bright glow.  The tunnel's walls are carved from sandstone.  They chose sandstone because it's an easy digging material.  You wonder how these scorpions can live in such a home.  The air here is very dusty from the digging that goes on. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24143}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24148}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24147}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (e,w)}{ }{Scorpion Caves Inside the reddish sandy cave a trickle of water runs down the wall. There is some reddish quicksand in the corner that could be deadly if you're not careful. The room is very dry and dusty. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24143}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24152}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24148}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (e)}{ }{Scorpion Caves This part of the tunnel is nearing the end of the scorpions' caves. The walls seem to be very moist, and has a dark reddish look. There are marks in the moist walls showing that there are creatures that do pass through here. There is a small trickle of water that runs down the wall. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24146}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24149}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (e,n,sw)}{ }{Scorpion Caves As you wander deeper into the caves of these peculiar creatures, the walls appear to have been carved recently.  There are marks on the wall to show they were carved with pinchers or claws.  The sandstone here looks fairly soft and would make the ideal digging material.  There is a small pile of sand in the corner. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24152}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24150}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24151}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24150}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (ne,s,w)}{ }{Scorpion Caves The sand floor shows many tracks and movements from the inhabitants of this cave.  You get the feeling that this room is the common room where all classes of creatures pass on the way to their own responsibilities and niches. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24149}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24139}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
