R {24153}{0}{}{Scorpion Caves (n)}{ }{Scorpion Caves The walls, ceiling, and floor are covered in reddish sandstone. The color of the sandstone is a bright red almost like a fire. The air is still very dry but you can tolerate it a little more than before. }{Scorpion Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24139}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24154}{0}{}{First Precinct (out,s,n)}{<168>O<088>}{You are standing in the Lobby of the NYPD First Precinct building.  All of the scum and evil from all over the great city of New York funnels down to this very room.  You stand in awe of the incredible diversity in the types of people that are represented in this room.  There is a registration desk here and many chairs.  Most of the people waiting to be registered look like street hustlers and pimps, not your crowd. However, there are also elderly ladies, rich preppy teens, and middle-aged business men. }{NYPD}{nypd}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {2455}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24155}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24156}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {2455}{e}{e}{2}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24155}{0}{}{First Precinct (n)}{ }{This section of the Station is all desks and small cubicles.  This is where most of the paperwork for the station is done.  After all the excitement of catching and arresting the criminals, it can be a relaxing change for the officers then again it can get extremely boring and tedious.  Some officers are busy with people at their desks. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24154}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24156}{0}{}{First Precinct (u,s)}{ }{This section of the Station is mainly information Billboards and Wanted posters.  There are stairs here leading to the second floor of the building. This whole place is quite run down, and very dirty.  With all this scum surrounding you want nothing more then to hop into a hot shower and rinse for several hours.  Perhaps the funding from the city is not pouring in anymore. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24154}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24157}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24157}{0}{}{First Precinct (Second Floor) (u,d,s)}{ }{The second floor.  As dirty as the first floor was, it seemed to be sterile in comparison to what this place is like.  There is a terrible stench that brings tears to your eyes as well.  The second floor of this building is mainly for holding prisoners.  You can see a cell to the south.  The stairs lead up to the third floor and back down to the first floor. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24156}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24158}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24159}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24158}{0}{}{First Precinct (Third Floor) (roof,d,s)}{ }{This is the third floor of the station.  Much to your relief, the stench that was so potent on the second floor is virtually non existent here.  The 'plain clothes' division has offices up here as well as the captain of the precinct. The stairs lead on to the roof and back down to the second floor. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24157}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24161}{roof}{roof}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24162}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24159}{0}{}{First Precinct (Second Floor) (cell,n)}{ }{This is a guard room and the entrance to the holding cell.  There is a desk here and a locked gun cabinet. You now realize that the origin of the terrible stench is certainly in the holding cell to the south. It is almost impossible to comprehend that human beings could tolerate such conditions day after day. Perhaps the entire police force has become desensitized to it. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24157}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24160}{cell}{cell}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24160}{s}{cell}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24160}{0}{}{Jail Cell (out)}{ }{You are standing in the Holding Cell of the police station. This is perhaps the most vile place you have ever been in.  The entire cell smells of urine and excrement not unlike the sewer system that runs beneath this fair city.  There are a few drunks and drug pushers in here, everybody looks pretty harmless.  Still, you had better watch yourself.  There are bunk beds on each wall, a sink and toilet in the corner, and numerous names carved or written on everything.  You feel like if you stay here too long they might never let you out. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24159}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24161}{0}{}{On Top of the First Precinct Building (d)}{ }{This is the roof of the First Precinct Building.  There is a helicopter pad up here but no helicopter.  There is an officer here apparently waiting for the helicopter.  The view of Lower Manhattan is amazing from up here. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24158}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24162}{0}{}{First Precinct (Third Floor) (n,s)}{ }{This section of the third floor is occupied by the 'plain clothes' division of the Precinct.  These guys are trying to look as undercover as possible, but they all have on Knicks hats and Yankee jackets. The Captain's office is directly south of here. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24158}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24163}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24163}{0}{}{First Precinct (Third Floor) (n)}{ }{This is the Captain of the Precinct's office. The walls are filled with police awards and pictures of all his hunting expeditions.  His desk is cluttered and there is a portrait of Ronald Reagan on the wall behind it. }{NYPD}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24162}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24164}{0}{}{The Grand Concourse (n,s,e)}{ }{The Grand Concourse. An amazingly huge chamber in Grand Central Terminal. There are a ton of people in here all moving around quickly. Most seem to be late for one thing or another. To the north is the Pan-America building, or what's left of it. Hallways to the rest of the terminal lead east. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {2458}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24165}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24166}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24165}{0}{}{Pan-America Building (n,s)}{ }{The run-down and vacant building seems to have become another endless hallway for travelers to pass through and bums to sleep in.  The Grand Concourse for Grand Central Terminal is south, doors leading out are north. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24164}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {2468}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24166}{0}{}{G.C.T Upper level (d,w)}{ }{You are in the Upper tunnels of the Grand Central Terminal.  A ramp leads down to the subway trains, and hallways lead to the Grand Concourse. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24164}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24167}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24167}{0}{}{Subway Entrance (w,u)}{ }{This appears to be the entrance to the New York Grand Central subway station.  There is a window on the south wall with a sign next to it.  Behind the bars, covering the window, sits a Vulcan man selling tokens.  Everything you can see is covered with a grey film of dirt, oil, and numerous other toxic chemicals. There is a ramp leading up to the rest of the terminal. A tunnel leads west to the trains. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24166}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24168}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24168}{0}{}{Subway Entrance Gate (w,e)}{ }{There is a turnstile on the west wall of this room.  Painted on the archway above the gates is: Train Loading Platforms.  The north and south walls are an ugly shade of grey and black.  The tunnel leads east toward the token sales booth. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24167}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24170}{deposit token}{deposit token}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
