R {24170}{0}{}{Train loading platform (s)}{ }{This is a subway station.  The walls are decorated with posters and graffiti of all colors and persuasions.  A few people are here waiting for a train, they look at you with distrust and fear.  A sign reads: ALL TRANSFERS and EXITS:  South }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24169}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24171}{0}{}{Subway loading platform B (d,n)}{ }{This is a section of the loading platform for the subway.  The floor has a thin layer of slimy water covering part of it.  The platform continues north, and a stairwell leads down.  The sign hanging above it says TRANSFERS \\/ DOWN. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24169}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24173}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24172}{0}{}{Train loading platform (e,enter)}{ }{You are standing on the loading platform for the Shuttle to Times Square.  Many people rush back and forth around you as if you were not here.  A few posters hang on the walls and trash can be seen everywhere.  The words: ALL TRANSFERS and EXITS is written above the east archway. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24169}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24177}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24173}{0}{}{Subway loading platform C (w,u)}{ }{There is a stairway here leading up.  The tunnel is full of trash, and the ground is nearly black with filth.  A sign hangs on the south wall which reads: EXIT AND TRANSFER TO BulletTrain   : Up TRANSFER to Musicland Express      : West }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24171}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24174}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24174}{0}{}{Subway loading platform D (e,d)}{ }{The tunnel comes to an end here with a stairway leading down.  A sign above the stairs reads: OUTBOUND Musicland Express : Down.  The hallway leads back to the east, above the archway is another sign reading: ALL EXITS AND TRANSFERS : East. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24173}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24175}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24175}{0}{}{Train loading platform (u,enter)}{ }{This train has been parked here, and is open as a museum.  It has no schedule and will not move.  Please feel free to use the bar in car 2. This train used to service several sites, which have passed on, such as the loading platform in Grand Central Terminal.  The walls are covered with grafitti.  Posters hang above some of the benches. There are a few people milling about\; most look rather unpleasant.  A stairwell here leads up with a sign reading: ALL TRANSFERS and EXITS. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24174}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24176}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24176}{0}{}{Musicland Express Train (out,car2)}{ }{This is the passenger car on the Musicland Express(R). The train car is especially well-kept for one running to New York City. The train appears to have been vandalized many a time, but always kept in good repair nonetheless.  The train is stopped\; the doors are open. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24175}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24182}{car2}{car2}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24177}{0}{}{GCT-TSQ Shuttle}{ }{This is a cramped little passenger train.  Judging by its appearance it rarely receives any maintenance.  You feel glad it's a short trip from one station to the other.}{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24172}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24181}{out2}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24178}{0}{}{Subway Entrance (u,e)}{ }{This is the entrance to the Times Square subway station.  There is a window on the south wall with a sign next to it.  Behind the bars, covering the window, sits a dude selling tokens.  A stairway leads up to the city.  The trains are east. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
