R {24180}{0}{}{Subway loading platform (w,e)}{ }{The exit can be seen thru the turnstyles to the west.  The walls here are an disgusting black slimy color.  A sign reads: SHUTTLE to Grand Central: East.  Above the south tunnel are the words: BROADWAY LOCAL However a sign is mounted under the local sign reading: CLOSED.  However, you do hear noise from the shuttle tunnel east. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24179}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24181}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24181}{0}{}{Train loading platform (w,enter)}{ }{The loading platform for the Times Square end of the Shuttle.  People are milling around all over the place, you can hear traffic coming from the road above. This is a busy part of NYC.  Above the western archway is engraved: ALL EXITS AND TRANSFERS. }{New York City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24180}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24177}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24182}{0}{<238>}{Bar Car of Musicland Express (car1)}{<238>[P]<088>}{    The Bar Car of the Musicland Express. This long subway car has peaceful music playing. A long bar runs along one side of the car. A sign above the bar reads: 	Beer               : 12 coins 	Coffee             : 100 coins 	Scotch             : 250 coins 	Minstrel Special   : 600 coins 	Special Welcome to Bard's Guild Members! }{New York City}{}{}{pub}{1.000}{1}
E {24176}{car1}{car1}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24183}{0}{<238>}{Mantle Corps :: HRC (w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The Human Resources Center is more of a class room than an office. Instead of cubicles filled with bureaucrats you see empty desks and a holoprojector. The room is poorly lit to facilitate viewing, but LED strips along the floor provide clear aisles for walking. The room is devoid of any living occupants at the moment. }{Mantle Corps}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24184}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24184}{0}{<178>}{Mantle Corps :: Foyer (e,n,exit,w)}{<158>*<168>*<138>*<088>}{It's clear from where you stand that getting into the prison is designed to be nearly hassle-free compared to getting outside. The foyer is divided into modular compartments with magnetically engaged locks. Cameras cover every angle of approach and the biometric scanner on this door includes a retinal scanner for additional security. Beyond all of the security a hallway continues, with doors on either side. }{Mantle Corps}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {2464}{exit}{exit}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24183}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24185}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24186}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24185}{0}{<268>}{Mantle Corps :: Employee Hallway (e,n,s,w)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The Mantle Corps hallway continues here. There are doors to your right and left as well as the opportunity to continue moving forward. While security is less pervasive than the exit you can still spot a few surveillance cameras, and you know that the vents are just as capable of expelling tear gas as they are of air conditioning the room. }{Mantle Corps}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24184}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24187}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24188}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24189}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24186}{0}{<238>}{Mantle Corps :: Employee Locker Room (e)}{<238>"""<088>}{The locker room is a series of aluminoid locker rows ensconced in a smelly blue room. The scents of chlorine and body odor intermingle in such a way to ensure that employees spend no more time here than is absolutely necessary. Speakers in each corner of the room play David Archuleta's Metallica tribute album on constant loop in an effort to focus the rage and hostility of Mantle Corps guards before their shifts. }{Mantle Corps}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24184}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24187}{0}{<138>}{Mantle Corps :: Armory (w)}{<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>}{This tiny room is just large enough for a few people at a time. The walls are completely unadorned and the room's only feature is a small window made of plasteel. This is where Mantle Corps employees can come check out equipment to help them perform their duties. A sign on the wall indicates the items currently available for requisition. }{Mantle Corps}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24185}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24188}{0}{<238>}{Mantle Corps :: Yard Access (n,s)}{<238>|@|<088>}{The hallway ends here at a pair of double reinforced steel doors. Black and yellow stripes are painted along the doorframe and it is clearly labeled AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY. This is the access door leading to the prison's main exercise yard. }{Mantle Corps}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24185}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24190}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24189}{0}{<238>}{Mantle Corps :: Access Point (w,e)}{<238>|@|<088>}{You've accessed the prisoner inprocessing wing of Mantle Corps 003. Prisoners are brought into the facility from a secure loading dock down the hallway, then they are strip searched and integrated into the general population of the prison. There is a large door here, complete with biometric access scanner.  }{Mantle Corps}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24185}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24196}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24190}{0}{<238>}{Mantle Corps :: Yard Access Point (nw,e,ne,s,w,n)}{<238>|@|<088>}{The wall of the exercise yard is interrupted by a large door. There are signs above the door indicating that only authorized personnel may pass beyond this point. There doesn't appear to be any graffiti on the wall near the door. }{Mantle Corps}{mantlecorpsyard}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24188}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24191}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
