R {24288}{0}{}{-(St. Mark's Cathedral, Venice)- (w,n)}{ }{This is the famous St. Mark's Cathedral.  The transition from the Renaissance music to the Baroque era took place here.  The Cathedral is one of the most massive buildings you have ever seen.  There are two choirs on opposite sides of the cathedral singing back and forth to each other.  The smell of incense and combined with the light mist floating around you makes this an intensely religious experience. }{Wax Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
