R {24628}{0}{}{Bart's Treehouse (d)}{ }{Considering this treehouse was built by the hand of Homer, your urge to leave it is great indeed.  Actually, it looks rather stable, and seems as though it has been here for a good long time...there are walls on all sides, and even a wooden roof that has been overlaid with plywood to keep out the water.  In the center of the little  house is a wooden crate that substitutes as a table.  }{Simpsons Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24627}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24629}{0}{}{A forest in the northcountry. (n)}{<108>S<088>}{You have entered a small clearing in a forest.  There is a large statue of a savage beast in the center of the clearing.  It looks as if this is the last remaining symbol of an ancient civilization that held great power in a bygone era.  To the north the forest continues.  The air is slightly chilling and you can tell that you have entered the north country. }{Valley of Forests and Glaciers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24630}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1774}{touch statue}{touch statue}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24630}{0}{}{A northern forest. (s,w,n)}{ }{You are standing in a dense forest of fir trees.  The air is cold and you shiver as you stand here.  Further north you see snow on the branches of some of the trees.  To the south you see a small clearing. }{Valley of Forests and Glaciers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
