R {24631}{0}{}{An old forest in the northlands (n,e)}{ }{This part of the forest seems different.  The trees here are much taller and larger than in the rest of the forest.  The trees are very old and dry\; they would make a very nice fire you think to yourself as you shiver in the cool mountain air while you stand in the shadows of many great trees. }{Valley of Forests and Glaciers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24630}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24633}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24632}{0}{}{A brushy area in the northlands (w,s)}{ }{Here the forest has thinned and the trees are few and far between.  You notice that it has become much colder here and you shiver while you look around.  To the north there is a large mountain that looks impossible to climb.  The top of the mountain is covered by a large glacier. }{Valley of Forests and Glaciers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24630}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24633}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24633}{0}{}{Another brushy area in the northlands. (s,e,n)}{ }{As you travel north out of the forest valley that you were in you notice you are becoming uncomfortably cold.  Also the trees have become few in number as you travel north.  To the north you see a trail that leads northward over frozen ground snaking its way between two snowcapped mountains. }{Valley of Forests and Glaciers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
