R {24757}{0}{<238>}{On a path (e,w)}{<238>. .<088>}{The ancient redwoods thin out, allowing more sunlight to seep through their leafy treetops.  Some blackberry bushes growing along the trail tangle themselves around the massive redwoods. Bumps cover the forest floor, made by the pebbles, rocks and dirt clods embedded into its surface.  A tangy odor resides here, mixing in with the sweet aroma carried in by a breeze, creating an odd but pleasant smell. }{Enchanted Spring}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24755}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {24758}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {24758}{0}{<238>}{A path through the forest (s,e)}{<238>. .<088>}{The dense leafy treetops keep most of the sun's light from penetrating the gloom residing in this part of the forest. Dark shadows cast from the trees make it nearly impossible to see clearly.  However, the deep grooves in the dirt trail help you find your way over this unfamiliar terrain.  The worn forest trail takes a sharp turn to the east, into more pleasant surroundings.  A gentle breeze carries in the sweet fragrance of flowers from the east. }{Enchanted Spring}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
