R {25304}{0}{}{A silent ossiary (s)}{ }{This would appear to be some kind of ossiary, perhaps where the loyal servants of the king were buried so that they may continue to serve him in the afterlife. Whatever their purpose it would appear that someone or something has denied them their peaceful slumber, pulling the bones from the numerous niches where they had been carefully stored scattering them all over the floor of this chamber. Judging by the dust covering the bones this  must have happened some time ago. }{Tomb of King Alaren}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25303}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25305}{0}{}{A silent ossiary (n)}{ }{This would appear to be some kind of ossiary, perhaps where the loyal servants of the king were buried so that they may continue to serve him in the afterlife. Lining three of the walls here are a large number of bone filled niches, each with their own gleaming white skull that glints in the light, their empty eye sockets pools of darkness that seem to follow your every move. A thick coating of dust covers everything here, indicating this room has lain untouched in many centuries. A large pile of bones dominates the center of the room here. }{Tomb of King Alaren}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
