R {25336}{0}{}{Hall of the King (se,e,w,ne)}{ }{Massive stone pillars ring the interior of this large chamber, each spaced ten feet apart and approximetly fifteen feet in from the chamber's stone walls. No expense has been spared here, from the carvings on the pillars to the quality of the marble on the floor and walls. Surely this chamber is fitting resting place for the last King of the Arovians. Lining the walls of this chamber, numerous torches continue to burn brightly illuminating this with flickering torchlight. From beyond the circle of pillars you can see a  large stone bier in the exact center of the room. Resting upon this bier  appears to be a large golden coffin occasionally glinting in the torchlight. }{Tomb of King Alaren}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
