R {25337}{0}{}{Hall of the King (n,nw,s,ne)}{ }{Massive stone pillars ring the interior of this large chamber each spaced ten feet apart and approximetly fifteen feet in from the chamber's stone walls. No expense has been spared here, this whole chamber speaks volumes about the love and respect the Arovians had for their king. Lining the walls of this chamber numerous torches illuminate this area. Creating the occasional pool of fleeting shadow. Beyond the ring of pillars in the exact center of  this chamber appears to be a golden coffin resting on a large stone bier. Just south of here you can see the entrance to a smaller antechamber. }{Tomb of King Alaren}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
