R {25413}{0}{}{-={@ Priest's Inn @}=-}{ }{An airy old fashioned inn with strong wooden benches and tables, and a crackling fire in the fireplace.  There is a sign posted on the wall beside the bar.  Priests of all faiths come here to rest and relax, have a meal and drink.  The prices are quite reasonable.  Type 'list' to see the prices. }{Priests}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25412}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25414}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25414}{0}{}{-={@ Priest's Pub @}=-}{ }{Here in this little pub, Priests come to obtain drinks to carry with them during their travels.  The Master of Beverages takes great pride in the quality of the guild's own beer, which he brews using ingredients grown in the gardens and fields of the guild, and from the hard waters deep below in the strata underlying the foundation of the cathedral.  To the east you hear the voices of other Priests as they move about their business.      Beer                : 12 coins      Coffee              : 100 coins      Scotch              : 200 coins      Pinnacle Special    : 650 coins      Strange brew        : 1600 coins      Water of Life       : 5000 coins }{Priests}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25413}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25409}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25415}{0}{}{-={@ Priest Hole @}=-}{ }{Just a dusty and abandoned alcove. Its purpose is recalled by few ... but whatever it was is no longer here. The dust lies thick and undisturbed, choking you as you kick it up. }{Priests}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25412}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
