R {25584}{0}{<278>}{Town Gates (ne,sw)}{<278>- -<088>}{You are standing just inside the town gates of Casaria. Casaria is a rather small-sized town, however, it is still rather popular. The arena is one of the best around, and draws crowds from distant lands. The infamous Library of Minassian can be found here, with many stories to be read waiting inside. The town plaza is to your northeast. }{Casaria}{casaria}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25583}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25586}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25585}{0}{<228>}{Forest Trail (se,nw)}{<228>( *<088>}{You are on a small trail, within a thick forest, leading away from the town towards the unknown. A large, fallen tree lies just to your right, and a small chipmunk has begun to claim the log as its new home. The steadfastness with which the trees stand makes you feel like you could live forever, that you could take on anything, perhaps even Javelin. Those feelings quickly leave your mind as you envision the power that Javelin controls. }{The Overlands}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25583}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25593}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25586}{0}{<278>}{Town Plaza (ne,sw,nw,n,s,e)}{<278>. .<088>}{You are standing in the town plaza of great Casaria. Townspeople are walking around the plaza, enjoying the day. Standing around, you feel very alive, seeing a town that is thriving as this one is. You can see quite a few people going in and out of the equipment shop to the northwest, as it is a very popular place to go. The Library of Minassian stands to the south, and is probably the first place one should go when visiting the town. The Adventurers guild hall is to the north, where adventurers go to rest. The town arena, where many adventurers either make or break it, is to the east.  You should probably not go there until you are sure that you want to fight. The magic shop, which sells many different types of potions, is to the northeast. If you wish to leave the town, the gates to the southwest would be the way to go. At the west end of the plaza, stands a statue of the great queen God of the Overlands, Samantha. Townspeople often present gifts to the statue, as a sign of respect for the great queen. }{Casaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25584}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25587}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25588}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25589}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25590}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25591}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25587}{0}{<138>}{Magic Shop (sw)}{<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>}{This is the magic shop for the town of Casaria. It is currently owned by an old man by the name of Marduk. Marduk came to these lands a long time ago, and first joined the Elundi monks. Utterly failing as a monk, Marduk decided to join the ranks of the silver order mages. Throughout his career, Marduk became a moderately powerful mage. Of all his accomplishments, his best was achieving the Yellow Rune. In the magic shop, you may buy various types of potions, or a few other items. The walls are lined with many different types of items, such as the horn from a herebeast. Marduk stands before you, behind a counter. }{Casaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25586}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25588}{0}{<138>}{Equipment Shop (se)}{<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>}{You are in the equipment shop for the town of Casaria. The shop is rather large, as it carries many different types of wares. The shop was founded, not too many years ago, by this man, Robobop. Robobop eventually bought out most of the other shops in town, save the magic shop, and decided that it would be more cost effective to combine the wares. Now he spends his remaining years as a shopkeeper, tired from his long days as a priest. Just above door is a large, golden plaque given to Robobop by his long time friend Mertel. The equipment shop is decorated with many different types of weapons and armors, however, the item that catches your attention the most is the Levinblade just behind the counter.  }{Casaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25586}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25589}{0}{<278>}{Guild Hall (s,ne)}{<278>. .<088>}{You are in the guild hall for the town of Casaria. This is where adventurers come to rest, to learn, or to record their tales. The room itself is rather large, and has been here for a long time. There is a fireplace in the north corner of the room. An old man sits near the fireplace sleeping, and you should probably not disturb him. The wall is lined with heads of different animals, probably slain by the old man when he was in his prime. There is a log book on a table next to the east wall, with the names of some very famous adventurers. To the northeast, lie residential homes. }{Casaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25586}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25589}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25590}{0}{<238>}{Library of Minassian (n)}{<238>"""<088>}{You are in the famed library of Minassian, founded by a great man, Varant. A long time ago, Varant was a level 17 druid who had reached the end of his adventuring. Varant had only obtained the yellow rune, and did not believe he would be able to get any more, so he decided to become a scholar. Walking around and talking to people, Varant compiled a large library of books, which tell the story of this area. There are rows of books to your right and left, with the main desk here in front of you. The librarian stands behind the desk, filling the position that Varant should be holding, but can not fill because he ran off. If you wish to read some of the books, you should probably check the stacks. }{Casaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25586}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25591}{0}{<238>}{Town Arena (w)}{<138>~ ~<088>}{You are in the arena for the town of Casaria. The town arena itself is a wide open room, with a lot of space for maneuvering around, to avoid attacks. There are many cages here, cages which hold weak monsters, strong monsters, and perhaps a super monster. High above the arena, there are seats for spectators to watch and learn. This arena was created soon after Orac cleared the town of the monsters. The townspeople hoped that having an arena would protect and train them, in case they were attacked again in the future. There is a small gong in the corner, which is used to summon the monsters.  }{Casaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25586}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

