R {25753}{0}{<238>}{On a steep mountain path (se,nw)}{<238>.^.<088>}{The path is much steeper in this section, and you have to tread carefully to avoid slipping and breaking a leg.  The path continues to the northwest. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25752}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25754}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25754}{0}{<238>}{On a steep mountain path (se,nw)}{<238>.^.<088>}{This is by far the steepest section of the mountain path, and your legs strain to keep you balanced and upright.  You notice for the first time how high you've climbed, and the temperature up here is dropping rapidly.  High winds whip up in gusts and almost knock you over the edge, but to your relief you can see that the path reaches an end further ahead. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25753}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25755}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25755}{0}{<238>}{Cave entrance (se,enter)}{<238>^<138>E<238>^<088>}{You are standing before a dark and smelly opening which has been crudely carved into the mountainside.  Strange hieroglyphs are dotted around it, some of which have been painted over in blood. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25754}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25756}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25756}{w}{enter}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25756}{0}{<248>}{In the hobgoblinzes lair (nw,e,sw)}{<248>% %<088>}{This is a large, cavernous chamber with three tunnelled exits at equidistant points around the wall. The smell here is overwhelming and you fight the dizziness that threatens your consciousness. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25755}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25757}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25758}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25757}{0}{<248>}{In the hobgoblinzes lair (se,w)}{<248>% %<088>}{You are in a fairly large tunnel leading from the main chamber to the southeast.  Set into the northeastern wall is a large door through which can be heard the tones of youthful laughter mixed with one whose tone is scalding.  Further to the west, a dim light can be seen. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25756}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25759}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25758}{0}{<248>}{In the hobgoblinzes lair (ne,w)}{<248>% %<088>}{The tunnel here becomes narrower by the step, and the ground is strewn with rocks and discarded skulls.  A strange, smelly substance sticks to the walls and makes your head spin with nausea.  Toward the west you can hear echoes of bickering and argument. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25756}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25761}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25759}{0}{<248>}{In the hobgoblinzes lair (e,n)}{<248>% %<088>}{You are at a bend in the passageway. The tunnel here is suddenly extremely narrow, and the ceiling is almost touching your head.  Light reflected from the north gives this place an eerie feel, but you are thankful that the air is relatively fresh. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25757}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25760}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25760}{0}{<148>}{In the hobgoblinzes lair (s)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{You find yourself in a small underground reservoir. Bright rays of sunlight filter into the cavern from a gaping hole high up in the ceiling, and bounce off the surface of the water.  The whole place has a certain ominous calm and coldness to it. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25759}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51374}{n}{leap reservoir}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25761}{0}{<248>}{In the hobgoblinzes lair (e,nw)}{<248>% %<088>}{You are at a curve in the passageway.  It continues on toward the northwest at a slow downhill gradient.  From that region, you can hear urgent bickering and argument being spoken, blurted, and shouted in a mish-mash of Orcish and Goblin tongue.  There is a lingering smell of death and decay, and other less savory excretions. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25758}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25762}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25762}{0}{<248>}{In the hobgoblinzes lair (se)}{<248>% %<088>}{The passage opens out into a large cavern illuminated by several huge torches attached to the wall.  In the middle of the room, a giant slab of rock cut into a rough circle is propped up by four flattened-off boulders. There is also a hole in the ceiling. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25761}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35428}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51375}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25763}{0}{<278>}{-= The Mews =- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{You have just entered a street so decrepit that even the mavens of the library can't remember what it is supposed to be called.  The citizens of this place just refer to the street, and its surrounding sink of sin and depravity, as `The Mews'.   Whatever its name, it is filthy, foul, and generally disgusting. }{The Mews}{the_mews}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4266}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25765}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25764}{0}{<278>}{-= Castle Street =- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{You are on Castle Street, which runs south from here while the busy Riverford Drive flows by to the north.  On both sides of the road are some fairly opulent houses belonging to officials of the city, doubtless built from the bribes and other perks which are part of public service the world over. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4266}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25789}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25765}{0}{<278>}{-= The Mews =- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{This street is a cesspool of human and inhuman refuse.  A crumbling brick wall is to your east.   An occasional brick falls in the street causing mayhem on the rare passerby.  To the west, a moldy, plastered, and stench-ridden building presents its backside to the `street'.  You feel watched and most insecure. }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25763}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25766}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25766}{0}{<278>}{-= The Mews =- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{The endless travail of human and nonhuman horrors continues unabated.  You're starting to think that slumming it wasn't that great an idea.  You feel eyes on the back of your neck but looking around, all you see is the same stench-ridden, refuse-laden street\; the same decrepit buildings and crumbling walls\; and the same wobbly bricks ready to fall on you at an instant's investigation. }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25765}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25767}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25767}{0}{<278>}{-= Skid Road =- (n,s,w,e)}{<278>-+-<088>}{You have entered a small intersection.  Or perhaps it would be more proper, as if anything could be proper in here, to refer to this as a sudden and only partial clearing in the refuse.  Whatever the terminology, and a preoccupation with verbiage is a most definite failure in this part of Wayhaven, there appears to be a catering establishment of some disrepute directly to your north.  Sounds of an angry bar fight, the stench of vomit, and other assorted benefits of advanced viniculture, assault your senses.   There are also eddies in the refuse to east and west which, combined with the fact that there appear to be no crumbling masonry in those directions, might well indicate passage in those directions. }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25766}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25768}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25769}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25770}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25768}{0}{<238>}{The Tall And Short Of It (s)}{<238>[P]<088>}{You have entered a louse-ridden, long, filthy room filled with some of the most disreputable looking scumbags you have ever seen in your life.  The stench is such that you nearly add to it with a heave of your own.  A few look you over with cold stares, measuring your wallet with remarkable accuracy. A `menu' of sorts is tacked to a scabrous oil-paper wall. }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25767}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25769}{0}{<278>}{-= Skid Road =- (w,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{You have entered a narrow passage between two crumbling excresences of masonry made up of crumbling red walls.  If you sneeze they will come crashing down on top of you!  You are now certain that someone is following you and eager to part your soul from your body.  If you haven't asked yourself why you're here, this is the time. }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25767}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25776}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25770}{0}{<278>}{-= Skid Road =- (s,w)}{<278>-+ <088>}{You have entered a narrow passage between two crumbling excresences of masonry made up of crumbling red walls.  If you sneeze they will come crashing down on top of you!  The walls come together far above your head, blocking out all light.  You are now certain that someone is following you and eager to part your soul from your body.  If you haven't asked yourself why you're here, this is the time. }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25767}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25771}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25771}{0}{<278>}{-= Skid Road =- (n,s,e)}{<278> +-<088>}{A smoke filled passage through a stretch of urban hell, you are walking down a narrow passageway between a crumbling red brick wall and a putrescent building.  The smoke seems to be coming from a large, stout door to the east.  The passage continues to the north and to the south. }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25770}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25772}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25773}{e}{turn doorknob}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25772}{0}{<278>}{-= Skid Road =- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{This interminable cesspit through the underside of Wayhaven continues on to north and south.  Darkness is all that can be seen to the south.  To the north the narrow, refuse-filled passage continues so it is probably reasonable to assume that the scabrous building and rotting red brick wall also continue to the south.  On the other hand, assuming can get you killed. Especially in the Mews!! }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25771}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25774}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {25773}{0}{<238>}{The Tall & Long Pub (n,s,w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{Your eyes smart from the smoke coming from the coal burner behind the greasy, messy, and extraordinarily slovenly bar just in front of you.  The place has no tables or chairs or even stools for the patrons.  I guess ogres drink standing up.  A long cracked mirror glares at you from behind the bar which, as best you can see, has already been ransacked for every single ounce of alcoholic beverage.  The ogres are rather poor, it is said.  Which makes them a bit mad. }{The Mews}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25771}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
