R {26620}{0}{}{Northeast corridor (nw,s)}{ }{You are in the northeast quadrant of a carpeted hallway that leads around the tower.  At periodic intervals, tall shuttered windows show the surrounding view outside the tower and send in a light refreshing breeze that smells of flowers and trees.  The ceiling of the hallway is high, with supporting stone arches every couple of feet.  On the inside wall, a large canvas mural stretches down the hall to the northwest.  To the south, you can see the guild foyer. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22091}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26624}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26621}{0}{<218>}{A blood pool}{<118>(<178>~<118>)<088>}{You are 20 feet below the surface of a pool filled with blood. As far as you can see, there is nothing but blood and more blood.  You  are totally surrounded by the thick, warm blood, unable to tell which way is up and which is down. }{Temple of Drackonus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26618}{n}{swim n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26619}{e}{swim e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26622}{0}{}{Southeastern corridor (sw,n)}{ }{You are in the southeast quadrant of a carpeted hallway that leads around the tower. The high ceiling of the hallway has supporting stone arches every couple of feet.  At periodic intervals tall shuttered windows show the surrounding view outside the tower, and a light refreshing breeze blows in through them from the east. On the inside wall is a large canvas mural that stretches down the hall to the southwest, where voices can be heard.  Through the doors to the north, you can see the guild foyer. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22091}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26638}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26623}{0}{}{Central Corridor (w,e)}{ }{The plush, dark red carpet is worn flat in the middle by the passage of many feet.  However it still muffles the sound of your footsteps in this wide hallway.  A plentitude of light streams in from the foyer at one end of the hall, and mysteriously from an opening at the other end.  Yet oddly, this hallway travels deep into the center of the tower.  Along both walls hang portraits with wise faces of bards in colourful regalia looking down upon you.  The distant sounds of cheerful music lilt down from the western end of the hallway, indicating the nonstop bustle of activity in the guild.  }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {22091}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26640}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26624}{0}{}{Northeast corridor (s,w,se)}{ }{As you continue through the northeast quadrant of the tower, a light gust of wind through the open shutters blows in the scent of flowers and freshly cut grass.  On the inside wall a large canvas mural stretches all the way down the hall to the southeast, leading to the guild foyer.  Directly to the south is an archway with no door, through which you see shimmering colors as if from light reflecting off the rippling surface of a pool. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26620}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26625}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26626}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26625}{0}{}{Backstage of a Theatre (n)}{ }{You find yourself in the backstage area of an old theatre.  Old props from past performances lie about the room.  The air is slightly musty from disuse, and a light film of dust covers most objects.  The exits to various stages and settings have long since been mortared over.  The room is a curious remnant from an old past. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26624}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26626}{0}{}{Northern intersection (s,w,e)}{ }{You are at the entrance to an open stone archway leading south, the center of three in the carpeted hallway.  Austere stone support columns propagate down the hallway at even intervals, extending overhead in light-dappled arches that catch the swaying shadows of plants and trees moving outside in the gentle breeze.  You can hear the rustle of leaves with each gust of cool air that billows in through the open windows.  Somewhere in the gardens outside a whippoorwill hoots a plaintive cry. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26624}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26627}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26628}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26627}{0}{}{Hall of Advancement (n)}{ }{As you pass under the archway you find yourself in a large hexagon-shaped room.  On each of the six walls is a large plaque upon which is inscribed calligraphic script.  Although the room is windowless, glass globes on either side of each of the plaques keep the room well-lit.  The room itself is bare save for six evenly arranged tall stands with square glass display cases protecting their contents.  These are softly illuminated from within.  In the center of this ring of displays, the seal of the Bard Guild is engraved upon the marble floor and inlaid with gold. There's a small placard here. Commands: advance [level,str,con,int,wis,dex,cha]           cost, tally, required, questansi,           list [name -or- # -or- short] }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26626}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26628}{0}{}{Northwestern corridor (s,e,sw)}{ }{You are in the northwest quadrant of a carpeted hallway that leads around the tower.  An errant bumblebee zips in one of the open windows then lazily floats out again.  On the inside wall is a large canvas mural that stretches all the way down the hall to the southwest, from where you hear the faint clinking of coins.  To the south is an archway with no door, through which you see a museum-like chamber. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26626}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26629}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26630}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26629}{0}{}{Hall of Achievement (n)}{ }{The width of a modest stateroom with a high gothic ceiling, the hall of achievement carries its size with elegance and aplomb.  Like the guild foyer, the crest of the bard guild is set into a marble floor, but here the seal is etched entirely in gold.  At the far end of the room, two statues, a gallant and a mystic bard, stand eternal guard.  Between them an arched window offers a direct view of the inner courtyard and the ancient rowan tree.  On the west wall next to the gallant bard, the Gallant standard hangs down from a brass bar mounted on the wall.  Similarly, the east wall is adorned with the standard of the Mystics.  But it is standing between the two on the great seal of the bard guild where you may come to advance your standing should you prove worthy. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26628}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26630}{0}{}{Northwestern corner (ne,s)}{ }{As you progress through the northwest quadrant of the tower, tall windows at periodic intervals show the surrounding view.  Sunlight streaming in through them catches on dust motes flitting through the air, brightening them like tiny hovering fireflies.  As they drift up into the shadows of the arched ceiling, they wink out of sight, their light extinguished.  On the inside wall is a large canvas mural that stretches around the hall to the northeast from where faint sounds of clanking equipment can be heard.  You also hear the clinking of coins coming from the south. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26628}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26631}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26631}{0}{}{Western intersection (n,e,s)}{ }{You can look down the carpeted hallway and see rows of stone arches across the ceiling forming a patterned tunnel of light and dark stonework, accentuated by light coming in from the windows.  This section of the hallway extends north and south, and a sign above the doorway to the east reads, 'Bard Guild Bank.' }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26630}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26632}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26633}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26632}{0}{}{Bard Guild Bank (w)}{ }{There are some who might argue that gold has a smell, that faint metallic hint in the air that signifies the accumulation of great wealth.  Closing your eyes and inhaling deeply, you might almost imagine it permeating this posh bank reception room.  In the center of the room is a wooden stand-alone counter with a protective glass top for filling out forms and paperwork.  Lined against the mahogany paneled walls are no fewer than five automated bank machines, all ready to accept your transactions with the greatest expediency.  No expenses have been spared, including highly realistic plastic ferns that adorn endtables throughout the bank, providing a splash of color without the tedium of watering live plants.  High quality print reproductions of famous paintings adorn the walls, as good as the real thing. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26631}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26633}{0}{}{Southwestern corridor (n,se)}{ }{As you continue through the southwest section of the tower a bird chirps somewhere nearby and the scent of pine tickles your nose through the open windows.  Light bounces off the ceiling arches that extend row after row down the hallway and onto the large canvas mural that stretches to the southeast.  A murmuring of voices comes from that direction down the hall, and there is also the distinct clinking of coins to the north. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26631}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26634}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26634}{0}{}{Southwestern corridor (nw,n,e)}{ }{You are in the southwest quadrant of the tower.  Workers must regularly come through here\; the carpet is spotless despite all the heavy traffic, and the wall sconces are polished to a high shine.  On the inside wall is a large canvas mural that stretches all the way down the hall to the northwest, from where the faint sounds of clinking coins is barely discernable.  To your north is an open doorway, above which hangs a sign that reads 'Bard Guild Shop'. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26633}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26635}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26636}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26635}{0}{}{Bard Guild General Store (s)}{ }{A portly old man sitting behind the counter gives you a beaming smile as you enter.  Light from the open window behind him brightens up the neatly kept store.  The walls are filled with shelves of items, mostly survival gear for long journeys.  You see a torch bin in one corner, and a tall display stack of music boxes in the center of the store that must have taken all morning to arrange.  There is a selection of tuners for instruments sitting on the counter next to the check-out stand.  Off to the west a curtained doorway leads to Barnaby's storage area where he keeps his more expensive items.  A sign propped up on the counter lists the full range of items for sale. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26634}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26636}{0}{}{Southern intersection (n,w,e)}{ }{Sunlight bounces off the white stone arches that arc over the ceiling, and somewhere outside through the open windows you hear birds chirping.  Their melodious songs are almost drowned out by the loud clinks and clanks of weapons and armours emanating from the doorway to the north.  Above the entrance a sign proclaims, 'Bard Equipment Storage.' The carpeted hallway continues east and west. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26634}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26637}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26638}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26637}{0}{}{Bard Equipment Storage (s)}{ }{As you walk into the shop the most bewildering assortment of items greets your eyes.  Hanging on display all over the walls are various pieces of body armour, some more dented than others.  Cloaks, hats, and helmets hang on a rack against the wall to your right.  A weapons rack on your left displays wicked looking swords and daggers.  At the end of the room is a large counter with a glass case housing all manner of pitch pipes, scrolls, and other objects.  Behind the counter, an old man with a sly twinkle in his eye relaxes on a bar stool in front of an open window. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26636}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26638}{0}{}{Southeastern corridor (ne,n,w)}{ }{As you walk through the southeast quadrant of the tower you idly admire the mural on the wall that extends to the northeast in the direction of the guild foyer.  Directly to the north is an open doorway above which is a sign that reads, 'Bard Guild Armoury.'  There is murmuring to the west, like the general hubbub of sound on a busy day in the marketplace.  Through the open windows to the southeast flowers are abloom in the garden, and the profile of a statue is barely visible in the shade of a tree. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26636}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26622}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26639}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26639}{0}{}{Bard Guild Armoury (s)}{ }{As you enter the armoury you have to check back over your shoulder to make sure that you are still within the guild hall.  Tanthis has hung rich red, purple, and blue dyed fabrics on all of the walls, and laid out samples of all of his wares on display tables around the room.  The large open area in the center encourages browsing through the tables.  All that is missing is the crunch of sand under your feet and the smell of blueberry pies in the air.  Perched on a stool at the back of the room next to the money till, Tanthis gives you a smile and a nod. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26638}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26640}{0}{}{Inner Courtyard (u,d,e)}{ }{A rush of wind hits your face and you have to squint your eyes against the bright sun.  The center of the tower is spacious and hollow, and by craning your head you can see straight up three stories to the baby blue sky.  The ground is made of the same flagstone materials as the courtyard outside, and in the center grows an ancient towering species of the rowan tree, but one far older and larger than any you have ever encountered.  To your right begins a stone staircase that hugs the tower wall and spirals around the courtyard to the upper levels.  Through open windows on the next story a cacophony of music floats down mixed with the sounds of clashing metal, creating a friendly buzz of noise overlaid with occasional shouts of laughter. Slightly to your left is a circular stairwell where stone steps lead down into darkness. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26623}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26641}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26642}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26641}{0}{}{On the spiral staircase (u,d,e)}{ }{The wide staircase crosses an opening in the tower wall as it spirals around the inner circle.  From here you can enter the second story of the tower to your east or continue to the upper or lower levels.  Although the wind tugs more briskly here, the broad stairs offer no danger of losing your balance.  In fact looking over the edge you are afforded a breathtaking view of the courtyard below. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26640}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26651}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26652}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26642}{0}{}{Anteroom to the Catacombs (u,e)}{ }{The stairwell from the courtyard above leads to this small anteroom.  It has a tiled floor that alternates beige and white in a diamond checker pattern, with a nondescript grating in one corner.  The walls have a rough stone texture and are painted a sierra brown.  The room is bare save for a small niche carved in the middle of the north, south, and west walls, each decorated with a musical instrument.  To the east, a set of double doors is thrown open.  Through them, you can see a hallway lit by globes set in brass sconces on the walls. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26640}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26643}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26643}{0}{}{Junction in the Catacombs (w,sw,e,nw)}{ }{Your footsteps echo hollowly in the underground passage, and the stone floor feels cold and hard beneath your feet.  Although the hallway is wide, you instinctively feel the entire weight of the tower pressing down overhead.  The flickering globes on the walls cast dancing shadows that leap towards you.  Feeling suddenly alone, your heart quickens and you keep your ears alert for sounds behind you.  Longing for company, you set eyes on the archway to the east from which emanates a murmur of voices.  Above the archway, neat gothic lettering is engraved into the stone. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26642}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26644}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26645}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26646}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26644}{0}{}{In the Catacombs (ne,s,nw)}{ }{Through the archway to the south you hear recitations of poetry.  The cheery sound is a welcome reprieve from the silence of the catacombs.  Above the archway is inscribed part of a sonnet by the master bard himself, carved in flowing script into the rock wall.  The hallway continues northwest and northeast. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26643}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26648}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26650}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26645}{0}{}{Lower Atrium (w)}{ }{If your sense of direction holds true, you are now directly below the main foyer of the guild hall.  This lower atrium is quite large, with columns throughout it supporting the roof.  Around the room are placed comfortable leather couches and low tables.  Large rugs fight off the chill of the catacombs, and tall lamps by each of the couches keep the atrium well lit.  Bookshelves to the left provide light reading material, and a large painting in an oak frame decorates the far wall. To your right is a message board on which bard guild members can tack up notices and discussions of the latest happenings in the realms. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26643}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26646}{0}{}{In the catacombs (n,sw,se)}{ }{Following the curve of the hallway, you come to an opening leading north to an alcove. Above the archway, flames from the light sconces in the hallway cast a flickering glow over a passage engraved into the stone.  The hallway continues to the southwest and southeast. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26643}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26647}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26648}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26647}{0}{}{Alcove of inspiration (s)}{ }{As you enter this small room you see that it is circular with a domed mosaic ceiling. Candles in tall black iron stands on either side of the entrance illuminate the room. The white stonewashed walls are offset by rich velvety red carpet. Your eyes are drawn to three equally-spaced white marble statues that stand quietly around the room, faces of muses gazing peacefully down at the room's attendants.  Curved white benches offer a resting place between each of the statues.  Off to the left on the south wall by the entrance, a message board has been placed for bards to share their ideas for the guild with fellow bard members as inspiration strikes them. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26646}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26648}{0}{}{In the catacombs (se,w,ne)}{ }{These are the innermost halls of the tower.  A hushed silence has fallen over your surroundings, and even your footsteps sound more muted.  An archway to the west invites you to enter the library which houses the vast stores of knowledge of the bard guild.  How unusual that there isn't a door here to guard one of the guild's greatest treasures.  There is a phrase inscribed above the austere entrance.  When you have gleaned the knowledge you sought within, you may return to the main guild hall by the corridor northeast or southeast. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26646}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26644}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26649}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26649}{0}{}{Hall of Knowledge (e)}{ }{Stepping onto the threshold of the library you stop and sway, for you find yourself at the top of a wide set of shallow stairs descending a short ways to the floor of the library.  Wall-to-wall mahogany bookshelves hold immense collections that disappear into the dim recesses of the ceiling.  Tall ladders on brass rails can be rolled around the room to reach the higher books.  In the middle of the floor, reading desks with small lamps provide the only source of illumination.  The centerpiece of the room is a large world globe easily as tall as a human.  Stepping down into the center of the library you are hit with the musty scent of ancient leather-bound tomes that have been written by bard scholars over the years.  A message board has been placed against the back wall for bards to share stories of their travels with fellow bards. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26648}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26650}{0}{}{Recital Room (n)}{ }{A medium-sized room, almost one third of it is taken up by a stage against the far wall.  The backdrop of the stage is a long dark red curtain hung on the wall.  The rest of the room contains lounge chairs and small tables, where bards may wander in and listen to performances of music and oratory being given.  Noteworthy performances are transcribed onto a board here for others to peruse, and other bards freely add their own writings to the board as well.  Many bards weary from their travels come down to relax in here with their brethren and regale each other with tales and performances while they recuperate. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26644}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26651}{0}{}{A circular walkway (d,n,w,e,s)}{ }{The spiral staircase ends at a walkway that encircles the third level of the guild.  The sun feels much hotter but the wind blows stronger and cooler against your face.  Fortunately there is an iron railing for security.  The very air seems infused with a greater vitality up here, and the few lazy clouds that amble across the sky create a slight feeling of vertigo if you look up at them too long.  Along the ramparts of the tower three flags snap smartly, displaying the proud emblem of the bard guild and its subguilds.  From the walkway four doorways into the tower are accessible for those bards of the proper standing.  To the east lies the Mystic Hall, opposite the Gallant Hall on the west.  The other ends of the tower house the meeting halls of the bard guild player administrators, with the highest echelons of the bard guild admitted to the north. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26641}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26677}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26678}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26679}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26680}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26652}{0}{}{Upper central corridor (w,e)}{ }{On this level of the tower, there is wall-to-wall royal blue carpeting.  Plenty of light streams in through the courtyard to the west, but there are also brass sconces set at equal intervals for lighting at night.  Against the walls are several glass display cases that feature objects from bard history.  The exit to the east intersects with the hallway that circles the tower.  As you travel down the hallway, a sudden gust sends a small swirling flurry of leaves in from the courtyard entrance into the otherwise immaculate corridor. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26641}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26653}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26653}{0}{}{Second Level Entrance (n,s,e,w)}{ }{You have come to a spacious intersection in the hallway.  Potted ferns in large brass urns sit on either side of french glass doors that open out onto a narrow stone veranda to the east.  Sunlight striking the imperfect paned glass is showered into the hallway in a million dots of rainbow colors that dance in and out of view as wispy clouds pass in front of the sun.  Although the walls and ceiling are made of thick stone, the effect is like standing inside a multifaceted crystal ball. The rich blue carpet continues to the north and south around the tower.  A small brass plaque is set in the stone wall next to the north exit. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26652}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26654}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26655}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26656}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26654}{0}{}{Northeast corner (nw,s)}{ }{There are no windows in this section of the hall, creating a darker cool interior. Your eyes are drawn to the inside wall where there is a large recessed alcove.  In the alcove a soft light from above illuminates a sculpture of a gallant bard dressed in full platemail astride a rearing stallion.  Next to the statue a small brass plaque is affixed to the stone wall.  You can see a spacious chamber to the south, and the carpeted hallway also continues to the northwest from where loud clashing of metal on metal rings out. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26653}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26657}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26655}{0}{}{Southeast corner (sw,n)}{ }{This windowless section of the hall is dim and cool.  The main source of light comes from an illuminated alcove set in the inside wall of the corridor.  In the alcove rests a striking sculpture of a bard standing tall with a real harp clutched in one arm and the other arm outstretched with fingers spread wide.  The bard's lips are parted as if in the act of speaking a phrase that only the stone can hear.  Thrown over the bard's shoulder is a cloak carved out of smooth dark amethyst.  Next to the statue a small brass plaque is affixed to the stone wall.  You can see a spacious chamber to the north and hear murmurings and incantations coming from the southwest where the carpeted hallway continues. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26653}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26673}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26656}{0}{}{Eastern Veranda (w)}{ }{A stiff breeze blows in from the east, wafting up scents from the garden below.  The balcony is narrow but has a pair of white marble benches near the stone railing.  On the corners of the railing are perched two smiling gargoyles that look out at the panoramic view of Wayhaven.  A few neatly trimmed tendrils of ivy growing up from below drape over the doorway that leads out onto the veranda.  Next to the french doors you see a small brass plaque affixed to the stone wall. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26653}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26657}{0}{}{Northwest corridor (se,w,s)}{ }{If you have ever tried walking when there is music playing, then you have experienced the sensation of rhythm.  As your ear listens to the rhythmic beat coming from the door to the south, your footsteps can't help but fall in line.  The merry syncopation floats down the hallway and out through the open windows.  A stone archway is visible down the hall to the west, and the hallway also continues in the other direction to the southeast. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26654}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26658}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
