R {26658}{0}{}{Northern intersection (w,e,s)}{ }{You are in the middle section of the hallway in front of an open archway, through which comes the loud sounds of clashing weapons.  Further down the hall to the east you can see another room with its door thrown wide open, while in the other direction the hallway curves out of sight to the southwest.  A few errant dust motes drift through the hallway and catch the light coming in from the open windows. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26657}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26660}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26661}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26659}{0}{}{Hall of Rhythm (n)}{ }{The Hall of Rhythm is a circular chamber that pulsates with the beat of drums drifting down from the dark recesses of the lofty ceiling, piped in from some unknown source.  Glass globes light the hall with a soft dim glow, the reflections from the flames forming shallow pools of light at the bases of the sconces around the room.  Various percussion instruments taken from different times and places decorate the walls.  The wooden floor in the room is completely bare, save for the slight gritty feel of resin as one might expect on a stage for dancing.  If you are ready to learn something new, perhaps you can try joining in the rhythmic beat with a dance of your own. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26657}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26660}{0}{}{Northwest corridor (e,sw)}{ }{A series of white stone arches and rows of tall narrow open windows extend down the carpeted hallway to the east.  Although the guild hall is already generally filled with noise, laughter, and music, the banging and clanging coming from down the hall is particularly loud even for the bard guild.  The hallway also curves around to the southwest. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26658}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26664}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26661}{0}{}{Hall of Alacrity (dodge,n,melee)}{ }{As you enter the Hall of Alacrity, you stand at the top of three concentric rings of stone seating that lead down to an oval sand-covered floor.  Shallow steps are carved into the stonework both from this entrance as well as extending from the arena floor up to east and west exits.  In the center ring, there is a standard of the gallant guild on one side and the standard of the mystic guild on the other.  The southern wall directly across from you has a row of windows along the ceiling that lets in light and a cool breeze.  Below the windows, a statue of the god Hermes watches over the proceedings. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26658}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26662}{dodge}{dodge}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26663}{melee}{melee}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26662}{0}{}{Guild Gymnasium (out)}{ }{A small exercise room, the guild gymnasium has various exercise and training equipment. The far corner is dominated by a large structure with ladders, netting, and rickety bridges similar to the kind seen in children's playgrounds, but this one looks far more dangerous, particularly if you imagine bards engaging in combat on the precarious walkways.  The rest of the room is an open area with exercise bars bolted to the walls and mats woven out of rushes that cover most of the wood floor.  Dust still hangs in the air from recent activity.  A smell of pine touches your nose from a few discarded resin bags lying around, mingling with the almost tangible taste of sweat in the air.  There is a window that must look out on the inner courtyard but its shutters are currently closed.}{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {26661}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26663}{0}{}{Sparring Chamber (out)}{ }{The sparring chamber is an alcove on the edge of the Hall of Alacrity. The floor is made of hard wood that bears innumerable nicks and scratches, and the room smells of well-oiled leather that reminds you of tack gear in horse stables.}{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {26661}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26664}{0}{}{Northwest corner (s,ne)}{ }{This windowless section of hallway is thrown into shadows by the light coming from the windows further down.  The indirect lighting dapples the floor like walking deep in a woods where only little bits succeed in filtering through the overhanging treetops.  In the recessed inside corner of the corridor is a large boulder that looks imported from the stone giant villages of the far dragon isles with a vivid forest backdrop painted on the back wall itself.  A sculpture of a satyr who reaches no more than chest height to you blows on a set of pan pipes to the rapt attention of his audience, a young nymph perched atop the boulder with head cocked.  Amongst the leaves and branches painted on the wall you see a small brass plaque.  The long hallway continues to the south and curves out of sight to the northeast. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26660}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26665}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26665}{0}{}{Western intersection (n,e,s)}{ }{The sun shines in brightly through the open windows, and you can look down into the gardens far below.  Beyond the tower walls lies the Garden District of Wayhaven.  Some distance away, you can just make out the gates of the city.  Within the tower walls, it is still and quiet for this moment as you absorb the tranquil scene.  Directly to  Thomdril Uptime: 3.8 days  Reboot: 5.5 days  Lag: 0.00  Idle: [00:00:01]   your east is a stone archway framing the entrance to the Hall of Harmony.  The royal blue carpeting continues north and south. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26664}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26666}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26667}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26666}{0}{}{Hall of Harmony (playing,singing,w)}{ }{Although birdsong can be heard throughout the tower due to the close garden grounds outside, in here the singing and chirruping is louder, coming directly from the lush plantlife around the room.  Ivy hangs from four supporting stone columns in the room and is also beginning to creep up the walls.  Small trees in large planters are set around the room, as are potted ferns and smaller flowering plants and bushes. In the center of the conservatory, a statue of the goddess Harmonia stands as the centerpiece of a large marble fountain with her hands outstretched.  Water sprays up in a series of shooting streams that encircle the basin around her, tossing sparkling mist into the air.  Additional alcoves to the north and south are almost obscured by the vegetation. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26665}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26668}{playing}{playing}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26669}{singing}{singing}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26667}{0}{}{Southwest corner (se,n)}{ }{Unlike the other corners of the tower, this section of the hallway has windows.  They are thrown open and sunlight brightens the hallway and bounces off the royal blue carpeting.  A recessed alcove contains a modest graceful display in which bamboo stalks rise out of an arrangement of basalt rocks set in a flat stone basin.  The stalks are of varying heights and widths, cut diagonally across their tops, and create an effect reminiscent of a pipe organ.  Water gurgling up from the bottom darkens the basalt to a dark gray and occasionally spills up and over the tops of the bamboo pipes.  Behind the fountain is a small brass plaque affixed to the wall.  The hallway continues to the north and southeast. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26665}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26670}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26668}{0}{}{Practice Hall (out)}{ }{The practice hall is bright and airy.  Against the far wall you see that someone has hung brightly colored scarves out the window that flap in the breeze.  Sunlight dapples the hardwood floors and plays off the few paintings adorning the walls.  One of the walls holds a bookcase that stretches up to the ceiling, crammed with sheaves of music paper and bound volumes containing the various compositions of bard apprentices throughout the years, some crude and others masterful.  In the corner a sheet music stand rests quietly next to a grand piano.}{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {26666}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26669}{0}{}{Acoustics Theatre (out)}{ }{As you cross the threshold you feel a slight tingle of electricity along the nape of your neck.  Almost as palpable, like walking head first into a soft spongy wall, is the complete absence of sound that buffets your senses.  This room has no windows but lighted sconces along the walls cast a soft glow, illuminating a single stool sitting on a wooden stage at the end of the room.  Behind the stool is a matte black sounding board, and in front of the sounding board but currently drawn back by gold cords are several layers of thick heavy red curtains.  A carpeted walkway leads down the center of the room to the stage.  There are benches along either side for any observers who wish to sit in, and towards the front are a pair of long tables with their own chairs.  Reclining back in one, a lanky bard snores softly.}{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26666}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26670}{0}{}{Southwest corridor (e,nw)}{ }{The royal blue carpeting extends down the hall to the east, where a single open archway is visible.  A cloud passing over the sun temporarily shades the hallway then each section gradually brightens again.  For the moment you are held captured in a bubble of silence as all activity in the tower seems to fall into a lull.  As the sun moves from behind the cloud you hear a faint snatch of song coming from down the hall to the northwest and the moment is broken. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26667}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26671}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26671}{0}{}{Southern intersection (n,e,w)}{ }{A cool wind blows through the hallway, lifting some of the heat that has built up from the sun shining in through the windows.  It is relatively quiet in this section, and even the birds that normally sing outside are unnaturally still.  Directly to the north is an open archway, through which you catch enticing glimpses of reflected light. The carpeted hallway continues to the east and west. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26670}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26672}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
