R {26672}{0}{}{Hall of Spellcrafting (power,mana,s)}{ }{The first thing you notice about the Hall of Spellcrafting is that it has five tall mirrors with elaborate gold-gilded frames positioned throughout the room.  In the center of these mirrors stands a beautiful woman in a flowing gown cupping a crystal ball in her hands. The color in her cheeks is so vibrant and she eyes you so expectantly that at first it is easy to mistake her for a real person instead of the stone statue that she is.  There are tapestries on each of the four walls, as well as alcoves to the west and east. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26671}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26674}{power}{power}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {26675}{mana}{mana}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {26673}{0}{}{Southeast corridor (n,w,ne)}{ }{A gentle breeze caresses your neck as a light wind blows in from the open windows in the hallway.  Looking down the corridor to the west, you see an open archway on the inner wall of the tower, and long tall windows on the outer wall.  Sunlight coming through the windows catches on dust in the hall creating slanting beams and illuminating the surrounding atmosphere with a soft glow. The hallway also bends out of sight around a corner to the northeast. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {26671}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
