R {26679}{0}{}{Hall of Mysticism (w)}{ }{Circling the upper ramparts of the tower, you stop at an elaborate archway leading east.  As you step into the spacious chamber, you find yourself at the apex of a pentagon-shaped room with a white marble floor, dominated by a large golden sphere in the center.  The ceiling angles slightly above you, the panels alternating in light blue and white.  There is one painting on each wall except for the farthest wall which has a stained-glass window overlooking Wayhaven.  Underneath the paintings, a low bookcase runs along the wall, encircling the entire room.  There are various circular sofas forming islands around the room where bard mystics can come to relax and study quietly. }{Bard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
