R {27524}{0}{}{Cardio Room (n,s)}{ }{This room is where people come to sweat, that much you could tell from two rooms over.  Two TVs are mounted on the wall and are permanently set to TSN... (The 'Canadian' Sports Network).  Arrayed in a multi-row semi-circle in front of the TV's is a hodge-podge of excercise machines. These machines range from your basic stationary bike, to the ever-popular rowing machine, treadmills, step machines, and even some odd contraption from Reebok that forces people to swing their legs in front of them in some sort of moon- walking motion. Scary. }{New World Fitness}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {27522}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {27515}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {27525}{0}{}{Universal Weight Room (s,e)}{ }{This room is filled with the more traditional mix of free weights and 'Universal' equipment.  The crowd in here also seems to be more interested in their own workouts than anything else, making quite a shocking contrast with the surrounding rooms.  A contrast that is very much welcome. }{New World Fitness}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {27515}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {27526}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {27526}{0}{}{Heavy Weight Room (w,n)}{ }{Upon entering this room you almost gag as a virtual wall of body odour hits you.  In a dazed state, you gaze around the room and are presented with quite a surrealistic sight. A number of people who are larger than you thought humanly possible wander around the room. Sturdy benches abound as well as huge steel plates that appear extremely heavy. A number of dumbbells sit on racks to one side, all of which are much heavier than you would ever wish to imagine. }{New World Fitness}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
