R {27599}{0}{}{A Small Dusty Keep (s,w)}{ }{The kitchen is in the same sad, sorry condition as the rest of the keep. All the foodstuffs rotted into one large, smelly mass that you would really rather not examine too closely.  There is no silverware, or other cooking utensils. In fact, the only thing that lets you know this was a kitchen is the enormous wooden chopping block in the center of the floor, and the oven built into the northern wall. }{Undead Keep (Newbie)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {27598}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {27601}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {27600}{0}{}{A Small Dusty Keep (e)}{ }{This room seems to have been a combination salle and armory. The western wall once contained some sort of mirror, as  evidenced by the amount of glass on the floor and overturned bench in front of it. A large cabinet fills the northern wall, its heavy door hanging by a single hinge. Dark stains liberally cover the sawdust floor, dimmed by a thick layer of dust. }{Undead Keep (Newbie)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {27598}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {48334}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {27601}{0}{}{A Small Dusty Keep (w,n)}{ }{This small chicken coop once housed one of the keep's meager  sources of food. The perches are empty now, as are the nesting boxes. Chicken droppings cover all surfaces liberally, creating an aroma that makes your eyes water and your lunch try to  reenter society. Through the odorous haze in the room, you can barely make out exits to the north and west. }{Undead Keep (Newbie)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {27599}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {27602}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {27602}{0}{}{A Small Dusty Keep (e,ladder)}{<138>L<088>}{There isn't much left in the barn of the keep, everything has long since turned to dust or things better left unmentioned. A single  stool remains, along with an old tin milk bucket. Both look like they would crumble with a touch. A decrepit old ladder leads up into the loft. }{Undead Keep (Newbie)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {27601}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {27603}{ladder}{ladder}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {27603}{u}{ladder}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {27603}{0}{}{In a hayloft (ladder)}{ }{The loft would once have held hay and grain, the food to feed  the hungry animals below. Now, however, the hay that is left is mildewed and molded, unfit for consumption by the hungriest  beast. Of the grain, you can see no trace. Assumedly, it was carried off long ago by mice and other rodents. The rafters  above your head are bare of even bats or owls, and you shiver at the thought that even they would not live in this place. }{Undead Keep (Newbie)}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
