R {29098}{0}{}{Entrance To A Space Station (n)}{<148>S<088>}{You stand in a circular room with a hallway extending to the north. The entire room is lined with floor to ceiling windows. Looking at the small strips of metal between the windows you estimate that they are over a foot thick. A small red glow is eminated from a device on the outside that lines the perimeter of each window. In the center of the room stands the nose of the rocket that brought you here. It appears a forcefield of some sort is projected from the floor to the rocket keeping the harsh vacuum of space from sucking all the air out of the room. }{Dexter's Laboratory - Spacestation}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
