R {29123}{0}{}{Space Station Hallway (w,e)}{ }{You run your hand over the wall as you walk, feeling every inch of its cold, smooth surface. Occasionally you tap your fingers to generate some noise other than the soft flickering of the lights. The room just continues on, devoid of detail, devoid of life, devoid of interest. You ponder whether to continue. }{Dexter's Laboratory - Spacestation}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29120}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29126}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29124}{0}{}{Space Station Post (w)}{ }{Reaching the end of the hallway, this area expands out into a cargo hold. There are no windows at this post, so the only light is the dim, flickering lights that have illuminated the rest of the station. From what you can see, it looks much dingier than the rest of the space station with stacks of crates and cargo netting strung everywhere. Some of the cargo netting appears to be draped in a very specific fashion on one end of the room, almost like a blind used for hunting ducks. }{Dexter's Laboratory - Spacestation}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29122}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29125}{0}{}{Space Station Corner (n,w)}{ }{This part of the station comes to an end here at this hallway corner. The sterile walls of the hallways continue throughout the corner without any indication of seams or other transitions, except for one small control nestled right against the corner of the room. The rest of the room is just as boring as the hallways themselves with nothing of interest illuminated by the flickering lights. }{Dexter's Laboratory - Spacestation}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29121}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29102}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29126}{0}{}{Space Station Duct (s,n,e,w)}{ }{You have entered the central duct for the space station. The gentle whoosh of warm air from the furnace floats past you. Numerous small ducts just barely large enough to fit an arm into branch off in every directly, but they are all covered by a synthetic mesh filter. Below you is a duct and above you appears to be a hatch of some sort. }{Dexter's Laboratory - Spacestation}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29101}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29114}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29123}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29108}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29127}{u}{search ceiling duct;u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29128}{d}{search floor duct;d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29127}{0}{}{Space Station Furnace Room (d)}{ }{This is the furnace room servicing the entire space station. The central duct that spans outwards throughout the station is behind you. Ahead stands a giant fusion powered furnace that generates not only immense heat to warm the station in the vast cold vacuum of space, but also is used to power the entire base as well. }{Dexter's Laboratory - Spacestation}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29126}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29128}{0}{}{Space Station Airlock (u)}{ }{You've entered the airlock for the station. Most stations utilize a two door system, but this particular station uses an airlock of Dexter's own design with a special forcefield that you can simply walk through but that air can't escape. It's sealed behind a thick steel door because, despite Dexter's best attempts, this early prototype airlock didn't work. As such, all traffic in or out of the station goes through the vehicle airlock. On the walls are various satchels secured in place. They probably once held space suits but with the airlock out of commision, it appears they've all been emptied. }{Dexter's Laboratory - Spacestation}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29126}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29129}{0}{}{Transport to Mos Eisly Spaceport (door)}{<138>N<088>}{You behold a landing pad that holds a lone YT-1300 transport landing pad, it is just to your north.  To board the transport and end up in Mos Eisley just go north from here. }{Mos Eisley Cantina}{mos_eisley_cantina}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8088}{door}{door}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
