R {29402}{0}{}{A seemingly barren planet (n,s,w)}{ }{You've reached what appears to be a rather large wall which looks like it might be part of this huge crater to your east. The crater here dwarfs all other craters you've seen on this  desolate planet and looks rather odd, almost unnatural. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29384}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29403}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29408}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29403}{0}{}{A seemingly barren planet (s,n,w,e)}{ }{To the south, the dim light of Phobos shines, brightening this section of the planet. A cold wind blows over the craters, making a cacophony of sound. Above, lies the endless region of space. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29381}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29404}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29407}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29402}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29404}{0}{}{A seemingly barren planet (s,n,w,e)}{ }{The planet surface is slightly lit by the light of Phobos, the second moon of Mars. The ground is marked with craters and rocks, the result of an ancient war of cosmic proportions. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29401}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29405}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29406}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29403}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29405}{0}{}{A seemingly barren planet (se,n,e,nw)}{ }{The vast expanse of space extends for light-years and light-years past the edge of this desolate planet. Stars shine brightly and steadily in the sky. You can feel a soft solar wind waft by, slightly warming you. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29400}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29399}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29406}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29404}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29406}{0}{}{A seemingly barren planet (n,e,nw)}{ }{The light of Phobos illuminates this side of the planet. As you gaze on the second moon of Mars, it seems  unfitting that a sight of such beauty should be named for the god of fear. Past the edge of the planet is only the forever of space. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29405}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29404}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29407}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29407}{0}{}{A seemingly barren planet (n,e,w)}{ }{The light of Phobos shines brightly on the planet here. Beyond the edge, is the deep unending blackness of space. Craters and rocks pock the land everywhere you look. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29403}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29408}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29406}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29408}{0}{}{A seemingly barren planet (w,n)}{ }{The light of Phobos illuminates the surface of the land with a pale white colour. Over the edge of the planet is the depths of endless space. Nothing to see there. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29402}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29407}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29409}{0}{}{Hallway in a crater (s,n,e)}{ }{As you continue your journey through the halls, you can hear sounds of partying off in the distance. The sound is hard to trace as it reverberates against the wall. The walls glow with a light all their own - a result of some property of the rock. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29386}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29413}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29414}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29410}{0}{}{Hallway in a crater (n,s,e)}{ }{The sounds of celebrations are quieter here. The walls of the cavern glow with a light all their own. To the east a sound of lamenting and pain can be heard. How could a planet full of such joy carry such suffering? }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29386}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29411}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29412}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29411}{0}{}{Hallway in a crater (s)}{ }{You've reached a dead end in the tunnel. Apart from the  glowing walls, there isn't much to see here, unless of course, there are aliens in here. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29410}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29412}{0}{}{Lab in a crater (w)}{ }{As you step into this cavern a stunning sight greets you. Beakers, and burners and flasks lie everywhere. In one wall sits a row of large tube-shaped cubicles, and in another wall, sits a computer. What is this place? }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29410}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29413}{0}{}{Vault in a crater (n)}{ }{The light from the rock glows brightly here. Embedded in the wall, is a large door with a hole in it. It looks like the entrance to some sort of vault. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29409}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29415}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29414}{0}{}{Hallway in a crater (s,n,w)}{ }{You continue your journey through the alien tunnels. To the north, you can hear sounds of revelry and celebration. You don't seem to need a light as the walls glow with a light of their own. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29409}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29416}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29417}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29415}{0}{}{Vault in a crater (w)}{ }{The room glows with a soft light. Hewn out of the rock, this vault is completely sealed off to the outside world. There is a pedestal in the middle of the room and on it, sits the power crystal. The door lies open to your west. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29413}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29416}{0}{<238>}{The Minkling Moon (n)}{<238>[P]<088>}{You've wandered into the Minkling Moon, which serves as a pub for all the cute aliens on this little known moon. It's just full of bouncing little critters. In a corner, you see an alien jazz band playing their own brand of jazz, and in the opposite corner, there is a bar carved out of the wall. It doesn't look like they serve non-aliens usually though. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29414}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29417}{0}{}{The throne room of the Grand Poobah (s)}{ }{You have entered the throne room of the Great Poobah of aliens. There is a throne carved from the crater and the Grand Poobah is attended by his attendants. Of course if he isn't here then none of this makes any sense. }{Fuzzy Aliens of Mars}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29414}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29418}{0}{}{A mech graveyard (leave,nw,sw)}{<138>L<088>}{Before you lies a mountain made of the shattered bodies of hundreds of mechs.  The parts from all the mechs litter the ground in every direction.  Through some of the cockpits you can vaguely make out the rotting forms of the pilots of these massive technological monoliths.  You begin to ponder about what could have reduced such a great army to this pile of scrap. }{Codename: Kodiak}{codename_kodiak}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29420}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29421}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {8083}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29419}{0}{<238>}{Traveling up a mountain path (se,e)}{<238>.^.<088>}{The mountain path takes quite a turn here almost doubling back on itself.  To your east a large pile of rubble blocks the path while to the southeast the trail continues on down the cliff.  High up on top of the peak the faint outline of a building is present. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29420}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29424}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29420}{0}{<228>}{The beginning of a trail to a worn down ruin (se,nw,sw)}{<228>( *<088>}{Ahead of you lies what's left of some kind of building.  The path you are on is surrounded by deep craters that still look rather fresh as does most of the destruction in the area. Behind you lies the forest and its eerie tranquility.  Turning toward the building, you begin to wonder if it's still inhabited. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29418}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29419}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29422}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {46522}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29421}{0}{<118>}{Along the southern edge of a war-torn path (ne,sw,nw)}{<118>` ^<088>}{The landscape returns to almost normal here from the burnt-out war-torn surroundings you have seen throughout this path.  The land here has begun to return to the forest that once surrounded this path. The trail of destruction continues to the northeast.  Craters seem to dot the landscape as far as you can see. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29418}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29422}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29423}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29422}{0}{<228>}{The scene of a recent battle (se,ne)}{<228>( *<088>}{This area is more littered than the rest of what you have seen.  The ground is almost completely covered with an assortment of mech parts.  Various mech cannons, missile turrets and other scrap metal have been scattered around.  Deep craters lie all about you.  Some of the craters are filled with the destroyed remains of missiles or whatever the missiles struck. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29420}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29421}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29423}{0}{<228>}{In the beginnings of the forest (ne)}{<228>( *<088>}{This appears to be the edge of the destructive path.  The forest seems to almost regain some of its majesty here.  Trees make a thick wall that seems to block passage to the south and east. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29421}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29424}{0}{<238>}{On a collapsed mountain path (w)}{<238>.^.<088>}{The path directly in front of you seems to have taken a direct missile hit in a skirmish.  Rubble and large chunks of earth have caved in across the road making the path impassable.  The path continues on to the west with the pile of rubble blocking all eastern passage. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29419}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29425}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29425}{0}{<238>}{A guard outpost before a command bunker (nw,se)}{<238>|@|<088>}{Barbed wire and trenches line the road leading up to the bunker ahead. A covered platform off to the side of the road acts as a station for the behemoth mechanized guards.  A few craters and empty shell casings are a testament to the guardians' resolve. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29424}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29426}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29426}{0}{<238>}{A scarred set of blast doors (nw,se)}{<238>|@|<088>}{You stand in an archway before the remnants of a set of massive steel-plated blast doors.  A shattered control console is centered on the west wall of the archway.  Even the concrete slab below your feet is split in half under the weight of a massive intruder.  To the southeast is the path on which you entered. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29425}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29427}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29427}{0}{<268>}{An intersection (se,sw,ne)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{You stand in an intersection of halls leading off in various directions.  Just in front of you are the doors of an old elevator.  This room seems to be in decent condition with only minor structural damage apparent along the walls.  As with most of the compound there is no power going to any of the systems and only a faint light shines through from the entrance behind you. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29426}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29428}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29429}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29432}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29428}{0}{<268>}{A burnt out room in a corner of a ruined bunker (ne,nw)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{This is the southwest corner of what remains of the Clan Wolf bunker.  The walls contain slits that seem to have been used at one time for defense.  The room has scorch marks everywhere as well as a giant hole in the ceiling apparently from a direct missile hit.  Rubble and shards of the ceiling lie strewn about the floor. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29427}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29430}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29429}{0}{<268>}{A corner room of a ruined bunker (sw,nw)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{This is the east corner of what remains of the Clan Wolf bunker, the walls contain slits that seem to have been used at one time for defense.  All along the floor there lay hundreds, maybe thousands of spent shell casings and jammed, worthless guns that were apparently used to fire on enemies when the base was under siege. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29427}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29431}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29430}{0}{<248>}{A mess hall in a ruined bunker (se)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{This room has been designed more for humanoid-sized occupants.  The tables and chairs, while broken down and in bad need of repair, are built for rather average people.  The steel counters and shabby collection of dinnerware remind you exactly what toll these attacks have taken upon the occupants of this base. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29428}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29431}{0}{<248>}{A darkened room in a ruined bunker (se)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{This room is almost completely dark.  Shattered and burnt-out lights hang above you.  This room looks as though it was completely stripped of anything it may have held.  The only things noticeable in this room are your own footsteps echoing off the walls. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29429}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29432}{0}{<278>}{An old elevator shaft in a ruined bunker (se)}{<278>.@.<088>}{This elevator shaft has obviously seen better days.  The shaft below you has been boarded up, creating a makeshift floor on which you now stand.  The elevator itself is nowhere to be found.  Even the cables that once guided its ascent and descent have been removed.  The elevator doors lie partially closed to the southeast. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29427}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29433}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29434}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29433}{0}{}{Commander Ford's office (d)}{ }{This small office is apparently all that remains of the highest level of the bunker.  A desk, covered with papers lies before you and a map of the area hangs along the back wall.  Some pictures hang askew along the walls to your left and right in a vain attempt to brighten this drab office space. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29432}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29434}{0}{}{The remains of a mech training hall (u)}{ }{This room is all that is left of one of the great Clan Wolf training halls.  This is where all the trainees would come to be instructed on how best to face their foes in combat.  The room looks almost like a large garage with stripes and other traffic controlling directions painted on the ground to guide the warriors without incident in the close quarters. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29432}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29435}{0}{}{Entry Tunnel (e,w)}{ }{This is the entry tunnel leading from the landing pad to the interior of the Harkonnen fortress.  It is rather large, but you still get the feeling of being trapped. }{Dune}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29216}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29436}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

