R {29539}{0}{<248>}{Small Arms Locker (e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{This is where small arms and munitions are stored on Galactica.  Surrounding you are shelves chock full of pistols, rifles, and explosive devices.  You feel like a kid in a candy store.  A metal door to the east leads back to Galactica. }{Battlestar Galactica}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29525}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29540}{0}{}{Inside a Viper Simulator (exit)}{ }{You are in a replica of a Viper Mark VII cockpit.  Surrounding you are screens to display your virtual environment.  In front of you is a DRADIS display.  Between your legs is a control stick.  Hanging from the ceiling is an instructions manual. }{Battlestar Galactica}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29532}{exit}{exit}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29601}{press launch}{press launch}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29541}{0}{}{Cart Path (n,path)}{<238>P<088>}{The one-lane cart path emerges from a forested area into a cleared countryside. It continues onward and upwards to a towering building which rests at the top of the highest foothill. The path is no more than eight feet in breadth and is primarily characterized by a set of ruts bored into the packed dirt. Vegetation sporadically interjects itself on the less trodden areas of the cart path but, on the whole, the path seems to be frequently used. A steady gust from the north-northeast rustles the grain crops\; creating an enthralling wave-like motion across the entire plain. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{aruwins_windmill}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {1621}{path}{path}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29542}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29542}{0}{}{Before a Barn (w,s)}{ }{Before you stands a looming windmill.  The structure itself is at least fifty feet in height at the apex of the stone tower\; the sails bring its skyward reach to nearly seventy feet.  A short and squat two-story barn made from wood extends from the eastern base of the tower.  A small bronze weather vane has been placed at front edge of the barn roof's ridge. You currently stand at the front of the barn where the road terminates into a small packed dirt courtyard. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29541}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29543}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29543}{0}{}{Foyer (w,e)}{ }{This level of the barn is one large room.  The sunlight pouring in through the open door is the primary source of light for the room. There are several windows on either side of the barn allowing a trickle of sunlight to supplement the light coming from the doorway. The remainder of the area is open space\; enough for a cart or wagon to back-in and receive finished goods or drop-off raw grains. To the west you see a large scale of some kind and to the east is the open door leading back to the courtyard. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29542}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29544}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29544}{0}{}{Middle of Barn (w,e)}{ }{The southern end of this area houses a massive scale. Adjacent to the scale are several stacks of flat stones piled neatly and ordered according to size. The central space is very open allowing for unobstructed travel to either end of the barn. The northern side has a small table and pair of chairs nestled close to a wide stone fireplace. To the fireplace's left is a collection of common blacksmithing devices. Deeper into the barn you can see a system of pulleys, while back to the east lies the desk and front doorway. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29543}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29545}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29545}{0}{}{Far-End of Barn (w,e)}{ }{The barn abuts and connects to a stone wall at the western end of this section. On that wall is a single stout oak door. To the right of the doorway several cleats have been affixed to the wall. In the center of this area, a system of pulleys dangles from one of the overhead support beams. A few steps from the tangle of ropes is a large inverted conical bin. Extending from the bin's bottom vertex is a long open chute that feeds into a chamber beyond the wall via a small opening to the left of the doorway. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29544}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29546}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29547}{d}{untie rope;open trapdoor;hook inix;lower inix}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29546}{0}{}{Milling Room (u,d,e)}{ }{This is where the grain is actually milled. The chute from the previous room continues its gradual descent toward the middle of the room. Two supports, one for the bottom stone and another for the top millstone, or runner stone, are located directly over a collection bin which rests in a hole in the floor. Another two holes can be seen in the ceiling. Next to the base support are two levers used to control the milling process.  A stone staircase spirals along the perimeter of the room allowing access to the basement and tower above.  }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29545}{e}{open door;e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29548}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29550}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29547}{0}{}{Grain Storage (w)}{ }{This room is the final destination of the milled grain. Along the walls are several wooden pallets, each one holding various amounts of finished goods.  In the middle of the ceiling is a large trapdoor which is wide enough to easily accommodate any of the pallets stored here. Two shelves storing odds and ends have been built into the eastern wall where the room ends, and to the west is an opening leading to the sacking room. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29545}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29548}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29549}{e}{push wall;e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29548}{0}{}{Sacking Room (e,u)}{ }{The stairwell ends here in a round room. The walls and floor are chiseled from the bedrock of the hill on which the windmill resides. The ceiling is wooden, like the one in the barn, but protruding from the center is a metal cone.  Centered below the cone is a table with a concave surface. On the ground, next to the table, are large sacks in a pile and a spindle of twine. A storeroom of some kind can be seen through the opening to the east. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29547}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29546}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29549}{0}{}{Wine Cellar (w)}{ }{The room is very small and cramped, mainly due to the wine racks that fill the walls from floor to ceiling. There are well over a thousand bottles and a wide selection. Oddly no dust has accumulated on any of the bottles, or the racks for that matter. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29547}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29550}{0}{}{Dressing Room (d,u,e)}{ }{The stairwell pauses here at a small landing. The room is circular in design, at the heart of the chamber is the grinding shaft\; it continues up from the large hole in the center of the floor through another hole in the ceiling. Four windows inset in the wall allow for some light to find its way into the otherwise dark interior. Nestled between the southern window and the door to the east, is a workstation of some kind. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29546}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29551}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29552}{e}{open door;e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29551}{0}{}{Storage Room (u,d)}{ }{Layers of dust have settled over this room's contents.  Circumspection of the room in a clockwise direction you notice four distinct storage areas. Several trails of footprints leading to the various storage areas and betwixt them can be seen. Each of the areas are partially lit by a window inset in the exterior wall. The grinding shaft continues from the hole in the floor upwards through a matching hole in the ceiling. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29550}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29553}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29552}{0}{}{Common Room (e,w)}{ }{This is where the master's apprentices live when not performing their various chores and obligations. There are four cots on the northern side of the room, each with its own footlocker. A small table, surrounded by four chairs, is located on the southern side of the room next to an opening that leads to the kitchen. The floor consists of thick planks, and the ceiling is nothing more than the barn's rafters and roof. }{Aruwin's Windmill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29550}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
