R {29947}{0}{<248>}{Cave (s,n)}{<248>% %<088>}{The cave tunnel is barely lit by large crystals that hang from the roof.  You hear the roar of Balooga falls outside the well lit cave entrance.  Moss covers the walls and the floor surface, making it slippery to walk on.  You hear the occasional drips of water from nearby stalactites.  It is cold, moist and dank here.  As your eyes become adjusted to the low light, you notice that there are several footprints leading deeper into the cave. }{Balooga Falls}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29945}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29948}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {29948}{0}{<248>}{Cave (w,e,s)}{<248>% %<088>}{As you look carefully at the ground as you navigate your way through the slippery moss, you suddenly bump into a cave wall.  On the wall, a white arrow points to the east.  Most of the footprints wander to the east, whereas one set decided to head west. }{Balooga Falls}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {29947}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {29949}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
