R {30000}{0}{}{The Bane of Angeldemons}{ }{You stand in a dome-shaped room which is sparsely furnished. It's the strangest library you've ever known.  You conclude that it senses your needs and reasons for coming.  It then tests your will and sincerity.  In many ways, this almost 'living' library has been kept in secrecy by machinations of the False God.  In many ways, the library is very much like the sun occluded by the moon.  Nevertheless, the long-kept secret of the Library of Raynaud is no more.  Perhaps victory over the False God and angeldemons is at hand...  Your morale soars! }{Balooga Falls}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23457}{go}{go}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30001}{0}{<088>}{stalls (n,s)}{ }{        Row upon row of plush seating lies either side of you in the stalls of the theatre.  The seats are all empty which suggests that it is closed or in rehearsal and you probably aren't welcome.  A rich carpet runs from the doors leading to the foyer all the way down the aisle to the stage.  The vaulted ceiling towers above you and exhibits an enormous mural that stretches from wall to wall.  Opulently decorated boxes run along the walls overlooking the stage, providing the best possible view of the performance below. }{Theatre of Souls}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
