R {30049}{0}{<238>}{Mountain Top, Outcropping (d)}{🐉}{You are standing at the very top of the Mountain, on a small stony outcropping.  From here you can view all of the Dragon Realms. Dragons fly around the sky, relaxed and in control.  Below them are miles of cave openings and hollowed mountains.  Every type of dragon imaginable can be seen within the realm, and each within their own form of dwelling. Occasionally, the smaller dragons come up here to get a look at all the land that lies below... The older dragons have long since memorized the layout and have better things to do than sit around. }{The Dragon Realms}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6279}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30050}{0}{}{Bath house (u)}{ }{This bathhouse was created to allow inhabitants of the pyramid to bathe and to partake in other, more physical activities in the afterlife.  The stone floor slopes downward to a large drain in the center of the room.  Along the wall is a large pile of bricks and a rickety ladder leads upward. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30003}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
