R {30051}{0}{}{Utter darkness}{ }{This small chamber is circular and made of closely fitted stone.  It is completely utterly dark, and there is a noxious odor all about.  The stone floor is covered in thick and slimy ooze that drains from somewhere within the walls. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30052}{w}{insert key;w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30052}{0}{}{Reception room (e,d)}{ }{This darkened chamber appears to be the true beginning of the pyramid. A dust covered plaque hangs on a square column which stands directly in the center of the room.  A large, wooden framed, mirror covers nearly the entirety of the western wall.  A number of elegant but dust-covered chairs act as thrones for the dead and their guests.  A sturdy ladder leads down and faint noises can be heard from within the darkness below. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30051}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30053}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30053}{0}{}{Altar of Rutha-Al (nw,sw,ne,se,u)}{ }{This huge rectangular room is lit by torches mounted within iron sconces.  The torches cast flickering light on the decorative carvings prevalent throughout the walls.  Small alcoves extend from the main chamber in many directions, although the torch light doesn't reach them.  An ancient wooden ladder leads upwards into darkness and a plaque is mounted on a large brown stone acting as an altar in the middle of this chamber.  Next to the altar is a tall statue with eyes that look alive. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30052}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
