R {30054}{0}{}{Sarcophagus of a servant (se)}{ }{In this alcove stands a tall sarcophagus, covered in a lifelike painting of the one presumably enshrined within it.  A thick layer of dust hangs on the engraved walls and stone floor alluding that nobody has disturbed this chamber for centuries.  Spider webs hang in the corners of the doorway leading to the main chamber to the southeast. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30053}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30055}{0}{}{Sarcophagus of the treasurer (ne)}{ }{In this small alcove stands a short, pear-shaped, sarcophagus covered in a lifelike painting of someone presumably enshrined within it.  The room is filled with thick layers of dust, and white cobwebs drape everywhere.  The stone walls are covered with engravings and carvings depicting the life of the pharaoh's servant. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30053}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30056}{0}{}{Sarcophagus of a Servant (sw)}{ }{This small alcove contains a tall brass sarcophagus that is layered in dust and dirt.  Thick cobwebs hang from the ceiling and doorframe that leads back into the main chamber.  The sarcophagus lid has a life-like painting on it, probably of whomever is enshrined within the coffin.  The walls are covered in engravings depicting life in the time of the pharaoh. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30053}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30057}{0}{}{Sarcophagus of a scholar (nw)}{ }{This dust filled small alcove contains a large bronze sarcophagus with a painting of an elderly man upon it.  The walls are covered in engravings, carved into the stone, which depict life in the time of the pharaoh.  The alcove is completely quiet, except for the occasional sound of a crackling torch coming from the main chamber to the northwest. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30053}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30058}{0}{}{Pharaoh's Tomb (sw,nw,stairs,e)}{ }{This large and ornate chamber must be the final resting place of Rutha-Al, evil pharaoh of Taslen during some long forgotten time.  A temple to his god, Apotep, has been erected to the east, and you can see the glistening of mounds of gold to the northwest coming from his treasure room.  A wardrobe closet seems to be over to the southwest. In the center of this chamber on a long gray altar is the sarcophagus of the infamous King.  Statues of many Taslanian gods line the walls of this chamber, which are themselves laced with solid gold trimming. The room is deadly still, and doesn't seem to have been disturbed for many centuries.  Dust covers everything, including the plaque over one of the statues' heads. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30059}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30060}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
