R {30059}{0}{}{Pharaoh's Wardrobe (ne)}{ }{This large chamber is used to store the linens and clothing for the entombed pharaoh.  The once regal garments were designed so that the pharaoh would have plenty of clothing in the afterlife.  Now deteriorated to mere strands and intermixed with dust, the unsalvageable clothing is lined on the right hand side with linens on the left. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30058}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30060}{0}{}{Hoard of Rutha-Al (se)}{ }{This small chamber is filled with treasure and is the treasure room of the ancient pharaoh Rutha-Al.  Like many pharaohs of his time, his treasure was to be kept near him so that he could utilize it in the afterlife.  The floor is littered in gold, the once neat piles of coins have been looted many times.  A large chest is surrounded by more coins in the far corner, and stacks of ivory rest upon long rotted wooden shelves.  A weapons rack, filled with shining swords and polearms, is directly across from a statue of the pharaoh himself. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30058}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30061}{0}{}{A pitch black pit}{ }{This deep pit is filled with bones, and dried blood across the stone floor.  The walls are very steep, far too steep to climb. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30058}{fly up}{fly up}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30062}{0}{}{Temple to Apotep (w)}{ }{This large chamber is obviously a place of worship, dedicated to the god Apotep.  The cavity is perfectly rectangular, and the ceiling is abnormally high, yet still made out of the same closely fitted stone as the rest of the pyramid.  A large archway leads to the west and is supported by two large pylons marked with a symbol of a black jackal.  There is an inner sanctuary surrounded by smaller walls on the eastern side of the chamber.  The head of a stone statue can be seen towering over the sanctuary walls. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30058}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30063}{0}{}{Base of the pyramid (sw,nw,ne,se)}{ }{This maze of stone tunnels runs seemingly in every direction.  A slight haze hovers in the air, making it difficult to determine direction and it also causes a slight headache.  The floor is covered in dirt with tracks leading in each direction.  Within the center-ceiling of this particular corridor is a large dirt hole with a rope hanging from it. }{Tomb of Rutha-Al}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
