R {30254}{0}{<238>}{powder room (w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The room opens up into a delicately feminine area with softly shaded furnishings and subtly patterned wallpaper.  Creating splashes of colour across the walls is an opaque stained-glass window with a delightful garden design.  The coloured glass is reflected in the mirror on the opposite wall, which is placed conveniently beside a washstand that displays and stores a matching china bowl and jug set.  Centered in this ladies' retreat is a large oval ottoman with several scatter cushions that complete the beckoning comfort. }{Aunt May's Cottage}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30250}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30255}{0}{<248>}{cottage kitchen (e)}{<248>.<018>#<248>.<088>}{In an explosion of gingham and wood, this small room manages to exude an air of being the hub of the household.  Beside the breakfast table overlooking the garden, is a rustic hutch dresser filled with porcelain and pottery.  Along the opposite wall is a kitchen necessity, a heavy slab of wood crafted as a sturdy bench.  Adding to the cheerful quaintness of the room is the sunshine that flows in through the windows. }{Aunt May's Cottage}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30250}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30256}{0}{<228>}{a cottage garden (n,s,w,e)}{<228>, .<088>}{Cobbles that sweep down from the cottage door cease here, leaving lush lawn to continue the trek towards the bottom of the garden.  The sun is not interrupted by a tree or bush before reaching the ground, as this is an open section of the garden.  Here the verdant turf acts as the great divide between a fountain courtyard and a hedge opening. }{Aunt May's Cottage}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
