R {30268}{0}{<278>}{stairs (d,e)}{<278>.@.<088>}{Beyond the evenly spaced posts of the mezzanine floor balustrade is the library, almost within full view.  With splashes of vertical colour, the books on the opposite wall reach up to the high ceiling in an impressive display of collected knowledge.  This gallery stretches from the top of the iron and hardwood curl of the staircase to the hallway, and is the perfect place to display the collection of family portraits on the wall.  The frames are an eclectic mix of sizes and colours but somehow manage to appear part of the same ensemble. }{Aunt May's Cottage}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
