R {30269}{0}{<268>}{hallway (n,nw,e,w)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{A long narrow hall table stands between two doorways and hugs the wall.  Pale coloured walls help disperse the dreary atmosphere that would otherwise be created from the darkly grained table wood.  A somewhat threadbare, woven wool runner stretches the length of the hall, lying atop the wooden floorboards.  Colours from this rug are also evident in the painting centered above the table.  With no fixed light source of its own, the hallway is brightened from the overflowing light from the adjoining rooms. }{Aunt May's Cottage}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
