R {30324}{0}{<278>}{Tookwich Town Limits (path,se)}{<278>[<238>P<238>]<088>}{You've stumbled upon the town limits of Tookwich, home of hobbits. This quiet little village lies nestled in the forest away from the hustle and bustle of Wayhaven. Hobbits aren't known for dealing often with strangers, preferring to lead a simple life away from the dangers and intrigue of other races. Visitors are scarce in this part of the realm, but perhaps you could wander in without causing too much of a fuss. The path leading into town heads off to the southeast. }{Tookwich}{tookwich}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8045}{path}{path}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30325}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30325}{0}{<278>}{Tookwich Road (s,nw,e)}{<278>[ ]<088>}{This dirt path leads deeper into the town of Tookwich. To the east you see a large grass covered hill with something very surprising in the front of it, a doorway! It seems that hobbits prefer to live underground rather than in above ground houses as humans do. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
