R {30327}{0}{<238>}{Brookenbill House (w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This small comfy house is actually dug right out of the hill. Since it's underground, it remains cool even in the hottest of days outside. You see two small chairs sitting in the room and a table that looks like it is used for dinner. Several small plates sit atop it along with a delicate blue glass vase. A small straw bed lies in the corner. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30325}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30328}{0}{<278>}{Tookwich Road (s,n,e,w)}{<278>-+-<088>}{This dirt path continues through the town of Tookwich. The ground you tread on is sloped, slowly rising as you get deeper into the town. To the east you hear the sound of song and the clinking of mugs. A sign hangs from a post near the road that you might want to read. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
