R {30329}{0}{<238>}{Pondwander House (w)}{B}{This quiet little house has a small bed of straw in one corner, a cloth-covered chair in front of a round wooden table and a long bookshelf along one wall. There is a small glass vase of flowers atop the table. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30326}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30330}{0}{<238>}{Wishwell House (e)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This little underground house features a small bed of straw, a long bench along one wall and a ceiling so low you have to crouch just to keep from bumping your head! A small fireplace crackles in one corner keeping the house extra toasty. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30326}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30331}{0}{<278>}{Tookwich Road (se,n,sw)}{<278>[ ]<088>}{The dirt path comes to an end at the southern border of the town. Further south you see many more of the now familiar hills which contain the houses of this town's residents. It looks like a few of them are reachable without traipsing about in the grass beyond the path. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
