R {30338}{0}{<238>}{W. Wagglerun House (s)}{E}{This cozy house looks old, but still well kept. Bookshelves line every wall and a table stands in the corner, papers strewn all over it. Two small, but comfy-looking chairs sit beside the table. There is also a lamp behind the chairs to provide extra light. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30337}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30339}{0}{<278>}{Tookwich Road (n,s,w)}{<278>-+ <088>}{The path continues through the winding hills of hobbit houses and shops. You still hear the birds calling to one another in the sky overhead and you think you can hear small animals scampering about in the grass around you as well. This part of the town is shaded heavily from the surrounding trees and it seems a bit cooler without the sun shining directly down on you. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30337}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30341}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30342}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30340}{0}{<238>}{Tookwich Town Hall (e,n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{You've entered the Tookwich Town Hall. This is where the hobbits come together for meetings whenever the need arises. Although empty now, you sense a history to this place, as if great events transpired here in the past. Rows of seats line the room facing a stage on the far end of the hall and paintings hang on the walls depicting scenes from hobbit lore. An office lies to the north. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30337}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30346}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30341}{0}{<238>}{Hoppinstop House (n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This quiet little house contains a straw bed, a table, two chairs and a small firepit. The pit is currently lit and cooking a black pot filled with something that smells delicious! }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30339}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30342}{0}{<278>}{Tookwich Road (s,w,nw,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{You've reached the western end of Tookwich Road. More hills lie off in the distance, but there is no apparent way to reach them. You do however, notice some hills closer to the path as well as a sign posted nearby. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30339}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30343}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30344}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30345}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30343}{0}{<238>}{Gondolot House (n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This quaint house doesn't contain much furniture, but looks well kept and cozy. A few pillows lie beside the bed and a small vanity and mirror sit against the far wall. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30342}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30344}{0}{<238>}{Tookwich Pipe Shop (e)}{F}{You've entered the local pipe shop. This is where all the denizens of Tookwich come to purchase their beloved pipes and smoking supplies. You see a long counter in front of the far wall and display shelves along the side walls. Smoke hangs heavily in the room and a sign hangs above the wall behind the counter that you may want to read. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30342}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30345}{0}{<238>}{Took House (se)}{G}{This quiet house is spacious and well decorated. The mayor doesn't seem to be home right now, but he left his house immaculately clean. Stuffed chairs sit in a circle that seems meant for sparking conversation, while a small table sits in the middle of them. A large fireplace sits in the corner of the house, unlit and cold. The mayor's bed sits on the far end of the room. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30342}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30346}{0}{<238>}{Mayor Took's Office (s)}{T}{This spacious room is decorated in rich colored fabrics and finely crafted furniture. Plush chairs and a large wooden desk sit on a thick burgundy rug. Several bookshelves line the walls and sconces are placed along the walls for ambient light. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30340}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30347}{d}{turn sconce}{32}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30347}{0}{<238>}{Hidden Tunnel (nw)}{<238>] [<088>}{You've slid underneath the Mayor's office and into some type of hidden tunnel! It's dark and cold in here, but relatively dry. The tunnel appears to have been dug right out of the earth, not surprising considering the hobbits' love of underground dwellings. You don't see any way to climb back out of this secret place, but it looks like the tunnel continues to the northwest. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30348}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30348}{0}{<238>}{Hidden Tunnel (w,se)}{<238>] [<088>}{The tunnel continues through the darkness and ends at a large vault door to the west. While the walls, floor, and ceiling of the tunnel are plain, nothing more than hard-packed dirt, the door is another thing entirely. Maybe you should take a closer look? }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30347}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30349}{w}{unlock door;open door;w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30349}{0}{<138>}{Tookwich Treasury (u,e)}{<138>[ ]<088>}{This musty room, cut from rock and earth, is the hidden vault for the hobbits' town treasury! Shelves have been cut from the rock and are lined with countless treasures. A magical aura surrounds the shelves and glows with a soft, warm light. A pedestal stands in the center of the room and a small hole has been dug from the ceiling above it, letting in sunlight and leaving piles of loose dirt on the floor. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30348}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {1633}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30350}{0}{}{Leafwind Tool Shed (out)}{ }{This little shed is stuffed full of all sorts of tools! It's also stifling hot in here due to a lack of ventilation, so you might not want to stay very long. It smells of old grass clippings, fertilizer, and rust. It's also quite dark. }{Tookwich}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30334}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30351}{0}{<238>}{A Hermit's Hut (leave)}{<238># #<088>}{It takes a moment for your eyes to adjust to the dim light of this cozy looking abode, and when they do, you are confused, but also pleasantly  surprised to find quite extensive collection of antique vases sitting atop ragged stands, along with other impressive memorabilia on the splintering shelves. Sometimes an old hermit sits here in his wicker  chair, greeting you between puffs on his old smoking pipe. You see many paintings hung above some of the vases, the color of the oils faded  from their original brilliance but still marvelously piebald. Every few yards there are small wooden hooks, most of which have little trinkets, medallions, or necklaces hanging from them, obviously remnants of ages  past. }{Hut}{hermits_hut}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {7838}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30352}{0}{<238>}{Center of a Camp (s,n,e,w)}{<238>, `<088>}{You are standing in the center of a dusty and idle camp.  There does not seem to be much activity going on.  Two small tents to the east and west, and what looks like an open sided, covered tent to the north.  You detect the smell of a stew cooking somewhere. }{A Missionary Camp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
