E {30355}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30353}{0}{<238>}{An Eating Tent (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{A long table sits here underneath the tent.  The tent itself is really just a large single piece of canvas, protecting you from the weather.  It is supported by several thin poles.  The scent of unwashed bodies underlies the strong smells of a warm stew cooking. }{A Missionary Camp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30352}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30354}{0}{<238>}{Entrance to a Tent (n,w)}{<238>, `<088>}{The front of the tent is sparsely decorated.  A small stool sits in one corner, next to a wooden table.   A candle rests on the the table and obviously has contributed to the small puddle of hardened wax there. }{A Missionary Camp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30352}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30357}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30355}{0}{<238>}{Entrance to a Tent (n,e)}{<238>, `<088>}{The front of this tent is pretty bare.  The flaps allow exit to the east, and the tent extends a short ways to the north.  A small set of shelves rests to the side, but they too are bare.   }{A Missionary Camp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30352}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30356}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30356}{0}{<238>}{Inside a Tent (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The tent is small, expanding only a short ways to the north.  There is barely enough room for the small bed that sits under the slope of the canvas.  A small pile of dust is off to the side. }{A Missionary Camp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30355}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30357}{0}{<238>}{Inside a Tent (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This portion of the tent is quite cramped, there is just enough room for the small bed to fit snugly within.  The canvas of the tent slopes down over the bed to the ground, forming the north end of the tent. }{A Missionary Camp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30354}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30358}{0}{<278>}{An overgrown trail (n,s)}{<228>,<278>|<228>`<088>}{Trees and bushes have grown close together here, almost entirely obscuring an old path or trail.  Gnarled tree roots threaten to trip you if you stop paying close attention to the ground.  Old, brown, wet, leaves cover the trail and make things very slippery.  The trail winds south, but you cannot really see what it leads to because of the undergrowth. }{Ancient Dolmen}{ancient_dolmen}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6723}{n}{n}{1}{1}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30359}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30359}{0}{<228>}{Along the trail (sw,n)}{<228>( *<088>}{The trail widens out slightly, although branches still reach out from the trees on either side to snag your clothing and scratch your skin.  The general background noises of the forest are somewhat muted, but you can still hear birds chirp occasionally.  The wind makes the leaves of the trees rustle gently, but things seem somehow calmer, and more serene here.  The trail narrows slightly to the north, and there is a suggestion of a clearing to the southwest. }{Ancient Dolmen}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30358}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30360}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30360}{0}{<228>}{A small clearing (ne,e)}{<228>, `<088>}{The trail has opened out into a small clearing here.  The trees form an impenetrable wall on all sides apart from the east.  The eastern edge of the clearing is dominated by a large dolmen which faces you, huge, cold and impassive.  The grass on the ground is short and springy and covered with a light dew.  The dolmen has probably not been visited by druids for many years, but there may still be traces of power here as the area feels quiet and serene.  The dolmen is large enough that you could walk under it by moving east slightly. }{Ancient Dolmen}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30359}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30361}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30361}{0}{<238>}{Under the dolmen (w)}{<238>^ ^<088>}{The huge stones of the dolmen stand to your north and south, and the large capstone blocks out the sky above you.  The capstone is as big as a small cottage and must weigh a whole lot more.  The stones are granite grey, and smooth sided.  The grass underfoot is even more damp than that of the clearing, as the shade from the capstone has prevented the sun from drying it.  It is very still and quiet beneath the capstone, almost unnerving. }{Ancient Dolmen}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30360}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30362}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30362}{0}{<238>}{Below the trapdoor (u,n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{There is a small hideout under the dolmen.  The walls are exposed earth propped up with wooden beams.  A rickety wooden ladder leads up to the surface.  A poorly built table and chair stand near the base of the ladder.  Dim, guttering light is provided by a small metal lantern sitting on the table.  There is another room to the north. }{Ancient Dolmen}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30361}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30363}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30363}{0}{<238>}{Bandit's den (s,e)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{Straw has been strewn liberally over the floor of this room, and hessian sacking has been nailed onto the wooden beams to cover the earthen walls to give this room a slightly more finished look than the entrance that lies to the south.  The room is dominated by two large wooden chests that lie open near the north wall.  There are also two chairs next to a medium sized table against the west wall.  There is a narrow, low tunnel leading east. }{Ancient Dolmen}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30362}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30364}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30364}{0}{<238>}{A small storage room (w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This small unfurnished room was probably designed as a simple store room, in fact you can see remnants of food and other sundries in the bottoms of the broken crates that litter the room.  It seems that it has also been employed as a makeshift cell as there is a dirty ragged blanket and empty water bowl in one corner, next to an iron spike that has been driven into the floor. }{Ancient Dolmen}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30363}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30365}{0}{<148>}{A small waterfall. (s)}{<148>~<238>C<148>~<088>}{After a short walk up the stream, you come upon a small  waterfall.  Water flows quickly over the hill and plunges quickly downward to the ground.  The trees form a circle surrounding the waterfall.  A small stream flows south  towards the mountain pool.  }{Owlbears}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
