R {30458}{0}{<248>}{Cave of the Green Lion (leave,sw)}{<248>%<228>L<248>%<088>}{This cave, carved out from the rock by the tiny stream at your feet, is a surprisingly beautiful sight. The rich reds and browns of the sandstone cave walls contrast strongly with the green cascade of moss and water falling from the cavemouth into the space where you now stand. Small chips of quartz within the walls glitter and flash, reflecting your light back to you as you move around the cave. }{The Green Lion}{the_green_lion}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {19821}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30459}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30459}{0}{<248>}{Cave of the Green Lion (ne,d)}{<248>% %<088>}{The glimmer of light from the cave mouth to the northeast is fainter here, but it is bright daylight compared to the dark hole beneath your feet. The little stream you followed into the cave has cut its way down into the bedrock and has collapsed part of the floor of the cave. The water now cascades over a steep slope of broken rock leading down into the gloom. }{The Green Lion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30458}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30460}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30460}{0}{<248>}{Boulder Field (u,nw)}{<248>% %<088>}{This section of the cave is completely full of huge boulders wedged together in the narrow passage of the cave to form an uneven floor of sorts. The rock pile seems to be fairly stable underfoot, but you must pay close attention so that you don't fall into one of the many cracks and crevices. It also doesn't help that the rocks in places are being soaked by a cascade of water from above as it falls through the cracks in the floor. }{The Green Lion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30459}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30461}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30461}{0}{<248>}{Edge of the Boulder Field (se,n,e)}{<248>% %<088>}{Standing at the edge of the boulder field, you can see three possible routes disappearing into the darkness. To the north the main passage of the cave contines, following the route of the little crystal clear stream. To the southeast, you have the option of clambering carefully up through the boulders to the passage out. There also seems to be a small crevice you could squeeze your way down leading east around the edge of the boulder cave. }{The Green Lion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30460}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30462}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30463}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30462}{0}{<238>}{Sandy Tunnel (s,nw)}{A}{The sandstone tunnel curves gradually down from the south to the northwest, following the path carved by the stream. At the point where the tunnel bends a large pile of rubble and debris has built up against the eroded rockface. On the opposite wall a picture has been drawn in black on the bare sandstone. }{The Green Lion}{wight_barrows}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30461}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30465}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
