R {30500}{0}{<238>}{[*]- Soldier Quarters -[*] (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{A small enclosed room with a few tables and chairs lying upon the ground.  The militia of the republic often come here to rest up and wait for the call of duty from the great council.  Beddings also line up along the stone walls as well.  On average, each quarters usually house approximately from three to five soldiers.  It may not be the most spacious place to hold so many of them, but it is the militia after all.  }{Mount Knivur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30499}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30501}{0}{<238>}{[*]- Soldier Quarters -[*] (e)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The soldier's quarters is less than what one would describe as extravagant or even well off.  The single beddings, tables and wooden chairs alone give this place an unappealing appearance.  The smooth stone walls of the mountain enclose the room and the only available exit is the wooden door on the eastern wall.  The ceiling above is not as high as it was in the corridor, so free space to move around in is limited.  }{Mount Knivur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30499}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30502}{0}{<268>}{[*]- Eastern Corridor of Knivur -[*] (n,e,w)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The corridor ends further east while a small door lies within the mountain northern wall.  The torches hanging down along the stone walls illuminate the room and the sound of movement keeps getting louder.  The cool breeze picks up and becomes heavier in concentration.  Looking back west, a small mental note is made to visit the city north of the main hall as soon as the corridor has been fully investigated.  }{Mount Knivur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
