R {30600}{0}{<238>}{[*]- Wizards' Chamber of Knivur -[*] (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The chamber is small and quaint, with not a lot of extremities inside of it at all.  The walls are made from the granite stone so commonly found, and are covered with a few tapestries of dwarven make.  Upon the floor are piles of riches that the great republic hordes for the monetary needs of the city.  An aura, magical in nature, covers over it and the sensation that it is some sort of protection spell rushes over you.  It is too bad too, you wonder if you could at least get a little treasure before leaving. }{Mount Knivur}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30599}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30601}{0}{<238>}{Secret Room (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{A faint, magical light fills the room with a reddish glow. It does not help one to see much. However, it shows the room to be larger and less icy than the rest of the cave. It's as if a portal arrived at a new place not of this world. A throne sits at the far wall about 20 feet ahead. Towering columns, with red light illuminating from them, stand high above. There does not seem to be a ceiling above, as sounds are not echoing back. The walls appear to be marble, reflecting back various shades of the light. }{Jaffa's Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
