E {30731}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30729}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30740}{4104}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {30732}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30729}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30741}{0}{}{Somewhere in the middle of the pews (s)}{ }{Hard, uncomfortable looking pews stretch east towards the rear of the church, and west towards the altar and south towards the aisle.  The sturdy stone wall rises just to the north, and you can see it slowly curves inwards as it climbs, hiding the balcony from your view. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30733}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30742}{0}{}{Among the pews (n)}{ }{Half way towards the altar, the pews are just as deserted as everywhere else, with only a handful of faithful cows praying to the Almighty Moo.  The southern wall arcs upwards, blocking any sight of the balcony that lies part way up its stony facade.  The aisle, which seems to be the only way to reach the front or rear of the church, lies back to the north. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30733}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30743}{0}{}{Towards the front of the church of Moo (n,s,w,e)}{ }{The front row of pews extends towards both walls, leaving an open space in front before the altar which sits below the impressive stained-glass window.  The balcony that encircles the room curves around to end on both sides of the altar, allowing viewing of any ceremony from above as well as from the pews. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30733}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30744}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30745}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30746}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30744}{0}{}{The front row of pews (s)}{ }{The front row of pews has an unobstructed view of the altar and stained-glass window backdrop to the southwest.  The wall to the north looms overhead as it slowly arches inwards to meet the opposing wall high overhead.  Between the pews and the altar is an open space, framed on either side by the church walls that curve inwards to focus attention on the altar. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30743}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30745}{0}{}{The front row of pews (n)}{ }{The front row of pews has an excellent view of the black and white hoof-shaped altar that stands before a huge stained-glass window at the front of the church.  There is an open space between the front pews and the altar, framed by the walls that curve in on either side.  The rows of pews stretch out towards the rear of the church to the east, occupied only by a few praying cows. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30743}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30746}{0}{}{An open space before the altar. (w,e)}{ }{The walls on either side of the church curve inwards around the open space to frame the altar and draw attention towards it.  The stone floor lining the area is heavily scuffed, from shuffling or writhing hooves no doubt.  Beams of light in a huge array of colors emanate from the wall-sized stained-glass window behind the altar. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30743}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30747}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43977}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43978}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30747}{0}{}{At the altar (e)}{ }{The black and white, hoof-shaped altar stands directly before the huge stained-glass window which glows with a radiant light.  A quiet sense of holy power seems to emanate from the altar, as if it were not a thing crafted by cows, but by the hooves of some omnipotent force.  The splotches of black and white marble making up the altar seem to pulse with light and darkness, but it is more a thing felt than seen, as if the two were struggling for dominance. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30746}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43979}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30748}{0}{}{The Northern end of Church Street (s,n,e,nw,ne)}{ }{Church Street reaches its northernmost point, ending at the doors of a large, imposing building painted entirely in blue.  Small paths lead past the building on either side, one leading northwest through a stone archway, one leading northeast into a thicket of plants, and another snaking eastward into the trees.  As with the rest of Church Street, this section is surrounded by trees which sway gently in a light breeze. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30726}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30751}{n}{open door;n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30752}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30753}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30754}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30749}{0}{<138>}{-()- The CowVille general store -()- (w)}{<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>}{Filled with shelves, the store has a friendly atmosphere that seems to encourage spending.  At the far end of the store from the door is the counter where purchases are made.  The windows and door are constructed of a bright yellow glass.  The sun shines through the glass giving the room a yellow tint. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{shop}{1.000}{1}
E {30726}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30750}{0}{}{The Branding Salon (e)}{ }{A dimly-lit, seedy little salon that claims to be the home of "The Latest thing in Personal Styling", but is really just a branding salon.  It's been done to cows for years free of charge, but now somebody is trying to convince gullible customers to pay.  The windows facing Church Street are blacked out, and only a sliver of light creeps under the door.  Bare light bulbs hang from the ceiling giving off a dim glow, and with the flames from the firepit, it provides the room with enough light to make out the notice on the wall. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30726}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30751}{0}{}{The CowVille police station (s)}{ }{Painted entirely in a bright blue, this building is none other than the CowVille police station.  A few posters are scattered around the walls that mostly look old and tattered, and a desk stands in the middle of the room, used for processing of criminals. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30748}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30752}{0}{}{an isolated restaurant (ne,w,e)}{ }{The forest thins to reveal an isolated restaurant and the glimpse of open water through the trees.  Beneath a swaying sign declaring the building to be La Mucca, is a red door painted with an emblem of a fish.  The building itself is small and quaint with a terracotta tiled roof and red-checkered curtains gathered to frame the sides of the windows. }{Cowville Moofia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30748}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30766}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30759}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30753}{0}{}{A calm graveyard (nw,se)}{ }{The sound of leafless trees rustling can be heard echoing around the graveyard, strangely soothing on the nerves.  The caw of a crow fills the air momentarily, a poignant reminder of the surroundings.  The moo-n can be seen clearly in the sky, hanging low over CowVille.  The archway leading out of the graveyard lies to the southeast, through which the north end of Church street beckons. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30748}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30768}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30754}{0}{}{A little garden hideaway (sw)}{ }{Surrounded by a dense thicket of trees, bushes and flowering plants is a small fountain, flanked by a couple of stone benches.  The air is damp and cool, and the plants block the sounds of CowVille.  This would be a great place to sit and relax for a time, simply enjoying the day. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30748}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30755}{4104}{}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {30725}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30704}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30756}{0}{}{A doctor's office (s)}{ }{Glaring whiteness fills the room, projected from a multitude of lights situated all over the small office, and reflecting off the white floor, ceiling and walls.  In one corner of the room, a small white chair sits behind a clean, white desk.  Opposite the desk is a small (white) sofa, and against the other wall is a thin bed, also white.  Everything looks extraordinarily clean. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30715}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30757}{0}{}{A reception (e)}{ }{Soft moosic fills the reception, soothing away the unease of anybody who comes to wait for the doctor.  You can't see any receptionist behind the large desk lining the west wall, nor are there any patients sitting on the chairs which surround the room.  The one exit from the room is eastward out to the hallway. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30715}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30758}{0}{}{Cowville Wharf (n,s,sw)}{ }{The wharf juts northward out into the sea, as if trying to reclaim the land with wooden poles and planking.  A thick lip of wood forms an edge next to the deep water and also helps to support a number of mooring posts.  A large, two-storied warehouse lines the dockside, with the first floor dominated by a huge roller door.  A single window on the second story casts its eye across the water. }{Cowville Moofia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30763}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30761}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30764}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30759}{0}{}{La Mucca (w,s)}{ }{Scattered in the room, beneath the watchful eye of a long bar, are round tables covered in crisp white linen and their accompanying wooden chairs.  Over each table is a pendant light, collectively drooping from the ceiling like teats on an udder. They provide enough light to eat by while still keeping the room in a semi-dark state.  Decorating the walls are framed posters of Italian harlots romping through Tuscan vineyards. }{Cowville Moofia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30752}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30760}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30760}{0}{}{La Mucca Kitchen (n)}{ }{The restaurant's kitchen is an explosion of wood and stainless steel.  A heavy butcher's block takes its morbid pride of place in the center, forming an island of wood.  Hanging directly above this bench is a wrought iron pot hanger, which is shaped like a fish and adorned with hooks.  On the outer walls are gas cookers, shelving and a large double-doored steel fridge. }{Cowville Moofia}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30759}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30761}{0}{}{Cowville Wharf (s,board)}{B}{The Cowville Wharf is weather-worn and rather old, but quite solid.  It is built from the trunks of the huge trees found all around Cowville, and has stood strong against many storms.  There is a small bell mounted on a pole, presumably to call a boat of some kind. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30758}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30762}{board}{board}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {30762}{0}{}{HMS Pasture (exit)}{ }{       Painted a gleaming green, the HMS Pasture is a small but sturdy passenger craft, only recently finished and commissioned.  Her route takes her between the Cowville wharf and the tropical Isle of Cows, a popular holiday destination for those cows looking to get away from it all.  Several lines of black and white cushioned seats are available to relax on during the trip, shaded by a matching canvas roof, leaving the sides of the ship open except for the safety rail. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30761}{exit}{exit}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43749}{board}{board}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

