R {30829}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* The Street of a Dozen Dreams *\x7D=- (nw,s)}{<278>[ ]<088>}{Stepping quietly on the loose pieces of mortar and stone of this street you listen for signs of life and hardly surprisingly, you detect none at all.  Any living thing with any common sense avoids this place.  Just off the street, the detritus of demolished buildings wait patiently for the original inhabitants to return and repair the devastated mess.  It is difficult to see your footing, as small creeping vines and grasses run over the waste rocks and timbers.  The forest comes right to the edge of the rubble.   }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
