R {31393}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* The Street of Sorrows *\x7D=- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{A small movement in some shrubs in the distance catches your eye.  You pause in the middle of the street and wish you could just disappear into the small rocks and hide.  If you wait out here in the open much longer your wish may come true.  This street defines the southeast border of the city.  On the east side of the street, the ruins of largely intact larger dwellings hold back the forests, while on the west side similar dwellings block access to an overgrown parkland.  It is very quiet.  Small weeds poke through the steps, stairs and ornamentation of the ruined buildings.  Just off to the sides of the street, bigger buildings that are almost intact pay silent testimony to the dreadful devastation that took place here. }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
