R {31394}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* The Street of Sorrows *\x7D=- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{This street defines the southeast border of the city.  On the east side of the street, the ruins of largely intact larger dwellings hold back the forests, while on the west side similar dwellings block access to an overgrown parkland.  A small movement in some shrubs in the distance catches your eye.  You pause in the middle of the street and wish you could just disappear into the cobblestones and hide.  If you wait out here in the open much longer your wish may come true.  By the street, bigger buildings that are almost intact hide both treasures beyond the imagination and unimaginable death.  It is unnerving, as small creeping vines and grasses run over the buildings. }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
