R {31410}{0}{<238>}{Tilver's Dam (sw,u,n)}{<238>^ ^<088>}{The banks rise steeply up from the creek to the city above.  Tangled brush obscures your view of what's overhead in the city.  Dark water in the stream moves past the gravel of the bank.  You are at a stone slab dam.  Constructed by a human engineer several centuries ago, the dam forces the stream to widen into an ornamental lake to the south.  The water rushes over the slabs from the lake, and continues its way northward through the parkland.  Access to the parkland above the banks of the stream is provided by a small path up to the east.   }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
