R {31451}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Bloors Street *\x7D=- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{It is hard to imagine, but there is not a living thing in sight.  Just off to the sides of the street, blasted bits and pieces of former buildings pay silent testimony to the dreadful devastation that took place here.  You watch the high towers in the distance for signs of predators as you proceed cautiously down this street made of dense rubble. }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30838}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {31452}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {31452}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* Bloors Street *\x7D=- (n,s)}{<278> | <088>}{Stepping quietly on the loose pieces of mortar and stone of this street you listen for signs of life and hardly surprisingly, you detect none at all.  Any living thing with any common sense avoids this place.  It is difficult to see your footing, as small creeping vines and grasses run over the waste rocks and timbers.  To the sides of the street, smashed and burnt pieces of homes and shops pay silent testimony to the dreadful devastation that took place here. }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {31451}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {31033}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {31453}{0}{<178>}{iIiIi Castle Jumbee iIiIi (s)}{<278>###<088>}{Here on the grounds to the northeast of Castle Jumbee, you look at the many towers and spires rising up from the massive walls.  There seems to be an entrance further south. }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {31029}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {31454}{0}{<178>}{iIiIi Castle Jumbee iIiIi (w)}{<278>###<088>}{In the southeast corner of the castle grounds, you survey the huge citadel.  Massive stone walls support a host of crenellated spires.  From your current vantage point you count seven massive towers connected together by the walls.  The castle appears to be largely intact, and on the battlements high above, you see dark forms moving furtively between the stones. }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {31029}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {31455}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* A lane *\x7D=- (ne,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{Following the course of a stream to the west, this small lane leads off into parkland dotted with smaller white stone buildings.  You watch the high towers in the distance for signs of predators as you proceed cautiously down this lane made of uneven worn dirt.  It is difficult to see approaching danger, as taller grasses obscure the approaches to the lower buildings.  To the sides of the lane, bigger buildings that are almost intact pay silent testimony to the dreadful devastation that took place here. }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {31009}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {31456}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {31456}{0}{<278>}{-=\x7B* A lane *\x7D=- (sw)}{<278>- -<088>}{Just off the lane, large houses and buildings in serious disrepair wait patiently for the original inhabitants to return and repair the devastated mess.  It is impossible to check the houses at a distance, as thick shrubs obscure the entrances, windows and holes of buildings.  Following the course of a stream to the west, this small lane leads off to the south into parkland dotted with smaller white stone buildings.  Far across the parkland to the north and through the trees, you can make out other buildings and the wall of forest beyond them.   }{Murus Faralain 2.0}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {31455}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

