R {32509}{0}{<238>}{An intersection in the garage (ne,w,s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This intersection in the garage appears to be where the gang mechanics work on the vehicles used to conduct lightning fast hit and run raids on opponent bases and equipment caches.  The floor is covered with all manner of tools and mechanical parts that seem to be strewn in no organised arrangement.  A damaged speeder in mid repair is propped up against the east wall.  The garage continues to the west, south and northeast. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32508}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32511}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32512}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32510}{0}{<238>}{A corner in the garage (n,e)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This corner of the garage appears to be where the gang mechanics work on the arsenal of weapons and other equipment used by the scavengers.  Like the rest of the garage, the floor is covered with parts and tools.  A sturdy workbench lies in the corner that appears to have seen a great deal of use.  The garage continues to the north and east. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32508}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32511}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32511}{0}{<238>}{A corner in the garage (w,n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This corner of the garage is surprisingly clean in comparison to the mess that covers the majority of it.  The equipment in this section appears to be more medical than mechanical.  You'd guess that this is a makeshift hospital but that doesn't seem to be the answer either.  A few tables stand against the wall covered in a variety of supplies and implements.  The garage continues to the north and west. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32510}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32509}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32512}{0}{<238>}{A tunnel in the garage (sw,e)}{<238>] [<088>}{This tunnel has been dug surprisingly wide, presumably to allow large vehicles access to the garage and repair facilities to the southwest.  The wood panelled walls are as unfurnished and bare as you would expect from an access tunnel such as this.  It would appear that there is a large entrance bay to the east that must serve as a vehicle egress point. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32509}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32513}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32513}{0}{<238>}{A vehicle entrance bay (out,w)}{<238>[<228>O<238>]<088>}{An enormous blast door dominates the entirety of the eastern wall and is presumably how vehicles enter and exit the garage.  A sleek looking motorcycle is parked in the middle of the room beside a heavily armoured hovercraft.  It appears that here under the swamps the gang must be prepared to engage the enemy both on land and on the water.  Three open lockers stand against the north wall with a security camera just above them, watching your every move. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32512}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {638}{out}{touch open;out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32514}{0}{<268>}{A hallway in the hideout (w,ne)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The stark steel of the walls, ceiling and floor seems to be never-ending.  On the east wall is a small green arrow pointing northeast and the words 'Elevator: All Floors'.  The paint is old and flecked, suggesting that the sign is from a bygone era when this building had an entirely different use.  The lights on the walls that guide your exploration flicker on and off occasionally, summoning your own shadow to dance with you as you delve deeper into the hideout. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32506}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32517}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32515}{0}{<238>}{A featureless supply room (e)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The featureless steel walls of this supply room have nothing to cover them and only serve as resting places for various shelves.  Boxes and crates overflow with junk, clothing and equipment that seems of little or no use to you.  It smells dank and oppressive in here and it looks like rats have begun to nibble away at the bottom of several of the boxes. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32506}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32516}{0}{<268>}{A hallway in the hideout (nw,s,n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The sound of chanting in a language you have never heard floats toward your ear from the north and echoes gently off the walls until it disappears into the air.  Coupled with the uncanny force that you feel inhabits the depths of the base you find the chanting extremely unnerving.  The lights continue to flicker gently on the walls and the shadows that you previously ignored seem increasingly ominous. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32506}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32519}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32520}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32517}{0}{<278>}{A hallway in the hideout (stairway,sw)}{<278>.@.<088>}{The stark steel of the building ends here at a dead-end in the hallway.  On the north wall is a small green sign that reads 'Elevator: All Floors' over a pair of sliding doors.  In the east wall is a smaller doorway that you presume gives access to the stairs.  An uncanny force emanates from deeper in the building and lures you with its siren song. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32514}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32518}{stairway}{stairway}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32518}{push down button}{push down button}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32518}{d}{push down button}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32518}{0}{<278>}{A hallway in the hideout (stairway,w)}{<278>.@.<088>}{There is a definite presence in these halls and it's something very powerful.  A chanting from deeper in the base magnifies the sense that you are in a place that mingles the ancient with the modern, the gris-gris with the gun.  On the north wall is a small green sign that reads 'Elevator: All Floors' over a pair of sliding doors.  In the east wall is a smaller doorway that you presume gives access to the stairs. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32517}{u}{push up}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32517}{push up}{push up}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32523}{stairway}{stairway}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32524}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32519}{0}{<238>}{A well-stocked armory (w,se)}{<238>] [<088>}{Gun racks line each of the four walls in preparation for rapid deployment.  Each rack is covered with a black metal grating to ensure that no equipment gets misplaced or stolen.  From a quick survey of the armaments in this room you calculate that there is enough to equip an army, never mind a gang.  With an arsenal this size it is easy to see how the gang became so influential in the area.  The armory appears to extend to the west. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32516}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32522}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32520}{0}{<238>}{A heavily defended entryway (n,s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{What greets you in this room is a bizarre juxtaposition of technology and voodoo culture.  A security camera beeps and whirs in the northeast corner of the ceiling next to a detailed lithograph.  The chanting in the next room seems to grow louder and you wonder what awaits you there.  On the floor next to the western wall lies a pile of animal skins and furs that look out of place for some reason. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32516}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32521}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32521}{0}{<138>}{A macabre throne room (s)}{<138>[ ]<088>}{Dark chanting and the rhythmic beating of drums floats through the dim gloom of this chamber but its source is unknown.  While it may be coming from this very room it seems more likely that the sound is drifting to your ear from piping or a hidden vent leading deeper into the base.  The north wall is covered by an enormous lithograph that appears to be the symbol of whoever sits on the bone throne in the middle of the room.  The steel walls found throughout the base have been painted over in this chamber and replaced with garish murals and obscure symbols. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32520}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {42471}{enter hole}{enter hole}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {42471}{n}{enter hole}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32522}{0}{<238>}{A well-stocked armory (e)}{<238>] [<088>}{Armour racks line each of the four walls in preparation for rapid deployment.  Each rack is covered with a black metal grating to ensure that no equipment gets misplaced or stolen.  There appears to be a rack for each member of the gang so that they can modify and tinker with their own armour.  The weapons racking is located in the armory to the east and a large window looks out into packed dirt to the west. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32519}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32523}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}

R {32524}{0}{<268>}{A hallway in the hideout (e,nw,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The steel walls of the building are less visible here as they are increasingly painted over with vast swirls of colour.  A rhythmic chanting echoes through the hallway accompanied by the steady beating of ceremonial drums.  Your baser instincts are telling you to leave now but a nagging curiousity toys with you, tempting you to stay.  A small figure hangs by piano wire from the ceiling. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32518}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32525}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32526}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32525}{0}{<268>}{A hallway in the hideout (s,se,n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The steel walls of the building are less visible here as they are increasingly painted over with vast swirls of colour.  A faint mist seeps down the hall from the north and an eerie chanting resonates through the base from the south.  A large symbol has been painted with painstaking detail across the floor of this hallway. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32524}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32539}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32540}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32526}{0}{<268>}{A hallway in the hideout (w,s,n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The hallway reaches an intersection here, branching off to the west or continuing to the source of the chanting coming from the south.  A small terminal is fixed to the east wall under one of the standard light fittings.  It looks like an old information point from the time long ago when this building had an entirely different purpose.  Sadly it appears that it has been broken for decades. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32524}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32527}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32528}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32527}{0}{<268>}{An empty hallway in the hideout (e,w)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{This part of the hallway seems well used but devoid of any major distinguishing characteristics.  Footprints in the thin layer of dust covering the floor run east to west and vice versa.  The walls are splashed with rich lashings of red and black paint, giving the hallway a eerie and lonely feel to it.  A little bag that you presume to be a gris-gris hangs on the south wall. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32526}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32534}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32528}{0}{<268>}{A bend in the hallway (se,n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The hallway bends here towards the southeast where the sound of chanting appears to emanate.  The steel walls of the building are less visible here as they are increasingly painted over with the gang's colours, red and black.  In a few places the paint has chipped slightly and is peeling off to reveal what appears to be an old logo of some kind, possibly the emblem of the corporation that once used this building. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32526}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32529}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32529}{0}{<268>}{A bend in the hallway (nw,e)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The hallway continues to bend here, turning towards the east.  A call like you have never felt seems to pull you down this hallway, drawing you like a moth to a flame.  For the first time you notice something entirely new about the strange sense of power surging within these halls - it is benevolent.  A large symbol has been painted with painstaking detail across the floor of this hallway. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32528}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32530}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32530}{0}{<268>}{A fork in the hallway (w,ne,se)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{A fork in the hallway leaves you with two choices.  You could follow the call of your heart and continue to the northeast or investigate the girlish giggling sound you hear coming from the southeast.  There is a definite sense of spirituality in this part of the building that juxtaposes oddly with its solid steel structure. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32529}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32531}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32532}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32531}{0}{<268>}{A bend in the hallway (n,sw)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The chanting has reached a crescendo in this room and draws your soul to the north, leaving your body racing to catch up.  It feels like every move you've made inside this building was leading up to this moment and this place in time.  A sign on the wall might provide a hint to what lies before you, but a soothing voice in the back of your mind tells you to follow your heart and not your senses. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32530}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32533}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32532}{0}{<268>}{An old office, now a shrine (nw)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{This old office has long been converted into a shrine to Eshu Elegua, the trickster loa.  It is a place where a hounsis, or apprentice voodoo priestess can study, train and meditate in peace.  The focus of the shrine is a battered old filing cabinet with a small statue atop it and open drawers full of offerings for the loa.  A bed lies in the northeast corner of the room with an an old locker next to it overflowing with an assortment of skulls.  Of all the oddities in the room it is the window in the east wall that surprises you the most.  A giggling sound seems to be coming from the statue, but maybe it's just in your head. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32530}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32533}{0}{<268>}{A quiet, serene hounfour (s)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{Upon entrance into this room you feel an overpowering sense of belonging, as if you had finally returned home.  A poteau-mitan stands precisely in the center of the room, forming a focal point for voodoo magic and for the hounfour itself.  Reagents and symbols overflow from a small shelf on the western wall.  A thin red carpet connects the poteau-mitan with a candle-covered altar at the north end of the room. On the back wall a series of concentric nesting hearts have been drawn in deep red, giving a warmth and charm to the room.  Perhaps surprisingly for an underground building there is a window in the east wall. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32531}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32534}{0}{<268>}{A crossroads in the hideout (e,w,s,n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The metallic gleam of the steel building is less visible in this part of the hallway due to the richly daubed red and black paint that adorns the walls.  In a few places the paint has chipped slightly and is peeling off to reveal what appears to be an old logo of some kind, possibly the emblem of the corporation that once used this building.  You hear chuckles and the clatter of rolling die from the south while soft whispers and a soothing voice drifts to your ear from the west. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32527}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32535}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32536}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32537}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32535}{0}{<268>}{An old office, now a shrine (e)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{This old room looks like it once might have been the office of a junior partner in the firm.  Now it appears to be a shrine to the loa Papa Ghede, the eternal figure in black.  It is a place where a hounsis, or apprentice voodoo priest can study, train and meditate in peace.  The room is less cluttered than you expected, forcing your perspective to focus on a desk against the south wall.  It appears to be some kind of altar with a statue as the centrepiece ringed by lit candles. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32534}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32536}{0}{<268>}{An old filing room, now a shrine (n)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{This old filing room has long been converted into a shrine to the loa known as Lady Luck.  It is a place where a hounsis, or apprentice voodoo priest can study, train and meditate in peace.  The walls are ringed with filing cabinets that once must have overflowed with papers and documents but now they are full of dice, playing cards, horseshoes and rabbit feet.  In the center of the room is a desk that has been converted into an altar and the focal point for the shrine.  A window in the south wall seems out of place in such a reliquary but as you recall the former purpose of this building it all becomes clear. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32534}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32537}{0}{<268>}{An intersection in the hideout (nw,e,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The hallway reaches an intersection here, branching off to the northwest or continuing south and east.  A small terminal is fixed to the north wall under one of the standard light fittings.  It appears to be an old information access point, a relic from the bygone age when this building served an entirely different function.  Sadly it appears that its connection to the building's power supply has been severed and the screen remains black and lifeless. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32534}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32538}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32539}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32538}{0}{<268>}{A once dead-end (w,se)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The steel walls of the building are less visible here as they are increasingly painted over with vast swirls of colour.  To the west it appears that a window in the outer wall once existed but it has now been knocked through to extend the hallway out into the earth.  A large symbol has been painted with painstaking detail across the floor. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32537}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32543}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32539}{0}{<268>}{A corner in the hideout (w,n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{Sounds bounce eerily off the walls of this corner and echo merrily down the hallway until they are lost in the distance.  The smell of myrrh and cinnamon drifts into your nostrils from sticks of incense fixed to the walls.  The heady scent mixed with such unearthly noises creates a claustrophobic atomosphere, almost as if the walls were closing in on you. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32537}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32525}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32540}{0}{<268>}{A corner in the hallway (e,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The mist coming from this hallway is gradually increasing in density but is still no more than a few wisps here and there.  What is most odd is that you can hear the sound of a bird squawking coming from the east.  The north wall is covered with an expansive mural depicting an enormous alligator locked in a battle to the death with a burly human. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32525}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32541}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32541}{0}{<268>}{A bend in the hallway (w,se)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The mist coming from this hallway is gradually increasing in density and is now enough to form a light fog that obscures your vision somewhat.  Squawks and roars that were previously quiet enough to be your overactive imagination can now be confirmed as real, and coming from the southeast.  A sign on the wall may provide a clue to what awaits you in the next room while a large symbol has been painted flawlessly across the floor. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32540}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32542}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32542}{0}{<238>}{A gloomy, humid room (nw)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{What strikes you most as you enter this dank room is the humidity.  Glancing around through the murk you see an assortment of cages lining the walls and a veritable jungle of plants growing from the dirt-covered floor.  A loud squawk rings throughout the room from an unseen bird and several large figures seem to loom through the mist.  In the far corner of the room you can barely make out a large pool encased in thick bars. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32541}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32543}{0}{<238>}{A dug out hallway (w,e)}{<238>] [<088>}{This hallway has been extended from the original limitations of the building in order to expand the size of the base without descending into the lower floors.  The earth that surrounds you is held at bay by the wood panelled walls and ceiling of the hallway.  It would appear that this particular tunnel provides access to a large excavated cavern to the west. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32538}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32544}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32544}{0}{<248>}{A carved out cavern (e,s,n)}{<248>% %<088>}{This cavern appears to have been carved out of the earth in order to accommodate an enormous cage.  The enclosure itself has been built on a three foot high base of concrete with steps leading up to a single door that serves as its only entrance and exit point.  A walkway leads around the cage to the north and south, providing access to a number of vantage points from where you could view the action taking place inside. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32543}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32545}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32546}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
