R {32551}{0}{<248>}{A carved out cavern (w,e)}{<248>% %<088>}{This cavern appears to have been carved out of the earth in order to accommodate an enormous cage.  The enclosure itself has been built on a three foot high base of unforgiving concrete.  An old wooden bench rests against the south wall providing some respite for either someone watching the fight or a tired combatant.  From here the walkway continues to the east and west. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32550}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32545}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32552}{0}{<248>}{The Bosou Pit (out)}{<248># #<088>}{Dedicated to the brutal loa Bosou, this cage is where members of the gang gather to train in hand-to-hand combat.  Hanging from the ceiling bars of the cage is an effigy of the loa himself.  His appearance is of a man with three horns, each representing a trait of the spirit\; strength, wildness and violence.  He stares down upon the combatants in the cage with grim approval as blood is spilt and bones are broken. The floor of the cage is solid concrete, not the standard matting that you would've anticipated.  If you take a fall in here, it's going to hurt almost as much as the hit that took you down.  It is only a matter of time before your blood joins the spatters and puddles that adorn the floor. }{Voodoo Scavengers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32544}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32544}{e}{out}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32553}{0}{<238>}{Entrance to power plant (leave,w,e,n)}{<238>[<228>L<238>]<088>}{You enter what looks to be the ruins of a fission reactor power plant widely used in the past century. From all the rubble laying about you can only conclude something must have gone wrong. There is an overturned desk here, and broken surveillance monitors are strewn about. Under the desk, you see a green puddle. There are security doors that have been ripped from their hinges to both the east and west. There looks to be more destruction to the north. }{Ruined Reactor}{ruined_reactor}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {696}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32554}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32555}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32556}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32554}{0}{<238>}{West corridor (e,n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{You find nothing but more destruction here. On the walls are smashed instruments and gauges. Rubble litters the floor. Broken conduit and wires dangle from what is left of the ceiling. In places, the bright sun shines through cracks and holes in the thick concrete making it possible to see, as well as displaying the massive damage this structure has experienced. To the north there looks to be a control console of some kind. To the east, through a smashed security door, is the entryway. }{Ruined Reactor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32553}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32558}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32555}{0}{<238>}{East corridor (n,w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The reinforced concrete ceiling has caved in here. The sunlight streams in illuminating the center of the room making it hard to see into the dark corners. Destroyed steam pipes lay on the floor with the rubble from the ceiling. To the north you can make out what looks to be a steam turbine and generator. West is the entrance to the building. }{Ruined Reactor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32553}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32557}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32556}{0}{<238>}{Reactor access room (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The corridor ends here. Looking through the shattered viewing windows, you can see the total destruction of the reactor core. The ten foot thick concrete walls have been obliterated into piles of rubble. Near one of the exposed fuel rods you catch a glimpse of movement, but it might have been the radiation playing tricks on you. On the wall there is a switch marked, "Danger - Radiation". To the south is the entrance to the building. }{Ruined Reactor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32553}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32557}{0}{<238>}{Turbine room (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This end of the building is dark compared to the sunlight streaming in down the corridor. There is a large turbine here that was once turned by the steam released from the reactor. The turbine turned the generator that once supplied nearby cities with power. The equipment is twisted and wrecked beyond any repair. }{Ruined Reactor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32555}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32558}{0}{<238>}{Control console (s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{Before you is a vast array of incomprehensible gauges and switches. Before the destruction this must have been where the workers monitored and controlled the workings of the reactor. Laying on the console is a rectangular black box that seems to be fairly intact. }{Ruined Reactor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32554}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32559}{0}{<228>}{A quiet swamp (ne,path)}{<228>;<238>P<228>;<238>}{You feel the noise of the swamp and distant road recede behind you as you walk up this peaceful trail.  An occasional bird flies past, landing briefly on a branch sticking out from the swamp, before taking off again. A small, slightly drier trail leads northeast through a wet bog. }{A Quiet Swamp}{quiet_swamp}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {627}{path}{path}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32560}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32560}{0}{<228>}{A wet bog (n,sw)}{<228>; ;<088>}{As you follow the dry path along, you notice the ground surrounding you getting wetter and generally more liquid\; you wouldn't even risk stepping off this path now.  However, the path stretching across the bog seems firm and secure enough. }{A Quiet Swamp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32559}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32561}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32561}{0}{<228>}{End of the path (s)}{<228>; ;<088>}{Here the path finally succumbs to the rising water level in the bog\; the width of dry land gradually gets smaller and smaller until continuing would force you off into the bog itself, where you'd be sucked down to drown.  The bog is looking wetter than ever, but you still wouldn't risk trying to swim in it. }{A Quiet Swamp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
