R {32616}{0}{<238>}{Devlin's Office (n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{You're in a simple office.  A large desk is the main item of interest in the room, and a leather chair sits behind it.  A steel filing cabinet sits in one corner, and the walls are plastered with maps, charts and reports.  A waste paper bin sits next to the desk, and a coat rack with a jacket sitting on it is by the doorway.  }{The Amazon Research Center}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32615}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32617}{0}{<238>}{A crumbling building (out)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{You've squeezed past the precariously hanging door and entered the half destroyed building.  From the wreckage all about, you can at best guess that this was some sort of  routing office.  Several metal desks rust slowly away, but defy time by simply still standing.  Chairs seem to have not been so lucky in their bid to survive, lying rotting and worm eaten on the floor.  The filing cabinets that covered the  back wall seem to have long ago lost their contents, and now  litter the floor or lean against one another like so much scrap metal. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14503}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14503}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32618}{0}{<238>}{The officers club (out)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{As you step through the door you know that you've come to the wrong place.  This isn't the dilapidated building it  appears to be from the outside.  It is in fact, a working  bar of sorts.  The interior is fairly clean, and definitely populated.  It looks like the Air Force moved out and left  the place to a gang of some sort, because these folks  certainly aren't boy scouts. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14506}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14506}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32619}{0}{<238>}{The base of the control tower (u,n)}{<238>] [<088>}{You've entered the bottom of the base's control tower.  A stairway circles the interior of the tower.  Amazingly, the tower is otherwise empty, just a few conduits of wires which run from the upper levels down the walls and into the ground. You kinda thought there'd be more to it than this. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14507}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32638}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32620}{0}{<238>}{A kennel (out)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{Passing into the fenced in area, you get the distinct smell  telling you that some animals have been or are currently being kept here.  Small paddocks line the central corridor, but each of them seems to have had the gates removed to let whatever's living here roam free. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14508}{e}{out}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {14508}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32621}{0}{<238>}{An enormous hangar (w,s,n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{You've entered what has to be the largest hangar you've ever heard of, let alone seen.  The roof hangs more than 50 feet  over head.  There are crates piled about, gathering dust  while waiting to be unpacked.  The entire east side of the  hangar is a sliding door, allowing the giant aircraft once serviced here to enter. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14509}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
