R {32623}{0}{<238>}{An old hangar (e,w,s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{This corner of the hangar appears to be cleaner than the rest.  The crates are pushed farther back into the hangar, and the floor is clear of debris before the giant hangar  doors.  The doors are partially open, looking out over the desolate wasteland beyond. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32621}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32625}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32627}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32624}{0}{<238>}{An old hangar (e,n)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{In this back corner of the hangar, you notice many newly deposited oil soaked rags.  A few cutting torches and even a few welding devices. Whoever's set up shop here after the military left is obviously planning on staying, that type of equipment you don't just carry around.  Wonder who would need such heavy duty equipment? }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32622}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32626}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32625}{0}{<238>}{An old hangar (e,w,s)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The walls along this sections of the hangar are piled high with crates and boxes.  Most of the crates seem to be empty though you can't really be sure about all of them.  The rest of the hangar appears to be empty space, the center cleared out for something rather large to come inside.  And from the looks of things, you figure that the people who did the cleaning probably don't want you here.  You notice that high above you, a steel catwalk runs the length of the hangar. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32622}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32626}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32623}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32626}{0}{<238>}{An old hangar (s,e)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{The northwest corner of an old hangar.  The walls are mostly hidden by wooden crates in various states of unpacking.  Some appear to have become tables and chairs for the current inhabitants of the base.  The markings on the crates have been marred beyond readability, so you can't possibly guess what was in them.  High overhead there's a small catwalk, though you can't see any way of getting to it from here. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32624}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32625}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32627}{0}{<278>}{A runway (w,e,plane)}{<108>|<178>:<108>|<088>}{Outside the enormous hangar, the total desolation of the  land comes back to you full force.  The runway shimmers in  the perpetual heat of the badlands, even though it is pock  marked and next to useless.  The enormous wreckage of a  Galaxy transport lies across the runway just to the south. Further to the east you can make out the other runway of the air base.  It too seems to be cluttered with the wreckage of several aircraft.  Back to the west the towering doors of the hangar stand slightly open. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32623}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32628}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32629}{plane}{plane}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32629}{s}{plane}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32628}{0}{<228>}{The midfield (w,e,s)}{<228>, `<088>}{Your feet sink into the mud up to your ankles.  The grass is very misleading in the solidness of the ground.  To either side, about 400 feet apart, the runways run parallel to the  midfield.  As you glance down the runways, you notice yet  another wreckage, in addition to the two which clutter the  head of the runways. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32627}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32630}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32631}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32629}{0}{<268>}{A wrecked Galaxy transport (u,out)}{<168>[<238>O<168>]<088>}{You stand inside the cargo bay of the Galaxy transport. From the looks of things, this plane could hold several transport trucks easily.  The hold appears to be empty, simply littered with debris such as fallen paneling and tangled wiring.  There's a small set of stairs leading up to either the cockpit or some other area above the cargo area. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32636}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32627}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32627}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32630}{0}{<278>}{A runway (plane,w)}{<108>|<178>:<108>|<088>}{Here on the far side of the landing field, the winds off the badlands have taken their toll, blasting the hull of the wrecked plane clean of any paint or markings and leaving the runways covered with dust.  The quagmire of a midfield lies just west of you, between the two runways.  The hulking wreck of the Galaxy transport lies silent in the distance. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32628}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32632}{plane}{plane}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32632}{s}{plane}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32631}{0}{<228>}{The midfield (s,n)}{<228>, `<088>}{You sink into the mud up to your ankles.  The ground here is very misleading in the solidness of the ground.  To either side, about 400 feet apart, the runways run parallel to the  midfield.  You stand abreast the plane wrecks on either side of you.  The third plane wreck is still further downfield on the second, furthest runway. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32628}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32633}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32632}{0}{<268>}{The wreckage of a plane (s,out)}{<168>[<238>O<168>]<088>}{This appears to be a mid sized passenger plane, probably  used by the government to ferry about minor government  officials.  This is the passenger cabin, filled with 4 rows  of seats, about thirty seats in all.  The interior has  suffered greatly the elements, most of its windows shattered and allowing the searing winds from the badlands to tear  through the cabin. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32635}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32630}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32630}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32633}{0}{<228>}{The midfield (plane,n)}{<228>, `<088>}{The mud clings to your feet here, trying to suck you down further.  The runways shimmer in the heat close by.  The  plane immediately east of you is a small craft, similar to the corporate Lear jets of the late twentieth century.  To the south, the grass seems to give way to pure mud, and appears impassable. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32631}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32634}{plane}{plane}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32634}{s}{plane}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32634}{0}{}{The Wreckage of a plane (out)}{ }{You appear to have entered a small jet, similar to those used by corporate executives or high ranking government  officials.  The fire wall between the cockpit and the  passenger compartment has been bent out of the way, leaving a clear view of the entire plane.  There are only 3 seats and a couch besides the pilot's and co-pilot's seats.  The galley seems to have been completely destroyed, glass littering the floor. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32633}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32633}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32635}{0}{<268>}{Cockpit of a plane (n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{You've entered the cockpit of the wrecked plane.  The  instrument panels seem to have survived most of the punishing weather intact, though their markings have long since been scoured off by the dust and grit carried by the winds.  This room is lightly dusted with dirt, but seems relatively clear of debris. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32632}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32636}{0}{<268>}{A wrecked Galaxy transport (d,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{This upper level seems to be a passenger area of some sort. Tattered seats remain bolted down to the floor here, their attempt at upholstery tattered and ripped.  Anything that  wasn't bolted down has since slid to the cargo bay below,  leaving the area relatively clean.  A short stairway leads to what can only be the cockpit of the aircraft. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32629}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32637}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32637}{0}{<268>}{The cockpit of a Galaxy transport (n)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{You've found the cockpit of the transport.  Most of the instruments and dials are cracked or shattered, leaving the floor covered with plastic fragments and glass.  The four  command chairs have been ravaged by the weather with the  absence of the windows.  Even now you can feel the winds  whipping in from the badlands. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32636}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32638}{0}{<238>}{A control tower (u,d)}{<238>] [<088>}{You stand about mid way up the stairs of the control tower. The stairs disappear through the floor above into what you  can only assume to be the flight control center.  You notice the conduits of cables running down from above, and notice  that one set is severed just below the ceiling. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32619}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {32639}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32639}{0}{}{Top of a control tower (d)}{ }{You've climbed to the top of the control tower.  The massive banks of displays and gauges is amazingly intact.  The huge windows which stretch nearly the entire height of the room  are obviously made of something other than glass, because  they show little damage other than the random spattering of bullet holes where someone tried to get through them. }{Air Force Base}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {32638}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32640}{0}{<238>}{The subway (e)}{<238>. .<088>}{The tunnel's west part stops abruptedly here, blocked by a huge amount of rubble. It looks like the bombs destroyed most of the subway after all. To the east you can go back to the entrance.  }{Collapsed Subway}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14518}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32641}{0}{<238>}{The subway (w)}{<238>. .<088>}{You are in the subway's east part, and further travel is totally impossible due to the massive rubble that blocks your path. On the walls you can see a large poster, partially torn apart.  }{Collapsed Subway}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14518}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {32642}{0}{<278>}{Compound Courtyard (w,e,n,s)}{<278>. .<088>}{You are standing in the middle of a large courtyard that forms the entrance to this strange compound. The ground is covered with little pebbles and stones, and there are many tire tracks and footprints in the soil. To the south you can see the entrance to this compound and to the north is a very large dark building. }{GenCorps}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14528}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
