R {33973}{0}{<268>}{A chapel (s)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{Compared to the simplicity of the other rooms, this one seems like it belongs in a palace.  Tapestries draped around the room cover the walls. You assume the walls are stone like the others in the Temple.  Lights from the time before the war shine dimly here with a soft illumination. The room is fairly crowded with oak pews setting in east-west rows, providing room for probably thirty worshippers to gather here before the Priests. What attracts your attention the most is the altar that rests a few feet before the north wall.  The scent of incense lingers in the air from a previous ceremony. }{Temple of Syrinx}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
