R {34157}{0}{}{The Tabard Inn (leave)}{ }{    You lightly shake off the rain as you step into the main room of     this small inn. The room is crowded with many travelers gathered     around a large table. The travelers are drinking ale and talking     amongst themselves and do not notice you. The soft glow from the     fireplace makes the room appear warm and cozy. There is an inn-      keeper behind a small desk in one corner and a sign is tacked on     the wall above the desk and a menu below it. There is also a         gold placard hanging on the wall.                                }{The Tabard Inn}{tabard_inn}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34146}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34158}{0}{<228>}{Green Angel Tower bell-tower (w,e,n,d,s,portal)}{<228>]<158>P<228>[<088>}{You stand in a bell-tower, consisting of a shiny white stone floor with a set of stairs leading down in the centre. The stairs are made of the same white stone as the floor. Although the tower stretches up another near hundred cubits, tapering to the Angel herself, the staircase ends here where the great bronze bells hang row after row from the vaulted rafters like solemn green fruit. The bell-tower is open on all sides to the air, so that when Green Angel's chimes sing from its high arched windows, the whole countryside might hear. Six pillars of dark smooth, rock-solid wood span from floor to ceiling. }{The Dragonbone Chair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
