R {34159}{0}{<228>}{Green Angel Tower bell-tower (e)}{<228>] [<088>}{From here, you can look out upon the waters of the Kynslagh as it rolls eternally against the Hayholt's massive sea wall. Many small boats ride the Kynslagh's swells, with lake men in black cloaks bent stolidly over their oars. }{The Dragonbone Chair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34158}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34160}{0}{<228>}{Green Angel Tower bell-tower (w)}{<228>] [<088>}{You have entered a small balcony that overlooks part of the keep and some of the land around it. Looking out towards the Thrithings, you can see a land filled with grassy plains and rolling hills. The occasional craggy mountain breaks up the greenery. What a beautiful view it is from here. }{The Dragonbone Chair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34158}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34161}{0}{<228>}{Green Angel Tower bell-tower (s)}{<228>] [<088>}{A low stone railing protects you from falling over the edge of the balcony you now stand on. Looking out, you can see part of a keep. Further northwards you can see the greenery of the Aldheorte Forest, a place which is reputed to be haunted. There is little hunting done in it, and few are willing to enter its leafy domain. }{The Dragonbone Chair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34158}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34162}{0}{<228>}{Green Angel Tower (d,u)}{<228>] [<088>}{These narrow steps are made of a clean, smooth white stone, unlike any other in the castle, slippery to the touch but sure beneath one's feet. The stone facing on the inside of the stairwell is different from those down below: a soft fawn colour, traced across with minute, puzzling designs in sky blue. A window lets the sunlight shine in upon the stairs, giving them an almost magical look. }{The Dragonbone Chair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
