R {34287}{0}{<108>}{Behind the curtain (s,e)}{<108>[ ]<088>}{You find yourself on the darkened stage of the opera house.  The shadows of props and scenery blend into the near darkness of the stage.  Off to the side you see a brighter area, off stage where the actors dress and prepare. }{Phantom of the Opera}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34286}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34288}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34288}{0}{<238>}{Backstage (n,w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{You stand just off stage in the hall to the dressing rooms.  The  gas lamps here are turned up to light the area fairly well.  The  hall is fairly short, having only a few rooms off of it.  The  majority of the hall seems to be used for the minor actors and  members of the chorus to change, not giving them the privacy that  the leading actors and actresses are given. }{Phantom of the Opera}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34287}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34289}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34289}{0}{<268>}{The back hall (w,n,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{A short hall which has a few doors off of it.  The space is  cluttered with racks of garments to costume the performers.  In  fact, several of the chorus girls are here changing into costume  now.  A small wooden door is closed to the west. }{Phantom of the Opera}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34288}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34290}{w}{open door;w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34291}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34290}{0}{<238>}{A dressing room (e)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{A small sparsely decorated room.  A small table littered with makeup hunches against one wall, a small mirror hung above it.  Two chairs are in the room, one at the table and another off to the side of the door.  A small privacy screen walls off one corner of the room. }{Phantom of the Opera}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34289}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34291}{0}{<268>}{The back hall (e,s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{The short hall ends here.  A small door is closed to the east, and  several more garment racks are scattered about the room.  People  seem to be shying away from this area of the theatre, as if something  about it should be avoided. }{Phantom of the Opera}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34289}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34292}{e}{open door;e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34292}{0}{<238>}{A dressing room (w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{A small dressing room.  A small table is nestled into one corner  of the room, its surface cluttered with makeup and other things.  Two small chairs sit near the table, both within reach of it.  A  small privacy screen sits in another corner of the room.  The most  striking thing you notice about this room is the large mirror on  the far wall. }{Phantom of the Opera}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34291}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34299}{mirror}{mirror}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34293}{0}{}{The upper hall (ne,w,nw)}{ }{Shadows dance eerily on the walls, cast by the chandeliers which  hang down to the main hall.  The carpet silences your tread, adding  to the strangeness of the hall.  The sculpted railing stands about  waist high, overlooking the main hall below.  The private boxes can  be reached from here, some of the best seats in the house. }{Phantom of the Opera}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34282}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
