R {34294}{0}{}{A twisting passage (ne,nw)}{1}{A small twisting passage between the walls of the opera house.   Apparently these were built in by the architect, since there's no  way they could have been added later.  The biggest problem seems to  be that you have no earthly idea which way you're going now, or how  to get out. }{Phantom of the Opera}{1}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34296}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34297}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34295}{0}{}{A private box (sw)}{ }{The seats in this private box offer an amazing view of the stage.   There are eight plush chairs set in two rows.  The box hangs out  over the seats below, yet has been built so that people cannot see  into it except from the stage or far across the theatre.  Two round  pillars stand on either side of the box, running up through the  ceiling, presumably to support the roof in some way.  A small shelf  runs along the front of the box.  Curtains hang in the back of the  box that can be pulled closed once the show starts. }{Phantom of the Opera}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34293}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

