R {34588}{0}{<228>}{(*) Vidarian Wilds (*) (w,nw)}{<228>* *<088>}{The forested jungle starts to subside.  The trees begin to be more separated and less concentrated.  The rays of the moon shine down here more than ever.  You start to almost get a clear glimpse of the alien sky.  The brush however, is still ever present, blocking any traveling in certain directions, but even this small relief of trees and their roots is most welcome. }{Vidaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34587}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34590}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34589}{0}{<228>}{(*) Vidarian Wilds (*) (n)}{<228>* *<088>}{You enter a cove of trees, and within the center lies one much smaller than its fellow brethren.  A yellow moss-looking growth covers the floor of the jungle.  Looking upward, the leafy foliage of the trees ignites in small explosions of light.  If you didn't know any better, you would think you were admist some holiday celebration. }{Vidaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34587}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34590}{0}{<228>}{(*) Vidarian Wilds (*) (e,w,s,n,se)}{<228>* *<088>}{Finally breaking out into the open, you find yourself in a wide open valley.  The heat beating on top of you is almost unbearable, and the cover of trees looks rather inviting.  The grass upon the ground is still and unmoving, as no signs of a relieving wind are forthcoming.  Westward the valley drops off at a large stone jutting from the earth. }{Vidaria}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
