R {34818}{0}{}{Secret area (out)}{ }{    You are standing in a secret room made completely of stone. The only thing in the room is a fountain which provides both light and healing rays. An exit leads back to the forest. This would be a good place to sit for a while. }{Dead or Alive 3}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34816}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34819}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}

R {34820}{0}{}{A Blurry Vision}{ }{You are standing on a hellish, desolate landscape. Pools of lava emit heat at you from all directions. Something here causes your vision to become blurry and you see trails of motion whenever something moves. The ground is cracked earth, so dry that you wonder if it has ever rained. }{Dead or Alive 3}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34798}{end game}{end game}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34821}{0}{}{-=  100 Aker Woods  =- (out,n)}{O}{-=  100 Aker Woods  =- This is the entrance to 100 Aker Woods, home of Winnie the Pooh and all his friends.  A cool breeze wisps through the air as you walk under a canopy of weeping willow trees.  Tall, green grass lightly sways back and forth, leading into the forest.  }{Winnie the Pooh}{winnie_the_pooh}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {6503}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34822}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34822}{0}{}{-=  A beautiful forest  =- (s,n)}{ }{-=  A beautiful forest  =- Thick trees blanket the forest, cutting off most of the sky above. The beauty of the forest sets your mind at ease.  The trees sway gently back and forth in the breeze.  All around the sounds of the forest and its inhabitants can be heard. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34821}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34823}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34823}{0}{}{-=  A beautiful forest  =- (e,s)}{ }{-=  A beautiful forest  =- The only activity is the whisper of the wind blowing through the trees.  A well-worn path leads either deeper into the forest or back out to safer ground.  A number of brown and gray pebbles lay along the path.  Occassionally, a small chipmunk scurries along the side of the path in search of food. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34822}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34824}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34824}{0}{}{-=  A path  =- (e,w)}{ }{-=  A path  =- The path through the forest leads both east and west.  A babbling brook flows under a small nature-made bridge.  Years of use have weakened this part of the path, making it a risky venture.  There is smoke billowing out of a chimney to the east. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34823}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34825}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34825}{0}{}{-=  Kanga and Roo's House  =- (e,w)}{ }{-=  Kanga and Roo's House  =- Puffs of smoke billow out of the chimney of this quaint house. It is a small house made of stone and wood.  A small mailbox sits directly on top of a bigger one.  One is marked Roo, the other marked Kanga.  A straw welcome mat sits in front of a red door.  A little rose bush brightens up the dirt yard.  The path continues to the east further into the forest or west, out. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34824}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34826}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34826}{0}{}{-=  A path  =- (n,w)}{ }{-=  A path  =- The path continues north into the forest.  A few rays of sunshine break through the pine trees here.  A woodpecker is busy making a home for himself in a large oak tree.  The back of Kanga's house can be seen from here.  Large puffs of smoke stream out onto the path. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34825}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34827}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34827}{0}{}{-=  A path  =- (n,s)}{ }{-=  A path  =- The pines begin to thin out in this part of the forest.  More green moss and a few vines drape from some oak trees on the right side of the path.  The ground becomes softer and cooler as the hard dirt turns to sand, northward. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34826}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34828}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34828}{0}{}{-=  A sandlot  =- (n,s)}{ }{-=  A sandlot  =- A large hole in the ground makes for difficult navigation here.  This appears to be a sandlot for a small child.  Small pine cones, acorns and twigs are being used as toys.  You resist the urge to take off your shoes and squish the sand between your toes.  The forest grows thicker to the north and is less dense to the south. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34827}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34829}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34829}{0}{}{-=  A forest  =- (n,s)}{ }{-=  A forest  =- The path seems to have disappeared in this part of the forest.  The pines have become very dense and numerous.  Tree roots crowd the forest path, making it difficult to navigate.  It takes a few moments for any light to make its way into this area. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34828}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34830}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34830}{0}{}{-=  Deep into a forest  =- (n,s)}{ }{-=  Deep into a forest  =- THUD!  You smack into a tree as you continue deeper into the dark forest.  While you should be a little wary of your surroundings, you feel pleasantly at ease here.  A small squirrel darts across the forest, making eerie noises. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34829}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34831}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34831}{0}{}{-=  A forest  =- (s,n,w)}{ }{-=  A forest  =- The forest here is not as dense as other parts of 100 Aker Woods.  The path continues west, north and south.  A large tree looms up ahead and the outline of a small house is visible to the west. Bright yellow wildflowers dot the forest path.  The way out of the woods lies to the south. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34830}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34832}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34833}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34832}{0}{}{-=  Christopher Robin's Tree  =- (s)}{ }{-=  Christopher Robin's Tree  =- You have reached the place where Christopher Robin likes to play quietly and read.  It is a large tree with a branch that stretches out far.  A rope with a knot tied at the bottom of it hangs from the branch.  A book and broken kite is on the ground. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34831}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34833}{0}{}{-=  P-P-Piglet's House  =- (w,e)}{ }{-=  P-P-Piglet's House  =- A very small house stands before you.  A small mailbox with the name P-P-Piglet painted on it stands in the front yard.  Small colorful flowers surround the house.  A miniature wooden swing sits in front of a window.  More forest leads off to the west. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34831}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34834}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34834}{0}{}{-=  A forest path  =- (w,e)}{ }{-=  A forest path  =- The forest path becomes visible again here.  A flurry of butterflies gather here, soaking up the sun that makes its way through the trees.  A fallen tree lends itself to hundreds of bugs and mosses.  You inhale deeply as you smell sweet honeysuckles up in the distance. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34833}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34835}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34835}{0}{}{-=  A forest path  =- (w,e)}{ }{-=  A forest path  =- The forest again begins to thin out here.  Several large rocks line the path.  A few purple flowers have sprung up between the rocks and trees.  More sunlight is visible here and the breeze is refreshing.  The path continues to the west. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34834}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34836}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34836}{0}{}{-=  A clearing  =- (w,e)}{ }{-=  A clearing  =- You come upon a large clearing.  The forest is now behind you and the beginning of a lovely meadow lies ahead.  A few tall oak trees sit to your right and left as you enjoy the walk in the open air.  You are finally able to enjoy the immense blue sky and large puffy clouds. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34835}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34837}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34837}{0}{}{-=  A meadow  =- (n,w,e)}{ }{-=  A meadow  =- A beautiful meadow spans the horizon.  Tall swaying grass beckons you. Large shadows float along the ground as low hanging clouds pass by.  A huge oak tree lies ahead.  You could continue to follow the path west or head north towards the darkening sky. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34836}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34838}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
