R {34858}{0}{}{-=  A forest  =- (s,n)}{ }{-=  A forest  =- You continue through the forest.  There isn't much here except some trees and some rocks.  The forest clears out to the south and another oak tree in the distance urges you to continue in that direction. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34857}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34860}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34859}{0}{}{-=  Owl's Howse  =- (d)}{ }{-=  Owl's Howse  =- You reach the top of the tree and discover Owl's Howse.  Owl is supposedly the smartest of all the creatures in 100 Aker Woods, but you have to wonder as you get a look at the sign in front.  The w in owl is backwards and house is spelled wrong.  The house is made from wood and a little red door adorns the front. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34857}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34860}{0}{}{-=  Winnie the Pooh's House  =- (n,s,in)}{I}{-=  Winnie the Pooh's House  =- You finally have found what you have been looking for, it's Pooh's House.  The house itself is set in a large oak tree.  An arched wood door with a little bell over it sits in the base of the tree.  A small sign hangs above the door. }{Winnie the Pooh}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34858}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34861}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
