R {34883}{0}{}{Covenant's Cabin (e)}{ }{You are in a small dark cabin\; the only light into the interior is from a small window over a desk to your right and the open door to your back.  The bed, floor, and walls are covered in a thick coating of some red material that looks suspiciously like blood.  The smell is overwhelming\; like that of a slaughterhouse. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34880}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {41754}{w}{turn doorknob;w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34884}{0}{}{A Corral (e)}{ }{You enter the corral overcome by nostalgia.  The memory of better days before the coming of the nerve-deadening, limb-destroying illness blur your eyesight.  Shaking your head, you notice the grass and weeds growing up out of the ground and festooning the corral gate and the fence.  You shrug.  The past is dead. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34881}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {41755}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

