R {34900}{0}{}{Revival Tent (w,e)}{ }{As you enter the tent you are immediately overwhelmed by the noise, heat, and oppressive atmosphere.  One to two hundred people are jammed in here, shouting, waving their hands, dancing in the aisles, and rolling on the floor frothing at the mouth.  The eeriness of people screaming in strange tongues makes you duck your head.  You can barely make out the evangelist on the platform over the waving hands of the braindead citizens of Lytton County! }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34898}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34903}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34901}{0}{}{County Park (w,e)}{ }{You find yourself in the middle of a small RV park.  A second RV vehicle, this one smaller but built like a tank, sits sandwiched between the RV to the west and a big truck to the east.  No one seems to be around. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34899}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34902}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34902}{0}{}{County Park (w)}{ }{You find yourself at the end of a small RV park.  A long truck is here, covered with banners celebrating the revival and its 'great' healer.  The back gate of the truck is down. To the west is the strange, nondescript RV.  To the east you see a thicket so dense that nothing mansized could possibly get through. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34901}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34903}{0}{}{Revival Tent (e,n)}{ }{As you continue to edge your way around to the side of the tent the noise, heat, and oppressive atmosphere become even more intent. One to two hundred people are jammed in here, shouting, waving their hands, dancing in the aisles, and rolling on the floor frothing at the mouth.  The eeriness of people screaming in strange tongues makes you duck your head.  You can barely make out the evangelist on the platform over the waving hands. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34900}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34904}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34904}{0}{}{Revival Tent (s,e)}{ }{You have now made your way almost completely around the tent. Your head is swimming from the noise and the odor of sweat and fear and blind and baseless hope.  You can now see a path open through the screaming throng to the platform upon which Sam Johnson, the evangelist, is holding court.  The old woman is gone.  And you realize, with a start, that all eyes are now turned towards you.  Whispers come to you through the din: `It's him!  That's the leper'!  You stumble as one particularly obnoxious singer's rendition of some song or another nearly tears your head off.  You move towards the platform. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34903}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34905}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34905}{0}{}{Revival Tent (w)}{ }{As you stumble on to the platform, the whole world seems to move in slow motion.  No one at this celebration of brotherly love seems very overjoyed to see you here.  The tent, that seemed so big a moment ago, has shrunk to a tiny point of confrontation. Sam, the Evangelist moves toward you.  His face contorts as he presents a triumphant smile to the marks, while scowling angrily at you. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34904}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34906}{0}{}{County Highway (s,n,w)}{ }{You are walking along a narrow, two-lane, paved but patched blacktop road running north to south.  The lines down the middle are barely visible.  Far to the north you make out the outline of a small New England village.  To the west you see a blinking neon sign and a gravel road leading towards a big, long roadhouse.  To the south, the road continues on eventually disappearing into a dense forest. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34893}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34907}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
