R {34909}{0}{}{Road House (w,e)}{ }{You've moved through the small and sparsely populated parking lot and are now at the entrance, a large green door, illuminated by nothing but a bare lightbulb.  There is a small sign by the door. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34908}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34910}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34910}{0}{}{Road House (n,w,e)}{ }{You enter a dark, smoky room.  There are small tables scattered around a stage to the northwest.  You catch a glimpse of the singer through the smoke and haze.  The bar is to the north, which may explain why The Door stinks like 7-day-old beer. A drunk trucker holds court (with himself) at one of the tables. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34909}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34911}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
