R {34911}{0}{<238>}{The Roadhouse Bar (s)}{<238>[P]<088>}{You've bellied up to the bar.  As you can see, the choices are extremely limited.  This place is near bankruptcy and now tends to attract only the most serious of drinkers.  Take a look at the menu and try to ignore the sloppy drunk. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{pub}{1.000}{1}
E {34910}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34912}{0}{}{Road House (n,e)}{ }{You make your way through the smoke-thick air, coughing and gagging on the stench of stale tobacco and old beer.  This is not a high-end of the scale joint. As you gag on the smoke, you are suddenly confronted by a Deputy Sheriff! }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34910}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {34913}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34913}{0}{}{Road House (s)}{ }{This is a dive!  A stage is just ahead, a dim spotlight shining on the postage stamp-sized stage.  Empty tables are scattered about, repelling you with their stains and ratty appearance. As you near the stage, you get your first good look of the singer.  She isn't bad.  And she sings pretty well.  Wonder how the sleeze Sheriff conned her into this gig? }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34912}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {34914}{0}{}{County Highway (n,s)}{ }{You are walking along a narrow, two-lane, paved but patched blacktop road running north to south.  The lines down the middle are barely visible.  To the north you see an intersection that marks the beginning of the town.  Just ahead a faded green road sign leans drunkenly to the east.  The road continues to the south, eventually disappearing into a dense forest. As you continue your walk to town, a screaming siren begins to wail behind you.  You look over your shoulder just as the sheriff's car cuts in front of you and screeches to a stop.  The sheriff steps out, swaggers toward you, and plants himself in front of you. }{The Chronicles of Thomas Covenant}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
