R {35344}{0}{<278>}{North Central Tencho (n,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{You keep walking along the road and crest a small hill in the center of town.  To the east is a small Shinto/Buddhist shrine and the rest of the area is taken up by the markets, though they seem oddly empty.  Even the few things up for sale seem somehow dull  and lifeless as if something had sucked the soul out of them.  What could possibly do such a thing?  Surely it must be a great evil. There is something strange about that booth over there, maybe you should take a look?  There's also a sign tacked to the booth. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35323}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35345}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35345}{0}{<278>}{North Tencho (e,s)}{<278>- -<088>}{The road curves off to the east here and back to the south.  Over the bamboo wall you can see Mt. Fuji rising up sharply, dominating the northern horizon.  A little ways up the slope you can see a small Japanese castle.  Wonder how one gets to the castle?  From the stout wall to the west a feeling of evil rolls over you, but you can not see its source.  Perhaps if you went the other way around you  might be able to find it.  There's a sign tacked up to the thick  bamboo wall. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35344}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35346}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35346}{0}{<278>}{NE Tencho Road (e,w)}{<278>- -<088>}{This road runs east along the northern wall.  To the south are some larger buildings.  Mt. Fuji still dominates the northern horizon.  The sense of oppression is a lot less in this part of town.  Maybe the great kami has driven the gloom away?  Who knows, but you certainly feel a lot better.  There is a clean sign here on the wall. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35345}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35347}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35347}{0}{<278>}{NE Tencho (shop,w,s)}{<278>. .<088>}{You stand at the Northeast corner of Tencho.  On the corner is a nice quiet looking shop.  An older, wise-looking man meditates behind the counter.  Perhaps he can answer some questions for you? The road curves south here and goes back to the west.  Further to the south the over spirit of the village seems to be a little bit lighter and there are actually people moving around without fear. Maybe it has something to do with the red-armoured sword-wearing fellows with the serious expressions wandering about this section. There is a sign posted on a wall of the shop. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35346}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35348}{shop}{shop}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35349}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35348}{n}{shop}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35348}{0}{<138>}{Tencho Shop (out)}{<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>}{You have walked into a Haven of Peace and Serenity.  The walls of this small shop are plain white pine, polished to a satin-smooth finish and lightly stained.  A man is seated behind the counter meditating peacefully.  If you need help he will stop to help you otherwise he looks quite content where he is. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35347}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35347}{s}{out}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35349}{0}{<278>}{Samurai Lane (s,n,alley)}{<278>- -<088>}{The road here goes north and south while a somewhat cleaner alley leads off to the west between two large buildings.  The people  are walking around here openly.  Even smiling and joking, they seem to have no fear.  Even the birds are chirping here.  In all it seems very peaceful and quiet here despite the bustle of activity.  There is a large sign posted here and a picture hangs on a nearby wall. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35347}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35351}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35352}{alley}{alley}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35352}{w}{alley}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35350}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {35351}{0}{<278>}{East Tencho (s,n)}{<278>- -<088>}{You are walking further along the East Tencho Road which continues to the north and to the south.  This part of town is made up of  many small shops and businesses jammed together under the eaves of the larger family residences.  People are moving around constantly and occasionally stopping to make way for some dignitary or other repectable person.  There is a sign posted on a wall here. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35349}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35354}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35352}{0}{<248>}{Samurai Alley (out)}{<248>. .<088>}{You are standing in a fairly clean alley. The cobblestones are actually visible and the garbage is neatly stored in cedar boxes that give off a pleasing aroma. There appears to be a symbol of some kind painted on the back wall of this alley.  }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35692}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35349}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35349}{e}{out}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35353}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {35354}{0}{<278>}{SE Tencho (w,n)}{<278>- -<088>}{The road through town curves north here and also curves west.  Again these are the homes of the more affluent of Tencho's great families.  This section seems to have re-acquired some of the gloom of the western portion of town, though not as bad.  The people here still walk around openly, though they do occasionally dart nervous glances to the west and keep moving.  There is slightly singed sign attached to a singed wall. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35351}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35355}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35355}{0}{<278>}{Dark Lane (alley,e)}{<278>- -<088>}{You have walked into a darker section of town.  Here the buildings seem to loom over you, casting their shadows on the street and  completely engulfing the alley to the north.  You occasionally  think you see movement out of one corner of your eye, but when you turn to look at it there's nothing there.  Probably just imagining  it.  There is a plain white sign posted at the mouth of the alley. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35354}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35356}{alley}{alley}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35356}{n}{alley}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35356}{0}{<248>}{Ninja Alley (out)}{<248>. .<088>}{Even with a good source of light this alley is still very dark. Trash is scattered everywhere and you can sometimes hear the  sounds of rats scurrying through the garbage.  There are a few large crates shoved up against the back of the alley, but  otherwise is little of note. }{Mortal Kombat}{brucelee}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35358}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35355}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35355}{s}{out}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35357}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {35358}{0}{}{Entrance, Ninja Base (e,u)}{ }{You are standing in a small room occupied by a single small table, with two chairs. The room itself has been painted black, unbroken except for the mark of the Lin Kuei on one wall. You appear to have stumbled onto the headquarters of the Lin Kuei, and the guards are eyeing you suspiciously. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35356}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35359}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35359}{0}{}{Lin Kuei Barracks (ne,w)}{ }{Like the entrance to the ninja's hideout, this room is all black  in color with the Heron symbol of the Lin-Kuei on the ceiling. The rest of this room is occupied by several bunked cots and a longer  table with several rickety wooden chairs around it. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35358}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35366}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35360}{0}{<268>}{A small chamber (s)}{<268>[ ]<088>}{You've found your way into a small chamber at the back of the  temple.  Three small candles light the spartan room, sending  small threads of smoke towards the ceiling.  A sleeping pallet  is wedged into the room, taking up at least a third of the floor  space.  A ragged reed rug covers the floor before a low table  holding an incense bowl. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35340}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35361}{0}{}{Yakuza Lobby (n,u)}{ }{You have entered a very nicely appointed room that would appear to be a lobby of some sort.  Nice oil paintings hang on the walls with gorgeous tapestries between them.  The floor is covered with a thick and beautifully woven persian rug.  There are several wonderfully carved wooden chairs, end tables and sofas with red coverings over them.  The room is so rich you almost miss the large wooden door to the north. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35330}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35362}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35362}{0}{}{Yak Barracks (e,s)}{ }{You've walked into a nice, comfortable room with a cozy fireplace. There are also several cushy looking bunkbeds lined up against the walls here as well as some very cushiony sofas and chairs.  A  small coffee table sits in front of the largest sofa and an ornate chandelier hangs from the ceiling.  A little gaudy but certainly  a nice enough place to live.  There's a wooden door to the south  an iron-barred door to the east from which the occasional moaning sound can be heard. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35361}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35363}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35363}{0}{}{Torture Room (n,w)}{ }{Wow what a change from the first two rooms.  This room has all the trappings of a torture chamber.  An iron maiden in one corner and thumbscrews on a table along with a rack in the corner.  There is also a blazing fire in the middle that looks just right for heating up some pokers to red-hot and branding some poor soul.  No wonder you were hearing moans, moans of pain.  There is a steel door north and the cell door opens to the west. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35362}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35364}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35364}{0}{}{Guard Room (w,s)}{ }{Like the first two rooms of this place this room is very nicely appointed.  Luxurious, yet tasteful.  The only real furniture in here are some wooden chairs and one coffee table.  Otherwise the only noticable items are the weapons displayed on the wall.  You notice that nothing in here is breakable or valuable enough to worry about being damaged.  There's a carved wooden door west that is similar to the one at the entrance and includes a black dragon. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35363}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35365}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35365}{0}{}{Yakuza Office (e)}{ }{You have walked into what appears to be an office of some kind. The large mahogany desk towards the back kind of gives it away. Like the rest of the place this office is very well furnished with the absolute best.  Several chairs surround a longish wooden table and several candelabra light up the room like daylight.  You begin to get nervous when the big man behind the desk gives you a long stare.  Maybe you shouldn't be here? }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35364}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35366}{0}{}{Practice Room (se,sw)}{ }{This room is decorated like the rest of the headquarters in basic black with the Heron mark, but the rest of it is made up of a maze of sliding, shifting panels and other obstacles used for practicing the art of ninjitsu.  The shredded portions of some of the panels attest to the sharpness of the blades they use.  You get the feeling that you'd best watch your step in here.  The door to the southeast  has a large symbol of some kind carved into it. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35359}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35367}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35367}{0}{}{An office in the ninja base (sw,nw)}{ }{You have walked into a room that seems vastly out of place in this subterranean base.  Richly decorated with deep red velvet tapestries and a solid mahogany desk.  There's even a large  chandelier dangling from the ceiling.  This rooms seems out of place for the rest of this subterranean area. }{Mortal Kombat}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35366}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35368}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35368}{0}{}{Prison (ne)}{ }{As you turn on your light you recoil in disgust at the condition  of this small prison cell.  It's absolutely filthy and the stench  is incredible.  The scuttling of rats can be heard and you can some times see them scamper across the floor.  The remains of some poor soul lie in one corner of the cell and another figure is chained  to the wall in the opposite corner. }{Mortal Kombat}{brucelee}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35367}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35369}{0}{}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {34735}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35370}{0}{<228>}{-= A small opening in the forest =- (n)}{<228>( *<088>}{-= A small opening in the forest =- You are standing in front of a tree about eight or nine hundred feet tall.  This tree is so tall you can't even see the top of it from where you are standing.  Many branches sprout from the base of the tree making it hard to walk around in this room.  You can hear birds chirping from above you.  The immediate area has been filled with this tree making it quite cramped.  You better watch where you walk or you'll end up with more than a few scrapes from the branches.  You could very easily sprain your ankle or knock yourself out on of of the roots sticking up from the ground. }{Talbo's Forest Home}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {34601}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35373}{climb branches}{climb branches}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
