R {35579}{0}{}{A deep and dark cave (sw,out,nw)}{ }{       The sound of the wind whistling through these deep caves can be heard distinctly at this cave mouth.  The strong wind blowing south through the forest gets caught on the lip and redirects down into the caves.  A layer of frost has built up on the dirt walls, and logs and bushes have been setup to conceal the cave entrance.  From this mouth the cave descends in both the northwest and southwest directions.  The smell of torch oil and soot flows upward from the caves. }{Mount Perplexus}{mt_perplexus}{}{}{1.000}{1}
