R {35590}{0}{}{A deep and dark cave (sw,se,nw)}{ }{      The majority of the western wall along this long corridor consists of a huge boulder, forever embedded within the mountain.  The hall is very wide, but filled with smoky haze.  This section of corridor is curved towards the northwest and southeast, and is very dark, as light from the burning cauldrons cannot reach around the bend.  A slimmer branch tunnel leads toward the southwest. }{Mount Perplexus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35589}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35607}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
