R {35609}{0}{}{A deep and dark cave (nw)}{ }{         This large room is designed to feed an army.  Large pits are lined with stone and each contains a blazing fire.  Over each pit is a steel grill used for cooking.  Barrels of dried meats and other foods are shoved against the wall, each with bits of dirt that have crumbled and fell off the wall.  Small ventilation holes have been burrowed into the ceiling, allowing the smoke and soot from the fires to escape, yet still leaving the kitchen at an uncomfortably warm temperature.  Several cooks hover over each pit, as the kitchen goes through continual food preparation to feed the army within the caves. }{Mount Perplexus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35608}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35610}{0}{}{A deep and dark cave (ne)}{ }{       Rows of wooden benches sit against long wooden tables in this large dining hall.  Barrels of burning oil heat the hall and provide minimal light, each strategically placed in the corners of the hall.  The ceiling is burrowed upward in the shape of a cone, with a dark gaping hole at the peak.  Smoke and soot from the burning barrels travel upwards through the ventilation hole, providing an escape for the haze. }{Mount Perplexus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35608}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35611}{0}{}{A deep and dark cave (w,e)}{ }{      A smoky haze fills this dirt tunnel leading east and west through darkness.  An eerie howling wind can be heard far to the east, and the faint sounds of soldiers echo off the dirt walls.  The tunnel is very dark, but wide enough for several men to walk abreast.  Fires from burning cauldrons can be seen down both ends of the hall, but their light is too faint to reach this section of the tunnel. }{Mount Perplexus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
