R {35658}{0}{}{Trudging through the underbrush (e)}{ }{     The trampled trail through the underbrush comes to an end here, surrounding you on all sides with awful, glistening prickers and otherwise unfriendly plant life.  You can return back to the east, where you can see the large bushes that lead back to the happy fields.  A large log impedes any further progress through the underbrush. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35657}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35659}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {35660}{0}{}{On a small trail (n,se)}{ }{    You are walking along a narrow trail of trampled underbrush, surrounded by nasty, prickly underbrush on all sides.  The trail appears to end a bit to the north.  You can hear noises in the near distance, probably animals moving around, startled at your presence. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35657}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35661}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35661}{0}{}{On a small trail (u,s)}{ }{    It appears that this is the end of the small trail you have been following, since underbrush flanks you on either side, and a large tree stands in front of you.  You might want to turn back and head toward the clean sanctity of the grass fields. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35660}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35662}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35662}{0}{}{Up a Tree (d,u)}{ }{       You are standing on a fairly large, sturdy branch of a tall oak tree.  At about fifteen feet off the ground, you have a pretty good view over the underbrush around you of the grassy fields somewhat southeast of here.  You can see a small hill rising from the level meadows at the north end of the fields, and you see a mirror floating a few feet off the ground at the southern end of the fields.  Above you, you can see the rest of the tall, healthy oak tree, with a couple large branches somewhat out of reach. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35661}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52409}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35663}{0}{}{In a dark basement (u)}{ }{   You are crouching in a stuffy hole under a dirty shed.  This place was probably dug to store things in a cool, lightless environment -- for storing potatoes or similar things. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35654}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

