R {35676}{0}{}{Inside the hill (w)}{S}{     This sloppy room must be a kobold guard barracks!  You can see stacks of disgusting, grimy, moldy mattresses piled along bunks on the walls and a couple on the floor, amid tons of garbage and smelly kobold underclothes! This place reeks of sweat and of kobold alcohol.  You better get out of here before one of the kobold brigade returns to find you here! }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35674}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35677}{0}{}{Kobold Hatchery (se,n)}{ }{    You stumble into a somewhat wider room, which you first mistake as a simple extension of the cavern passages.  However, a few steps farther in, you realize this room has another purpose.  The walls on either side are lined with straw, in an evident nest-like compilation. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35675}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35679}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35678}{0}{}{Inside the hill (e)}{ }{     Now this is rather unlike the dirty but usually sound kobold construction that you have seen in the rest of this system of caverns.  There is rubble covering the ground, as if part of the ceiling caved in, although the ceiling appears to be stable.  Most of the rubble lies in a large pile to the west. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35675}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35681}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35679}{0}{}{Damp tunnel (se,nw)}{ }{      The low ceiling drips water on your back as you waddle your way into this part of the cavern.  Both the floor and the air around you has a very damp stale scent, heavily laden with the noisome odors of fecal compost and rotting food.  Choking your bile back into your gut, tears streaming down your face from your stinging eyes, you barely notice that the cavern floor is sloping downward and the walls outward toward the far end of the tunnel. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35677}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35680}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35680}{0}{}{Wet cavern dead-end (nw)}{ }{      You stretch your aching legs as you stumble into this more open area.  The downward-sloping cave floor changes from hard rock, to clay, and then to mud as it meets a dank, murky pool of water which extends to the far wall.  High above you at the far end of the cavern is a round hole, through which you can make out the sky.  The foul odors of rot and fecal decay still assail your senses here. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35679}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35681}{0}{}{Inner Kobold Sanctum (se)}{ }{       Beyond the cleared rubble, the cavern again opens up into a large room, of sorts.  This room's decor is dominated by a statue of a giant weasel, menacing over a large obsidian altar.  Towering over you, the statue of such a cowardly animal makes you want to both run and laugh -- the kobolds have really outdone themselves with their figures of worship, but you're quite afraid your irreverence will get you in more trouble here than you have seen thus far. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35678}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {35682}{climb statue}{climb statue}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {35682}{0}{}{Standing on top of a statue (d)}{ }{      Wow, look at you!  You're teetering precariously at the top of the weasel statue, just above its left eye.  To either side, you can see the crudely-built ridges of a huge stone weasel ear.  Peering over the head as far as you can, you see the snout of the giant statue, and beneath it, the edge of the obsidian altar built into the ground below.  Please be careful that you don't slip -- a fall from this height might very well kill you. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
