R {35687}{0}{}{Inside the hill (enter,w)}{ }{          This end of the cavern has been carved and then carefully sculpted, in much sharper contrast to the rest of this system of caves.  Pillars have been carefully designed in each corner, carved with hideous kobold figures like tiny demons.  In the center of the room, a large throne with points at each end of its short back menaces the silent grins of the two skulls impaled upon it.  The whole room looks and feels important, and absolutely dreadful.  Your only desire is to leave before you meet the kobold that this room was designed to satisfy.  In the wall behind the throne you see a somewhat small entrance hole, flanked by small stations, probably for guards. }{Attrition}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
