R {36120}{0}{}{-=( A dimly lit cave )=- (e)}{ }{    Several small cracks fill the walls of this small cave, allowing in light and fresh air.  The floor is littered with small stones, detritus from the formation of the cracks.  The ceiling is rough and bare, while several small patches of fungus grow on the stone floor. }{Azziruth's Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36118}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36121}{0}{}{-=( A massive stone chamber )=- (w)}{ }{     The walls of this massive stone chamber stretch away into the distance.  The cave is over two hundred feet in diameter, strangely illuminated by the flickering glow of several strange glass spheres that float roughly twenty feet off the floor.  The ceiling of the cave is obscured by rolling clouds, move slowly as if caught by gentle winds. }{Azziruth's Lair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36119}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36122}{0}{}{Dark Sinkhole (u,se)}{ }{    You've stumbled into a small open area that was hidden by loose snow.  A small shaft of light beams down, illuminating this immediate area and showing you the entrance to a cave.  The cave itself is completely dark. From the dim shaft of light, you can see many large tracks in the snow. }{Snowbeast}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36124}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23983}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36123}{0}{}{-The bottom of the well- (u,bucket)}{ }{        This is the bottom of the water well.  There are no obvious ways of getting back up on your own.  The walls are unclimbable and the rope is too wet.  The area is a big circle in shape with about a ten foot diameter.  This is one of the biggest, if not the biggest, ever. Since it is so big, a lot of things can get lost down here.  Looking above, you see a speck of light that makes up the well's entrance. You estimate the top is about one hundred feet high.  There's also a bucket sitting here in the middle of the muck. }{Monte's Well}{montes_well}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4724}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53185}{bucket}{bucket}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36124}{0}{}{Snow Cave (e,nw)}{ }{    The snow here runs red and pink with splashes of dried blood.  Bones litter the ground, and many more are stuck into the walls.  A few frozen organs also inhabit the walls, and a few are actually stuck into the ceiling far above you.  More claw marks are ripped into the sides of the cave. }{Snowbeast}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36122}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {36125}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36125}{0}{}{Snow Cave (d,w)}{ }{      This part of the cave is very cold.  As you look down into the dark hole that spans nearly half of this chamber, a chill feeling of dread creeps up your spine.  Other than the large dark hole in the middle of the floor, this area holds no distinguishing features.  Something seems to draw you to the hole, though.  As you try to peer down into it, gazing into the complete darkness, you sense something.  You sense... movement. }{Snowbeast}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36124}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {36126}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36126}{0}{}{Snowbeast Lair (u)}{ }{     This large chamber is filled with the bones of past victims.  In one corner lies a pile of recent kills.  The carcasses range from mountain tigers to large polar bears.  Splatters of blood, both dried and fresh, line the walls and floor.  Great slash marks also pocket the walls and floor.  The stench of death and decay here is overwhelming. }{Snowbeast}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36125}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

