R {36129}{0}{}{The top of the lighthouse (d)}{ }{       You stand atop the ancient lighthouse, commanding a view of the Wayhaven docks along the northern horizon and the rippling expanse of the sea stretching out to the east and south.  The stone floor and crenellated wall are slick with water, both condensed from the warm air onto the chill stone and from the spray of the surf pounding against the rocks below.  A small wooden hatchway leads down into the lighthouse and keeps out the rain. }{Tower of Fire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {15827}{down}{down}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {15827}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

