R {36395}{0}{}{The alchemist's workroom (n,w)}{C}{      If you thought the living area of the house was a bit messy, this half almost defies description.  There are reagents and unguents piled on top of scrolls and bits of alchemical apparatus, beakers, flasks, clamps, spirit burners and more lie haphazardly atop the workbench.  In a relatively clean section of the workbench stands a largish brown cow. }{Alchemist's House}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36393}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {36396}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36396}{0}{}{Servant's room (s)}{ }{     This room is where Hovis, Zosimus's servant, sleeps.  It is he who obviously tends to the garden, as his room is neat and tidy.  A simple servant's cot sits next to a small table with neatly stacked papers.  There is precious little else here that suggests the room is regularly inhabited. }{Alchemist's House}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36395}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36397}{0}{}{A large cave}{C}{"The cave is clean and dry. The entrance of the cave is to the south. Looking closely, you can see a transparent shield blocking the entrance. There is a crack on the western wall. You might be able to squeeze through it. There is also a large pearl hanging in mid-air near the northern wall."}{Cave}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
