R {36603}{0}{}{West burial chamber (e)}{ }{         You have just entered an ancient burial chamber. You can see that the floor, ceiling and walls are made out of granite but still you feel a bit uncomfortable, probably because this is a dead man's grave. The floor is covered with a half-foot thick layer of dust, and around the sarcophagus that is placed in the middle of the room you can see four braziers filled with long-ago burnt out charcoal. On the walls hang the rotted remains of tapestries and you can see a large statue in the west end of the room that seems to have been placed there to guard the sarcophagus from intruders like you. }{Ruins of an Old City}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
