R {36606}{0}{<268>}{Rocky Tundra (se,nw)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{               You are standing not far off from the base of Trophea's Peak.  Rocks of varying shapes and sizes surround you, all of which seem to have shaken loose (or been thrown from) the peak of the volcano itself.  Legend tells of how the Dragon Queen Trophea birthed her only son, Nussicon, upon this very peak.  When the immortals came down to praise the dragon-child, the denizens of the 9 hells seized the opportunity to engage them in an epic battle for the 7 heavens.  Trophea fled with her newborn child while the good and evil immortals battled on, nearly tearing the mountain down.  It is not clear how the battle ended but there are rumors that the elder gods, of both realms, were not in favor of this conflict and snapped the astral links of all participants.  This sudden shattering of the link between mortal and immortal realms left a permanent rift between the two realities.  It is said that if you ascend the mountain to Trophea's Peak that you, too, could become immortal... }{Desert Palace}{desert_palace}{}{}{1.000}{1}
