R {36621}{0}{<268>}{The Stable (w)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{   A row of holes on the east wall lets in ample sunlight and warm desert  wind. The room is larger than you expected\; the dozen or so horses and camels only take up a third of the total space. }{Desert Palace}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36619}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36622}{0}{<268>}{Kitchen (e)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{      The kitchen is dimly lit. The smell of baking pies and cooking meat  mixed together is surprisingly pleasant. There is a fire set well off to the north end of the kitchen. There are many kettles and pots around the kitchen, some being moved closer to or farther from the fire regularly, apparently to affect the preparation of the food. A counter near the door holds a few heavy mugs. }{Desert Palace}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36619}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36623}{0}{<268>}{Grand Hall (s,n)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{   This is a large hallway leading to the throne room to the south. Large  columns lie on two sides of of the hallway. A door lies on each side  the hallway, but they are closed. A courtyard is to the north. }{Desert Palace}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
