R {36659}{0}{}{At the base of a massive hollow sycamore (out)}{ }{          You are all but awed as the interior of this sycamore opens up above you.  There in the dim expanses of the hollow, flying in all directions, are what must be hundreds of man/birds.  The walls high above are punctuated with holes which act as destinations for the soaring hybrids, ostensibly openings to hollow branches where these bizarre beings must make their quarters.  As the giant sycamore thrusts ever upward, it is shrouded in darkness, such that its conclusion cannot be seen.  Almost forgetting that you are landbound, you notice an oddly polished stump of pitted, petrified wood sprouting up from the ground.  There is a narrow break in the trunk to the east that would permit exit to the cooler, more sane pastures of the western forest. }{Forest of Types}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {20138}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {36662}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

