R {36662}{0}{}{Accipiter's Alcove (e)}{ }{                 A delicately golden glow, as though the sun were sending its rays through lenses of thick amber, covers the walls of this alcove like an ethereal film. The ruddy wood outlining this deeply-set alcove is ancient-looking, as though aged through some artificial means which left it violently withered and cracked.  On the north side of the room, growing out of the wall itself, is a long shelf of solid wood.  Directly beside this vague bed is a peculiarly-shaped perch, also sprouting up from the floor like a mutant stump.  The ground is a very tightly packed surface of completely dry mud, split with veiny cracks in sad, sanguine imitation of the walls which rise from its dusty depths.  Atop the three-pronged perch sits a terribly infirm-looking mutant bird, with the legs of an old hawk and only the vaguest of human suggestions in its frail, irregularly-shaped body and head.  Against the south wall, a very low, slightly slanted desk, itself shaped as a coarse ellipse of wood, is the resting place for several tomes, each monstrously oversized and opened to a specific page.  To the east, you can see the dark, mysteriously lit interior of the sycamore, a cavernous chamber which only hints at the infinite heights above, which from here are but an assumption. }{Forest of Types}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36659}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36663}{0}{<238>}{A small strip of land outside a dense forest (s)}{<238>|||<088>}{      You stand on a narrow strip of land which juts out into the sea around you.  Immediately to the south lies the wall of a great forest, a natural barrier composed of trees, vines and wide leaves of many colors.  An opening in the glade allows passage into the forest proper.  On the north end of the islet is a relatively new-looking dock, its planks of oaken wood bright and unsplintered. }{Forest of Types}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36664}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

