R {36689}{0}{<228>}{The west bank of a circular inlet (ne,n,w,s)}{<228>( *<088>}{        The ground beneath you is unusually damp in this region, as the water from the inlet seems to have saturated it underground.  The inlet itself is colored a serene shade of lavender, dark and shadowed from the blanket of foliage which covers this entire open area.  From having fallen from this living dome, some stray bits of leaf and bracken float atop the surface, still and buoyant. With wood of powdery blue, the trunk of the tree before you is streaked with effervescent swirls of bright white! }{Forest of Types}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
