R {36806}{0}{<238>}{Plains (e,n,w)}{<238>, `<088>}{       Plains The plains look pretty much the same all around you.  The place appears to get enough rain but there still isn't much life around.  You notice some light tracks but you have no idea where they lead.  A slight wind blows across the plains and the grass shimmers slightly.  Further to the west you notice that the plains continue.  There is a huge lake just to the south, turbulent and dark. }{Fantasy}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}

R {36807}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {9009}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36808}{0}{}{Jackalman Den (se,sw)}{ }{     The tunnel widens a bit, and deepens as well.  The piles of excrement you've found throughout the tunnel deepen, as well.  It seems this part of the passage is a toilet, in the sense that the jackalmen are slightly more likely to go here than wherever they're standing at the moment.  A few flies buzz about.  You wave them aside. }{Rocky Hill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36767}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {36809}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36809}{0}{}{Jackalman Den (nw,w,n)}{ }{    The passage splits here, running in three directions.  The southeast side of the tunnel is formed by the side of a giant boulder that is sunk lower in the sand than the others.  You can see tiny patches of blue sky peeking through the rocks overhead. }{Rocky Hill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36808}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {36810}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {36811}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36810}{0}{}{Jackalman Den (se,e)}{ }{     You nearly slip in a pile of jackalman dung as you duck through the passage here.  It's dimmer here than elsewhere in the tunnel, seems to smell just as intensely, and some of the ceiling boulders jut low enough to hit your head if you move too hastily.  All told, it's really unpleasant.  It seems you can go east or southeast from here. }{Rocky Hill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36809}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {36812}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36811}{0}{}{Jackalman Den (s)}{ }{     This dead end in the tunnel seems to be where the jackalmen store their fresh kills and discoveries.  The bloated carcass of a camel is sprawled across the ground.  It has been rotting for probably a couple of days.  Flies hop around on its fur, and it's beginning to smell.  The jackalmen probably don't care. }{Rocky Hill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36809}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {36812}{0}{}{Jackalman Den (nw)}{ }{      The tunnel widens here, and the floor drops so that the boulders are comfortably overhead.  It seems a bit cooler here.  Not much light makes it through the rocks.  There isn't quite as much litter covering the floor as there was toward the front of the tunnel.  Maybe the jackalmen don't come back here as often.  Wonder why.  A large wooden chest lies half-buried in the sand here. }{Rocky Hill}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36810}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

