R {37178}{0}{<248>}{Cave Sump (u)}{<248>% %<088>}{        The chill of the water is the first thing you notice here, enough to take your breath away if you were not holding it. From this angle, you can see that the floor of the cave above falls away at the side of the rockpile, and the stream has over time filled the entire space with water to a depth of ten feet or more. At the bottom, the sandy bed of the pool is glowing faintly green, some kind of algae is growing in great abundance down there. There is a wide gap in the rockpile here that you could possibly get through to the north west. }{The Green Lion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
