R {37235}{0}{<138>}{A run-down shop (s)}{<138>*<128>$<138>*<088>}{        This was once the old bait shop for the anglers who used this old fishing shack.  Once the trolls moved in it was only a matter of time before one decided to convert it into a general store in an effort to make money from his comrades.  Like the rest of the shack the floor is nonexistent, leaving the mud and grime of the swamp to ooze up and over your feet.  The moist, warm earth creates an ideal home for various mushrooms and ferns, providing they don't get ground underfoot by the heavy traffic that this shop generates. }{Troll Alliance}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37232}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {37236}{0}{<238>}{A large stone shack (w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{     Sat directly before you amidst the clutter and dirt of the shack floor is a large ramshackle throne.  Made of driftwood, clay, and stone it looks likely to fall to pieces if you were to breathe on it, nevermind sit on it.  A large poster adorns the back wall displaying the rather grim countenance of a man with striking icey blue eyes. }{Troll Alliance}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37234}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {37237}{0}{<238>}{The Black River Pub (s)}{<238>[P]<088>}{       This is perhaps the dirtiest, rowdiest, and loudest drinking establishment that you've ever set foot in.  Kicked over bar stools litter the ground, collecting mud and other filth as they roll around by the table legs.  Drunken trolls periodically stagger in and out, downing pints of Gutrot's home brewed beers before racing out into the swamps to empty their stomachs.  So swagger up to the bar and order something, you don't want the trolls to think you're a wimp, do you? }{Troll Alliance}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37234}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

