R {37266}{0}{}{A lonely grotto (n)}{ }{        Walking down the trail, you begin to sense an enormous, dark presence ahead.  The stumps of what were once swamp trees line the trail.  The passage is defined by a gossamer web of spider silk pointing you in one direction.  The rancid stench of rotting fish combined with the rank odor of bile makes your stomach turn. Resting at the end of the path is a toppled cypress tree.  Barely visible through the whirling clouds of mosquitos is a large moss  curtain, worn significantly from the passing of some large body. }{Fachan Village}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
