R {37356}{0}{}{Small library (n)}{ }{    You stand in a room with bookshelves covering every wall. A circular mahogany table with four chairs around it marks the center of the room. A big red candle in the center of the table lights up the room with its extremely bright and impossibly-still, white flame. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23420}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {37357}{0}{}{At a big table (w)}{ }{       This very big room is dominated by a long table stretching from the north end of the room to the southern end. The table is set with simple plates, and from the looks of the food in them you don't want to eat here. You can't seem to find any light source in here, although the room is brightly illuminated. It looks as if someone has had a violent fight in here. The only way out of the room is through a dark red curtain on the west wall in the southwestern corner of the room. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23411}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {37358}{0}{}{Wartniiflium's room (e)}{ }{      Everything is in strict order in this room. The sense of perfect lines, each in perfect relation to the other, overwhelm your senses. The items formed by the lines, like a table, a bed, a closet, and the opening in the east wall seem secondary compared to their perfect dimensions. The room is kept in a dim grey colour, making it seem insignificant. Maybe that is why the lines seem so significant. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {23414}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {37359}{0}{}{Vagramon's room (e)}{ }{     You are in a fairly big rectangular room. The walls and ceiling are made of some sort of yellow rock, while the floor is covered with an orange carpet. The room is furnished by a small wooden cabinet, a bed, and a big circular table with four chairs around it. There is only one way out of here, and that is through the curtain to your east. }{Durhal's Ant Caves}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
