R {37417}{0}{<268>}{Samantha's Cathedral (n,s,w,e)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{                    You stand inside Samantha's great cathedral.  The entire building is very beautiful.  Whoever built it seems to have put a lot of work into it. There are no walls.  Instead, massive white pillars line the perimeter. The floor is made of lustrous, black marble.  You can even see your reflection in it.      Perhaps the most amazing thing about the cathedral is the ceiling. Mounted atop the pillars a hundred feet above the ground, the ceiling is painted with nine marvelous masterpieces.  Whoever painted this ceiling, must have been a genius.  Possibly even the greatest painter that ever lived. You wonder who it could have been.  The cathedral extends further to the north, west and east.  You could also leave the cathedral through the giant pillars to the south.  You can see seven statues spread throughout the cathedral as well as a large fountain in the center, though they are too far away to make out details. In the center of the room, stands a life size statue of Pervasius, God of the Sea. }{The Cathedral}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
