R {37771}{0}{<248>}{A Dimly lit cave (w,s)}{<248>% %<088>}{      The floor drops off into hand carved layers of stone that descend toward the centre of what appears to have once been an arena. The steps circle like an amphitheatre. What must have taken hard work to assemble, now lies forsaken and smashed from eons of moisture and neglect. Small rows form flat slopes to the middle of the larger up and coming rooms for easier passage. }{Mount Knivur Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37770}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {37774}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {37772}{0}{<248>}{A Dimly lit cave (e)}{<248>% %<088>}{      Bones of every type line the walls and lay scattered across the floor, covering it almost entirely. Decayed and musty, these bones are mostly cracked, broken or ground into fragments or powder. Huge stalactites line the corners of the walls within this room, while broken stalagmites lay in huge piles of rubble stacked against the west wall. The combination of built up dust, decay and must is almost more then your nose can bear. }{Mount Knivur Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37770}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {37773}{0}{<248>}{A Dimly lit cave (e,n)}{<248>% %<088>}{      Large ruts have formed in the floor here where you surmise large beasts of all types were dragged unwilling to their deaths.  The only solace of the victor being carried, exhausted and broken, to a night of restless sleep to prepare them for the next days' accosting.  The walls are spotted with sconces where torches once illuminated the area for easy observation by the bloodthirsty onlookers. }{Mount Knivur Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37770}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
