R {37780}{0}{<248>}{A Dimly lit cave (e,w)}{<248>% %<088>}{      The floor stretches out into a valley as the small, narrow cavern widens into what could be misconstrued as a hewn room. However, the small, glowing mounds in the floor seem to blatantly belie this. Steam rises out of tiny pockets in the small craters, making the atmosphere here heavy and thick. Loud squeals split the air, though there is nothing to suggest that in this section of the inlet. }{Mount Knivur Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37779}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {37781}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {37781}{0}{<248>}{A Dimly lit cave (e,s)}{A}{           You hear the slow, steady drip of water, and smell the moist, sulfurous air.  The stalactites sparkle beautifully like giant icicles hanging from the stone roof.  You can see your breath in the chill, underground air, and if it weren't for the jagged stone path, you'd swear this was a winter wonderland.  A clear deep stream winds its way through the floor of stalagmites.  A pure white toad croaks, blinks, and splashes into the stream from its nearby stone.  The water briefly ripples, then stills.  You hear the flutter of small leathery wings, and see some nesting bats curiously watching you from their rocky perch.  Their beady eyes seem to follow you, and they lick their lips.  You see a flash of neat little rows of sharp pointy bat teeth. }{Mount Knivur Expansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37780}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
