R {38025}{0}{}{EMA Security Station (s,e,w,n)}{ }{      The security station exists to ensure only those with proper clearance are permitted inside the Research and Development area. A metal desk sits against the wall with a plain metal chair behind it. A row of monitors hangs on the wall above. A camera swivels back and forth from its place in the corner of the wall and ceiling, filming any and all that pass by. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38023}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38026}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38027}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38028}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38026}{0}{}{EMA Hallway (s,w,e,n)}{ }{     This north-south hallway is floored in the same gray cement as the walls that surround you. Open doorways lead both east and west towards what look to be offices of some kind. Fluorescent lights in the ceiling overhead illuminate the area nicely. Further to the south is a room shelved floor to ceiling and full of file folders. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38025}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38029}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38030}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38031}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38027}{0}{}{EMA Locker Room (s,w,n)}{ }{      This locker room serves as storage space for the belongings of the employees of the agency. Since many of the employees put in long hours, they find it convenient to be able to store extra clothes and gear here rather than cart them across town daily. There are two long benches that sit in the middle of the room and along all four walls are rows of lockers. Open doorways lead to the north, south, and west. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38025}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38031}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38035}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38028}{0}{}{EMA Hallway (s,w,e)}{ }{     This rather dull hallway consists of gray cement walls and flooring beneath a white drywall ceiling. Open doorways lead both east and west. The hall itself continues toward the south. Your footsteps echo as you move about these underground rooms, but little else can be heard. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38025}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38036}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38035}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38029}{0}{}{EMA Hallway (s,w,e,n)}{ }{     This north-south hallway is floored in the same gray cement as the walls that surround you. Open doorways lead both east and west towards what look to be offices of some kind. Fluorescent lights in the ceiling overhead illuminate the area nicely. Further to the south is a room shelved floor to ceiling and full of file folders. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38026}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38033}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38034}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38030}{0}{}{EMA Laboratory (e)}{ }{        This laboratory has shiny metal counters running around the edges of the room, encircling a matching metal work station in the center of the room. Between the work station and the counters is a white tiled floor about four feet wide that the EMA's scientists can use to make their way around the laboratory as they work. Above the work station, embedded in the ceiling, is a bright fluorescent light that sheds enough illumination on the room to allow the scientists to handle their delicate tasks. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38026}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38031}{0}{}{EMA Development Office (s,w,n)}{ }{        This spartan office is floored in raised white tile with white painted walls and a white drywall ceiling to match. Along one wall are a pair of six foot rack mount server cases. They seem to house the main computers for this facility. A bundle of colored cables run from the back of the cases into a small hole in the corner of the ceiling. The opposite wall has a drafting table set up in front of it that is covered with a pile of schematics. A navy blue drafting chair sits empty beside the table. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38026}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38034}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38027}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38032}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {38029}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38033}{0}{}{EMA Office (e)}{ }{       This office typically houses the assistant to the agency's researchers and scientists. It is spartan, containing a small oak desk against the wall furthest from the doorway, a leather chair in front of the desk, and two wooden chairs in front of a set of pine bookshelves. A small lamp sits atop one corner of the desk and a neat stack of papers sits beside this. On the shelves are about a dozen leather-bound books which are sandwiched between two iron bookends. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38029}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38034}{0}{}{EMA File Room (n,w)}{ }{        This file room is covered in metal shelves from floor to ceiling. The shelves house thousands of file folders containing the history and secrets of this city government organization. Once merely in charge of maintenance and disaster recovery, these files document the EMA's changing role since the apocalypse destroyed much of Atlanta's population and landscape. While there is enough material here to keep a bookkeeper busy for days, the shelves continue to the west and a doorway leads into an emptier room to the north. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38029}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38031}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38035}{0}{}{EMA Development Office (s,w)}{ }{        This tidy office is typically used by the EMA's engineers as they work on new projects for the agency. Several desks and chairs are set up in rows along the walls. Atop the desks are large computer monitors and keyboards. Underneath each desk is a computer to be used for their work. A long table sits in the middle of the room, apparently this is used as a work bench for any mechanical items the engineers may be developing. A large fluorescent light is embedded in the ceiling over the table to provide extra illumination for the engineers' work. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38027}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38028}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38036}{0}{}{EMA Laboratory (e)}{ }{      This white-floored laboratory has a large metal table sitting in the middle of the room and a multitude of machinery along the walls. Wires are strewn along the tops of the walls where they meet the drywall ceiling. Pipes run along the corners of the room, leading up into the ceiling and down into the floor, more than likely conduits for a power supply. A large metal case sits near the open doorway to the east. }{EMA Complex}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38028}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38037}{0}{<238>}{Strange path (n,portal)}{E}{     You stand in something that seems to be a small forest of some kind. All around you, you can see large trees, and it seems to be impossible to walk in any other direction than north. Next to you, the portal that you entered this area from stands, and you can enter it again. You think it could take you back to where you came from.  }{Midgard and Valhalla}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38038}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38039}{portal}{portal}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38038}{0}{<238>}{Turn in the path (s,e)}{<238>. .<088>}{      The path turns here. All around you, you can see a dense but beautiful forest. Birds are chirping in the trees, and you hear frogs in your surroundings. To the east you hear the sound of people moving around. You stumbled right into a new civilization here! The path continues east, and to the south you can go back to where you entered this strange place.  }{Midgard and Valhalla}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38037}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38040}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38039}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {38040}{0}{<238>}{Southern Village (se,n,w)}{<238>[ ]<088>}{     You have reached the southernmost part of a strange village. To the north, you see many people walking around, and you realize that the center of this village must be there. A few trees stand here, behind a couple of houses. To the west, you can follow the path back, out of this strange place.  }{Midgard and Valhalla}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38038}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38041}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38042}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38041}{0}{<228>}{Smaller clearing (nw)}{<228>, `<088>}{     You stumble into a smaller clearing, and the silence here makes you calm. In the center of the clearing a large stone is placed, and you can see some runes carved in it. The grass here is soft, and almost reaches up to your knees. You wish you had time to sit down and rest for a while.  }{Midgard and Valhalla}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38040}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38042}{0}{<238>}{Village Center (n,s,w,e)}{<238>(<148>~<238>)<088>}{    This seems to be the center of the strange village. Many people move along the paths between the small houses that you can see around this place. In the center of the area you can see a well, where young women usually get water. The village continues in all directions.  }{Midgard and Valhalla}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38040}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38043}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
