R {38139}{0}{<178>}{Ruins of the Damned (n,s)}{<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>}{         The twilight of the evil moon above shines down upon the dead\; their bones illuminated.  Only small patches of grass grow here.  Most of the ground is bare earth.  A howling wind blows across the graveyard, compelling you to buckle your muscles in resistance.  Withered skeletons protrude slightly from the dirt\; most of them flattened with time.  As you peer into the dark mist momentarily, you think you see some sort of humanoid figure walking toward you.  But then it is gone. }{The Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25637}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38140}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38140}{0}{<178>}{Ruins of the Damned (n,s)}{<178>{<148>*<178>}<088>}{        Broken and overturned tombstones litter the ground before you.  Hovering above the tombstones and ground, lies a blanket of black mist.  The pale moon shines brightly, but cannot penetrate the mist.  Dead leaves blow about in a spiral as a gust of chilling air blows in.  As you look to the moon itself, the silhouette of a wolf stalks slowly past it.  On the eastern side of the graveyard, stands a dead oak tree. }{The Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38139}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38141}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38141}{0}{<248>}{Mausoleum (n)}{A}{                The black mist that fills the rest of the graveyard is strangely absent here.  A white marble shrine twenty feet across shines brightly, guarding the area against the black mist.  A rectangular, marble slab, intricately cut, forms the base of the shrine.  It is approximately four feet tall. Atop the base is a dome, also made of white marble. The dome is a full three-quarter sphere, with only the bottom cut off by the base.  The dome is open on the side facing you, revealing a large stone slab which appears as if it's covering a hole.  Red glyphs of a foreign tongue cover the slab.  Though you cannot read the glyphs perfectly, you get the distinct impression that it is some kind of warning.      In addition, beyond the shrine to the south lives a thick and dark forest.  Many fierce sounds emanate from within.  Though it is probably not wise, you might be able to enter the forest. }{The Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38140}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38142}{enter hole}{enter hole}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38142}{0}{<248>}{Underground Corridor (n,u)}{}{             You are now beneath the graveyard, in a man-made underground corridor. You feel as if you're sinking into the ground.  It is not made of solid earth, but rather mud.  Though light shines into this room from the shrine, you fear that if you were to move farther ahead things would become dark. The ceiling appears extremely unstable.  Patches of mud and dirt continuously fall down from it.  The walls are not stable either.  Tiny rivers of mud flow from top to bottom. }{The Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38143}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38141}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38143}{0}{<248>}{Underground Corridor (n,s)}{<248>. <178>+<088>}{      You stand in what appears to have once been a burial site.  A rotted skeleton hangs from the ceiling.  It hangs from its skull, which the ceiling covers.  The walls are becoming more and more solid as you walk farther down the corridor.     Also, on the floor before you lies a petrified head.  The expression of the head is that of mortal terror. }{The Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38142}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38145}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38144}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {38142}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38145}{0}{<248>}{Underground Corridor (n,s)}{<248>. <178>+<088>}{         The walls are now almost completely solid as you appear to be approaching the end of this underground corridor.  The floor slants downward slightly, and you almost trip as a result.  The corridor seems to be getting wider and wider. The ceiling is now approximately twenty feet above you.  Toxic fumes fill the hot air, making it hard to breathe.  The room to the north appears to be very meticulously built. A doorway, though no door, is carved out of the rock leading into the well lit room. }{The Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38143}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38146}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38146}{0}{<268>}{Pytheria's Chamber (s)}{A}{            The underground corridor comes to an end in this final room. The stone doorway to the south leads back out into the corridor.  Stone effigies of unknown adventurers fill the room.  Many appear to be in a state of terror. A multitude of what appear to be vampire bats hang upside-down on the domed ceiling.  There are two objects of interest in the room.  The first, a bronze casket on the left side of the room.  Many strange markings cover the casket. On the right side of the room sits a shining silver altar.  Upon the altar, the symbol of a lion is etched.  The coffin and the altar are placed in such a way that they appear to be opposing one another. }{The Graveyard}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38145}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38147}{0}{}{A Mine Cart}{ }{You are in a mine cart that is crashing down mine tracks at lightning speed.  Hopefully it won't crash.}{Mine}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38148}{look}{look}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38148}{0}{<238>}{Sweltering Passages (e)}{<238>] [<088>}{        You stand deep within the heart of Mt. Silvermoon.  Steam wells up from the ground beneath you.  The hot ground warms your feet through your shoes.  Though this area is extremely remote, there does seem to be some activity here.  Workers chisel away at the walls of the passages.  These walls, however, are not made of the beautiful minerals like the outer region of the mine.  They are simply made of rock.  You wonder what these miners could be mining for?  You could climb back up the mine shaft if you wanted. }{Mine}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38149}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {37408}{climb up}{climb up}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38149}{0}{<238>}{Sweltering Passages (w,e)}{<238>] [<088>}{     You are deep within a set of sweltering passages inside Mt. Silvermoon.  Hot gas rises from cracks in the ground.  The heat is almost unbearable.  Several tools lay scattered around near the walls.  Everything here is dark, and your eyes yearn for sunlight. }{Mine}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
