R {38248}{0}{<268>}{Inside a Temple (e,n)}{<268>{<178>+<268>}<088>}{        The temple is primitive but quite beautiful. Seashells of all sizes, colors, and shapes decorate the temple. Drawings of a mighty sea serpent cover the walls. Small pools of water made from rocks placed together contain many small fish. There are a few steps leading up to a simple throne at the far wall. Upon the throne sits the leader of the natives. She wears a dress made of dry seaweed and a crown made of seashells. In her right hand she holds a staff which has the tooth of a sea serpent at its end. The tooth glows slightly. }{Island of Tapan}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
