R {38936}{0}{}{Cave-in (n)}{ }{     You stand here on the edge of a cave-in. There is no way to go back through the tunnel which led to this place, the only chance now is to go on. Ahead of you leads a narrow ice cavern, which appears to have been naturally formed from water running through the ice. Then again, perhaps it is not natural ... }{Seahaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38937}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38938}{leap pit}{leap pit}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {38937}{0}{<168>}{Ice Tunnel (s,n)}{<168>~ ~<088>}{        Ice Tunnel. A cold and frozen tunnel. Ice crystals sparkle on the roof, refracting light from the walls which glow with an unknown source of internal illumination. The air is so cold, you can feel it penetrating into the core of your bones. Nothing lives here, there is no perturbation of the natural order which has created this place. If you were to die, your corpse would surely remain preserved for eternity... Interestingly there seems to be a lot of soft snow here. }{Seahaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {38936}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {38938}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
