R {39020}{0}{<178>}{White Marble Square (s,w,n)}{<178>[ ]<088>}{             White Marble Square All the towers, the shops, the libraries, and the places of worship, have long been consumed by the ice of the glacier. All that remains of the ancient city of Seahaven is a small portion of the central market tiled in huge squares of alternating color. The ground here is pure white, as if it has been bleached or purged of all imperfections by blasting it with heat. There is nothing here but a white ash. On the floor there is a symbol. Progress east is prevented by a huge crevasse which drops precipitously away before you. To the north of you, is the rock face which forms the roots of a towering mountain. Clearly the city was built right up to the edge of this natural wonder. Progress in that direction is impossible. There is a tunnel cut in the rockface to the north. }{Seahaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
