R {39041}{0}{}{Yakuza Mansion (w)}{ }{     This large office is richly decorated with Asian treasures.  Ample sitting room is present with several couches and chairs.  A large desk rests near the rear of the room, covered in various papers and files.  A large chandelier lights the room, and is supported by several lamps in the room.  In the center of the room is a large area rug. }{Mega-Tokyo}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {36037}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {39042}{0}{}{Genom Corporation (out)}{ }{       This small elevator bay once traversed up the massive Genom skyraker, but it has been converted to an ultra modern teleportation chamber.  The floor consists of a huge, red circular pad, and the ceiling is white but made of a strange unknown material.  The elevator buttons have been removed, and there is only a single large red button remaining.  A set of double doors leads out of the chamber, back into the Genom lobby. }{Mega-Tokyo}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {39044}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {39043}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {39044}{0}{}{Genom Corporation (exit)}{ }{      This large circular office is lined with glass, allowing one to see the entire city of Mega-Tokyo.  To the north, the sight of Mt. Fuji is spectacular.  The city itself is clouded in a haze of smog.  A large desk, made of black and white marble is the centerpiece of the office. The desk is complimented by a black leather chair, and a set of guest chairs.  A bookcase is mounted within the western wall. }{Mega-Tokyo}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
