R {39511}{0}{}{Underneath Hjeldins Tower (u)}{ }{    The smooth walls of the tower have been replaced by rough hewn rock. This large, dark and dusty chamber appears to have been part of the old keep, back when A'sua was ruled by the Sithi. Now, it is empty, and blockaded by rubble. The only exit appears to be back up the stairs. }{The Dragonbone Chair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {39509}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {39512}{0}{}{A room in the tower (out)}{ }{    The torchlight bleeding in from outside reveals a room filled entirely with furnishings made from bones that have been tied and glued together. Among which is a large chair which has, as if in mockery of the High King's throne, an awning made entirely from skulls - human skulls. }{The Dragonbone Chair}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
