R {39841}{0}{<238>}{Enterre Vivant (s)}{<238>] [<088>}{   This empty chamber is devoid of all decoration. The stone walls are bare of painting or picture. The room is dark and forboding, like a tomb waiting for its tenant to come home to rest. }{Paris: Theatre des Vampires}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {39840}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {39842}{0}{<138>}{Chambre d'Armand (w)}{<138>[ ]<088>}{       This room is softly lit by candlelight, shadows playing in the corners. Medieval chairs surround a dark wood table sitting on a blood red rug in the center of the room. The candles sit atop the table, burning close to the wick in cooling pools of wax. A blazing fire burns in the hearth on the southern wall across from a shiny black coffin to the north. The room's point of focus is a large painting of Satan's fall from Heaven which dominates the wall above the fireplace. }{Paris: Theatre des Vampires}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {39840}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

