R {40877}{0}{}{An old-fashioned dining room (ne,e,s)}{ }{        The dining hall has traditional oak-paneled wainscotting with light blue, striped wallpaper. A long oak table has place settings for eight and tall, silver candlestick holders. Directly over the table, a fine crystal chandelier glitters with refracted rainbows. Blue porcelain plates with windmill scenes hang above a buffet on the west wall, and the delicious smell of roast chicken wafts in from the south. A set of double French doors leads to the gardens to the northeast, while through the entryway to the east you catch a glimpse of the foyer. }{Bennebroek Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
