R {40879}{0}{}{A busy kitchen (n)}{ }{       The wood floor is clean but scuffed from the shoes of the many servants that have shuffled over them over the years. A large kettle is simmering in a wide fireplace on the south wall. A slow fire is also burning under a brick oven to the west, which adds to the general heat and humidity being generated by all of the activity.  In the center, a large thick table full of nicks and scrapes is used to prepare the dishes. A swinging door leads north to the dining room. }{Bennebroek Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {40877}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {40880}{0}{}{A musty library (n)}{ }{       It is warm and hushed in the library, like an empty schoolroom after hours on a hot sunny day. Sunlight filtering in through two tall western windows catches on dust motes that barely stir in the still air. On the south wall, bookshelves stretch from floor to ceiling, filled with rows upon rows of musky old leather-bound tomes. Two large leather chairs are angled towards a cold dead fireplace on the east wall, a large reading table between them.                             }{Bennebroek Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {40876}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {40881}{0}{}{In a hallway (w,s)}{ }{     The hallway has oak wainscotting with pale-yellow, striped wallpaper.  Brass lanterns are set in the wall at regular intervals.  This section of the hall is adorned with portraits of the lord of the manor's paternal ancestors. The most ornately carved oak door in the household suggests that the master bedroom must lie to the south. }{Bennebroek Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
