R {40883}{0}{}{A tidy guest room (n)}{ }{           The guest room is as large as a suite and carefully decorated in that matching manner of an artificially comfortable hotel room\; enough to impress but not to encourage an overlong stay. The room has white furniture set against tan wallpaper. A plush white rug covers the floor, and a large wrought-iron four-post bed in the center of the room is hung with a curtain of transparent white chiffon fabric. In the southeast corner, a white upholstered chair is positioned next to a window on the east wall, affording a view of the grounds below. There is a rustic wooden chest at the foot of the bed, and a matching armoire in the southwest corner. An end table under the window sill next to the armchair completes the set. }{Bennebroek Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {40882}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {40884}{0}{}{The master bedroom (n)}{ }{       From the inlaid wood floor to the high ceiling, the master bedroom speaks of luxury.  A crystal chandelier sparkles and tinkles gently as a light breeze blows in through a partially open bay window on the east side. A king-sized sleigh bed with a mahogany frame lies against the west wall, with traditional landscape paintings decorating the walls. At the south end of the room, an oak desk stacked with open books and loose paper looks to be in frequent use. }{Bennebroek Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
