R {40995}{0}{}{Royal Banquet Hall (w,n)}{ }{       You have entered a magnificent banquet hall.  There is a long table here set with fine linen and silver, and enough chairs on each side of the table to seat a large number of guests.  Light shines down from a crystal chandelier hanging above.  The table is currently devoid of both diners and food, but you imagine that many fine meals have been served in these quarters.  A doorway to the north leads to a kitchen and a passage to the west leads back to the main hall. }{Humpty Dumpty}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
