R {41212}{0}{}{The neck (n,s,w,e)}{ }{      You are now standing in the neck region of Mr. Plank.  Running down the back side of this region is the spinal cord, protected by the bony vertebrae.  The main vein that brings back blood from the brain is the famous jugular vein, which if slit causes almost immediate death.  Other important structures located in the neck include the thyroid gland, and obviously the vocal chords. }{Innerspace}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
