R {41215}{0}{}{The hand (e)}{ }{       You are now in the hand of Mr. Plank.  This area is one of the most sensitive parts of the body, with numerous nerve endings that sense pressure and temperature in every square millimeter of tissue.  There are an incredible number of bones in the hands, making up a significant portion of the total number in the body.  An opposable thumb is one of the distinguishing features of primates, and allows us to pick up small objects and grasp them effectively. }{Innerspace}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
