R {41384}{0}{}{The north end of the Mentos Art Gallery (s)}{ }{       The north end of the Mentos Art Gallery is decorated in a very. . .  abstract  manner, by Salvador Dali himself.  The room itself is made out of the same  white stone used in the gallery, but looks like it has been pitted and  scarred by sledgehammers.  Paint has been splashed all over the place, and  weird, randomly arranged faces stare down at you from the ceiling.  It  looks like a bunch of blood and entrails have been splattered on the  walls!  }{Mentos}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
