R {41386}{0}{}{The west end of the Mentos Art Gallery (e)}{ }{      The west end of the gallery is made from the same dazzling  white stone that the main hall is.  A large glass roof above  allows sunlight to shine in and brighten up the area.   The most prominent feature of the room is the fact that  lines of red, blue, and yellow are painted along the  otherwise bare white stone.  }{Mentos}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
