R {41674}{0}{<228>}{On the plains (se,ne,sw,n,e,s,w)}{<228>. ^<088>}{         The grass here is ankle deep, the plains and rolling hills stretching off in all directions.  Far to the north a massive cliff rises up out of the plains like a giant wall, stretching upwards for at least six hundred feet.  To the west the plains become rockier and give way to a large mountain range, while to the south, forestland can be seen. The air is cool and fresh here, a gentle breeze tickling at your skin, bringing a myriad of smells and sounds to your senses.  The Sun's rays warm your bones as it continues on its daily cycle across the skies, the occasional clouds casting long shadows across the land.  You can hear the calls and movement of animals off in the distance. }{Prehistoric Earth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
