R {41681}{0}{<238>}{A rocky shoreline (sw,nw,n,s,w)}{<238>^ ^<088>}{         The lake's shore becomes rocky here, millions of small rocks and pebbles scattered all over the area.  Looking like giant stepping stones, large rocks can be seen rising out of the lake's waters in a rough line stretching eastwards.  The largest of the rocks protrudes from the sand just in front of you, which appears to be a popular nesting place for the birds that sit all over it.  The air is cool and fresh, a steady breeze blowing in off the lake and heading off across the plains to your west.  The birds fill the air with their constant chatter and the sound of their wings flapping, large flocks taking flight when something disturbs them. }{Prehistoric Earth}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
