R {41705}{0}{}{At the base of a small waterfall (sw)}{ }{              At the base of a small waterfall  A large rock face looms above you to the north, sheltering the area from the red-tinted moonlight.  Blood-red water cascades down its face in a series of small, stepped waterfalls, before plunging into a swirling pool, etched deep into the rocky ground by countless years of wear.  The water then flows southwest, following a creek that is cut deep into the ground.  Squat-looking trees grow along the creek's high banks, their small, round leaves growing in clumps from the few branches which grow at odd angles from the trunks.  Strange, red-tinted clouds drift slowly by overhead, wandering aimlessly across the star-filled night skies, partially obscuring the three deep-red moons which look close enough to touch, and startling in their clarity.  The steady pounding of the water crashing into the pool obscures all other sounds, and fills the air with a crisp, damp smell. }{Red Creek}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
