R {41708}{0}{}{Dense, spiky grass (w,sw,e,s)}{ }{          The two foot high, needle-like grass becomes incredibly thick here, even more so as you look northwards, where it grows tall and looks impassable. Attached to nearly every blade of grass, spider webs litter the area, the tiny droplets of dew caught in them sparkling bright-red in the moonlight. Stars twinkle in the partially cloudy skies, matching the dew droplets, but a bright silver colour, as opposed to the red of the droplets.  A light breeze barely manages to rustle the stiff grass, also doing little to hide the unmistakable sound of something nearby moving around in the grass.  A short distance away to the southwest you can see what you guess to be a large pond, which shines like a red, metallic disc. }{Red Creek}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
