R {41719}{0}{}{Rocky ground (ne,n,w,e,s)}{ }{        As if in answer to the stars above you, thousands upon thousands of tiny flecks of crystal in the ground shine.  Trapped within the rocks, they sparkle bright-red as they reflect the moonlight from above.  To the north, east and west of you the grass appears to flourish, while here only the odd patch manages to grow successfully.  Southeast of here you spy a large rock formation, about fifteen feet tall and covered with spider webs. A bright light can be seen coming from a small opening in the formation, its colours and intensity fluctuating randomly. }{Red Creek}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
