R {42476}{0}{<228>}{Deep in Mantis Swamp (e,n)}{<228>; ;<088>}{     Pools of stagnant water remain, but most of the ground is firm enough to walk on without trouble. The cypress trees grow in abundance, rooted deep in the moist earth and stretching up out of the haze towards the hidden sun above. Vines and tendrils wind around the tree trunks and moss grows over the bark, dark and green. }{Mantis Swamp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {42475}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {42477}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {42477}{0}{<228>}{Deep in Mantis Swamp (w)}{<228>; ;<088>}{      The trees crowd the swamp this deep into their midst. Branches laden with green leaves hang low to the ground, almost touching the marshy surface. The thick mist that infiltrates virtually every corner of this swamp swirls in and around the branches of the trees, leaving a spooky unearthly quality to the place. It looks like the trees are too densely packed to travel any further. }{Mantis Swamp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {42476}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {42478}{0}{<228>}{Deeply Hidden in Mantis Swamp (e)}{<228>; ;<088>}{      The ground is firmer in this part of the swamp, still marshy, but not full of standing water. The vegetation is so thick it almost seems to be choking the life out of the few lichen covered trees that have managed to survive. The vines and tendrils twist in and around the puny tree trunks, covering them in greenery and sucking up what little sun there is within the misty haze. }{Mantis Swamp}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
