R {42688}{0}{}{A Genetics Lab (s)}{ }{      You've entered the Lab's main electrical equipment room.  Massive archaic computers stand ready, lights ominously off.  In the corner of the room is a small backup UPS and small backup generator pair\; glancing at the backup generator which was used to supply power to the equipment you realize that its batteries were drained years ago.  Which does bring to mind a mystery -- why are all the lights still on?  What powers them?  }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {42686}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {42689}{0}{}{A Genetics Lab (e,n)}{ }{    You've entered a cryogenic storage area to the lab.  It has large shelves on the walls, with translucent shimmering light around them.  Laying on the shelves are the bodies of human genetic experiments, seemingly not aged since they were put into this form of stasis years ago. }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {42686}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {42691}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {42690}{0}{}{A Genetics Lab (n,s,w,e)}{ }{          You've entered a large biological mixing room.  Long, supple robotic arms, and small conveyor belts snake around the room.  These methods are used to transfer and transport the contents of vials, undoubtedly this is the room where the actual biological work was done\; combining the half-helix with a `soup' to generate a molecule, and then splicing that molecule into living DNA ... Fascinating!  A long table set against the east wall contains worn sketches and notes, which have faded with time and you have difficulty making them out.  Several tall DNA molecule models, showing the double helix with brightly colored genes and base pairs sits atop the table.  Undoubtedly the professor will be interested in this discovery! }{Genlab}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {42686}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

