R {42974}{0}{}{Docking}{ }{     You are standing in a very small, tight docking bay.  The bay is just large enough to provide a snug fit for the shuttle.  A bright flashing light swirls in circles near the airlock, showing you the way deeper into the satellite. A bright red panel with a button on it is next to the airlock. A LARGE warning sign with bright yellow and black paint seems to grab your attention. }{Weather Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {42975}{airlock}{airlock}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {42975}{0}{}{Inside the airlock (dock)}{ }{    This tight, cramped area is brightly lit by harsh white lights.  On one side is a door leading out to the shuttle docking bay - and to the cold vacuum of space.  The other leads farther into the station.  A large red panel is mounted into the wall, with several buttons on it. }{Weather Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
