R {43461}{0}{<228>}{Chapel Grasslands (se,e,w,ne)}{<228>, `<088>}{        The booming sounds of thunder shake the grassland floor, each sound unique in size and rugged style.  Over time, rainwater has bled through the cracks in the ground, and dissolved enough soil to create a miniature network of streams.  These muddy flowing channels have the smell of fertile earth, and are multiplying as droplets of rain dive gracefully into their flow.  The brightly forked flashes of lightning cast wavering shadows that seem to change their appearance as they dance amongst the blades of grass. }{Chapel Field}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
