R {43462}{0}{<228>}{Chapel Grasslands (nw)}{<228>. ^<088>}{     Sparkling crystalline water droplets cascade down the cracks and crevices within the canyon, and all around you the fields sway in the breeze.  Tall, slender stalks of grass rise overhead, forming a dancing canopy that provides little shelter from the relentless drizzle. }{Chapel Field}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43461}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43463}{0}{<238>}{Mountain's Edge (w)}{<238>^ ^<088>}{       The edge of Chapel mountains lies directly in front of you, covered in places with dense, lush trees.  The grass of the valley runs right up to the base of the mountains almost as if it intends to scale the rock wall.  The rain is definitely cooler here, as wind sweeps across the snow capped peaks and down into the valley.  Towering walls of deep grey stone rise out of the ground halting any passage further, as the rock cliffs are almost sheer and impossible to climb. }{Chapel Field}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43461}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43464}{0}{<228>}{Chapel Grasslands (ne,sw)}{<228>. ^<088>}{       Looking down you notice a decaying cobble stone path, the remains of a small road that at one time cut through the area.  Droplets of mist cover the scattered worn cobbles, causing their surface to appear smooth and lustrous.  Brilliant white light flashes out of the sky, casting a haunting glow across the surface of the crossroad that lies to the northeast.  A chilling wind howls through the blades of grass, while blowing droplets of rain diagonally through the air. }{Chapel Field}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43461}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43465}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43465}{0}{<278>}{Crossroads (se,sw,ne,nw)}{<278>-+-<088>}{       The field presses around the crossroad as you continue to follow the worn cobble-stone road.  Slender stems of sprouting grass rise up between the decaying stones and grass that dominate the area.  Thick moss creeps its way up the pebbles of the road on the western side. The cobbles are densely carpeted with blue-speckled translucent rain droplets, and the whistling wind carries with it the scent of a distant bed of wildflowers. }{Chapel Field}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
