R {43688}{0}{}{The mess hall (w,nw)}{ }{     The large mess hall is filled with empty tables and chairs, indicating that it probably isn't chow time at present.  The strong smells of cooking food waft from behind the counter, but none of the food is laid out.  The doors out on to the parade ground to the northwest stand open, allowing the tempting (?) aromas to drift out. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43686}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43695}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43689}{0}{}{A small patch of grass (w)}{ }{      Between the buildings of the compound and the trees which surround it, this small patch of grass is home to a large sign.  What looks to be the start of a cownfidence course starts at the eastern edge, disappearing into the trees, and reappearing on the southern side of the grass to finish.  You should READ THE SIGN if you are considering attempting it. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43687}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43690}{0}{}{The northeast corner of a parade ground (s,sw,e,w)}{ }{    A large black and white building stands to the east, with its door wide open, right on the edge of the parade ground.  The trees that line the north side of the field stop where they meet the end of the building, creating a square corner of the field. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43687}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43682}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
