E {53020}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43691}{0}{}{Inside a spacious barracks (e,w)}{ }{     The door out of the barracks stands open to the west, through which can be seen the expanse of the parade ground.  Rows of beds against the north and south walls of the barn-like barracks start here and extend eastwards as far as you can see.  At the foot of each bed is a small trunk, painted black and white, and secured with a sturdy lock. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43690}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43692}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43687}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43692}{0}{}{Deep in the barracks (e,w)}{ }{    The coolness of the barracks building is evident further away from the exit out onto the parade ground.  There are a few windows that partially illuminate the otherwise shadowy interior, leaving the beds and trunks murky shapes in the poor light. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43691}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43693}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43693}{0}{}{At the end of the barracks (w)}{ }{    The barracks comes to an end as it started, with more rows of beds and trunks.  The end wall is bare, the black and white paint clean and shiny.  There are more windows lining the walls than elsewhere in the barracks, providing a little light and a cooling breeze. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43692}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43694}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {43687}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43695}{0}{}{The mess hall (e)}{ }{     Tables and chairs fill this end of the mess hall, creating plenty of room for the masses when the chow-bell rings.  At the far end of the mess hall, near the doors, you can see the counter, which is probably where the ... interesting aroma that fills the hall is originating from. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43688}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43696}{0}{}{Before a hidden structure in the trees (w,enter)}{ }{      Hidden away amidst the trees, an ancient stone archway stands revealed by a recently fallen tree.  Moss encroaches on the lower stones of the arch, suggesting that perhaps the structure has been in place even longer than the trees surrounding it.  There are several worn runes carved into either side of the archway, their meaning lost in the mists of time. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30727}{w}{w}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43697}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43697}{0}{}{A clump of trees (portal,s)}{ }{   Beneath the sheltering canopy of trees the heat segues into shade. Not wanting to be forgotten, the wind occasionally blows the thick stench of hot air into the trees. }{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43699}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43696}{portal}{portal}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

