R {43972}{0}{}{A quiet graveyard (se)}{ }{      The last resting places of the deceased inhabitants of CowVille are all around, a peaceful testament to their lives.  Most of the graves are marked with simple stone headstones, carved into the shape of an upturned hoof, and engraved with the details of the deceased.  Bare earth, devoid of grass or shrubs, makes up the graveyard, as if even the plants have been laid to rest. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43981}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {30778}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43973}{0}{}{On a balcony in the church (w,e)}{ }{     The southern balcony stretches out to the east, wide enough to hold quite a number of cows at once, but it looks to be all but deserted at present.  There is a railing along the side of the balcony, stopping errant cows from toppling off, but also making it possible to peer safely over into the church below. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30732}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43974}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43974}{0}{}{Halfway along the southern balcony (w,e)}{ }{    The balcony continues in both easterly and westerly directions.  Below in the church, a handful of cows praying to the Almighty Moo can be seen among the rows of pews, their soft murmurings drifting up over the railing of the balcony. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43973}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43975}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43975}{0}{}{Near the end of the balcony (nw,e)}{ }{     The southern balcony looks to end just to the northwest, where it likely overlooks the altar at the front of the church.  The railing continues to run along the length of the balcony, and can be peered over to see what is going on in the church below, though it sounds pretty quiet down there. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43974}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {43976}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43976}{0}{}{Overlooking the altar (se)}{ }{      The balcony comes to an end overlooking the black and white altar at the front of the church.  Serving as a focal point and backdrop to the altar is a huge stained-glass window which fills the entire wall with a depiction of the head of the Almighty Moo.  On the wall of the balcony is hung an ornate tapestry woven with a cascade of blue threads, showing a quotation from the Almighty Moo. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {43975}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43977}{0}{}{The front row of pews (n)}{ }{      The front row of pews has an excellent view of the black and white hoof-shaped altar that stands before a huge stained-glass window at the front of the church.  There is an open space between the front pews and the altar, framed by the walls that curve in on either side.  The rows of pews stretch out towards the rear of the church to the east, occupied only by a few praying cows. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30746}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43978}{0}{}{The front row of pews (s)}{ }{      The front row of pews has an unobstructed view of the altar and stained-glass window backdrop to the southwest.  The wall to the north looms overhead as it slowly arches inwards to meet the opposing wall high overhead.  Between the pews and the altar is an open space, framed on either side by the church walls that curve inwards to focus attention on the altar. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30746}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {43979}{0}{}{At the altar (e)}{ }{       The black and white, hoof-shaped altar stands directly before the huge stained-glass window which glows with a radiant light.  A quiet sense of holy power seems to emanate from the altar, as if it were not a thing crafted by cows, but by the hooves of some omnipotent force.  The splotches of black and white marble making up the altar seem to pulse with light and darkness, but it is more a thing felt than seen, as if the two were struggling for dominance. }{Northern CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {30747}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
