R {44552}{0}{}{Windraker Manor: Attic (d)}{ }{      The attic is very musty and dust has settled everywhere.  The boards you're standing on have small cracks between them letting you see into the rooms below. This room expands over the whole of the house and has many boxes and chests laying around, but they all appear to be locked or otherwise sealed for long term storage.  There's a hatch to go back down into the study. }{Windraker Manor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {24552}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {44553}{0}{}{House entranceway (e,leave)}{ }{    This is the entrance to the merchant's house. Intricate tapestries line both sides of the hallway here.  Gold and silver threads are not used sparingly. You can tell immediately you have entered the home of somebody better off than they should be in a town that holds so much poverty. }{Rich Mansion}{rich_mansion}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {44554}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {4068}{leave}{leave}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {44554}{0}{}{Central hallway (se,e,w,n)}{ }{      This is the central room of the house which is not only for greeting guests  but also for entertainment.  Off to the south end you see a magnificent  fireplace inlaid with gold designs of eagles and what appears to be the family  crest.  To the north your nose detects the wonderful smells of what appears to  be roasting pheasant.  But you are not here for pleasure, this is a business man's home and you are here for business. }{Rich Mansion}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {44553}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
