R {45128}{0}{}{Inside An Elegant Tent (out)}{ }{            The Brigand's tent is the epitome of luxury and allows the ruler to reconcile semi-nomadic and sedentary life styles.  This tent is exceptionally large and was transported, fully assembled, by placing it on a wheeled contraption pulled by oxen.  Its interior is lined with sumptuous textiles made by the best weavers of Fantasy.  Its floor is covered with the warmest and most comfortable tribal rugs.  Gold and silver cups, ewers, and bowls are placed on low red-lacquered wooden tables and trays.  A crystal bookcase sits the northwest corner of the tent, right next to a liquid metal bed that ripples as disturbed water does.   A stove is placed in the center, its vertical pipe piercing the circular aperture in the roof. }{Chapel Field}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {35442}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

