R {45224}{0}{<248>}{The Zoo of Death (d)}{<248>% %<088>}{        This is the entrance to the dreaded Zoo of Death. Rumored to be the hidden playground for Humperdinck's evil amusement, stories say he built it years ago to house the world's most dangerous animals. Built underground, its existence denied to the populace, it serves the Prince's whims when he desires to hunt wild game... or torture those that get in his way. It seems the place exists afterall. Now the question is, how do you get out? More importantly, can you do it alive? }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45225}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45225}{0}{<088>}{The Zoo of Death (d,u)}{ }{        Long straw-like grass surrounds you, the occasional clump of bushes breaking up the monotony. This room would resemble a jungle plain if it weren't for the fact you remain underground. The grass ends abruptly at the dirt walls on the perimeter of the vaguely circular room. The bushes are green and thorny, providing good cover for hidden predators. From this room you can head back up towards the entrance of the zoo or further below towards whatever unknown dangers may lurk in its depths. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45224}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45226}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45226}{0}{<228>}{The Zoo of Death (e,u)}{<228>; ;<088>}{       The grass beneath your feet is soggy, laden with muddy water. Stagnant and stale, the ground water smells awful. The terrain has flattened out in this part of the zoo, no longer sloping downward as it did closer to the entrance to this wretched place. The dark rock that makes up the walls and ceiling drips with condensation, adding to the muck created by the seeping floor. The humidity is stifling, the air heavy and difficult to breathe. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45225}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45227}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45227}{0}{<148>}{The Zoo of Death (s,w)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{      You stand chest deep in water, apparently in the middle of an underground lake. Dark and murky, you can't see the ground you stand upon. The water is cold, chilling you to the bone. The sound of the lake water slopping against the rock walls of this underground cavern echoes in the darkness. The muddy shore of the lake lies to the west and a river flows southward, out of the lake and deeper into the zoo. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45226}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45228}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45228}{0}{<148>}{The Zoo of Death (e,n)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{         You're wading in a swift underground river. It seems to stem from a lake to the north and flows ever faster towards the east. The river nearly roars as it picks up speed in that direction, dropping out of sight into what might be some type of waterfall by the sound of it. There is no shore, the river spanning from one rock wall to the other. The ceiling is pitch black, much too high for any light you might carry to illuminate. It looks as if there is nowhere to go but back towards the lake or further into the roaring river and whatever might lie beyond. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45227}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45229}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45229}{0}{<148>}{The Zoo of Death (s)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{         The pool you're standing in is hip deep and a little warmer than the river and waterfall to the west. The waterfall is loud, the water splashing all around you at it hurls its way from the river into this pool below. It doesn't look like there's any chance of you moving back to the west with the drop being so steep from the falls, but a muddy shore lies to the south and it looks like heavy vegetation lies beyond. The walls are the same black rock seen throughout most of this underground cave system and the ceiling is high above you, far beyond your reach. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45228}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45230}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45230}{0}{<228>}{The Zoo of Death (se,n)}{<228>* *<088>}{        Thick, tangled vegetation surrounds you. The wet leaves and twisting vines slap at you as you move about, stinging your skin. It seems Humperdinck has created an underground jungle, complete with trees, a myriad types of plants, and if the other portions of this zoo are any indication, some type of dangerous predator nearby. Slick mud squelches underfoot and the humidity is nearly unbearable. To the north lies the shore of a subterranean pool and the jungle continues further to the southeast. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45229}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45231}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45231}{0}{<228>}{The Zoo of Death (w,nw)}{<228>* *<088>}{         The buzzing of insects drones in your ears as you make your way through the leafy vegetation of this underground jungle. Stalks of various shades of green rise from the muddy terrain, spreading out in brilliant fans of foliage that drip moisture, creating a humidity in the air that's almost thick enough to cut with a knife. The mud underfoot sticks to your feet, squelching as you move about, giving away your location to any nearby predators. It looks like a break in the wilderness lies to the west where you can make out the edge of what looks to be a rocky outcrop. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45230}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45232}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45232}{0}{<238>}{The Zoo of Death (d,e)}{<238>^ ^<088>}{        You stand atop rocky ground, much like the walls and ceiling that surround you. This portion of the underground caves is bare of any false habitat. It is nothing but the craggy stone that lies beneath the grounds of Lotharon's Castle. Every sound you make echoes off the dark walls and high-pitched ceiling, eerily reminding you of your lonely existence within this subterranean nightmare. To the east lies a jungle of vegetation and just in front of you is a steep drop off the rock and down into a sand-filled pit. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45231}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45233}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45233}{0}{}{The Zoo of Death (s)}{ }{     Soft golden sand lies beneath your feet and spreads out in all directions. This pit appears to have been naturally formed between the steep rock face that surrounds it on all sides. The only means of getting out of it that you can see is to the south where the rock looks a little more scalable. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45234}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45234}{0}{<248>}{The Zoo of Death (d,sw)}{<248>% %<088>}{      Standing atop the dark rock of the cave system, you see that this portion of the zoo is barren of any other feature save one. Bat guano. The rock walls and floor are covered in the stuff. Dried, light-colored bat excrement. The odor is stale and putrid, enough to urge you to retch. Down below you lies a sand-filled pit and to the southwest there appears to be some type of huge nest. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45233}{n}{down}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45236}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45233}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45235}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45234}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45236}{0}{<238>}{The Zoo of Death (e,ne)}{<238># ]<088>}{      This nest is one gigantic collection of straw and debris. It must be at least eight feet in diameter and over five feet in height. Scraps of cloth and various types of bones litter the nest, apparently the remains of previous unfortunates that found their way here. Feathers cling to the straw where the nest's inhabitant shed them. Rock walls border the nest in all directions but to the northeast and the east. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45234}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45237}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45237}{0}{<148>}{The Zoo of Death (e,w)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{       A narrow but swift moving underground stream runs through the cave. It disappears under a large nest of straw to the west and heads towards what appears to be a small pool to the east. The cave is quite narrow, not much wider than the stream itself. The sound of the rushing water echoes along the dark walls and ceiling, creating a rather disturbing effect of disorientation. Which way heads out of this place or are you stuck here forever? }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45236}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45238}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45238}{0}{<148>}{The Zoo of Death (se)}{<148>~ ~<088>}{       You're immersed in a freezing cold pool of water. It's deep. You'd guess probably 40 feet or more. The water is dark, no light filtering in from above, nothing to see above the surface but the black rock walls and ceiling of the cave. It appears this is where the underground stream dumps out, disappearing into some deep hole far beneath you. The water is so cold, your limbs start to feel numb. You might want to leave this place as soon as possible. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45239}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45239}{0}{}{The Pit of Despair (u)}{ }{         This underground workroom appears to have been cut directly out of the rock lying beneath the castle grounds. Various ropes and pulleys hang from the ceiling and walls, machinery of all types lining the walls beneath them. Candelabra stand in the corners, providing enough light to illuminate this dreary place and a winding staircase leads up into the darkness above. A beat-up wooden desk stands in one corner of the room and the rest of the floor is taken up by a huge contraption that resembles a waterwheel attached to a bench with hoses and suction cups hanging above it. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45238}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45240}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23732}{flip switch}{flip switch}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45240}{0}{<238>}{An Underground Stairwell (d)}{<238>. ^<088>}{       Steep stone stairs as black as night lead down into the depths of the earth below and seem to dead-end into a rock wall above. The slight glow of candlelight from the bottom of the stairs provides just enough light to see that this stairwell is very narrow, cut straight out of the rock that lies beneath Lotharon's Castle. The air tastes stale, as if this underground passage has been here for quite some time, but is rarely used. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
