R {45242}{0}{}{The Ship Revenge (enter,u)}{ }{           The hold of the ship is dim, the wood dark and only the light of a lantern hanging from an embedded hook in the wall giving off any illumination. The sound of the ship's hull creaking under the strain of the sea's weight echoes through the room along with the sound of water lapping up against the outside of the ship. The ceiling of the room is low, not much more than seven feet. It leaves this place feeling small and claustrophobic. Large black cannon balls are piled along one side of the room while the other wall is nearly hidden by stacks of wooden crates. The fore wall contains several racks of weapons and in the middle of it is a large door. Carved into the door is a single word. 'Roberts'. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45243}{enter}{enter}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45245}{fore disembark}{fore disembark}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {23798}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45243}{n}{unlock door; open door; enter}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45243}{0}{}{The Ship Revenge (exit)}{ }{          Roberts' Quarters below deck of the ship Revenge are modest but well kept. Lanterns hang on each wall to provide adequate reading light. A bunk lies against the starboard wall, while bookshelves, a desk, and chair are on the port wall. Charts and maps are hung on the walls in several places depicting the local waterways and shorelines. Piles of papers and scrolls sit on the desk along with an inkwell and quill pen. The desk and shelves are made of walnut as is the chair with its leather seat and back. The bunk is neatly made, covered with a navy colored blanket and a white down pillow. A chest lies at the foot of the bed between it and the door back out of the room. }{The Princess Bride}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
