R {45446}{0}{}{Middle Bridge (w,e)}{ }{     A stone arch bridge that used to be at this site has been replaced with a modern-day four-lane highway bridge.  Beneath the road the waters of Antietam Creek swirl downstream to the south.  The Union's Fifth Corps crossed the original Middle Bridge during the afternoon of September 17, 1862, marching west towards the town of Sharpsburg. }{Antietam Battlefield}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
