R {45451}{0}{}{General McClellan's Headquarters (s)}{ }{    On top of a grassy hill sits a red brick house.  The home was owned by the Pry family, but was commissioned by George McClellan for use as the Union headquarters during the battle.  It is now operated as an annex to the National Museum of Civil War Medicine. }{Antietam Battlefield}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
