R {45455}{0}{}{Cow Pasture (w,s)}{ }{     You pick your way carefully across the pasture, avoiding any gifts left behind by the farm animals.  The persistent manure smell would be barely tolerable if only the sun were not amplifying the stench.  A family of dairy cows graze upon a patch of grass uphill to the west of you.  The pasture continues downhill to the south. }{Antietam Battlefield}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45454}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45452}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45456}{0}{}{Smoketown Road (s,w)}{ }{    You are at the north-eastern corner of Antietam Battlefield.  The broad branches of tall maple trees hang over Smoketown Road.  The tree coverage thins further west.  Smoketown Road runs south along a glen past a stone monument. }{Antietam Battlefield}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
