R {45491}{0}{<238>}{An empty runway (w,e)}{<238>|||<088>}{      This stretch of concrete seems too short to be an aircraft runway, but that's undoubtedly what it is\; the painted lines and symbols and the pattern of rubber scorch are proof enough. No aircraft are in sight, but the massive hangar to the west would seem the most likely place to find one. The basin curves abruptly upwards to the south, cutting off all further travel in that direction. }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14277}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45497}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45492}{0}{<238>}{The exercise yard (e,w)}{<238>, .<088>}{    This expansive field is neatly divided into sporting areas. A soccer field is marked out and a netted section for volleyball can be seen. To the east and north lies a large, sprawling building, bordering the field. It looks like the living area of the base. }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {14277}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45493}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45493}{0}{<248>}{The recreation room (w,n)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{     This recreation room is well stocked with all the necessities of active relaxation. The room is sectioned off into living areas\; a television, surrounded by a semicircle of reclining chairs\; a pool table, dart board and vending machine\; a fully optioned kitchenette. You hardly know where to begin. }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45492}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45494}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45494}{0}{<248>}{The barracks (s,w)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{     This narrow room must serve as the base's barracks. Twelve bed spaces in two orderly rows. Each space consists of a single bed and a footlocker\; a cloth covered divider separating it from the next. You can continue south to the rec room or head west into the hygiene facilities. }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45493}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45495}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45495}{0}{<248>}{The hygiene facilities (e,w)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{       Tile and glass abound in this sparkling clean hygiene facility. A bank of four toilet cubicles lie against one wall, the opposite wall sporting several curious attachments, similar to hand-dryers but more complex. A row of lockers with mirrored surfaces stretch towards an unusually high-tech shower which stands alone but significantly in the corner. A doorway leads east to the barracks and you can head outside to the west. }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45494}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45490}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45496}{0}{<248>}{The operations suite (s,e,w)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{          This must be the operations suite. Everything is black, the surfaces are covered in a dark material that has the appearance of woven metal. The northern wall is taken up by a large screen displaying an image of the planet\; constellations of satellites cluster over continental America, others with circling halos of trails in polar and equatorial orbits. Two computer stations occupy the floor space. The larger station sits in the center of the room, facing the display, while the smaller station is positioned against the southern wall. Doorways lead west and east from this room, with the exit to the compound to the south.  }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45490}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45501}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45502}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45497}{0}{<238>}{The hangar (e,n)}{<238>|||<088>}{     Your footsteps echo loudly as you move around the hangar. There are bays in here for a dozen or more aircraft. A lone Apache helicopter gunship occupies this hangar, seemingly filling the cavernous space with its brutal presence. Maintenance equipment, fuel tanks and workbenches are arrayed along the walls. An exit to the north leads onwards. }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45491}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45498}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45498}{0}{<248>}{The storage depot (s,e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{    This small, narrow room is lined floor to ceiling with shelving. This would appear to be the storage area for the base's maintenance and ordnance supplies. Shelves run eastwards along both walls, leaving generous maneuvering space through the middle.  }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45497}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45499}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45499}{0}{<248>}{The generator room (w,e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{     This room hums with energy\; a low thrumming vibrates up through your feet, settling in your back teeth to create a visceral feeling of power. The vibrating originates from a massive generator that occupies most of the room. A bank of complicated looking gauges occupy the northern wall. A small door continues to the east. }{Satellite Tracking Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45498}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45490}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
