R {45742}{0}{<238>}{The Tower of Vindaes (n,e)}{<238>] [<088>}{                     -=< The Hanging Cage >=- To the west of the entrance, the floor is littered with bits of straw and rust. Suspended from the ceiling is a cylindrical cage with wide spacing between its bars. The cage is large enough for a tall man, but the space between the bars would not permit a small woman to escape. To the north is the stairwell. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45704}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45743}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45743}{0}{<238>}{The Tower of Vindaes (u,e,s)}{<238>] [<088>}{                        -=< Stairwell Entrance >=- From this corner of the room, there is access to the covered stairwell that curves up and around the tower. Thick stone walls separate it from the rest of the tower, perhaps so that prisoners being marched up or down to their dooms could hear the cries and wails of the tortured without being able to see what was happening. Here on the main floor of the tower, opposite the entrance, the stairwell begins its circular path. But, to the south and around to the door, the wall is just as thick... Could there be something hidden in there? }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45706}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45744}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45742}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45744}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (d,u,e,s)}{ }{                       -=< Stairwell Entrance >=- From this corner of the room, there is access to the covered stairwell that curves up and around the tower. Thick stone walls separate it from the rest of the tower. Surveying the large room that is the second floor, a few tables can be seen, littered with items. To the east, ropes hang from the ceiling, the south is built with a thick beam across the corner, and to the southeast is a very inconspicuous chair. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45743}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45745}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45746}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45747}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45745}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (u,d,e,s)}{ }{                      -=< Stairwell Entrance >=- From this corner of the room, there is access to the covered stairwell that curves up and around the tower. Thick walls separate the stairs from this large room which holds only three implements. In one corner is a huge table, in another a large wagonwheel-like item, and another holds the rack. There is a door in the stairwell preventing passage further up the tower.  }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45744}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45749}{u}{unlock door; open door; u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45750}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45751}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45746}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (s,w)}{ }{                      -=< Implements of Ropes >=- High overhead, there are three anchoring loops built into the corner where the massive stone walls meet. Through each loop a rope is hung, tied at waist level to a securing pin. The free ends of the ropes hang limply in the corner, awaiting a torture adept to decide the use they will be put to. Hanging on the wall you see a collar, wrist restraints, and a waist restraint. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45744}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45748}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45747}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (e,n)}{ }{                    -=< Suspensions from the Ceiling >=- Across this corner of the room is a thick wooden beam, eight feet above the floor. From a hook on the wall hang various lengths of rope and chain, as well as a bag large enough to stuff a man into and a saw nearly six feet long. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45744}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45748}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45748}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (w,n)}{ }{                     -=< Implements of the Chair >=- A sturdy wooden chair sits in this corner, looking quite uncomfortable. There are straps for securing someone in place on various parts of the chair, but all torture implements are displayed on a small table beside it. You see a collar, a fork-like item, a pair of thumbscrews, and a set of needles and pliers. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45747}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45746}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45749}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (d)}{ }{                        -=< Vindaes' Chamber >=- The chamber that has housed the many men and women who have worn the hood of Vindaes over the years is very bare. A bed rests against the wall, covered in linen sheets, with a small table beside it. The floor's cold stones are covered with several thick woolen rugs, woven into intricate designs. In the back corner, next to the table, is a tall iron candlestand with a dozen thick white candles burning. Over the bed is window, four cubits in width. The room is peaceful and friendly, a strange contrast to the tower itself. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45745}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45750}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (s,w)}{ }{                      -=< Implements for the Table >=- This room is dedicated to some of the more horrific and bloody torture devices in the Tower of Vindaes. In this corner stands a table of oak as thick as a large man and rises as high as his waist. There are straps to secure someone to the table, and a small stand at the foot with a couple of implements upon it. Against the wall rests a large slab of granite and several weights. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45745}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45752}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45751}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (e,n)}{ }{                         -=< The Wheel >=- This unassuming corner of the tower might just as well be the workshop of a wainwright as it is a place of torture and death -- were it not for the blood stains upon the wagon-like wheel resting on the ground. Beside the wheel, propped against the wall is a large sledgehammer. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45745}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45752}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45752}{0}{}{The Tower of Vindaes (w,n)}{ }{                           -=< The Rack >=- This deadly floor of the tower houses one of the most well-known and well-feared devices of torture: the rack. This incarnation is an oaken frame, nearly ten feet long, with ropes attached to the rollers at either end. The loose ends of the ropes terminate in knotted loops large enough to slip a hand or foot. }{Tower of Vindaes}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45751}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45750}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45753}{0}{<148>}{In a sweet smelling bakery (u,out)}{<118>|<138>|<148>|<088>}{           The bakery is full of people jostling and crowding their way in to buy some freshly baked goods. A large glass counter serves both to display many of the finely baked breads and pastries as well as provide a barrier between the ever pressing crowd of customers and the tired-eyed bakery personnel. A delicious aroma fills the small space within, setting your mouth watering and you decide it must be one of the best smells in all of Westersea. A colorful mat hangs from the northern wall, the once vibrant colors dampened by a light dusting of flour that has settled on its surface. In the northeastern corner hulks a large stone oven, its gaping mouth ablaze as the most recent batch of buns bakes within its belly.  }{The City of Westersea}{westersea_water}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {5836}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {5836}{n}{out}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45754}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45754}{0}{}{In the private room of the baker (d)}{ }{         The private quarters of the bakery owner is much like any other living quarters. A broad bed occupies one corner, the lumpy mattress visible below the colorful patchwork quilt that lies atop it. Several articles of clothing lie strewn across the floor, apparently never making it to the wicker laundry hamper nearby. A small window sits in the southern wall giving the baker view to the city outside. Mounted to one of the walls is a peculiar looking metallic basin with pipes and other oddities attached. In the northwestern corner is the small stairway that leads back down to the shop below. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45753}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45755}{0}{}{You drift under the old stone bridge...}{ }{}{Tunnels of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45756}{l}{l}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45756}{0}{}{Under (s)}{ }{      Atop a pile of rocks, the bridge suspends above you, magnifying the sounds of the water as the river eddies and gurgles its way past the rocks and on down the cavern. The rocks look natural enough though their placement seems a bit odd. The pile extends west from the eastern wall to about one third of the way across the river. It seems the only way to get back up is to continue south with the flow. }{Tunnels of the Rohm Giddor}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45757}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
