R {45762}{0}{<238>}{Crevice (w,ne)}{<238>] [<088>}{     The gurgling stream echoes hollowly through this rocky subterranean cavern.  Not only are you still going deeper, but now the surface is also rising as you move toward the eastern hill.  It is becoming very dim and as the crevice turns a bit here it becomes too dark to make out anything that lies ahead. }{Crevice in the Hills}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45760}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45763}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45763}{0}{<238>}{Crevice (sw,e)}{<238>] [<088>}{     The daylight above becomes just a memory as outcroppings on the walls obscure what little light had been filtering down.  The stream stops abruptly here as it dives into several cracks in the otherwise solid bedrock.  There is not much space to maneuver and the walls seem to be absorbing the light, allowing little to be seen ahead. }{Crevice in the Hills}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45762}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45764}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45764}{0}{<238>}{Crevice (w,e)}{<238>] [<088>}{      Here is blackness so intense that it seems almost viscous...or perhaps it is.  The light you carry disperses an arm's length away, as if it were trying to illuminate a deep and narrow mine shaft.  Navigating mostly by touch, you find the ground here to be smooth and dry, and the walls are now close enough to make passing someone going the other direction rather difficult. }{Crevice in the Hills}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45763}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45765}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45765}{0}{<238>}{Crevice (w,se)}{<238>] [<088>}{       This room is shadowed in darkness, except where brilliant beams of light illuminate your immediate surroundings from above.  Excluding the continuation of the crevice and the cleft through which you came, the walls here are made of perfectly smooth stone and rounded into a cylinder. Far above, the stone gives way to packed soil smoothed in a similar fashion. With the exception of what appears to be the remains of a carriage, the floor is bare and unnaturally flat. }{Crevice in the Hills}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45764}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45766}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45766}{0}{<238>}{Crevice (nw)}{<238>] [<088>}{      The ground has taken on a somewhat sticky texture in this dank corner of the crevice.  Just ahead the passage finally comes to an end as the shifted rock forms a wall that climbs out of sight and into the darkness. Strewn about the area are numerous white strands that appear to be part of a web.  A web much larger than any ordinary spider could weave. }{Crevice in the Hills}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45765}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

