R {45778}{0}{<248>}{Ramp (sw,e)}{<248>% %<088>}{       The cavern widens slightly as it climbs upward and curves to the southwest.  The floor is somewhat steep but it levels off some in either direction.  The high ceiling arches over your head and is about three times the height of the skeleton's ribcage at its peak.  Pieces of the skeleton have broken off and lay on the floor, but the wide gaps between the bones leave plenty of room to maneuver, both on the ground and in the air. }{Loft}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45775}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45779}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {45779}{0}{<248>}{Den (ne)}{<248>% %<088>}{       The cave widens even further as it comes to an end.  Once likely the dragon's den, it is easy to imagine this place full of treasures.  Alas, it is now all but empty.  There are, however, a few signs of more recent occupancy.  Bits of small animals and other remains litter one section of the floor, and what is left of a small cooking fire smolders nearby.  The skull of a dragon has been moved from its skeleton and rests at the far end of the cavern. }{Loft}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
