R {46268}{0}{}{The Barracks (nw)}{ }{           Rows of bunk beds are the dominate feature of this room. A smell of mildew assaults your senses from every direction. Old clothes are strewn everywhere as well as sheets and pillows. The disarray that everything is in leads you to believe the castle was attacked at an inopportune time, either at night or during some event. Rows of chests line the foot of each bunk bed and sacks hang down from the posts of the top bunks. There are no windows to the outside world from here, most likely to prevent sabotage from outside forces. The walls are lined with shelves and hooks to hold various pieces of armour and weapons. Everything seems to have been stripped from the walls during the final battle to defend this castle. }{3Kraft Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46265}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46269}{0}{}{In the Crapper (w)}{ }{     This room is very small and cramped. A round hole on a wooden box with some straw in a pile beside it are the only features. A strong odor is wafting up from the hole. A small candle rests on a ledge attached to the wall to provide some light during night-time deposits. Every so often you see a fly buzz up out of the hole. }{3Kraft Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46265}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46270}{0}{}{Stairs Down (sw,stairs)}{ }{    The floor drops away quickly, swallowed up by a stairway leading into complete darkness. There is something decidedly ominous about what might lie below this castle. Not a single thing is in this room that might distract somebody from being unsettled. }{3Kraft Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
