R {46287}{0}{}{The Royal Bedroom (ne)}{ }{      A once lavish bedroom now lies looted and ransacked almost beyond recognition. A gigantic king sized bed-frame stands against one wall with no mattress, sheets or even a headboard left. The curtains from the windows have been removed, and the carpet has been pulled up leaving the stone floor bare. The only luxury that has been left in the room is a picture that hangs above the bed. }{3Kraft Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46286}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46288}{0}{}{The Throne Room (n)}{ }{       A domed ceiling with artwork on it reaches over head to shape this regal looking chamber. A flowing red carpet leads toward two large wooden thrones with bright red cushions. Chairs are aligned along the sides of the room for people to observe the royal proceedings of the day. Armour stands, long since looted, stand at either side of the entrance to the room and banners of the royal family droop down from the ceiling. }{3Kraft Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46286}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46289}{0}{}{The Head Maid's Room (n)}{A}{      The head maid's quarters is located upstairs away from the rest of the servants. The furnishings are much higher quality here, a wooden dresser, a vanity mirror, a wooden bed and a dressing shade. This room also has a window with flowing white curtains, a rug on the floor and an oil lamp on a small table. The northern door leads back out into the hallway. }{3Kraft Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
