R {46321}{0}{}{<*<*Sorrowful Granite Slab*>*> (ne,n,e)}{ }{          To your utter dismay you've stumbled onto a slab of granite on which rests the corpse of a unicorn foal.  Its eyes are open and liquid, calling out in a last cry for help.  The horn that would normally decorate its equine forehead has been hacked off, probably by a poacher.  The golden hide shows an arrow that looks like would have hit the heart.  Oddly enough, no carrion eater has touched the carcass and it appears to be immune from rotting.  An eternal reminder of the horrible loss of life and innocence.  The trees around the corpse continuously weep flower petals which cover the ground with a layer of pink and white.  All of nature will mourn this loss for all eternity. }{3Kraft}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
