R {46489}{0}{}{In a large dining room (w,n)}{ }{      You've reached what once used to be the dining room. A tilting table is in the centre and several broken chairs litter the floor. Old wooden frames cover the cracked walls and you draw the conclusion that they either used to house paintings or tapestries. Glancing towards the inner ceiling you see a faded painting of a sunset. In the center, where the sun should be, is a big gaping hole. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46484}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {46490}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46490}{0}{}{In a barren room (w,e)}{ }{     Located directly adjacent to the dining room is the kitchen. However, there is no clear evidence that this used to be one. Broken wooden barrels cover most of the floor and mounted on the southern wall you see several small shelves. Standing against the northern wall is a large table.  }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46489}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {46491}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46491}{0}{}{In an old kitchen storage (e)}{ }{     This almost closet sized room must have once been the kitchen storage. Several mouldy sacks cover the floor and as you step closer you notice a faint musty odour which seems to linger in the air. There are no windows in any wall and only a small opening leads back to the kitchen. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46490}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46492}{0}{}{On the upper floor of an old mansion (w,s,e,n)}{ }{     You're in a four way crossing. The hallway continues off in the eastern, western and southern directions. Nothing really strikes you as particularly interesting and the dark empty mood is starting to affect you. It's almost as if you can hear the building itself cry out in despair.  }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46488}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {46493}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {46494}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {46495}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46493}{0}{}{On the upper floor of an old mansion (w,e)}{ }{     This part of the corridor appears to be even gloomier than the others. It's difficult to pinpoint exactly why but you get the nagging feeling that something is very wrong. As you glance about, you notice that the flakes of paint hanging from the walls oddly remind you of dried blood. If they were red the illusion would be complete. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46492}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {46496}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46494}{0}{}{On the upper floor of an old mansion (e,w)}{ }{     You're on the top floor of the large mansion. The hallway continues in a straight eastern to western direction. Several frames hang empty on the walls, the paintings therein having long since rotted away. The floor is old and cracked and and you should probably watch your feet so you don't fall through.  }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46492}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {46498}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46495}{0}{}{In a barren room (s)}{ }{      Immediately as you enter the room you think you can hear the sound of children playing. You peer rather confusedly around the room but fail to pinpoint the source of the sound. The room itself is almost completely barren. Only broken pieces of odd looking wooden furniture litters the northeastern corner. A large window sits in the northern wall providing the room with ample daylight. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46492}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {46496}{0}{}{On the upper floor of an old mansion (e,n)}{ }{    The drab corridor continues along the upper floor of the house. Here, a dusty window is fitted in the western wall and beneath it sits a fairly large window ledge. Once, it might have acted as a bench but no one has been here in ages. }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46493}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
