R {47314}{0}{<278>}{Temple of Qiao Hou (se,u,n,e)}{<278>.@.<088>}{         You have stepped into an expansive chamber, a domed circular room approximately thirty meters in diameter.  The floor is level, constructed of worked stone, and covered with what must be centuries of accumulation of grime.  The domed stone ceiling is draped in cobwebs.  The air is stale, smelling faintly of must and decay.  Three old metal braziers are bolted to the floor around the circumference of the room.  Stone archways frame passages leading north and east\; a shallow, narrow staircase descends southeast.  A crack in the west wall reveals a passage leading up and out of the room. }{Temple of Qiao Hou}{temple_of_qiao}{}{}{1.000}{1}
