R {47610}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 1 (page2,withdraw)}{ }{                   	Chapter 1: Movement Of Your Character One of the first things you should familiarize yourself with is how to swiftly move about rooms here on Three Kingdoms (3K).  As you may have noticed, each room you have entered lists 'obvious exits'. These are directions in which to move your character.  Each direction will move you to a corresponding room that attaches to the one you are currently in. Most rooms use cardinal directions (directions on a compass).  For example 'north', 'east', 'south', 'west'.  for such directions, you may either type the direction name out fully (example: 'north') to move in a northerly direction, or you can simply type 'n'.  You can type the common abbreviations for cardinal directions as seen on most compasses to move about rooms that use them (examples: n, e, s, w, w, ne, sw, se, nw). However, other rooms, such as this one, use non-standard exits.  The exits here are 'withdraw' and 'page2'.  Withdraw will return you to the forest cove within Newbie Land, while typing 'page2' will move you to the second page of this newbie tutorial.  Which direction will you go? }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
