R {47611}{0}{<088>}{Newbie Lore:Page 2}{ }{                    	Chapter 1: Movement Of Your Character Very good!  Had page two actually been 'bugged', you would have been transported to the City of Pinnacle.  Since it was not, it brought you here.  If you use the 'bugfree' command and the room is not bugged, you would normally receive a message saying as much.  You would then be faced with three remaining options. The room might have a hidden exit that must be located by interacting with something within it, it might indeed be meant as a trap, or something beyond the rescue of the 'bugfree' command might have caused an error preventing any exits from being created.  After you have exhausted your energy trying to find a way out, you may send a tell to an online wizard and ask if the room is bugged.  If they reply that it is working as it's suppose to, you may have to quit the game and login again to leave the room.  Please do not skip to sending a wizard a tell immediately after discovery. Lastly, there are items that may allow you to 'teleport' to various places on the mud.  The Necromancer guild even has an ability that can teleport people from great distances across 3K.  These are intricacies you will discover more about as you continue your adventuring here online. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
