R {47616}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 4 (page5,page3)}{ }{                       	Chapter 2: Character Help Files The most important command for a newcomer is the 'help' command. Three Kingdoms has an extensive library of help files.  Each file was written as an instructional aid for players to explain how many of the commands here operate.  There are also files that provide information regarding general game-play (terms, rules, and tutorial aid). To access the help system, you must type 'help'.  Typing it by itself (with no words/arguments following it) will display a menu with various starting topics.  One such example is the 'General Topics (general)' that gets listed.  The word or phrase within the parentheses is a sub-category, in this case, 'general'. You may then type 'help general' to display a list of topics within that sub-category.  A very important topic within this sub-category is labeled 'faq'.  You may then choose to pull up that help file by typing 'help faq'. It is not necessary to page through each menu to pull up a help file.  The menu is there to simply list out existing files(topics) for you to read through.  As you continue this tutorial, we recommend you use the 'help' command to find out more information regarding the topic being covered, or if you have any questions regarding any command. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
