R {47619}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 6 (page7,page5)}{ }{                 	Chapter 3: Character Core Commands The 'search' command is an advanced form of 'examine' or 'look'. Some rooms may have hidden clues about how to proceed to the next one detailed within their description.  Other rooms may have certain objects hidden within that require a search to find. Each room has an inventory.  Objects, NPCs and other players in the room are listed there, just below the obvious exits. You have an inventory as well, type 'i' to see your own.  There you store the items you have picked up while adventuring around the realms.  This leads us to our next set of commands. The 'get' and 'take' commands allow you to pick up objects that you see inside the room.  Most objects are seen within the room inventory, but others might be hinted at within a description. So let's tie all of this in, shall we?  Let's pretend that our tree is in this room as well.   Examine it for clues, then search it to see if you find anything.  If you do, follow the hints and we'll see if you get rewarded for it. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
