R {47621}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 7 (page8,page6)}{ }{                       	Chapter 3: Character Core Commands You are doing quite well to have reached this far.  By now, you should be somewhat familiar with how to interact with a room and some of the key commands used to play.  There are only a few more core interactive commands we will cover, and then we'll move on to another topic.  They are as follows: give, drop, keep and unkeep. 1. The 'give' command allows you to give up an object from your own    inventory to another NPC or player in the same room.  Type 'give object    to person' (where object is what you are giving away, and person is the    the NPC or player to whom you are giving it) to accomplish this.  You    may wish to type 'help give' if you have any further questions. 2. The 'drop' command will enable you to drop something out of your    inventory by typing 'drop item' (where item is the object you specify).    There are two main reasons why dropping an item might fail.  It may    either be kept, or there is something 'magical' about the item that    prevents you from doing so.  To prevent dropping an item, you have the    option to 'keep' it.  Next, the 'keep' and 'unkeep' commands. 3. Typing 'keep item' will prevent you from either accidentally dropping    it when you type 'drop all' or selling it to a store.  You may also    alternatively type 'unkeep item' to allow you to move it out of your    inventory.  Keep in mind however, that most objects do not save when    the mud reboots or you quit out.  So even if it's kept, an item may    be lost upon next login. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
