R {47623}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 8 (page9,page7)}{ }{                      	Chapter 3: Character Core Commands It is important for you to know that you are not alone here on 3K. After all, what fun would a game be if you were the only one who played it?  The next few commands we will discuss are general who and character information utility commands. 1. Typing 'who' will give you a list of all currently online players.    You may also type 'who wiz' to see which wizards (game programmers)    are online as well. 2. Typing 'players' is yet another way to view the same list with a    slightly different view.  'Players' will show people listed    according to their guilds. 3. Finally, another list command is the 'finger' command.  This will    either allow you to pull up a list of currently online players,    or it will allow you to pull up information on any individual    player (online or off). Typing 'finger' by itself will show all    online characters.  Typing 'finger name' (where name is the name    of the player you are looking up) will show you their individual    information. There are many other ways to have each list sorted.  You should read the help files on each of these commands to get a better understanding of how they operate.  Try to pull up an individual character's profile before proceeding to the next page. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
