R {47629}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 9 (page10,page8)}{ }{                     	Chapter 4: Character Communication Now that you realize you are not the sole player here on the mud, perhaps it's time to interact a bit with others.  We will now discuss the various communication methods.  The commands being covered are 'say', 'tell', and 'shout'. 1. The 'say' command is a way to broadcast a message to everything in    the same room.  If you type 'say message' (where message is what you    wish to send), you will have essentially told everything in the    room 'this message'. 2. The 'shout' command acts much like 'say'.  There are only a couple    of differences between the two.  Instead of speaking to just the    room you are in, you will be in effect, talking to every player who    is currently logged in.  The message you shout should also be 'clean',    and free from demeaning remarks.  Do not shout obscenities or any    other bigotry, racial slurs etc.  This ability also has some other    restrictions.  Read the help file on 'shout' for more information. 3. The 'tell' command is a form of private communication.  This is a    message sent to a person you specify.  Only they will receive the    message you supply.  For example, if you wish to tell the character    Bob hello, you would type 'tell bob hello'.  Sounds pretty easy    doesn't it?  Why don't you introduce yourself to someone. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
