R {47631}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 10 (page11,page9)}{ }{                  	Chapter 4: Character Communication Other help files you should read pertaining to the 'tell', 'shout' and 'say' communication commands are: 'tellb' (allows blocking of tells), and 'earmuffs' (allows toggling off shouts).  Familiarize yourself with them.  They may become useful in the future. Newbies also have a unique command available to themselves and other designated players on Three Kingdoms.  This is called the 'newb' command.  This is a chat line meant for newcomers, such as yourself, to ask any questions about how to play this game.  To use it, simply type 'newb message' (where message is what you wish to say). To list who is currently listening to the newbie chat line, you need only to type 'newb -w'.  As previously mentioned, not only newbies have access to this communication command.  More experienced players who have volunteered their time to helping you understand how to play also have the ability to speak on it. Drop them a line, if you haven't already, and ask them any questions you might have up to this point.  Read the help file on the 'newb' command for further information on its uses. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
