R {47633}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 11 (page12,page10)}{ }{                  	Chapter 4: Character Communication Although there are various other ways in which to communicate to other players, you have learned the core commands for basic interaction with them.  The last thing we will discuss within this section is called 'souls'. Souls are in actuality pre-made 'feelings' that you can type.  Some can be directed to other players, while others can only be seen by people in the room with you.  Type 'feelings'.  That command tells you how many are currently available to you.  You will notice there are simply too many to discuss individually. Typing 'soul <letter>' will list all soul commands you can use that start with the specified <letter (a-z)>.  One example of a particular soul is 'smile'.  This soul can either be used by itself by typing 'smile', or you can use it on someone else\; type 'smile who' (where who is the person you wish to smile at). You may turn souls on and off by typing 'soul on' or 'soul off'.  We suggest you read the help file on 'trs'.  That is another command involving soul functionality. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
