R {47635}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 12 (page13,page11)}{ }{                   	Chapter 5: Character Advancement Welcome to the Character Advancement section of this tutorial.  This is where most people like to be.  Advancing your character is not that difficult.  There is only one primary method\; to kill.  Each time you kill an NPC (monster), you will gain what is called 'experience' for it.  As you increase your experience, you will have the opportunity to spend those 'experience points' on either raising your primary level, or character stats. Levels are sequential.  You start at level 1 and go upwards.  To see how much experience is required for each level, type 'levels'.  Every level you will have the opportunity to raise a few stats.  It is highly recommended that you do raise the maximum allowable stats that the level will allow. There are six primary stats that each character has: strength (str), dexterity (dex), wisdom (wis), charisma (cha), intelligence (int), and constitution (con).  You may see a list of your character stats by typing 'score'.  You will have to figure out intuitively how advancing these stats affect your character.  Type 'score' now to view your character information. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
