R {47636}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 13 (page14,page12)}{ }{                     	Chapter 5: Character Advancement You may advance your stats and levels within a pre-designated area. These rooms are most often called 'advancement rooms', as the name might suggest.  There is an advancement room in Newbieland with a sign explaining how to advance your level or individual stats.  There is also another room designated for adventurers like yourself located in Pinnacle, just up from the reception area. So you might be now saying 'So just tell me how to fight!'.  We will now cover gaining experience through combat.  However, there are a few commands and terms you will need to know prior to just going bananas on an NPC (monster). Hitpoints (hp) and Spellpoints (sp) are your two core power pools. While hitpoints concentrate on your physical health, spellpoints are most often associated with your mental fitness.  If you lose all of your hitpoints, you will die.  However, if you lose all of your spellpoints, you will not. When you die, you will leave behind a corpse within the room where you were killed.  It will have all of the items you had on you as well as any money.  Your 'ghost' however, will then be transported to Death's room.  You will need to return to get your belongings back.  Read the help on 'death' for more information. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
