R {47641}{0}{}{Newbie Lore:Page 15 (page16,page14)}{ }{                         	Chapter 5: Character Advancement Combat as an Adventurer is not that complex.  Once you reach level five, you may choose to join a guild.  Upon joining a guild, your choice and style of how you fight will be dependent on which guild you chose.  However, you should first get orientated with basic combat as a newbie. There are four general combat commands to learn.  You will use these throughout your time on 3K. 1. The 'wimpy' command allows you to set a certain percentage of    health before you will attempt to flee from the room.  If you type    'wimpy' by itself, it will show you how to set it up.  If you type    'wimpy 0', you will then fight until you kill the NPC or die.  If,    for example, you type 'wimpy 50', you will attempt to flee at 50%    of your hitpoints. 2. To see what your wimpy is currently set to, type 'score'.  Examine    the help file on 'wimpy' for more detailed information. 3. Type 'hp' to see your 'health bar'  It will show you how many    hitpoints and spellpoints you have.  To toggle showing your    healthbar each round you are in combat, type 'autohp'.  If you use    the Portal client to play this game, you may also have to type    'forcehp' to show your hpbar each round. 4. Lastly, the 'kill' command allows you to initiate a fight with an    NPC.  You need only type 'kill NPC' (where NPC is the name of the    creature you wish to attack).  If you feel ready enough to give    combat a chance, type 'ready', Otherwise you may continue on. }{Newbieland}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
