R {47687}{0}{}{Along the southern edge of a war-torn path (ne,sw,nw)}{ }{     The landscape returns to almost normal here from the burnt-out war-torn surroundings you have seen throughout this path.  The land here has begun to return to the forest that once surrounded this path. The trail of destruction continues to the northeast.  Craters seem to dot the landscape as far as you can see. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47685}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47689}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47690}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47688}{0}{}{The beginning of a trail to a worn down ruin (se,sw,nw)}{ }{     Ahead of you lies what's left of some kind of building.  The path you are on is surrounded by deep craters that still look rather fresh as does most of the destruction in the area. Behind you lies the forest and its eerie tranquility.  Turning toward the building, you begin to wonder if it's still inhabited. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47685}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47690}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47691}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47689}{0}{}{In the beginnings of the forest (ne)}{ }{   This appears to be the edge of the destructive path.  The forest seems to almost regain some of its majesty here.  Trees make a thick wall that seems to block passage to the south and east. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47687}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47690}{0}{}{The scene of a recent battle (se,ne)}{ }{      This area is more littered than the rest of what you have seen.  The ground is almost completely covered with an assortment of mech parts.  Various mech cannons, missile turrets and other scrap metal have been scattered around.  Deep craters lie all about you.  Some of the craters are filled with the destroyed remains of missiles or whatever the missiles struck. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47687}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47688}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47691}{0}{}{Traveling up a mountain path (se,e)}{ }{    The mountain path takes quite a turn here almost doubling back on itself.  To your east a large pile of rubble blocks the path while to the southeast the trail continues on down the cliff.  High up on top of the peak the faint outline of a building is present. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47688}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47692}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47692}{0}{}{On a collapsed mountain path (w)}{ }{    The path directly in front of you seems to have taken a direct missile hit in a skirmish.  Rubble and large chunks of earth have caved in across the road making the path impassable.  The path continues on to the west with the pile of rubble blocking all eastern passage. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47691}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47693}{search rubble}{search rubble}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47693}{nw}{search rubble; northwest}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47693}{0}{}{A guard outpost before a command bunker (nw,se)}{ }{    Barbed wire and trenches line the road leading up to the bunker ahead. A covered platform off to the side of the road acts as a station for the behemoth mechanized guards.  A few craters and empty shell casings are a testament to the guardians' resolve. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47694}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47692}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47694}{0}{}{A scarred set of blast doors (nw,se)}{ }{     You stand in an archway before the remnants of a set of massive steel-plated blast doors.  A shattered control console is centered on the west wall of the archway.  Even the concrete slab below your feet is split in half under the weight of a massive intruder.  To the southeast is the path on which you entered. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47693}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47696}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47695}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {47693}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47696}{0}{}{An intersection (se,sw,ne)}{ }{      You stand in an intersection of halls leading off in various directions.  Just in front of you are the doors of an old elevator.  This room seems to be in decent condition with only minor structural damage apparent along the walls.  As with most of the compound there is no power going to any of the systems and only a faint light shines through from the entrance behind you. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47694}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47697}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47698}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47702}{nw}{search elevator; nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47697}{0}{}{A burnt out room in a corner of a ruined bunker (ne,nw)}{ }{     This is the southwest corner of what remains of the Clan Wolf bunker.  The walls contain slits that seem to have been used at one time for defense.  The room has scorch marks everywhere as well as a giant hole in the ceiling apparently from a direct missile hit.  Rubble and shards of the ceiling lie strewn about the floor. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47696}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47699}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47698}{0}{}{A corner room of a ruined bunker (sw,nw)}{ }{     This is the east corner of what remains of the Clan Wolf bunker, the walls contain slits that seem to have been used at one time for defense.  All along the floor there lay hundreds, maybe thousands of spent shell casings and jammed, worthless guns that were apparently used to fire on enemies when the base was under siege. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47696}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47700}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47699}{0}{}{A mess hall in a ruined bunker (se)}{ }{     This room has been designed more for humanoid-sized occupants.  The tables and chairs, while broken down and in bad need of repair, are built for rather average people.  The steel counters and shabby collection of dinnerware remind you exactly what toll these attacks have taken upon the occupants of this base. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47697}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47700}{0}{}{A darkened room in a ruined bunker (se)}{ }{    This room is almost completely dark.  Shattered and burnt-out lights hang above you.  This room looks as though it was completely stripped of anything it may have held.  The only things noticeable in this room are your own footsteps echoing off the walls. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47698}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47701}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {47696}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47702}{0}{}{An old elevator shaft in a ruined bunker (se)}{ }{     This elevator shaft has obviously seen better days.  The shaft below you has been boarded up, creating a makeshift floor on which you now stand.  The elevator itself is nowhere to be found.  Even the cables that once guided its ascent and descent have been removed.  The elevator doors lie partially closed to the southeast. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47696}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47703}{d}{search floor; climb down}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47704}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47703}{0}{}{The remains of a mech training hall (u)}{ }{      This room is all that is left of one of the great Clan Wolf training halls.  This is where all the trainees would come to be instructed on how best to face their foes in combat.  The room looks almost like a large garage with stripes and other traffic controlling directions painted on the ground to guide the warriors without incident in the close quarters. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47702}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47704}{0}{}{Commander Ford's office (d)}{ }{     This small office is apparently all that remains of the highest level of the bunker.  A desk, covered with papers lies before you and a map of the area hangs along the back wall.  Some pictures hang askew along the walls to your left and right in a vain attempt to brighten this drab office space. }{Codename: Kodiak}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47702}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47705}{0}{}{Landing Pad 6 (mirror)}{ }{    Surrounded by craters, this newly repaired landing pad is the jumping off point to Halfways space station. A large sign sits along the narrow path to the pad which is lit up with landing lights. A mirror leads back into the Newbie Tower. }{Halfway's Space Station}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
