R {47880}{0}{}{Royal Kitchen (e,se)}{ }{      Dust plums clouds your vision as you enter this room. However, once the dust settles you notice a large hearth with a half-circle opening is in-set into the outer wall.  The rest of the room is plain otherwise.  A long table with pots hanging above extends the length of the room.  Dull knives and other utensils are scattered about.  The is a swing door to the east. }{Town of Woonsocket}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {47878}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {47881}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {47881}{0}{}{Royal Dining Room (e,w)}{ }{      Passing through the threshold you notice this room has no dust at all. You can feel a slight breeze circulating the air.  The ceiling angles towards the middle and you notice a grating system at the top.  A dark stained table is in the middle of the room, with chairs all around it. Various paintings hang on the walls and seem to be ancestors of this castle. }{Town of Woonsocket}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
