R {48340}{0}{}{Cathedral (s,n)}{ }{       You stand inside the ruins of a once-great cathedral. Rows of pews lie broken all around you, stacked into piles or simply left to rot. Pale shafts of light beam down from holes in the ceiling, and are scattered by the rain into a prismatic glow as they pass through broken stained-glass windows, now barely more than empty holes ringed with coloured shards. A feeling of decay is palpable. To the north, you can hear the sound of rude laughter and gunfire. }{Newbie Cathedral}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
