R {49772}{0}{}{Strahd's crypt (out)}{ }{      A darkness clouds this room and the essence of evil permeates the very air.  The smell of freshly turned earth is here.  This room appears to be 50 feet long from east to west and 30 feet across.  The feeling of evil you get is strong enough to repel even the mightiest warrior, but the Icon provides you with the strength to remain.  A large coffin rests in the cold black dirt on the floor. }{Ravenloft Castle}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {45921}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {45921}{d}{out}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {49773}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {49774}{0}{}{In a damp cave (pool)}{ }{       You stand in a dark and wet cave. A large pool is behind you that was used to gain access to this cavern. No form of natural light can be detected coming into this cave, it is completely sealed. The walls and ceiling are made of jagged and dark colored rock while the ground of muddy and wet. Large paw prints can be seen in the mud indicating some creature has made a home in here. The only way out of the cave is via the pool behind you. }{Dundee Poachers}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {3406}{pool}{pool}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {3406}{u}{pool}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {49775}{0}{}{Hidden Shaolin Library (stairs)}{ }{     You've reached the secret underground library of the Shaolin monks.  The room is unnaturally dark, and it is quite difficult to get detail of anything in the room.  The room has a deep musky smell and you would guess that nobody has been down here in years.  The only thing that you can make out in this room is a strange pedestal. }{Shaolin Temple}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {25569}{stairs}{stairs}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {25569}{s}{stairs}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {49776}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {49777}{0}{<248>}{-= Dirty Alley =- (e,w)}{<248>. .<088>}{     You find yourself in a small dirty alley leading east from here. Everything is filthy, and it smells pretty bad too. You wish you could get out of here as soon as possible.  To the west is the main road, to the north you can see the massive city wall, and to the south is a somewhat dilapidated building. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {4108}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {49778}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {49778}{0}{<248>}{-= Dirty Alley =- (w)}{<248>. .<088>}{     You find yourself at the eastern end of a filthy little alley.  It really stinks in here--you wonder why you even bothered coming in. To the west the alley runs on.  To the north you can see the massive city wall, to the east is one of the city's towers, and to the south is another somewhat dilapidated building. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {49777}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {49779}{0}{}{Apprentices' quarters (e)}{ }{        This must be a very strange room, since by your own reckoning you are currently standing outside the tower walls, yet this room seems to adjoin the tower very snugly. The room is rectangular, about 40 feet long by 20 feet wide. There are three comfortable-looking beds, and three desks also. It is a bit of a mess in here-- there are books and bits of parchment everywhere. Typical student's quarters, in fact. The only way out seems to be back through the portal through which you came. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46561}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {49780}{0}{}{A council chamber (w)}{ }{        This room is circular. It appears to be some kind of a council chamber. Which seems strange considering that you must be outside the tower  walls. Perhaps you're in a pocket dimension. You really have no idea. But whoever created this must be very powerful. The room has a ring of seats within it, and an open floor in the middle, made of something that looks like granite. The only exit seems to be back through the portal. There are no windows, and the light is provided by the same sort of ball as you saw on the ground floor. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {37798}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {49781}{0}{}{Zalasta's laboratory (n)}{ }{              This is a very strange room, since by your reckoning you should now be standing in mid-air somewhere outside the tower walls. In fact, what you can see seems to confirm this--this room appears to have no walls. There must be some kind of invisible barrier between you and the open air. Looking down, you can see the bottom of the tower about 250 feet below you. The sky is also clearly visible above you, as is the city to your left and right. Behind you, next to the portal, the outside wall of the tower can be seen, while straight ahead you look out towards Dragonspine Bay. There is a huge  table in the middle, made of some kind of white stone. Amazingly, it seems totally unmarked by all the reagents and alchemical powders that are on top of it. To the north, where you surmise the "wall" to be, is something that looks like a door. The only exit appears to be back the way you came. }{Wayhaven}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {46563}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {49782}{0}{<258>}{Swirling Mists (anotherway,thisway,overthere,overhere)}{<258>(<158>P<258>)<088>}{  You stand in a field of swirling mists,  there are no directions here and no landmarks. }{Hell}{hell_entrance}{}{}{1.000}{1}
