R {50071}{0}{}{The mind of a philosopher (sw,d)}{77}{       Cogito ergo sum, they say. Here you are, however, existing because some one had thought you up. You are no more than a figment, perhaps, but a figment nonetheless. Around you whirl other fragments, fractions of thoughts discarded or forgotten, all of them hurling non-spatially through this mental landscape. What passes for air here is crystal clear, and overhead, you see what passes for a sun shining brightly in what passes for the sky. }{Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
