R {50077}{0}{}{A small gothic church (nw,d)}{18}{          You stand in the aisle of a small gothic church as the dignified treble of basset-horns drifts toward you, chased swiftly by violins palpitating in a manner that betrays utter hopelessness.  A cross hangs above the back wall and the thorn-crowned symbol upon it stares down into an opened coffin and several mourners.  The women wear veils while the men are clad in dark, hooded cloaks and grim steel death masks.  What appears to unfold before you is a funeral mass, the somber farewell to a figure of some repute by those who knew him best. The pews around you are largely empty and look to be an excellent vantage point from where you could watch the ceremony progress. }{Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
