R {50097}{0}{}{Rocky Beach (e,n)}{ }{        The beach is narrower here than the wide expanse of sand to the north.  The rocky cliff wall slopes more gently here - though not enough to climb up.  The beach ends at a barnacle-covered pile of rocks to the south, full of nooks and crannies.  The rocks are slippery, and many of them are covered with greenish algae.  The sun beats down in the midst of the blue sky. Extending eastward into the ocean is a wide expanse of rocky sandbar peeking out of the water. }{Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
