R {50098}{0}{}{In a Strange Forest (ne,se,cabin)}{?}{         All around you trees tower overhead, the rustling of their branches whispers on the wind. Where you are standing the trees have retreated to a rough ring, creating a clearing. As if some poison has touched the earth here, trees will not grow in the rocky soil. Only short grass, scrub and the occasional bush has been able to take root here. In the center of this poisoned clearing sits a cabin, squatting like a bloated toad in some fetid swamp. The sky flashes warnings of an impending storm and the wind begins to sing a slow dirge-like melody through the leaves. }{Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
