R {50103}{0}{}{Inside an Abandoned Cabin (doorway)}{ }{         The sun filters in through the dirt scarred windows, its pale light illuminates motes of dust that float lazily in the stagnant air. Along the north wall sits something that resembles a bed. The east wall is made entirely of shelves full of mouldering books. The south wall contains a door that leads outside and a small window beside it. Your eyes follow the peculiar lines of the house and come upon the west wall, completely blank except for a small hole, probably made by a rat. The cool air is dank and fills your nostrils with the stink of loamy rot. }{Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
