R {50134}{0}{}{514 Main Street (enter)}{ }{          You have arrived at the scene of the house fire.  You can feel the heat of the fire warm your face.  Fire fighters are scurrying about the fire scene attending to different tasks.  There are multiple radio transmissions coming across the air adding to the confusion.  The senior fire fighters call it organized chaos.  Your task is to supply water from the pump to the fire fighters who are trying to extinguish the fire.  There are two lines pulled off the rig.  An inch and three quarter line is inside the house fighting the fire, and a two and one half inch line is pulled to the side protecting the house that is exposed to the fire. }{Museum}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
