R {50365}{0}{<248>}{Mayor's Chambers (s)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{       A strong gust of wind whips across this large balcony, seemingly from every direction.  The skyrakers of Mega-Tokyo extend as far as the eye can see and there are many of them along Bu-Do street.  Far below is the city street, with hundreds of citizens traveling to unknown destinations.  The patio has a small table, and chairs for relaxing in the open air.  A large sliding glass door leads southward, back into the Mayor's chambers. }{Mega-Tokyo}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {50362}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {50366}{0}{<248>}{Mayor's Chambers (e)}{<248>[ ]<088>}{       This large kitchen doesn't have a lot of floor space as it's packed with supplies, cooking appliances, as well as a large food preparation counter within the center.  A large double sink is surrounded by tiled counters.  Against the wall on the top of the counters is a plethora of appliances used to create elegant meals for the mayor and her guests.  A small wooden door in the southern section of the east wall swings on double hinges and allows for entry to the dining room. }{Mega-Tokyo}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
