R {51169}{0}{}{Impassable Forest (n,s)}{ }{    The forest is thick and healthy on each side and quite impassable.  A svelte woman blocks the path.  She would be remarkably beautiful, were it not for her completely hairless scalp and the ferocious scowl she wears upon her face! }{The Enchanged Kingdom}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51139}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51171}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51170}{0}{}{A field of fruit trees (w)}{ }{       The sun shines through the branches of row after row of fruit trees.  Where it strikes the ground, colors burst forth and dazzle the eyes.  The uniformity of each row tells you that this must be an orchard of some sort. As a gentle breeze threads its way through the branches, small objects begin to flash and twirl sending rainbow sparks in all directions.  Sparse grass grows between the trees due to the hardiness of that particular weed rather than any attempt at landscaping. }{The Enchanged Kingdom}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51139}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51171}{0}{}{Impossible Road ... (n)}{ }{           The woods are lovely dark and deep, but you have promises to keep and miles to go before you get out of this place.  The well traveled road goes north while impassable wood continues to close off the east and west sides.  But the truly odd thing is how it ... Now that's odd.  How can a road ...   It's got to do something.  Roads don't just ...  In fact, everytime you think of how odd it is that the road ...  You're certain you were thinking of something.  Oh yes, the road.  Where did all of these signs of travel come from if the road just ...  Probably best not to think of the road. You try your best not to think about the road, but that way lies madness.  What way?  The road just ... }{The Enchanged Kingdom}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51169}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51172}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51173}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51172}{0}{}{The end of the road (nw)}{ }{    The road ends here at the edge of a cliff.  A single solitary tree grows near the edge.  Judging from the road, it looks like previous travelers just walked, like lemmings, off the edge of the precipice to fall into the ocean far below. }{The Enchanged Kingdom}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51171}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51175}{boat}{boat}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51175}{se}{boat}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51173}{0}{}{End of the Road (w,n)}{ }{      This is the end of the line.  At least, it's the end of the road.  Cliffs drop down the the ocean to the south and east while the road retreats back into to the north. The view to the east is blocked by a wall of sea spray, and the vertigo inducing view to the south reveals a stunning ocean of tanzanite blue.  To the west lies a brick building with tall white pillars and too many windows to be anything but a schoolhouse. }{The Enchanged Kingdom}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51171}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51174}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51174}{0}{}{Hall of Doors (e)}{ }{        This long hallway stretches toward the horizon with doors lining both sides.  The size of the hall should occupy your attention but what you notice instead is... This hall smells of students: students who skipped showering after gym, who slopped fluids in chemistry class, who felt that sneaking away with a dissection gecko was a cool idea, and students who have never figured out the importance of human hygiene... All of these smells cover up the scent of fine wood paneling, window glass cleaner, and floor wax. }{The Enchanged Kingdom}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
