R {51910}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (w,e)}{ }{     Deep under the ocean surface, this cave snakes its way through the rock.  There's plenty of room to swim, and since it's so dark in here, you occasionally have trouble seeing the walls.  The cave floor is covered in a thick layer of mud.  The water is cold and still.  The cave drops slightly as it opens up to the west. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51678}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51911}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51911}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (n,w,e)}{ }{     You have swum a few dozen strokes inside the cave at the bottom of the ocean.  It levels out here, heading upward to the east and west.  An alcove splits off the main passage to the north.  The mud on the cave floor is as thick as ever here.  It's eerily still, making your hair stand on end. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51910}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51912}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51913}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51912}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (s)}{ }{     This alcove off the main tunnel of the cave is filled with nothing but rock, water, and mud.  The rock ceiling slopes down to the floor just to your north, ending this split-off's short run from the main tunnel. Pointy rocks dot the mud below you like an island archipelago.  There are no signs of life anywhere. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51911}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51913}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (s,e)}{ }{     The cave turns here, heading east and slightly downward, as well as south and sharply upward.  The floor is caked with mud\; the rock walls curve to a ridge above you, like the vaulted ceiling of a cathedral.  The slope heading upward to the south is bare, gnarled rock.  A faint clicking noise emanates from some place deeper in the cave. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51911}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51914}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51914}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (w,n,s)}{ }{     This junction of the cave is low-ceilinged and wide.  A rocky slope drops off to the north, while the cave opens up a bit to the south.  To the west, a low, many-columned chamber opens up.  The floor here is bumpy, irregular, and coated with mud.  A mysterious, faint sound echoes through the cave. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
