R {51918}{0}{}{In a dark, forboding trench under the sea (d,u)}{ }{     The wide trench continues to plunge deeper into the seabed, not narrowing noticeably as you swim downward.  You have an eerie feeling about this place.  The squid, fish, and octopi seem to be avoiding it. Maybe they know something you don't.  You can see only blackness below you\; there's no evidence the trench bottoms out soon. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51760}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51919}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51919}{0}{}{In a dark, forboding trench under the sea (d,u)}{ }{      The forboding trench plummets deeper and deeper, still alarmingly wide.  The dark water is still and undisturbed by the comings and goings of fish and their lesser predators.  You cannot see the top of the trench from this far down, nor can you detect the bottom - or anything beneath you, for that matter.  Only terrible silence and blackness awaits you. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51918}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51920}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51920}{0}{}{In a dark, forboding trench under the sea (d,u)}{ }{     The massive trench continues to plunge down into the darkness, far underneath the ocean floor.  For the first time since you entered the trench, you detect current flowing in the water around you.  It seems you have finally found the abode of the creature the fish are avoiding. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51919}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51921}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51921}{0}{}{In a dark, forboding trench under the sea (u)}{ }{      The bottom of the trench is a midden strewn with bones of the kraken's victims, among other miscellaneous detritus.  Rocks and reflective scraps of metal are half-sunk into the thick pungent mud.  Somewhere far above you, the trench opens up to the deep sea floor.  The water feels unnaturally warm here.  You've swum so far down, you wonder if that's because you're closer to the center of the earth. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51920}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51922}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (n,e)}{ }{    The cave widens here, bending north into the unknown, and east into a low, columned chamber.  There's enough space here for you to swim upright, without touching the muddy floor.  The water is still and chilly.  A mysterious clicking echoes through the cave. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51915}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51923}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51923}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (s)}{ }{     You've reached a dead end.  This wide chamber is surrounded by rough rock walls on all sides, and a thick helping of gooey mud on the floor.  Bones and fish skeletons litter the mud.  It seems you've found something's lair.  The freezing water presses in on you, heightening your panic. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51922}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51924}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {51915}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51925}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (d,w)}{ }{     A shaft opens up here, plunging nearly straight down into the rock.  You can't see the bottom through the murky water.  A crack, easily wide enough to swim through, but narrow enough to make you feel constrained, leads west from here.  Its bottom surface is covered in thick, gooey mud. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51916}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51926}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51926}{0}{}{Spelunking far under the ocean surface (u)}{ }{     The shaft terminates a short swim down from its apex.  The bottom is filled with mud to an unknown depth.  The rock walls close in around you, giving you barely enough space to turn around.  Above you, the shaft disappears into darkness.  You feel as though you've found the most inhospitable part of the ocean. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51925}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51927}{0}{}{Swimming through a tunnel (ne,u)}{ }{      The tunnel takes a sharp bend here around a gigantic igneous rock, heading northeast and slowly downward.  The horizontal section is a couple meters wide at its narrowest point, which somewhat relieves the pressure of the current flowing up and out of the tunnel.  You have to swim carefully to avoid hitting your head on sharp protrusions of the walls. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51907}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51928}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51928}{0}{}{Swimming through a tunnel (d,sw)}{ }{     The tunnel here widens again, now to twice your armspan, and plunges downward at a steep angle.  The current coming up the shaft is much weaker than it was in the narrower tunnel above.  You can't see the bottom of the shaft through the gloom of the seawater.  Somewhere above you, up the twisting tunnel, is the open ocean. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51927}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51929}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51929}{0}{}{Swimming through a tunnel (n,u)}{ }{      The chasm bottoms out here, a dozen meters or so beneath its summit up above you.  A fissure on the north side of the shaft is just wide enough to admit you.  The current rushes powerfully from the fissure, swirls about you, and rises up.  A very faint greenish glow emanates from somewhere far back into the fissure.  It's the first light you've seen around here in a long time. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51928}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51930}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51930}{0}{}{Swimming through a tunnel (s,n,u)}{ }{       Brightly glowing green algae clings tenaciously to the rock walls at the north end of the fissure, which at this point has widened to comfortably admit you.  The current sweeps quickly by the rounded corners of the rock walls, making you wonder how the algae sticks.  It looks as if you could swim up here - the walls open up, and the green glow of the algae gives way to a stronger glow reminding you of... daylight?  It can't be, this far under the sea - can it? }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51929}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51931}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51932}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51931}{0}{}{Swimming through a tunnel (s)}{ }{      The fissure narrows rapidly to the north, quickly becoming too small to admit you.  It seems this is the end of the line, at least until someone does some excavation work.  The current rockets powerfully past you as you brace against the rocky walls.  The algae you found to the south is not found here, although you can still see the unearthly green glow to the south. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51930}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51932}{0}{}{In an undersea grotto (d)}{ }{       You have emerged from the fissure into a grotto which, surprisingly enough, is filled with perfectly breathable air.  The light which shines down on the algae emanates from a ball of warm light that hangs motionless in the air here, like a tiny artificial sun.  A beach of smooth rock offers a respite from the crushing pressure of the ocean.  A dilapidated wooden chest sits on the beach, its lid propped open.  Krat     Reboot: 9.3 days [00:00:01]  Controller: None Deadman: 0 }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
