R {51946}{0}{}{Swimming in the deep sea (u,d)}{ }{     You're swimming through a crevice in the rock ceiling of a gigantic underwater cavern.  The walls are a mere fathom apart, giving you barely enough room to swim.  Beneath you, the crevice opens up into the open reaches of the cavern.  Above, it continues to climb.  The chilly water draws the heat from your body. }{Mystic Seal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51441}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51949}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51947}{0}{}{In an undersea alcove (e,n)}{ }{     The alcove continues here, meandering among the rocks that form the cavern ceiling.  It's a tighter fit here than in the mouth of the alcove to your north.  The alcove continues to the east, but someone has ringed the walls on the way east with spears of sharp bone.  You'd have to swim carefully to avoid impaling yourself on the sharp spikes. }{Mystic Seal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51936}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51948}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51948}{0}{}{In an undersea alcove (w)}{ }{     The alcove ends here, in a small chamber that has evidently been set up as a home for some aquatic hunters.  Fish bones litter the floor.  Some of them have been roughly hewn into tools for cutting and sharpening.  There's no evidence of furniture anywhere - it seems whoever lives here leads a crude existence. }{Mystic Seal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51947}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51949}{0}{}{Swimming in the deep sea (d)}{ }{      The crevice terminates here, in a tiny chamber completely filled with water.  An unusual and beautiful collection of creatures populates the rocks lining the chamber - many starfish, their gossamer tendrils writhing slowly and silently.  The ghostly blue echinoderms cling to the rock surfaces, filtering the water for their food.  There must be over a hundred of them. }{Mystic Seal}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51946}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {51950}{0}{}{Elemental plane of water (w,n,s,portal,e)}{ }{      You're surrounded by light, blue, pure water.  It extends away in all directions as far as you can see.  A portal here seems to be draining water into itself, but it doesn't seem the water here is at all limited.  A large structure of some sort is visible a ways off.  Lacking any way to tell directions here, you decide to call that way north. }{Mystic Seal - Lair of the Kraken}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {51951}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {51952}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
