R {52573}{0}{<248>}{Sarkath Khan's Crypt (se)}{<248>. <178>+<088>}{                                  Sarkath Khan's Crypt This is obviously the crypt of Sarkath Khan. Long copper tapestry holders hang on the walls with rotted remains of cloth hanging from them. By the farmost wall you can see two large full armours with two-handed swords in their hands. In the center of the room there's a large coffin. There are also four golden braziers placed by each corner of the coffin. The dustfilled air in the crypt causes you to choke constantly and the overwhelming smell of troll causes your nostrils to scream for fresh air. }{Sarkath Khan}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52572}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52574}{0}{}{It is narrow in here, and the walls rise interminably (out,stairs)}{ }{                 >  Krat     Reboot: 3.2 days [00:00:02]  Controller: None Deadman: 0  Krat     Reboot: 3.2 days [00:00:03]  Controller: None Deadman: 0  Krat     Reboot: 3.2 days [00:00:01]  Controller: None Deadman: 0 =S=It is narrow in here, and the walls rise interminably (out,s=S=      ---*---   Walls that seem as though they are made of soaked wood circle around you, dark and soft to the touch.  The smell is of rotting earth, moist and old, pungent and thick like freshly tanned leather.  Above you, far into the reaches of this twisting, seemingly organic spire, the darkness stretches and contorts, blackness shifting within itself against a backdrop of even denser pitch.  The ground beneath you is patchy with grass and brown weeds, several small rocks forming interesting patterns against the otherwise lifeless permafrost.  Rising up around the periphery of the spire, against the sodden walls is nestled a precarious set of stairs made of decaying planks of raw, hastily assembled bark.  A semicircle of dim light at the base of the tower might be large enough to crawl through, back outside to the arid, unforgiving tundra. }{Spire}{spire}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {8481}{out}{out}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52575}{stairs}{stairs}{0}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52575}{u}{stairs}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52575}{0}{}{Several meters above the ground (u,d)}{ }{       You stand precariously, perched upon a rough-hewn scrap of flaking, damp wood which can hardly seem to hold its own weight against the dark, seemingly ancient series of supports which prop it from beneath.  The wall of this pungent, cramped circular tower of wood is tempting to lean against, though any excessive movement in this place would seem unwise.  The ground of the spire is several feet below, easily seen through the wide cracks between each step, though the view above, dark as wet tar, bears just as little comfort. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52576}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52574}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52576}{0}{}{There is a bizarre, circular door of mud here (u,d)}{ }{         The unsteady, ancient steps circle around and around, outlining the periphery of this narrow spire as it extends inexorably upwards.  The bottom of the tower is far enough away that a leap down would break the legs of even the most hardy human adventurer...all you can see of the ground is a small semicircle of light coming in from the miniature orifice at the base.  Immediately to the west is a rather unusual circular structure that at first glance resembles a door...it would seem likely that beyond it lies one of the protruding 'branches' that are visible from the exterior of the spire.  Up above you, in empty blackness, lies what seems like a never-ending ascent. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52575}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52578}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52593}{w}{punch door}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52577}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {52575}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52578}{0}{}{On the stairs, quite high up (u,d)}{ }{     The ground now both a distant and a fond memory, you are giving your total complement of weight and faith to the shady planks of barky wood which rest upon rickety supports.  Nothing can be seen above you except for more steps disappearing into a thick, organic darkness.  Several steps beneath you, fit into the wall, is a round, black...door? }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52576}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52579}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52579}{0}{}{A hole opens up to the east (d,e,u)}{ }{        A welcome sight -- directly to the east of you, cut into the wall, a large hole opens up, leading into one of the giant branches which grace this bizarre, living spire.  The steps you have been traveling seem to be darker and more brittle up here (the ones at the base of the spire were sketchy, though slightly thicker and more regular), and the odor in the air is mildly different...it is less earthy where you stand, more rancid and bitter.  The walls remain the same\; dark, moist, ever so slightly pliable and wholly organic. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52578}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52580}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52581}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52580}{0}{}{Inside a giant branch (w)}{ }{     You have entered the interior of one of the giant branches which sprout from the trunk of the spire.  At its far end, it tapers off to a point.  The room itself is tubular and irregular...there is no distinction between the floor and the walls\; it is all dark, wet, splintery wood.  To the west is a hole that leads out into the main space of the tower. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52579}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52581}{0}{}{The spire is beginning to narrow slightly (u,d)}{ }{        As the oppressive spiral of the stairs continues onward and upward, the walls confining them begin to narrow ever so slightly, evident only in the tighter curl of the steps as they ascend.  Even though it is obvious to your senses that this place -- whatever it may be, and whatever era in which it must have originated -- was born of evil, you begin to acquire a sense that everything in this spire is exactly as it should be...that whatever purpose this place serves is a necessary one.  It could, however, just be the bitter odor of rotting, soaked wood distorting your cells. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52579}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52582}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52582}{0}{}{To the west is an opening to another branch (w,d,u)}{ }{       A narrower opening than the one encountered several yards below, there is nevertheless ample room for an individual to crawl into the space to the west.  The opening is dark, but it appears to be quite empty.  You are standing on the stairs which circle around this wooden spire, easily over 100 feet up by now.  The ground all the way below is nearly impossible to see save for what is now a tiny speck of light demarcating the entrance point to this gruesome living tower. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52581}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52583}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52584}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52583}{0}{}{Passing through a narrow crawlspace (w,e)}{ }{     Narrower than it would appear from outside, this has turned into a miniature tunnel.  The walls are soft and laden with strange, yellow fungi, lending the air an odor even more sour than before.  Back to the east is the aperture which opens out into the main spire, and to the west, several yards beyond, the branch inside which you are crawling appears to widen. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52582}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52585}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52584}{0}{}{Easily 200 feet above the ground (s,d,u)}{ }{        The ground, countless yards below, is embedded in a darkness that can only seem this thick when there is simply massive amounts of space within which it may dwell.  By now you barely even notice the speck of light at the base of the spire, as it is but the size of a pinprick from this distance.  You are acutely aware that the spaces between the steps are rather forbidding, and the lack of handholds is a preeminent conundrum, yet it hardly seems to dampen the strange, almost melodious aura that this entire structure emits.  Directly south of you is another opening to a branch. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52582}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52586}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52587}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52585}{0}{}{A disturbing wooden chamber (e)}{ }{      This room casts a pallor upon the air which you immediately sense.  The interior of a giant branch, the walls and floor are all irregular and seamless, the wood soft and damp.  The centerpiece of the room is a large metal contraption, with a strangely deformed skeleton attached to it.  The room tapers off to a point to the west, and an orifice in the wall to the east leads to a narrow crawlspace. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52583}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52586}{0}{}{A room dense with thorny vines and barbs (sw,n)}{ }{     You are immediately confronted by countless hanging vines, all of which seem to be covered with thorns and barbs of varying shapes and sizes.  You can make out some strange noises -- moaning? -- to the southwest, as this giant hollow branch sinews about.  To the north, beyond a tangle of dead brambles and woody fibers, is an opening to the main cavity of the spire. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52584}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52588}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52587}{0}{}{The walls are changing color (d,u,e)}{ }{       You had not noticed that they had been subtly shading into red, but the walls here are most certainly ruddy and shimmering.  Whether it is the natural color of the wood, or if it is an external affectation is not apparent, but the deep, dense iridescence within the fibers of the bark is certainly not common.  In fact, the bark now seems not so much like wood, as skin...the texture is smoother, no longer fibrous.  Set into this puzzling wall is a hole to the east, from which you can hear some dubious noises. }{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52584}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52589}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52590}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {52588}{0}{}{The hollow of a branch (or 'strange things are happening here') (ne)}{ }{}{Spire}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52586}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

