R {52999}{0}{}{On the top of the fungus (nw,e)}{ }{     The bleached bone head of the fungus has a patchy appearance. Some of the eastern parts are faded. The edge of the fungus makes a turn to the northwest. A few cracks can be seen in the edge of the fungus after it has made its turn. The grass sea spreads out to the horizon on all sides. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52998}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53008}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53000}{0}{}{On top of the fungus (e,sw)}{ }{     As you move further round the fungus you see the head of the fungus has the same bleached bone appearance. Here the bleached bone is intermittently dotted with a black powder like substance of some kind. The grass that surrounds the fungus can be seen spreading to the horizon. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {52998}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53001}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53001}{0}{}{On top of the fungus (e,w)}{ }{     You walk further along the head of the fungus. The bleached bone colour of the head of the fungus squashes underfoot. Each step seems to release more of the smell that enshrouds the fungus. The head of the fungus is covered in tracks. The sea of grass and fungus spreads out to the horizon on all sides. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {53000}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53002}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53002}{0}{}{On top of the fungus (e,w)}{ }{      A small breeze can be felt blowing across the fungus here. The surface of the fungus is more weather beaten than other areas you have seen. Small cracks on the surface of the fungus are starting to open up. The cracks seem too small to reduce the structural integrity of the fungus' head yet the edge of the fungus has started to crumble away. The sea of grass and fungus spreads out to the horizon on all sides. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {53001}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53003}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53003}{0}{}{On top of the fungus (se,w)}{ }{      A large dark spot breaks up the monotony of the bleached bone colour that exists around you. The dark spot is black in the centre and fades out to a dark grey on the edge. It is round like a circle but is not a perfect shape. Small cracks exist near the edge of the fungus yet the edge itself is in good condition. The sea of grass and fungus spreads out to the horizon on all sides. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {53002}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53004}{se}{se}{6}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53004}{0}{}{On the east side of the fungus (sw,nw)}{ }{         The squared head of the fungus has made a sharp turn. The long straight edges have turned into shorter lengths that eventually do a complete turn and head back in the direction you have come from. The short edge of the fungus is indeed quite short yet this edge seems to hide its size rather well. The surface is organised into sections with an arch in the center of these sections. A red carpet runs from near where you stand off to the west through an arch. Around the arch are a few sets of tracks. The sea of grass and fungus spreads out to the horizon. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {53003}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53005}{sw}{sw}{12}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53006}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53005}{0}{}{On the top of the fungus (w,ne)}{ }{        The normally smooth texture of the head of the fungus is broken up here by a large crack. The crack is in the centre of the fungus and looks large enough for you to fit into. Most of the edges of the crack are jagged but some have been broken off. The shadows in the crack make it difficult to work out how deep the crack itself is. The edge of the fungus is still in good condition with no obvious cracks or blemishes. Over the edge of the fungus you can see the sea of grass and the heads of other fungi. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {53004}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53007}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53006}{0}{}{The throne room (e)}{ }{     The throne room is enclosed within a translucent bubble. The walls are smooth and allow light to pass through. The light reflects off of the golden throne. The throne sits towards the rear of the room in line with the arch through which you came. The red carpet leads directly to the foot of the dais on which the throne is placed. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {53004}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53007}{0}{}{On the top of the fungus (w,e)}{ }{      The bleached bone head of the fungus continues along in a straight line here. The cracks along the edge and centre of the fungus have disappeared. The smooth surface texture gleams brightly in the sunlight. Past the edge of the fungus the sea of grass starts. The grass spreads out to the horizon and is broken up by other fungus heads.  }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {53005}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53008}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53008}{0}{}{On the top of the fungus (w,e)}{ }{      The sun's rays seem to be focused on this part of the head. The temperature seems a few degrees higher here than other areas. The bleached bone colour has lightened slightly here making the head of the fungus look enticing to eat. The surface of the fungus does not display any noticeable cracks or blemishes. The sea of grass and fungus spreads out to the horizon on all sides. }{The Magic Fungus}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
E {53007}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {52999}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53009}{0}{}{At a jousting tournament (out)}{ }{  You're in the fight of your life! No time to smell the daisies or you'll end up pushing them! }{The City of Westersea}{}{}{}{1.000}{1}
