R {53350}{0}{}{A gently sloping passage (e,nw,s)}{ }{The passageway gently slopes downward here, splitting to the east and the south.  The walls are the same sturdy rock that makes up the entire sietch, along with the wear and use of the years.  You can feel some moisture in the air, but it is not very close to where you stand now.  To the south you can see the passage takes a turn towards the east eventually.  A fremen yali can be seen off to the east, illuminated by the glowglobes that inhabit it.}{Fremen Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53349}{nw}{nw}{9}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53377}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53378}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53351}{0}{}{A set of stairs carved into the stone (d,ne)}{ }{The path takes a turn and heads down a stone stairway here.  A small ledge can be seen running alongside the stairs, and glowglobes hang above to light the way.  Fremen frequently move up and down these stairs with a sense of purpose.  You hear a murmur of voices coming from below, as if a meeting were taking place.}{Fremen Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53349}{ne}{ne}{3}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53359}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53352}{0}{}{A cavern pathway in the sietch (n,s,e)}{ }{You find yourself standing in the entryway to Sietch Tabr, a city in its own right, below the arid desert sands.  Moisture can be felt in the air, as a reminder that you are no longer in grips of the arid desert atmosphere.  The walls are made of stone, not man-made but not entirely natural either.  The cavern you now stand in splits off in various directions, winding out to the other branches of this vast sietch and its inhabitants.}{Fremen Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
