R {53404}{0}{}{Top of the Tower of the Crimson Rose (d)}{ }{Top of the Tower of the Crimson Rose. You are in the inner sanctum of the Crimson Rose. You can rest here if you desire, or leave items for your other School members. No one but other members of your school can get here. A small spiral staircase winds down through the floor to the level below.}{Mage Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53320}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53405}{0}{<118>}{}{ }{}{}{}{}{}{1.000}{}

R {53406}{0}{}{Bottom of the Staircase (e,s,w,u)}{ }{Bottom of the Staircase. The pieces of rubble are somewhat smaller and getting around is a little easier. The perimeter wall is almost complete here, composed from large stones which fit together seamlessly. This is probably not a good place to hang around\; suspended above you is the only remaining section of the ceiling and you can only but wonder how stable it really is. A spiral staircase winds its way up through the ceiling and looks passable. You can also follow the walls around to the east or west, and a small path leads off south through the debris towards the exit.}{Mage Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53322}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53407}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53408}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53409}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53407}{0}{}{Charred room (w)}{ }{Charred room. This was once clearly a grandiose room, but nothing remains of the interior walls except the huge fireplace. Even there, the bricks which form the firebox which once fed a chimney are broken in places and the mantlepiece has been completely destroyed. Large windows in the exterior indicate this was clearly a major hall. Unfortunately, this entire area has been blasted with intense heat and all the rocks and debris are completely blackened. At first glance, there is nothing interesting here except the path which leads back to the staircase.}{Mage Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53406}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53408}{0}{}{Remains of a laboratory}{ }{Remains of a laboratory. This is a comparatively interesting room, considering how little is left of the rest of the tower. Parts of interior walls are left standing, and amongst all the stones and boulders on the floor are pieces of glass and wood. A table leg is clearly the original use of one piece of timber and mounting brackets for a shelf are visible on one wall although the shelf itself is long gone. What is clear from the glass shards and broken vials and jars is that this was probably originally some kind of laboratory or a place for developing magical reagents. An old iron stove is tipped on its side near the far wall.}{Mage Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53406}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53409}{0}{}{Open to the sky (d)}{ }{Open to the sky. As you climb to the top of the stairs, brilliant daylight floods over you. The tower is open to the sky providing a fantastic view of the passing clouds. It is difficult to see past the remains of the broken circular walls which rise to roughly the same height as you are now at, but you notice in places the dark energy field shimmering and the darkness beyond. This was clearly once the floor of the second level of the tower but most has collapsed and this small platform is all that remains.}{Mage Guild}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53406}{d}{d}{32}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53410}{0}{}{Sunken ruins (w)}{ }{The water is calm within the ancient stone walls of the some sort of building.  Your light bounces off the dark stone, casting strange shadows in the water.  Strange burbling sounds ripple through the building, echoing off the walls.  You think you could squeeze through a gap in the stone to the west.}{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53411}{w}{w}{8}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53411}{0}{}{A confusing underwater ruin (e,u,n)}{ }{The ancient ruins of some crumbling building surround you, the stone walls worn by the soft motion of the ocean.  Small streams of bubbles rise from cracks in the stone below you, and disappear through more in the darkness above.  It may prove to be easier to get into the building than to find your way out again.  You think you could squeeze through gaps in the stone to the north, to the east and above you.}{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53410}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53412}{n}{n}{1}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53427}{u}{u}{16}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53412}{0}{}{Deep in some underwater ruins (s,e)}{ }{The ancient ruins of some crumbling building surround you, the stone walls worn by the soft motion of the ocean.  The otherwise clear water is filled with suspended particles of stone and dirt.  It is hard to tell up from down, let alone determine which way you came from.  You think you could squeeze through gaps in the stone to the east and to the south.}{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
E {53411}{s}{s}{4}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}
E {53413}{e}{e}{2}{0}{}{1.000}{}{0.00}

R {53413}{0}{}{A confusing underwater ruin (u,w)}{ }{All around, the walls of some sort of ancient submerged building block out the light.  Small streams of bubbles rise from cracks in the stone below you, and disappear through more in the darkness above.  The water shifts behind you, but when you swivel around there is nothing there.  You think you could squeeze through gaps in the stone to the west and above you.}{CowVille}{}{}{}{1.000}{}
